# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agents as employees, with a kernel between them and the host.** *web-app-hermes* and *web-app-openclaw* deploy agents behind the single sign-on gate, wired to the gateway's models and to the MCP servers discovery hands them, each proving on deploy that it can actually reach them. *svc-virt-kata* runs that tier under a kernel-isolating container runtime, and *svc-ai-robot* embodies an agent on a dedicated device. Every sandboxed agent acts as its own platform account rather than borrowing yours. See [web-app-hermes](roles/web-app-hermes/README.md), [web-app-openclaw](roles/web-app-openclaw/README.md) and [svc-virt-kata](roles/svc-virt-kata/README.md)."
msgstr "**Gníomhairí mar fhostaithe, le eithne eatarthu agus an t-óstach.** *web-app-hermes* agus *web-app-openclaw* gníomhairí a imscaradh taobh thiar de na comharthaí-ar geata aonair, sreangaithe chuig samhlacha an geata agus do na freastalaithe MCP teacht ar lámha iad, gach chruthú ar imscaradh gur féidir é a bhaint amach i ndáiríre iad. *svc-virt-kata* Ritheann an tsraith sin faoi runtime coimeádán eithne-iseolating, agus *svc-ai-robot* embodies gníomhaire ar ghléas tiomnaithe. Feidhmíonn gach gníomhaire sandboxed mar a chuntas ardán féin seachas mise a fháil ar iasacht. Féach ar [web-app-hermes](roles/web-app-hermes/README.md), [web-app-openclaw](roles/web-app-openclaw/README.md) agus [svc-virt-kata](roles/svc-virt-kata/README.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agents consume tools as MCP clients via the [025](025-mcp-role-integration.md) mechanism.** Hermes and OpenClaw are configured as MCP clients of the repository's MCP server roles over HTTP/SSE (not stdio: under microVM isolation and multi-node placement a stdio subprocess cannot reach an MCP server in another container). Discovery and credentials reuse 025's [`roles_with_service`](../../plugins/lookup/roles_with_service.py) lookup and `credentials:` blocks. Both roles are added to 025's MCP audit as client roles. Only 025's shared contract (the `services.mcp` schema) and the lookup extension are prerequisites for this requirement; 025's audit tooling, full lint set, and baserow+openwebui slice are independent later work."
msgstr "**Gníomhairí ithe uirlisí mar chliaint MCP tríd an [025](025-mcp-role-integration.md) meicníocht.** Hermes agus OpenClaw atá cumraithe mar chliaint MCP na róil freastalaí MCP an stór thar HTTP / SSE (Ní stdio: faoi aonrú micreaVM agus socrúchán il-node Ní féidir le subprocess stdio teacht ar fhreastalaí MCP i gcoimeádán eile). Discovery agus dintiúir athúsáid 025's [`roles_with_service`](../../plugins/lookup/roles_with_service.py) lookup agus `credentials:` bloic. Cuirtear an dá ról leis an 025's MCP iniúchadh mar róil chliaint. ach amháin 025's conradh comhroinnte (an `services.mcp` scéim na scéime) agus tá an síneadh Lookup réamhriachtanais don riachtanas seo; 025's tooling iniúchóireachta, leagtha lint iomlán, agus baserow + openwebui slice bhfuil obair neamhspleách ina dhiaidh sin."

msgid "**Agents on demand:** The first completion of a user for ``hermes`` or ``openclaw`` creates that user’s agent; later requests reuse it, and a stopped agent is started again with its state volume re-attached."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Agents on demand:** The first completion of a user for `hermes` or `openclaw` creates that user's agent; later requests reuse it, and a stopped agent is started again with its state volume re-attached."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agents that spin up containers use nested Docker inside the isolated runtime; host socket passthrough is forbidden.** When an agent needs to run compose workloads (see the scenario below), it runs a nested Docker daemon inside its own isolated runtime. Mounting the host `/var/run/docker.sock` into an agent that executes model-generated code is **forbidden**: it grants root-equivalent host control and defeats the isolation entirely. Nested Docker costs performance and, on gVisor, may need `runsc` with the appropriate platform; the role README MUST document the overhead. An agent role that requires containers MUST declare this capability explicitly."
msgstr "**Gníomhairí a casadh suas coimeádáin a úsáid Docker neadaithe taobh istigh den runtime iargúlta; Tá passthrough soicéad óstach forbidden.** Nuair is gá do ghníomhaire ualaí oibre a chumadh (féach an scéal thíos), ritheann sé Daemon Docker neadaithe taobh istigh a runtime iargúlta féin. Mhúnlú an óstach `/var/run/docker.sock` i gníomhaire a fhorghníomhú cód samhail-generated **cosc iomlán**: tugann sé rialú óstach fréimhe-choibhéiseach agus defeats an aonrú go hiomlán. Nested Docker costais feidhmíochta agus, ar gVisor, d'fhéadfadh gá `runsc` leis an ardán cuí; an ról README MUST doiciméadú an lastuas. Ról gníomhaire a éilíonn coimeádáin MUST dhearbhú an cumas seo go sainráite."

# translated-by: libretranslate
