# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Keycloak sign-in:** With Keycloak in the deployment, the role sets ``services.sso.flavor: oidc`` and the LiteLLM Gateway reads the platform’s OIDC endpoints from ``GENERIC_CLIENT_ID``, ``GENERIC_CLIENT_SECRET``, ``GENERIC_AUTHORIZATION_ENDPOINT``, ``GENERIC_TOKEN_ENDPOINT`` and ``GENERIC_USERINFO_ENDPOINT``. Sign in at ``/sso/key/generate``; ``PROXY_ADMIN_ID`` carries the administrator’s username. LiteLLM serves SSO for up to five accounts in ``litellm_usertable`` and refuses beyond that without ``LITELLM_LICENSE``."
msgstr "**Keycloak comhartha isteach:** Le Keycloak san imscaradh, tacair an ról ``services.sso.flavor: oidc`` agus an LiteLLM Gateway léann an ardán ar OIDC endpoints ó ``GENERIC_CLIENT_ID``, ``GENERIC_CLIENT_SECRET``, ``GENERIC_AUTHORIZATION_ENDPOINT``, ``GENERIC_TOKEN_ENDPOINT`` agus ``GENERIC_USERINFO_ENDPOINT``. Cláraigh ag ``/sso/key/generate``; ``PROXY_ADMIN_ID`` Déanann ainm úsáideora an riarthóra. LiteLLM feidhmíonn SSO ar feadh suas le cúig chuntas i ``litellm_usertable`` agus a dhiúltóidh níos faide ná sin gan ``LITELLM_LICENSE``."

