# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With Home Assistant deployed, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The MCP server list itself lives in ``openclaw.json``, not in the container environment."
msgstr "**MCP conradh cliant:** Le haghaidh Home Assistant imscaradh, dearbhaíonn an ról an taobh cliant MCP an chonartha ardán mar chliant insruthaithe-HTTP inmheánach le polasaí uirlis léamh-amháin. Tá an liosta freastalaí MCP féin ina chónaí i ``openclaw.json``, ní sa timpeallacht coimeádán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With Home Assistant deployed, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The MCP server list itself lives in `openclaw.json`, not in the container environment."
msgstr "**MCP conradh cliant:** Le haghaidh Home Assistant imscaradh, dearbhaíonn an ról an taobh cliant MCP an chonartha ardán mar chliant insruthaithe-HTTP inmheánach le polasaí uirlis léamh-amháin. Tá an liosta freastalaí MCP féin ina chónaí i `openclaw.json`, ní sa timpeallacht coimeádán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With an MCP server deployed alongside it, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The deploy registers every discovered provider in the instance-level `/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers` registry under an `infinito:` name, stores the bearer as an encrypted `CUSTOM_HEADERS` `authConfig`, authorizes each entry and compares the discovered tools against the provider's declared allowlist. `CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse` pins the deployment to URL-based MCP servers, so no flow can spawn a local stdio command. Reaching an MCP server whose URL resolves inside the container network requires `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false` plus an `HTTP_DENY_LIST` that keeps loopback and the cloud-metadata addresses denied; both are rendered only while MCP servers are discovered, and the deploy proves the list is live by pointing a throwaway entry at each denied address. One managed Agentflow fixture calls a single named tool with fixed arguments and is executed on every deploy. Wiring a provider into a flow of your own stays an operator step."
msgstr "**MCP conradh cliant:** Le freastalaí MCP imscaradh taobh leis, dearbhaíonn an ról an taobh cliant MCP an chonartha ardán mar chliant inmheánach sruthú-HTTP le polasaí uirlis léamh-amháin. Na cláir imscaradh gach soláthraí fuair sé amach sa chás-leibhéal `/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers` clárlann faoi `infinito:` ainm, siopaí an settings mar criptithe `CUSTOM_HEADERS` `authConfig`, údaraíonn gach iontráil agus cuireann sé i gcomparáid leis na huirlisí a fuair sé amach i gcoinne an tsoláthróra ar dhearbhaigh an cheadúliosta. `CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse` bioráin an imscaradh chuig freastalaithe MCP URL-bhunaithe, mar sin ní féidir aon sreabhadh sceite ordú stdio áitiúil. Reaching freastalaí MCP a réitíonn a URL taobh istigh den líonra coimeádán éilíonn `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false` móide `HTTP_DENY_LIST` go gcoinníonn lúb siar agus na seoltaí scamall-metadata dhiúltú; araon a dhéantar ach amháin nuair a freastalaithe MCP aimsithe, agus go gcruthóidh an imscaradh go bhfuil an liosta beo ag cur in iúl iontráil throwaway ag gach seoladh dhiúltú. Iarrann fixture One bainistiú Agentflow uirlis ainmnithe amháin le hargóintí seasta agus tá sé chun báis ar gach imscaradh. Roinnt soláthraí isteach i sreabhadh de do chuid féin tréimhsí céim oibreoir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With an MCP server deployed alongside it, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The deploy registers every discovered provider in the instance-level ``/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers`` registry under an ``infinito:`` name, stores the bearer as an encrypted ``CUSTOM_HEADERS`` ``authConfig``, authorizes each entry and compares the discovered tools against the provider’s declared allowlist. ``CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse`` pins the deployment to URL-based MCP servers, so no flow can spawn a local stdio command. Reaching an MCP server whose URL resolves inside the container network requires ``HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false`` plus an ``HTTP_DENY_LIST`` that keeps loopback and the cloud-metadata addresses denied; both are rendered only while MCP servers are discovered, and the deploy proves the list is live by pointing a throwaway entry at each denied address. One managed Agentflow fixture calls a single named tool with fixed arguments and is executed on every deploy. Wiring a provider into a flow of your own stays an operator step."
msgstr "**MCP conradh cliant:** Le freastalaí MCP imscaradh taobh leis, dearbhaíonn an ról an taobh cliant MCP an chonartha ardán mar chliant inmheánach sruthú-HTTP le polasaí uirlis léamh-amháin. Na cláir imscaradh gach soláthraí fuair sé amach sa chás-leibhéal ``/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers`` clárlann faoi ``infinito:`` ainm, siopaí an settings mar criptithe ``CUSTOM_HEADERS`` ``authConfig``, údaraíonn gach iontráil agus comparáid a dhéanamh idir na huirlisí a fuair sé amach i gcoinne an tsoláthróra dearbhaithe ar cheadúliosta. ``CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse`` bioráin an imscaradh chuig freastalaithe MCP URL-bhunaithe, mar sin ní féidir aon sreabhadh sceite ordú stdio áitiúil. Reaching freastalaí MCP a réitíonn a URL taobh istigh den líonra coimeádán éilíonn ``HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false`` móide ``HTTP_DENY_LIST`` go gcoinníonn lúb siar agus na seoltaí scamall-metadata dhiúltú; araon a dhéantar ach amháin nuair a freastalaithe MCP aimsithe, agus go gcruthóidh an imscaradh go bhfuil an liosta beo ag cur in iúl iontráil throwaway ag gach seoladh dhiúltú. Iarrann fixture One bainistiú Agentflow uirlis ainmnithe amháin le hargóintí seasta agus tá sé chun báis ar gach imscaradh. Roinnt soláthraí isteach i sreabhadh de do chuid féin tréimhsí céim oibreoir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**MCP is declared, not wired.** A role states an *mcp* block in *meta/services.yml*, and the vocabulary, discovery and rendering layer derives endpoints, clients, credentials and network edges from it. A client-provider pairing is declared once, on the provider; *sys-svc-mcp-reconcile* converges clients from the complete provider set; a refused pairing is expressed as off rather than gated at the call site; and *svc-ai-mcp-adapter* is a reusable per-provider sidecar rather than a standalone application. The contract is proven on deploy, including refusal on *initialize* and the tool inventory itself. The design, its delegation rules and a machine-checkable audit live under [docs/contributing/design/role/services/mcp.md](docs/contributing/design/role/services/mcp.md)."
msgstr "**Dearbhaítear MCP, ní sreangaithe.** Deir ról *taise* bloc i *meta/services.yml*, agus tagann an stór focal, fionnachtain agus ciseal rindreáil endpoints, cliaint, dintiúir agus imill líonra uaidh. Fógraítear péireáil cliant-soláthraí uair amháin, ar an soláthraí; *sys-svc-mcp-reconcile* cliaint a chiontú ón soláthraí iomlán atá leagtha; tá pairing diúltaithe in iúl mar as seachas gated ag an suíomh glaonna; agus *svc-ai-mcp-adapter* Is sidecar in-athúsáidte in aghaidh an-soláthraí seachas iarratas standalone. Tá an conradh cruthaithe ar imscaradh, lena n-áirítear diúltú ar *tús a chur leis* agus an fardal uirlis féin. Tá an dearadh, a rialacha tarmligin agus iniúchadh inseiceáilte meaisín ina gcónaí faoi [docs/contributing/design/role/services/mcp.md](docs/contributing/design/role/services/mcp.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**MCP server contract:** Declares the `/mcp` path over streamable HTTP as an internal, bearer-token-authenticated endpoint served by the `svc-ai-mcp-adapter` instance running as compose service `giteamcp`. The adapter listens on container port `8080` and is never published to a host port or fronted by the public reverse proxy; clients reach it as `http://giteamcp:8080/mcp` on the container network. It is off by default and switches on only where Hermes Agent or OpenClaw is part of the deployment."
msgstr "**conradh freastalaí MCP:** Dhearbhaigh na `/mcp` cosán níos mó ná HTTP sruthaithe mar chríochphointe inmheánach, bearer-token-authenticated sheirbheáil ag an `svc-ai-mcp-adapter` mar shampla ag rith mar sheirbhís chumadh `giteamcp`. Éisteann an adapter ar phort coimeádán `8080` agus ní fhoilsítear é riamh chuig calafort óstach nó os comhair an seachvótálaí droim ar ais phoiblí; sroicheann cliaint é mar `http://giteamcp:8080/mcp` ar an líonra coimeádán. Tá sé as de réir réamhshocraithe agus lasca ar ach amháin nuair Hermes Agent nó OpenClaw cuid den imscaradh."

