# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Mitigation:** Targets still cannot bypass `allowWrite`, `allowedDomains`, or the `deny` list. A malicious target that called `rm -rf .` would be stopped by the `rm -rf*` deny rule."
msgstr "**Mitigation:** Ní féidir le spriocanna fós seachbhóthar `allowWrite`, `allowedDomains`, nó `deny` liosta. Sprioc mailíseach ar a dtugtar `rm -rf .` bheadh a stopadh ag an `rm -rf*` riail deny."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Mitigation:** `docker run*` and its synonyms are in `ask`, so the operator reviews them (subject to Assumption 5). The `deny` list blocks `sudo*`, so direct privilege escalation via `sudo` is unavailable."
msgstr "**Mitigation:** `docker run*` agus tá a comhchiallaigh i `ask`, mar sin athbhreithnithe an t-oibreoir orthu (faoi réir Tomhaltas 5). An `deny` bloic liosta `sudo*`, mar sin díreach escalation phribhléid trí `sudo` Níl sé ar fáil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Mitigation:** `sandbox.enabled: true` with `sandbox.failIfUnavailable: true` refuses to start when the backend is unavailable. `sandbox.allowUnsandboxedCommands: false` rejects the `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` tool parameter, so there is no per-call escape."
msgstr "**Mitigation:** `sandbox.enabled: true` le `sandbox.failIfUnavailable: true` diúltú chun tús a chur nuair nach bhfuil an cúlú ar fáil. `sandbox.allowUnsandboxedCommands: false` Diúltaíonn an `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` paraiméadar uirlis, mar sin níl aon éalú in aghaidh an-glaoch."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Mode-aware:** absent optional sources are skipped, not failed, so the same role works in both self-signed and Let's Encrypt setups."
msgstr "**Modh-aware:** foinsí roghnacha as láthair a skipped, ní theip, mar sin oibríonn an ról céanna i setups féin-sínithe agus A ligean ar Criptithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
