# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Multi-statement chains in shell invocations are FORBIDDEN. ⛔** You MUST NOT chain independent statements inside a single Bash tool call with **any** statement separator (`;`, literal newline, `&&`, `||`, `&` background operator, or subshell/brace groups around the same). The ban covers causally-dependent chains (`cd X && cmd`) just as much as optional ones, and applies to trailing `&` used to background a command (use the Bash tool's `run_in_background: true` parameter instead). Reason: identical to the loop rule. Split the work across **separate Bash tool calls** or use a single-command equivalent (`xargs`, `grep` with multiple args, a make target)."
msgstr "**Tá slabhraí il-ráiteas i sonraisc bhlaosc FORBIDDEN. ⛔** NÍ MÓR duit ráitis neamhspleácha slabhra taobh istigh glaoch uirlis Bash amháin le **bláthanna cumhra: aon cumhráin** deighilteoir ráiteas (`;`, líne nua litriúil, `&&`, `||`, `&` oibreoir cúlra, nó grúpaí subshell / brace ar fud an gcéanna). Clúdaíonn an toirmeasc slabhraí causally-spleách (`cd X && cmd`) ach oiread agus cinn roghnacha, agus baineann sé le trailing `&` a úsáidtear chun cúlra ordú (úsáid a bhaint as an uirlis Bash `run_in_background: true` paraiméadar ionad). Cúis: comhionann leis an riail lúb. Scoilt an obair ar fud **glaonna uirlis Bash ar leith** nó úsáid a bhaint as coibhéis aon-ordaithe (`xargs`, `grep` le args il, a dhéanamh sprioc)."

