# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Onion opt-in, not a port.** A category-keyed map of booleans naming which of the entity's own categories get a `HiddenServicePort` on the node onion. It declares no numbers: the port is read from `local` when the category is declared there and from `public` otherwise, matching what `container_ports` publishes. Collision detection ignores it."
msgstr "**Rogha oinniún, ní calafort.** A léarscáil catagóir-eochairithe de booleans ainmniú cé acu de na catagóirí an eintitis féin a fháil `HiddenServicePort` ar an nód oinniún. Dearbhaíonn sé aon uimhreacha: Tá an calafort a léamh ó `local` nuair a dhearbhaítear an chatagóir ann agus ó `public` ar shlí eile, meaitseáil cad `container_ports` foilsiú. neamhaird a bhrath collision é."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Onions, firewall and name resolution.** *svc-net-firewall* owns the packet filter as one nftables table per role. Tor carries mail to a .onion in both deploy modes, rejects forged sources on the guarded ports, and binds its dnsmasq listeners statically so a failed re-enumeration can no longer drop every one of them. The deployment declares its own address space once, the egress range moved out of the Docker pool, and the container resolver follows the live bridge instead of a guessed address. Every host-bound port requires an explicit onion decision. See [svc-net-firewall](roles/svc-net-firewall/README.md)."
msgstr "**Oinniúin, balla dóiteáin agus réiteach ainm.** *balla dóiteáin svc-líon* úinéireacht an scagaire paicéad mar tábla nftables amháin in aghaidh an ról. Déanann Tor ríomhphost chuig .onion sa dá modhanna imscaradh, Diúltaíonn foinsí brionnaithe ar na calafoirt cosanta, agus cuireann sé ceangal ar a éisteoirí dnsmasq statically ionas gur theip ar ath-áireamh a thuilleadh titim gach ceann acu. Dearbhaíonn an t-imscaradh a spás seoladh féin uair amháin, bhog an raon egress amach as an linn Docker, agus leanann an réiteoir coimeádán an droichead beo in ionad seoladh guessed. Éilíonn gach calafort ósta cinneadh oinniún follasach. Féach ar [balla dóiteáin svc-líon](roles/svc-net-firewall/README.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Only bridging addons add a service block.** A `<target>:` service block is added to the row role ONLY for addons that declare a `bridges:` dependency (per Decision 3), i.e. the in-repo cross-role integrations; a plain addon with no cross-role dependency adds no service block. Each bridging addon's `<target>:` block carries the standard dynamic `enabled`/`shared` flags with matching true/false `meta/variants.yml` coverage, and (for web-facing pairs) a co-deploy Playwright spec. Across the in-repo ✅ set this is a bounded, mechanical expansion scoped to the bridging integrations, accepted as part of Decision 15's full scope."
msgstr "**Ach cuiríní brící cuir bloc seirbhíse.** Amharc ar gach eolas `<target>:` Cuirtear bloc seirbhíse leis an ról as a chéile ARLY do bhreiseáin a dhearbhaíonn `bridges:` spleáchas (in aghaidh an Chinnidh 3), i.e. na lánpháirtithe tras-ról in-repo; addon plain gan aon spleáchas tras-ról Cuireann aon bloc seirbhíse. Gach breiseán bridging ar `<target>:` bloc ndéanann an caighdeán dinimiciúil `enabled`/ Baile`shared` bratacha le meaitseáil fíor / bréagach `meta/variants.yml` clúdach, agus (do péirí gréasáin-facing) a spec comh-imlonnú Playwright. Ar fud an in-repo ✅ a leagtar síos é seo faoi cheangal, leathnú meicniúil raon feidhme na lánpháirtithe brící, glactha mar chuid de Chinneadh 15's raon feidhme iomlán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Only the first start serves nothing.** The env is authoritative again on every start, so what `TOOL_SERVER_CONNECTIONS` carries is the state the container comes back with. Before any group exists that is a disabled entry, which is the safe direction: no access rather than every administrator. Once the provisioning task has created the group, its id lives in the token store, `vars/main.yml` reads it back on the next deploy, and the filter renders the entry enabled with its exact group grant. From then on a bare container restart restores a served, correctly scoped connection without a deploy."
msgstr "**Ach feidhmíonn an chéad tús rud ar bith.** Is é an env údarásach arís ar gach tús, mar sin cad `TOOL_SERVER_CONNECTIONS` Is é seo an stát a thagann an coimeádán ar ais le. Sula bhfuil aon ghrúpa go bhfuil iontráil faoi mhíchumas, a bhfuil an treo sábháilte: aon rochtain seachas gach riarthóir. Nuair a bheidh an tasc a sholáthar chruthaigh an grúpa, a shaol id sa siopa chomhartha, `vars/main.yml` léann sé ar ais ar an chéad imscaradh eile, agus déanann an scagaire an iontráil ar chumas lena deontas ghrúpa cruinn. Ón am sin ar atosú coimeádán lom restores a sheirbheáil, i gceart raon feidhme nasc gan imscaradh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Only the first start serves nothing.** The env is authoritative again on every start, so what ``TOOL_SERVER_CONNECTIONS`` carries is the state the container comes back with. Before any group exists that is a disabled entry, which is the safe direction: no access rather than every administrator. Once the provisioning task has created the group, its id lives in the token store, ``vars/main.yml`` reads it back on the next deploy, and the filter renders the entry enabled with its exact group grant. From then on a bare container restart restores a served, correctly scoped connection without a deploy."
msgstr "**Ach feidhmíonn an chéad tús rud ar bith.** Is é an env údarásach arís ar gach tús, mar sin cad ``TOOL_SERVER_CONNECTIONS`` Is é seo an stát a thagann an coimeádán ar ais le. Sula bhfuil aon ghrúpa go bhfuil iontráil faoi mhíchumas, a bhfuil an treo sábháilte: aon rochtain seachas gach riarthóir. Nuair a bheidh an tasc a sholáthar chruthaigh an grúpa, a shaol id sa siopa chomhartha, ``vars/main.yml`` léann sé ar ais ar an chéad imscaradh eile, agus déanann an scagaire an iontráil ar chumas lena deontas ghrúpa cruinn. Ón am sin ar atosú coimeádán lom restores a sheirbheáil, i gceart raon feidhme nasc gan imscaradh."

