msgid "**Token verified against the hub:** Every deploy asks the hub whether the stored token still authenticates and re-mints it when the hub rejects it, then fails the deploy if the fresh token is rejected too. A hub whose ``.storage/auth`` was recreated leaves a stored token pointing at a deleted refresh token, and clients would receive a 401 on every call."
msgstr "**Token fhíorú i gcoinne an mol:** Iarrann gach imscaradh an mol cibé an bhfuil an chomhartha stóráilte fíordheimhnithe fós agus ath-mints sé nuair a dhiúltaíonn an mol é, ansin theipeann ar an imscaradh má tá an chomhartha úr diúltaíodh freisin. mol a bhfuil ``.storage/auth`` a bhí recreated duilleoga a stóráil chomhartha dírithe ar chomhartha athnuachana a scriosadh, agus go mbeadh cliaint a fháil 401 ar gach glaoch."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Tokens & Secrets:** Unified token handling through a centralized token store, added user token defaults, and fully centralized secrets path definitions across roles."
msgstr "**comharthaí & Rúin:** Láimhseáil chomhartha aontaithe trí siopa comharthaíochta láraithe, teipeanna chomhartha úsáideora breise, agus sainmhínithe cosáin go hiomlán láraithe ar fud róil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Tor = compose sidecar**, `network_mode: host`, keys on a named volume, restored from the vaulted mint **before** Tor starts. Backup via `svc-bkp-container-2-local`."
msgstr "**Tor = a chumadh sidecar**, `network_mode: host`, eochracha ar toirt ainmnithe, ar ais ón mint boghtach **roimh** Tosaíonn Tor. Cúltaca via `svc-bkp-container-2-local`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Tor as a first-class deployment axis.** The new *svc-net-tor* role routes onion names through Tor via DNS instead of per-app proxies, offers a chutney flavor for private-net test deployments, and ties its dnsmasq listener to ownership rather than the deploy mode. Applications follow: server-side OIDC discovery and token exchange reach plaintext onion issuers through the SOCKS proxy (WordPress, Joomla, PeerTube, Mobilizon, EspoCRM, Nextcloud), session cookies drop the *Secure* flag where an onion cannot carry it (Taiga, Pixelfed, Joomla), and mail authenticates on the submission port the onion relay actually serves. The deploy matrix gained a tor axis with an onion marker plus enforced and exclusive modes, and lint now requires the onion in every variant. See the [svc-net-tor](roles/svc-net-tor/README.md) README."
msgstr "**Tor mar ais imscaradh den chéad scoth.** An nua *svc-net-tor* róil bealaí ainmneacha oinniún trí Tor via DNS in ionad proxies per-app, Cuireann blas chutney le haghaidh imscaradh tástála príobháideacha-líon, agus ceangail a éisteoir dnsmasq úinéireacht seachas an modh imscaradh. Iarratais a leanúint: freastalaí taobh OIDC fionnachtain agus malartú comharthaíochta a bhaint amach eisitheoirí oinniún plaintext tríd an seachfhreastalaí SOCKS (WordPress, Joomla, PeerTube, Mobilizon, EspoCRM, Nextcloud), fianáin seisiún titim an *Amharc ar gach eolas* bratach nach féidir oinniún a iompar (Taiga, Pixelfed, Joomla), agus fíordheimhnithe phost ar an gcalafort aighneacht feidhmíonn an Relay oinniún iarbhír. Fuair an maitrís imscaradh ais tor le marcóir oinniún móide modhanna forfheidhmiú agus eisiach, agus éilíonn lint anois an oinniún i ngach leagan. Féach an [svc-net-tor](roles/svc-net-tor/README.md) README."

