# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Your tools reachable from your assistants.** About twenty applications now speak MCP. Gitea, GitLab, Mattermost, Nextcloud, n8n, Baserow, Jenkins, Home Assistant, Moodle, Snipe-IT and WordPress serve their own endpoints; ten more get one through a locked-down sidecar. Open WebUI, Flowise and the agents discover what the deployment offers and register it automatically. Access is bounded rather than assumed: blocked paths are declared, every served path is gated, tools a provider calls mutating are withheld, reader and writer roles are separate, and each provider authenticates callers as its own service account. See [svc-ai-mcp-adapter](roles/svc-ai-mcp-adapter/README.md)."
msgstr "**Do uirlisí reachable ó do chúntóirí.** Maidir le fiche iarratas labhairt anois MCP. Gitea, GitLab, Mattermost, Nextcloud, n8n, Baserow, Jenkins, Home Assistant, Moodle, Snipe-IT agus WordPress freastal ar a gcuid endpoints féin; deich níos mó a fháil ar cheann trí sidecar Glas-síos. Oscail WebUI, Flowise agus na gníomhairí amach cad iad na tairiscintí imscaradh agus é a chlárú go huathoibríoch. Tá rochtain faoi cheangal seachas glacadh leis: Tá cosáin bac a dhearbhú, tá gach cosán a sheirbheáil gated, uirlisí glaonna soláthraí mutating a choinneáil siar, tá rólanna léitheoir agus scríbhneoir ar leith, agus fíoraíonn gach soláthraí callairí mar a chuntas seirbhíse féin. Féach ar [svc-ai-mcp-adapter](roles/svc-ai-mcp-adapter/README.md)."

