# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A handler MAY import stdlib, [parser.py](../parser.py), [runtime.py](../runtime.py), and any repo module whose own import closure is stdlib-only. The whole closure MUST import and run on the bare bootstrap python, before any dependency is installed. `utils.cache.files` and [yaml_bootstrap.py](../../yaml_bootstrap.py) qualify; `utils.cache.yaml` does not, because it imports PyYAML. Read SPOT files with `utils.cache.files.read_text` plus `utils.yaml_bootstrap.load_block` or a stdlib line parse. `load_block` accepts block mappings, block lists and string scalars only, and raises `BootstrapYamlError` on everything else, so a SPOT file read this way MUST stay inside that subset. [test_bare_bootstrap.py](../../../tests/integration/meta/env/test_bare_bootstrap.py) enforces this by running the generator with every non-stdlib import blocked."
msgstr "A láimhseálaí MAY allmhairiú stdlib, [parser.py](../parser.py), [runtime.py](../runtime.py), agus aon modúl repo a bhfuil a dúnadh allmhairiú féin stdlib-amháin. An dúnadh ar fad MUST allmhairiú agus a reáchtáil ar an python buataisí lom, sula bhfuil aon spleáchas suiteáilte. `utils.cache.files` agus [yaml_bootstrap.py](../../yaml_bootstrap.py) cáiliú; `utils.cache.yaml` nach bhfuil, mar gheall ar allmhairí sé PyYAML. Léigh comhaid le `utils.cache.files.read_text` móide móide `utils.yaml_bootstrap.load_block` nó parse líne stdlib. `load_block` Glacann mapaí bloc, liostaí bloc agus scalars teaghrán amháin, agus ardaíonn `BootstrapYamlError` ar gach rud eile, mar sin a léamh comhad a MUST ar an mbealach seo fanacht taobh istigh go fo-thacar. [test_bare_bootstrap.py](../../../tests/integration/meta/env/test_bare_bootstrap.py) forfheidhmiú seo ag rith an gineadóir le gach allmhairiú neamh-stdlib bac."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A handler MUST NOT import another handler. Cross-handler data flows through `eb.get(...)` / `eb.set(...)` only."
msgstr "A láimhseálaí NACH allmhairiú láimhseálaí eile. Sreabhann sonraí tras-láimhseora trí `eb.get(...)` / Baile `eb.set(...)` ach amháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A handler MUST NOT import from [writer.py](../writer.py) or [builder.py](../builder.py) at runtime. The `EnvBuilder` and `BuildContext` types MAY be referenced under `TYPE_CHECKING` for annotations only."
msgstr "A láimhseálaí NACH allmhairiú ó [writer.py](../writer.py) nó [builder.py](../builder.py) ag runtime. An bhfuil `EnvBuilder` agus `BuildContext` cineálacha MAY a tharchur faoi `TYPE_CHECKING` le haghaidh nótaí amháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A handler module name MUST match the lowercase of the variable it owns:"
msgstr "A ainm modúl láimhseálaí MUST mheaitseáil leis an níos ísle ar an athróg úinéireacht sé:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A handler that targets a conditional branch (GHA-only, NIX-only, ...) MUST self-check the relevant `ctx` flag and return early. The registry calls every handler unconditionally."
msgstr "Láimhseoir a dhíríonn ar bhrainse coinníollach (GHA-amháin, NIX-amháin,...) MUST féin-seiceáil an ábhartha `ctx` bratach agus filleadh go luath. Iarrann an clárlann gach láimhseálaí gan choinníoll."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A high-performance e-commerce stack optimized for conversion and analytics."
msgstr "A Stack ríomh-thráchtáil ard-fheidhmíocht optamaithe le haghaidh comhshó agus Analytics."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A higher-level orchestration wrapper, *sys-stk-front-proxy* ties together several lower-level roles:"
msgstr "Clúdaigh ceolfhoirne ardleibhéil, *sys-stk-front-proxy* ceangail le chéile roinnt róil níos ísle ar leibhéal:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A host that cannot serve it"
msgstr "óstach nach féidir a sheirbheáil air"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A host that cannot serve the assigned kind"
msgstr "óstach nach féidir freastal ar an chineál sannta"

msgid "A jeff that cannot be reached rejects the request. It is not routed around, because the caller named an alias precisely so it would not have to know which model answered, and substituting a different decider would make that answer mean something else."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A job URL narrows the download to that job's app; a bare run URL pulls every `role-runtimes-*` artifact in the run."
msgstr "A post URL Cúngú an íoslódáil chuig an post app; a lom reáchtáil URL pulls gach `role-runtimes-*` Déantán sa reáchtáil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A job counts as failed when it never finished, when the module reported ``failed``, or when a command returned a non-zero ``rc``. What distinguishes a real failure from an idempotent no-op differs per API and lives in different keys: modules put it in ``msg`` (cloudflare answers \"An identical record already exists\"), commands put it in ``stdout`` (``ollama pull`` prints \"up to date\" and exits non-zero). Both are searched, so a caller passes the tolerated phrasing and does not have to know which key carries it."
msgstr "Comhaireamh post mar theip nuair riamh críochnaithe é, nuair a thuairiscigh an modúl ``failed``, nó nuair a d'fhill ordú neamh-zero ``rc``. Cad idirdhealú teip fíor ó idempotent aon-op difriúil in aghaidh an API agus ina chónaí i eochracha éagsúla: modúil a chur i ``msg`` (taiseachas aeir: fliuch \"Tá taifead comhionann ann cheana féin\"), orduithe a chur i ``stdout`` (``ollama pull`` priontaí \"suas go dtí dáta\" agus bealaí amach neamh-zero). Tá an dá chuardach, mar sin a théann glaoiteoir an frásaí fhulaingt agus nach bhfuil a fhios a bhfuil eochair ndéanann sé."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A job title states its whole combination, which lets `--failed` replay the mode, onion state and distribution, and makes a plan table row comparable to the job it predicts."
msgstr "Deir teideal poist a meascán iomlán, a ligeann `--failed` replay an modh, stát oinniún agus dáileadh, agus a dhéanann sraith tábla plean inchomparáide leis an bpost tuartha sé."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A job's green conclusion is **NOT** evidence for a specific change. Before citing a run as proof, you MUST locate the line in that job's log where the change executed: a Playwright spec's `✓` (a leading `-` means the spec was skipped), the env var inside the container, or the command text of an `if:`-gated step. If the string is absent, report the run as silent on the change, not as supporting it."
msgstr "Tá post ar chonclúid glas **Déan teagmháil linn** fianaise ar athrú sonrach. Sula lua reáchtáil mar chruthúnas, MUST tú a aimsiú ar an líne sa phost sin logáil i gcás an t-athrú fhorghníomhú: spec Playwright ar `✓` (le rá `-` Ciallaíonn go raibh skipped an spec), an var env taobh istigh den choimeádán, nó an téacs ordú ar `if:`-gated céim. Má tá an teaghrán as láthair, tuairisc a thabhairt ar an reáchtáil mar adh ar an athrú, ní mar thacaíocht dó."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A key that some environment declares per run therefore MUST be written by a dedicated handler through `eb.set`. The exporting shell still wins for its own run, because [load.sh](../../scripts/meta/env/load.sh) preserves non-empty caller values when it sources `.env`; the file keeps the derived default. `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB` and `INFINITO_CACHE_STACK` are written this way. Note the consequence: for those keys `.env` and the running shell can legitimately disagree, and `.env` is not the authority."
msgstr "A eochair go Dearbhaíonn roinnt timpeallacht in aghaidh a reáchtáil dá bhrí sin MUST a scríobh ag láimhseálaí tiomnaithe trí `eb.set`. Bhuaigh an bhlaosc onnmhairithe fós lena reáchtáil féin, mar gheall ar [load.sh](../../scripts/meta/env/load.sh) caomhnaíonn luachanna glaoiteora neamh-empty nuair a fhoinsíonn sé `.env`; Coinníonn an comhad an réamhshocraithe díorthaithe. `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB` agus `INFINITO_CACHE_STACK` scríofa ar an mbealach seo. Tabhair faoi deara an iarmhairt: do na heochracha `.env` agus is féidir leis an bhlaosc ag rith easaontas dlisteanach, agus `.env` nach é an t-údarás."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A key's comment is the most recent contiguous block of `# ...` lines directly above the `KEY=...` line, joined with single spaces. Section headers (`# --- ... ---`) are treated as separators: they reset the pending comment so the next key starts fresh, instead of inheriting the heading line as its own documentation."
msgstr "Is é trácht eochair an bloc is déanaí contiguous de `# ...` línte díreach os cionn an `KEY=...` líne, ceangailte le spásanna aonair. Ceannairí na Roinne (`# --- ... ---`) cóireáilte mar deighilteoirí: athshocrú siad an trácht ar feitheamh mar sin tosaíonn an chéad eochair eile úr, in ionad oidhreacht an líne ceannteideal mar a doiciméadú féin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A label that silently stops resolving to arm64 turns the whole axis into a green lie."
msgstr "A lipéad a stopann go ciúin réiteach a lámh64 casadh an ais ar fad isteach i bréag glas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A lightweight, Docker-powered UI framework that offers Infinito.Nexus users a unified interface to access all their applications in one intuitive dashboard. 🚀"
msgstr "A lightweight, Docker-chumhachtaithe Chomhéadain creat a thairgeann Infinito.Nexus úsáideoirí comhéadan aontaithe chun rochtain a fháil ar gach a n-iarratas i Painéal na nIonstraimí iomasach amháin. 🚀"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A list of external links relevant to the software or the deployment. Link text MUST be a descriptive label or the domain name. Never use the full URL."
msgstr "Liosta de na naisc sheachtracha a bhaineann leis na bogearraí nó leis an imscaradh. Link téacs MUST bheith ina lipéad tuairisciúil nó an t-ainm fearainn. Ná bain úsáid as an URL iomlán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A literal ``shared: false`` (not a Jinja expression) is the role author pinning an engine the central provider cannot serve. Honouring it is only safe on a manager-pinned role, where the volume stays node-local and the sidecar carries the matching placement constraint."
msgstr "A litriúil ``shared: false`` (Ní léiriú Jinja) Is é an t-údar ról pinning inneall nach féidir leis an soláthraí lárnach freastal. Onórach go bhfuil sé ach sábháilte ar ról bainisteoir-bioráin, i gcás ina bhfanann an toirt nód-áitiúil agus déanann an sidecar an srian socrúcháin meaitseáil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A local deploy is failing on the host"
msgstr "Tá imscaradh áitiúil ag teip ar an óstach"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A location not starting with ``/`` is a remote ``[user@]host:/path``."
msgstr "suíomh nach bhfuil ag tosú le ``/`` Is iargúlta ``[user@]host:/path``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A long-running worker (own image, gated on both endpoints present) that:"
msgstr "A oibrí fada ag rith (íomhá féin, gated ar an dá endpoints láthair) sin:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A malformed filter expression."
msgstr "A léiriú scagaire malformed."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A manager-pinned role keeps its volumes node-local (``swarm_nfs_backed``) and its DB sidecar carries the matching placement constraint, so a literal ``shared: false`` there is honoured instead of overridden — Magento hard-fails ``setup:install`` on the central MariaDB major."
msgstr "Coinníonn ról bainisteoir-bioráin a méideanna nód-áitiúil (``swarm_nfs_backed``) agus déanann a sidecar DB an srian socrúcháin meaitseáil, mar sin litriúil ``shared: false`` tá onóir in ionad ró-mharcaíochta - Magento crua-fails ``setup:install`` ar an MariaDB lárnach mór."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A mapping deep-merges, so naming one key changes that key and nothing else. ``null`` empties the topic, which is the only way to say \"bring nothing\": merged, an empty mapping is a no-op and would leave exactly the services the round was trying to shed."
msgstr "A mapáil domhain-cumasc, mar sin ainmniú athruithe eochair amháin go eochair agus aon rud eile. ``null`` empties an ábhar, a bhfuil an t-aon bhealach a rá \"rud ar bith a thabhairt\": chumasc, Is mapáil folamh aon-uair agus bheadh a fhágáil go díreach na seirbhísí a bhí an bhabhta ag iarraidh a chaillfidh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A mapping of docker volume names and database names to ``postgres`` or ``mariadb``. Both volume spellings are emitted per application, because which one a host used depends on ``shared``, which is inventory-dependent and therefore unknowable from a checkout - and both spellings resolve to the same engine anyway."
msgstr "A mapáil ainmneacha toirt docker agus ainmneacha bunachar sonraí a ``postgres`` nó ``mariadb``. Tá an dá litriú toirte astaítear in aghaidh an iarratais, mar gheall ar a bhfuil ceann amháin a úsáidtear ag brath ar ``shared``, atá ag brath ar fhardal agus dá bhrí sin unknowable ó checkout - agus an dá litriú réiteach leis an inneall céanna ar aon nós."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A marker value MUST be a non-empty string. If the marker key is present but the value is of the wrong YAML type, empty, or whitespace- only, the role's typing is broken: :func:`get_role_types` raises :class:`RoleTypeError` so the misconfiguration surfaces at the first call instead of silently degrading to a different type."
msgstr "A luach marcóir MUST a bheith ina teaghrán neamh-empty. Má tá an eochair marcóir i láthair ach tá an luach ar an gcineál YAML mícheart, folamh, nó bán- amháin, tá clóscríobh an ról briste: :func:`get_role_types` ardaitheoirí :class:`RoleTypeError` mar sin na dromchlaí misconfiguration ag an gcéad glaoch in ionad go ciúin táireach le cineál éagsúla."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A matching `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` variable defined anywhere in Ansible variable scope (inventory, group vars, host vars)."
msgstr "A meaitseáil `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` athróg sainithe in áit ar bith i raon feidhme athróg Ansible (fardal, vars grúpa, vars óstach)."

