msgid "An app that needs an extra mapper MUST add it through a per-client scope. See [nextcloud.json.j2](../../../../roles/web-app-keycloak/templates/import/scopes/nextcloud.json.j2) for the precedent: a dedicated scope holds the Nextcloud-specific UID and quota mappers and is attached only to the Nextcloud client."
msgstr "Aip go bhfuil gá MUST mapper breise a chur leis trí raon feidhme per-client. Féach ar [nextcloud.json.j2](../../../../roles/web-app-keycloak/templates/import/scopes/nextcloud.json.j2) don fhasach: tá raon feidhme tiomnaithe an UID Nextcloud-shonrach agus léarscáileoirí cuóta agus tá sé ceangailte ach leis an gcliant Nextcloud."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An application SHOULD opt in to `axis: domain` only when its authorisation model is genuinely per-tenant and the tenant axis is the canonical domain. Typical consumer: WordPress Multisite. Applications whose authorisation is one global user set (Nextcloud, Gitea, Keycloak itself) MUST keep `axis: none`."
msgstr "iarratas SHOULD roghnú i `axis: domain` ach amháin nuair atá a shamhail údaraithe fíor in aghaidh an tionónta agus gurb é ais an tionónta an fearainn Canonical. tomhaltóir tipiciúil: WordPress Multisite. Iarratais a bhfuil a n-údarú socraithe úsáideoir domhanda amháin (Nextcloud, Gitea, Keycloak féin) MUST choinneáil `axis: none`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An application id is expanded to the service key(s) that role provides; every other token is kept verbatim. Order-preserving, de-duplicated. Used wherever the operator supplies service references (``disable``, include/prune closures) so both spellings resolve identically."
msgstr "Tá iarratas id leathnú chuig an eochair seirbhíse(s s) go soláthraíonn an ról sin; coimeádtar briathra ar gach dearbhán eile. Ordú-preserving, de-duplicated. Úsáidte cibé áit a sholáthraíonn an t-oibreoir tagairtí seirbhíse (``disable``, lena n-áirítear/clúdaigh phrune) mar sin an dá litriú réiteach mar an gcéanna."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An application that authenticates its own API with a bearer MUST expose that path through the SSO ACL whitelist. The proxy cannot validate an application bearer, so a fully gated vhost answers an API call with an identity-provider redirect, which a client following redirects reads as a successful 200."
msgstr "Iarratas a fhíoraíonn a API féin le MUST settings nochtadh go cosán tríd an Liosta bán SSO ACL. Ní féidir leis an seachfhreastalaí a bhailíochtú ar iompróir iarratais, mar sin freagraí vhost go hiomlán gated glao API le haitheantas-sholáthar atreorú, a bhfuil cliant tar éis atreoruithe léann mar rathúil 200."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An application whose registration rejects the shell-safe alphabet states that in its own meta/users.yml rather than carrying a second credential beside the account it already owns."
msgstr "Maidir le hiarratas a ndiúltaíonn a chlárú an aibítir sliogáin-sábháilte a deir go bhfuil ina chuid féin meta/users.yml seachas a iompar dara credential in aice leis an gcuntas úinéireacht sé cheana féin."

