# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Databases travel as sql dumps, not as a file tree (`--dump-only-sql`), so they have their own recover leg: `recover database <generation>`, which `recover full` plans right after the volume steps. That leg is the one part of the chain that cannot run on a bare host: a dump is replayed through `docker exec`, so the database service has to be deployed and up, with its consumers stopped. The engine of a dump is resolved from the consuming role's `meta/services.yml` service key in `utils/recovery/databases.py` — the same value the backup seed used — and a replay refuses to run while a consumer of that database is up, because `--empty` pre-cleans the schema and a booting consumer would recreate it underneath the replay."
msgstr "Bunachair Taisteal mar dumpaí sql, ní mar chrann comhad (`--dump-only-sql`), mar sin tá siad a n-cos ghnóthú féin: `recover database <generation>`, a, `recover full` pleananna ceart tar éis na céimeanna toirt. Is é an cos sin an chuid amháin den slabhra nach féidir a reáchtáil ar óstach lom: tá dumpáil replayed trí `docker exec`, mar sin ní mór an tseirbhís bunachar sonraí a úsáid agus a chur suas, lena tomhaltóirí stop. Réitítear inneall dumpála ón ról Tógann `meta/services.yml` eochair seirbhíse i `utils/recovery/databases.py` — an luach céanna ar an síol cúltaca a úsáidtear — agus a dhiúltóidh replay a reáchtáil le linn do thomhaltóir den bhunachar sonraí sin a bheith suas, mar gheall ar `--empty` réamh-ghlanadh an scéimre agus bheadh tomhaltóir tosaithe recreate sé thíos an replay."

