# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each PR-opening job in [cron-update.yml](../../../../../.github/workflows/cron-update.yml) runs an `actions/create-github-app-token@v2` step gated on `steps.diff.outputs.changed == 'true'`, then forwards the minted token as `GH_TOKEN` and the resolved `APP_SLUG` to the subsequent PR step. The job's `permissions:` block keeps the workflow-provided `GITHUB_TOKEN` read-only; write access is provided exclusively by the App token, scoped to the App's repository permissions."
msgstr "Gach post PR-oscailte i [cron-update.yml](../../../../../.github/workflows/cron-update.yml) Ritheann an `actions/create-github-app-token@v2` céim gated ar `steps.diff.outputs.changed == 'true'`, ansin ar aghaidh leis an dearbhán minted mar `GH_TOKEN` agus an réiteach `APP_SLUG` leis an chéim PR ina dhiaidh sin. An post ar `permissions:` coimeádann bloc an sreabhadh oibre-ar fáil `GITHUB_TOKEN` léamh-amháin; Tá scríobh rochtain ar fáil go heisiach ag an Aip chomhartha, faoi raon feidhme na ceadanna stór App."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each Raspberry Pi joins the swarm as an agent node labelled `kata-capable` with the isolating runtime as its daemon-wide default (Decision #3, applied per node). Flowise and the gateway run on a manager node. Swarm distributes agent replicas across the Pis; adding a Pi adds agent capacity with no code change. The Pis do **not** run large models locally: agents speak only the gateway `/v1`, which routes light work to a small local `svc-ai-ollama` and heavy work to a GPU or external backend. All node-run images MUST be `arm64`."
msgstr "Gach Raspberry Pi théann an Swarm mar nód gníomhaire lipéadaithe `kata-capable` leis an runtime isolating mar a réamhshocraithe daemon-leathan (Cinneadh #3, i bhfeidhm in aghaidh nód). Flowise agus reáchtáil an geata ar nód bainisteoir. Swarm Dáileann macasamhail gníomhaire ar fud an Pis; cur Pi Cuireann cumas gníomhaire gan aon athrú cód. An Pis dhéanamh **bláthanna cumhra: aon cumhráin** reáchtáil samhlacha mór go háitiúil: gníomhairí labhairt ach an geata `/v1`, a bealaí obair éadrom go dtí áitiúil beag `svc-ai-ollama` agus obair throm le Leas GPU nó seachtrach. Gach íomhánna node-reáchtáil MUST a `arm64`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each Recoverer parses and validates its own colon-encoded ``source`` and builds the role's ``files/python/recover.py`` invocation. Colon segments are classified by shape: an ABSOLUTE path is the restore destination (replacing a --target flag); for device a RELATIVE segment is the on-device snapshot subpath and an all-digit ``YYYYMMDDHHMMSS`` segment is the generation to restore. No colon means the derived standard-layout target and the newest generation. The uniform console command ``<type> <source> <target>`` dispatches to one Recoverer via :data:`RECOVERERS`."
msgstr "Gach parses Recoverer agus bailíochtaíonn a colon-ionchódaithe féin ``source`` agus a thógann an ról ``files/python/recover.py`` sonrascadh. Tá codanna Colon rangaithe de réir cruth: Is cosán ABSOLUTE an ceann scríbe ar ais (bratach --target a chur in ionad); le haghaidh gléas is deighleog GAOLMHAch an fo-bhealach ar-gléas agus uile-digit ``YYYYMMDDHHMMSS`` Is deighleog an ghlúin a chur ar ais. Ciallaíonn aon colon an díorthaithe caighdeánach-leagan amach sprioc agus an ghlúin nua. An t-ordú consól aonfhoirmeach ``<type> <source> <target>`` seolta chuig Earcaitheoir amháin trí :data:`RECOVERERS`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each `tasks/02_manager_ops/06_plugin/<step>.yml` file owns exactly one OCC stage and one decision about whether to continue."
msgstr "Gach ceann `tasks/02_manager_ops/06_plugin/<step>.yml` úinéireacht comhad go díreach céim OCC amháin agus cinneadh amháin faoi cibé acu a leanúint."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Each `test()` runs in its own isolated browser context. Specs MUST NOT share session state between tests. Running biber and administrator as two separate `test()` blocks already gives that isolation by default. When a single scenario needs more than one identity at once (peer-to-peer messaging, RBAC promotion observed by the admin, …), it MUST open a fresh `browser.newContext({ ignoreHTTPSErrors: true })` per identity and close them in `finally`."
msgstr "Gach ceann `test()` Ritheann ina chomhthéacs bhrabhsálaí iargúlta féin. Specs MUST NACH stát seisiún roinnt idir tástálacha. biber Rith agus riarthóir mar dhá ar leith `test()` bloic Tugann cheana féin go leithlisiú de réir réamhshocraithe. Nuair is gá cás amháin níos mó ná aitheantas amháin ag an am céanna (teachtaireachtaí piaraí le piaraí, cur chun cinn RBAC faoi deara ag an admin,...), MUST sé oscailt úr `browser.newContext({ ignoreHTTPSErrors: true })` in aghaidh aitheantais agus iad a dhúnadh i `finally`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each additional MCP server role SHOULD land in a focused commit or PR when it can be validated independently."
msgstr "Gach ról breise freastalaí MCP talamh SHOULD i tiomantas dírithe nó PR nuair is féidir é a bhailíochtú go neamhspleách."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each additional role SHOULD land in a focused commit or PR when it can be validated independently."
msgstr "Gach ról breise talamh SHOULD i tiomantas dírithe nó PR nuair is féidir é a bhailíochtú go neamhspleách."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each addon lives in its own file `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml`: **the file root IS the addon spec, there is NO wrapping `<addon_id>:` key, and the filename stem supplies the addon id.** All files in the directory are collected into `applications.<role_id>.addons`, keyed by `<addon_id>`. The materialised path is `applications.<role_id>.addons.<addon_id>`, read via `lookup('config', application_id, 'addons.<addon_id>')`."
msgstr "Gach addon saol ina comhad féin `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml`: **IS an fhréamh comhad an spec addon, tá NÍL timfhilleadh `<addon_id>:` eochair, agus soláthraíonn an ainm comhaid an id addon.** Gach comhad san eolaire a bhailiú isteach `applications.<role_id>.addons`, keyed by `<addon_id>`. Is é an cosán ábhartha `applications.<role_id>.addons.<addon_id>`, léamh trí `lookup('config', application_id, 'addons.<addon_id>')`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each addon spec MUST guard on the addon being enabled via `skipUnlessAddonEnabled('<addon_id>')`, backed by the `ADDON_<ID>_ENABLED` flags rendered into `templates/playwright.env.j2`, and skip cleanly when it is not."
msgstr "Gach addon garda MUST spec ar an addon á chumasú trí `skipUnlessAddonEnabled('<addon_id>')`, tacaíocht ag an `ADDON_<ID>_ENABLED` bratacha a rinneadh `templates/playwright.env.j2`, agus skip go glan nuair nach bhfuil sé."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each agent now claims its own key in `meta/users.yml` and declares nothing about the password there, because provisioning stores one for every declared account. An earlier attempt pinned the password to a separate `identity_password` credential in `meta/secrets.yml`; that was the wrong home for it. An account password belongs to the account, and the provisioning code says so directly: a role whose registration rejects the shell-safe alphabet states that in its own `meta/users.yml` rather than carrying a second credential beside the account it already owns. The `{{ 42 | strong_password }}` that re-renders per read is the fallback for an inventory nobody provisioned, not the value a deployed account holds."
msgstr "Éilíonn gach gníomhaire a eochair féin anois `meta/users.yml` agus dearbhaíonn aon rud mar gheall ar an focal faire ann, mar gheall ar siopaí a chur ar fáil amháin le haghaidh gach cuntas dearbhaithe. An iarracht níos luaithe pinned an focal faire ar leith `identity_password` credential in `meta/secrets.yml`; ba é sin an teach mícheart dó. Baineann pasfhocal cuntas leis an gcuntas, agus deir an cód soláthair mar sin go díreach: deir ról a ndiúltaíonn a chlárú an aibítir bhlaosc-sábháilte féin `meta/users.yml` seachas a iompar dara credential in aice leis an gcuntas úinéireacht sé cheana féin. An bhfuil `{{ 42 | strong_password }}` go bhfuil ath-renders in aghaidh an léamh an t-aiseolas le haghaidh fardal nobody ar fáil, nach bhfuil an luach cuntas imscaradh."

