# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each invocation MUST be reviewed individually for billing + data-flow impact."
msgstr "Déanfar gach MUST sonraisc a athbhreithniú ina n-aonar le haghaidh billeála + tionchar sreabhadh sonraí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each invocation MUST be reviewed to confirm the target workflow and inputs."
msgstr "Déanfar athbhreithniú ar gach moladh chun an sprioc-sreabhadh oibre agus ionchuir a dheimhniú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each invocation carries a unique risk profile depending on flags. `docker run` can mount host paths (`-v /:/host`), expose privileged capabilities (`--privileged`, `--cap-add`), bypass the sandbox via the Docker daemon's root privileges, and pull arbitrary images from any reachable registry. Middle-wildcard false positives (e.g. a container name containing \" run\") land here as harmless extra prompts, an acceptable trade-off against per-synonym enumeration."
msgstr "Déanann gach sonrasc próifíl riosca uathúil ag brath ar bhratacha. `docker run` Is féidir mount cosáin óstach (`-v /:/host`), nochtadh cumais phribhléid (`--privileged`, `--cap-add`), seachadann an bosca gainimh trí phribhléidí fréamhacha Docker daemon, agus íomhánna treallacha a tharraingt ó aon chlárlann insroichte. Deimhneachtaí bréagacha an-chárta (e.g. ainm coimeádáin ina bhfuil \" reáchtáil\") talamh anseo mar leideanna breise harmless, trádáil-uaire inghlactha in aghaidh an-comhchiallaithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each key is preceded by its documentation comment when the builder carries one, mirroring the convention used in `default.env`."
msgstr "Tá gach eochair roimh a comment doiciméadú nuair a dhéanann an tógálaí amháin, ag léiriú an choinbhinsiún a úsáidtear i `default.env`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each list entry MUST be either:"
msgstr "Gach taifead liosta MUST a bheith:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each module in this directory owns exactly one lint tool and exposes a single `ensure()` function. The CLI in [__main__.py](__main__.py) groups these ensure calls and applies the stamp-based skip for the default \"all\" invocation."
msgstr "Gach modúl sa eolaire úinéireacht go díreach uirlis lint amháin agus nochtann amháin `ensure()` feidhm. An CLI i [Tuilleadh eolais](__main__.py) grúpaí na glaonna a chinntiú agus a chur i bhfeidhm ar an scipe stamp-bhunaithe don réamhshocraithe \"all\" sonrascadh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each module in this directory owns exactly one variable, or one tightly-coupled group resolved by a single helper call. The orchestrator in [builder.py](../builder.py) iterates the registry in [__init__.py](__init__.py) and calls each handler's `apply(eb, ctx)` in order."
msgstr "Tá gach modúl san eolaire seo díreach athróg amháin, nó grúpa amháin go daingean-cúpláilte réiteach ag glaoch cúntóir amháin. An ceoltóir i [builder.py](../builder.py) iterates an chlár i [Tuilleadh eolais](__init__.py) agus glaonna gach láimhseálaí ar `apply(eb, ctx)` in ord."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each module owns a private `_reset()` that clears its own cache dicts. The package-level `utils.cache._reset_cache_for_tests()` orchestrates all six (`base`, `applications`, `users`, `domains`, `yaml`, `files`) plus the shared fingerprint memo. Unit tests that exercise the cached paths MUST call it in `setUp` to guarantee clean state across test cases."
msgstr "Gach modúl úinéireacht príobháideach `_reset()` go soiléiríonn a dheachtanna taisce féin. An leibhéal pacáiste `utils.cache._reset_cache_for_tests()` orchestrates gach sé (`base`, `applications`, `users`, `domains`, `yaml`, `files`) móide an meamram méarloirg roinnte. tástálacha Aonad a fheidhmiú na cosáin i dtaisce MUST glaoch air i `setUp` stát glan a ráthú i gcásanna tástála."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each module, class, or function MUST have exactly one responsibility so that changes to one concern do not ripple into unrelated code."
msgstr "Tá gach modúl, rang, nó feidhm MUST go díreach freagracht amháin ionas nach athruithe ar imní amháin ripple isteach cód neamhghaolmhar."

msgid "Each one undoes a shape a translator produced and the source did not ask for. They read the source only to decide whether something was lost, never to change what the translation says."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each operator workflow has a skill that routes the agent to its authoritative procedure and drives it — clarifying open requirements first, then acting autonomously to completion. Most are `i8-` skills specific to this repository; a few (such as `triage`) are portable skills shared across projects."
msgstr "Tá scil ag gach sreabhadh oibre oibreoir a chuireann an gníomhaire ar a nós imeachta údarásach agus a thiomáineann é - soiléiriú a dhéanamh ar riachtanais oscailte ar dtús, ag gníomhú go neamhspleách chun críche. An chuid is mó `i8-` scileanna a bhaineann go sonrach leis an stór seo; cúpla (den sórt sin `triage`) Tá scileanna iniompartha roinnte ar fud na dtionscadal."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each override is gated on the resource it needs being present, not on the instance slot: an override whose `:?` guard is unsatisfied would abort the stack outright, so a checkout that was never handed a shared git dir or cache network simply does not layer that file in."
msgstr "Tá gach override gated ar an acmhainn is gá é a bheith i láthair, ní ar an sliotán mar shampla: a shárú a `:?` Tá garda míshásta bheadh abort an ceart Stack, mar sin a checkout a bhí riamh láimh dir git roinnte nó líonra taisce nach bhfuil ach ciseal go comhad i."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each persona scenario MUST be named `<persona>: <flow>`, where `<persona>` is the literal token `guest`, `biber`, or `administrator` and `<flow>` is a concise step description (e.g. `dashboard → app → logout`). The persona token MUST appear at the very start of the test title so the Playwright reporter groups runs by persona without further parsing."
msgstr "Gach cás persona MUST a ainmniú `<persona>: <flow>`, i gcás `<persona>` Is é an comhartha litriúil `guest`, `biber`, nó `administrator` agus `<flow>` Is cur síos céim achomair (e.g. `dashboard → app → logout`). An MUST persona le feiceáil ag tús an-an teideal tástála mar sin ritheann na grúpaí tuairisceoir Playwright ag persona gan a thuilleadh parsáil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each recover mirrors a snapshot with `rsync -a --delete` and first runs the role's backup unit as a rollback point. `--no-safety-backup` skips that (only when the target holds nothing worth saving: fresh host / empty / disposable). `--preview` prints the exact commands without running them."
msgstr "Gach scátháin a ghnóthú léargas le `rsync -a --delete` agus ar dtús ritheann an ról aonad cúltaca mar phointe rollback. `--no-safety-backup` scipeanna go (ach amháin nuair a bhíonn an sprioc aon rud fiú a shábháil: óstach úr / folamh / indiúscartha). `--preview` priontaí na horduithe cruinn gan iad a reáchtáil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each role group must contain the default host."
msgstr "Ní mór do gach grúpa ról an óstach réamhshocraithe a bheith ann."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each role in that closure is then narrowed to the variants that actually reach a seed: variant `i` of a role is kept only when round `i`'s closure — walked on the same variant-merged services maps [the matrix planner](../../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/inventory/planner.py) builds its rounds from, and therefore variant-aware at every generation of the chain — contains one of the seeds. A role whose variants do not all qualify enters the whitelist as a `role#0,2` selection token, so an image bump in a provider no longer redeploys the variants that switch that provider off. This applies to every auto-derived whitelist — the weekly update PRs, Dependabot, and any other diff-driven run — because they all resolve through this one path."
msgstr "Tá gach ról sa dúnadh caol ansin leis na leaganacha a bhaint amach i ndáiríre síol: malairt `i` de ról a choimeád ach amháin nuair bhabhta `i`'s dúnadh — shiúil ar na léarscáileanna seirbhísí athraitheacha céanna le chéile [an pleanálaí maitrís](../../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/inventory/planner.py) Tógann sé a babhtaí ó, agus dá bhrí sin tá malairt-earraí ag gach glúin den slabhra - tá ceann de na síolta. Téann ról nach gcáilíonn a leaganacha go léir isteach sa liosta bán mar `role#0,2` roghnú chomhartha, mar sin bump íomhá i soláthraí a thuilleadh redeploys na leaganacha a athrú go soláthraí as. Baineann sé seo le gach whitelist auto-derived - an PRs cothrom le dáta seachtainiúil, dependabot, agus aon reáchtáil diff-tiomáinte eile - toisc go bhfuil siad go léir a réiteach tríd an cosán amháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each row is a migration target. The \"Bridges\" column is the cross-role dependency this requirement makes explicit. \"Today's location\" is where the declaration lives before migration."
msgstr "Is sprioc imirce é gach sraith. An bhfuil \"Bridges\" Is colún an spleáchas tras-ról a dhéanann an ceanglas seo follasach. \"Suíomh an lae inniu\" i gcás ina bhfuil cónaí ar an dearbhú roimh an imirce."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each row recomputes the role's embedded (forward) service deps from that variant's merged ``services`` map, so toggling a sidecar off in a variant drops it from the variant's ``embeds``/``weight``. The consumer (reverse) side is the variant-independent role-level graph: who else in the catalog embeds this role does not change with the role's own variant selection."
msgstr "Gach as a chéile recomputes an ról leabaithe (Toir agus Crainn) deps seirbhíse ón leagan ar chumasc ``services`` léarscáil, ionas go mbeidh tú ag dul i ngleic le taobhcharr i malairt titeann sé as an leagan ``embeds``/ Baile``weight``. An tomhaltóir (athrú) Is é an taobh an graf ar leibhéal róil athraitheach-spleách: cé eile sa chatalóg leabú nach bhfuil an ról seo a athrú le roghnú leagan an róil féin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each runner instance is provisioned as an ephemeral container using **DooD** (Docker-out-of-Docker — it mounts the host `docker.sock`). Isolation is keyed on the instance number, so parallel jobs never collide:"
msgstr "Tá gach cás rádala ar fáil mar coimeádán ephemeral ag baint úsáide as **Déan teagmháil linn** (Docker-amach-de-Docker - mounts sé an ósta `docker.sock`). Isolation keyed ar an uimhir shampla, mar sin ní poist comhthreomhar collide:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each scenario MUST live in its own `test-*.js` module (e.g. `test-login-oidc.js`, `test-seaweedfs.js`). `playwright.spec.js` is the thin aggregator that `require()`s every scenario module, keeping each case atomic and individually inspectable. The runner globs every `*.js`, so no extra wiring is needed."
msgstr "Gach cás MUST beo ina féin `test-*.js` modúlach (e.g. `test-login-oidc.js`, `test-seaweedfs.js`). `playwright.spec.js` Is é an aggregator tanaí go `require()`s gach modúl cás, a choinneáil ar gach cás adamhach agus ina n-aonar ininiúchta. An dara háit globs gach `*.js`, mar sin níl aon sreangú breise ag teastáil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Each script MUST be entered via `cli.administration.deploy.development exec --env KEY=VAL` (or an equivalent `docker exec -e …` invocation) so the host wrapper can inject the required environment. Each script MUST assert its required env-vars at the top with `: \"${VAR:?}\"` so missing context surfaces immediately. Each script MUST `cd \"${INFINITO_SRC_DIR}\"` before running anything so relative paths resolve against the bind-mounted repo. Each script SHOULD run `./scripts/docker/entry.sh true` for entry bootstrap before the deploy step."
msgstr "Gach MUST script a chur isteach trí `cli.administration.deploy.development exec --env KEY=VAL` (nó coibhéis `docker exec -e …` invocation) mar sin is féidir leis an fillteán óstach instealladh an timpeallacht is gá. Gach script MUST dhearbhú a env-vars ag teastáil ag an mbarr le `: \"${VAR:?}\"` mar sin dromchlaí comhthéacs ar iarraidh láithreach. Gach MUST script `cd \"${INFINITO_SRC_DIR}\"` sula rith aon rud mar sin cosáin coibhneasta réiteach i gcoinne an repo ceangal-mounted. Gach script SHOULD reáchtáil `./scripts/docker/entry.sh true` le haghaidh buataisí iontrála roimh an chéim imscaradh."

msgid "Each service entry lives in the provider role's own `meta/services.yml`, where the file root IS the services map keyed by `<entity_name>` (no `compose:` and no `services:` wrapper). See [layout.md](layout.md) for the full per-role meta layout."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each service in host vars MAY carry a `mirror_policy` field that controls how the override is applied:"
msgstr "Déanann gach seirbhís i vars óstach MAY `mirror_policy` réimse a rialaíonn conas a chuirtear an ród i bhfeidhm:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each service-account integration MUST provision a dedicated non-login identity with only the upstream permissions needed by the declared tool allowlist. The lookup MUST resolve `mcp.credential.owner`, `source`, and `key`; it MUST NOT hard-code `administrator`. Deployment MUST fail if the resolved principal is missing, empty, more privileged than `auth_subject` declares, or shared with an unrelated provider."
msgstr "Gach comhtháthú seirbhís-cuntas MUST a chur ar fáil aitheantas neamh-login tiomnaithe leis na ceadanna suas le sruth ag teastáil ag an deisliosta uirlis dearbhaithe. An lookup MUST réiteach `mcp.credential.owner`, `source`, agus `key`; MUST sé NACH crua-cód `administrator`. Imscaradh MUST theipeann má tá an príomhoide réiteach ar iarraidh, folamh, níos phribhléidí ná `auth_subject` Dearbhaíonn, nó a roinnt le soláthraí neamhghaolmhar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each settings change MUST be reviewed before it lands. Approval here is equivalent in blast radius to approving a `deny`-rule edit: the next tool call may run under new rules. Operators SHOULD diff the proposed change against the live file before approving and SHOULD decline any change that widens `allowWrite`, removes a `deny` entry, adds a broad `allow` wildcard, or registers a hook command."
msgstr "Gach suímh athrú MÓR a athbhreithniú sula tailte sé. Ceadú anseo comhionann i ga soinneáin a cheadú `deny`-rule in eagar: Is féidir leis an chéad glaoch uirlis reáchtáil faoi rialacha nua. Oibreoirí SHOULD diff an t-athrú atá beartaithe i gcoinne an comhad beo sula gceadaíonn agus SHOULD meath aon athrú a leathnú `allowWrite`, cuireann sé `deny` iontráil, Cuireann leathan `allow` wildcard, nó cláraíonn ceannas Hook."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each shim MUST resolve the repository root relative to its own location so it can run from any working directory, MUST forward arguments to the underlying CLI so `--dry-run` and similar flags keep working from the shell, and MUST exit non-zero on CLI failure so the workflow surfaces the error."
msgstr "Gach MUST shim réiteach an fhréamh stór i gcoibhneas lena suíomh féin ionas gur féidir é a reáchtáil ó aon eolaire oibre, MUST argóintí ar aghaidh chuig an CLI bunúsacha mar sin `--dry-run` agus bratacha den chineál céanna a choinneáil ag obair ón bhlaosc, agus MUST scoir neamh-zero ar teip CLI mar sin dromchlaí an sreabhadh oibre an earráid."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each stage entry below lists the criteria a role MUST satisfy to claim that stage. Promotion to the next stage is a deliberate human decision, not an automated transition. A role MAY only be tagged with a stage whose criteria are fully met; any drift MUST be corrected by either fixing the role or demoting the lifecycle key to the highest stage whose criteria still hold."
msgstr "Liostaíonn gach iontráil céim thíos na critéir a chomhlíonann MUST ról chun an chéim sin a éileamh. Is cinneadh daonna d'aon ghnó é cur chun cinn go dtí an chéad chéim eile, ní aistriú uathoibrithe é. Ról MAY a clib ach amháin le céim a bhfuil a critéir comhlíonta go hiomlán; aon MUST sruth a cheartú trí shocrú ar an ról nó a thaispeáint ar an eochair saolré go dtí an chéim is airde a bhfuil a critéir fós i seilbh."

