# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Imported by the lint bootstrap, which runs on a bare interpreter before any dependency is installed, so this module stays on the standard library. It also stays inside its own package: the Dockerfile copies it into the image beside ``utils/__init__.py`` and ``utils/install/__init__.py`` and nothing else, so importing any other ``utils`` submodule raises ``ModuleNotFoundError`` in the layer that runs it. The requirements files it reads are this repository's own and hold one shape: a ``collections:`` list of ``- name:`` entries with an optional ``version:``. A line that does not match that shape leaves the entry unpinned, which the caller treats as unsatisfied and installs."
msgstr "Iompórtáil ag an boottrap lint, a ritheann ar ateangaire lom sula bhfuil aon spleáchas suiteáilte, mar sin fanann an modúl ar an leabharlann caighdeánach. Fanann sé freisin taobh istigh dá phacáiste féin: cóipeanna an Dockerfile sé isteach an íomhá in aice ``utils/__init__.py`` agus ``utils/install/__init__.py`` agus aon rud eile, mar sin iompórtáil aon eile ``utils`` Ardaíonn submodule ``ModuleNotFoundError`` sa tsraith a ritheann é. Is iad na comhaid ceanglais léann sé an stór féin agus a shealbhú cruth amháin: ``collections:`` liosta de na ``- name:`` iontrálacha le roghnach ``version:``. Tá líne nach bhfuil comhoiriúnach a fhágann an cruth an iontráil gan staonadh, a dhéileálann an glaoiteoir mar gan sásamh agus a shuiteáil."

