msgid "Tests that verify real runtime component interactions MUST live under `tests/integration/`."
msgstr "Tástáil a fhíorú idirghníomhaíocht chomhpháirt runtime fíor MUST beo faoi `tests/integration/`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Tests 🧪"
msgstr "Tástáil 🧪"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Thank you for contributing to a safe and inclusive Infinito.Nexus community!"
msgstr "Go raibh maith agat as cur le sábháilte agus cuimsitheach Infinito.Nexus pobail!"

msgid "That choice is wrong in two directions at once. A prompt that needs a large context window reaches a model that cannot hold it, which is how [`web-app-hermes`](../../roles/web-app-hermes/) answers HTTP 500 when the agent model declares fewer than 64000 tokens. And a one-line factual question reaches whatever the deploy happened to pick, which is usually the largest model available."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That contract is wrong for one class of failure. When a value could not be measured and substituting one would be a guess, silence turns a loud stop into a wrong number nobody sees. Such a failure raises from here and every render layer re-raises it untouched."
msgstr "Tá an conradh mícheart le haghaidh aicme amháin teip. Nuair nach bhféadfaí luach a thomhas agus a chur in ionad amháin go mbeadh buille faoi thuairim, casann tost stad os ard i uimhir mícheart Feiceann aon duine. Ardaíonn teip den sórt sin ó anseo agus ath-mheasann gach ciseal riuched sé."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That file brings the client to its desired MCP state from scratch, so the same file serves the role's own run and this one. `tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py` fails when a client role lacks it."
msgstr "Tugann an comhad sin an cliant ar a staid MCP atá ag teastáil ó scratch, mar sin feidhmíonn an comhad céanna an ról ar reáchtáil féin agus an ceann seo. `tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py` go mainneoidh nuair nach bhfuil ról cliaint é."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That file brings the client to its desired MCP state from scratch, so the same file serves the role’s own run and this one. ``tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py`` fails when a client role lacks it."
msgstr "Tugann an comhad sin an cliant ar a staid MCP atá ag teastáil ó scratch, mar sin feidhmíonn an comhad céanna an ról ar reáchtáil féin agus an ceann seo. ``tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py`` go mainneoidh nuair nach bhfuil ról cliaint é."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is also what a retrigger replays: `--failed` reads the glyphs off the failed job's title and writes them back as a token, so the row comes back in the mode, onion state, distribution and architecture it died on rather than on whatever the rotation would pick next. The architecture is replayed because it is the machine the job ran on, not a preference it could fall back from. The filesystem is deliberately left out. A title states the kind the matrix *assigned*, which a deploy is allowed to fall back from, so pinning it would both misstate what the job ran on and turn the kind into a demand, failing the retrigger on the very condition the fallback absorbs."
msgstr "Is é sin freisin cad replays retrigger: `--failed` léann an glyphs as an bpost theip ar teideal agus scríobhann siad ar ais mar chomhartha, mar sin a thagann an tsraith ar ais sa mhodh, stát oinniún, dáileadh agus ailtireacht fuair sé bás ar seachas ar cibé an rothlú a bheadh a roghnú in aice. Tá an ailtireacht replayed toisc go bhfuil sé an meaisín an post ar siúl ar, ní rogha d'fhéadfadh sé titim ar ais ó. Tá an córas comhaid fágtha amach d'aon ghnó. Deir teideal an cineál maitrís *sannta sannadh*, a bhfuil a imscaradh cheadaítear titim ar ais ó, mar sin pinning bheadh sé an dá misstate cad a bhí ar siúl ar an bpost agus cas an cineál isteach éileamh, ag teip an retrigger ar an riocht an-ionsaíonn an fallback."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is what stops the supervisor flow rather than effort. Flowise reaches an MCP server over the container network, and a stdio server has no address there: the client spawns and owns the process, so a shared endpoint two consumers could hold at once does not exist, and the deploy-time contract probe would consume the only session. Wrapping each agent in a stdio-to-HTTP bridge would put an unreviewed process on the platform's most privileged path — an agent with tool access — to work around a transport upstream has not shipped, which is the workaround this project refuses. Re-review when either upstream serves MCP over HTTP."
msgstr "Is é sin a stopann an sreabhadh maoirseachta seachas iarracht. Sroicheann Flowise freastalaí MCP thar an líonra coimeádán, agus tá freastalaí stdio aon seoladh ann: sceitheadh an chliaint agus úinéireacht an phróisis, mar sin d'fhéadfadh dhá tomhaltóirí a shealbhú ag an am céanna nach bhfuil ann, agus bheadh an probe conradh imscaradh-am ithe an seisiún amháin. D'fhágfadh gach gníomhaire i stdio-go-HTTP go gcuirfí próiseas neamhathbhreithnithe ar chonair an ardáin is pribhléidí - níor sheol gníomhaire le rochtain uirlise - obair a dhéanamh thart ar sruth iompair, rud a dhiúltaíonn an obair ar fud an tionscadail seo. Ath-athbhreithniú nuair a fhreastalaíonn ceachtar sruth MCP thar HTTP."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is why the repo favors:"
msgstr "Sin é an fáth go bhfuil an repo favors:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is why the repo has:"
msgstr "Sin é an fáth go bhfuil an repo:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is why you will find host work in `sys-*` roles and app work in `web-app-*` roles instead of one giant deployment script."
msgstr "Sin é an fáth go bhfaighidh tú obair óstach i `sys-*` róil agus obair app i `web-app-*` róil in ionad script imscaradh ollmhór amháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That last step is deliberately the deployed [`sys-ctl-hlth-container` script](../../../sys-ctl-hlth-container/files/shell/script.sh) rather than a check of the drill's own: it is what watches the host in production, it knows swarm services, and it dumps 200 log lines per sick container. It is invoked as a script, not as its systemd unit — the unit's `OnFailure` starts the soft-repair service, and a drill that repairs what it found has stopped measuring. It cannot replace the drill's own wait either: a container that never came back is in no `container ps` filter, so only the recorded-set check sees it."
msgstr "Is é sin an chéim dheireanach d’aon turas ar imscaradh [`sys-ctl-hlth-container` script script](../../../sys-ctl-hlth-container/files/shell/script.sh) seachas seiceáil ar an druil féin: is é an méid a uaireadóirí an t-óstach i dtáirgeadh, tá a fhios aige seirbhísí swarm, agus dumpálann sé 200 línte log in aghaidh an coimeádán tinn. Tá sé agairt mar script, ní mar a aonad córasach - an t-aonad `OnFailure` Tosaíonn an tseirbhís bog-deisiú, agus druil a deisiúcháin cad a fuair sé stop a thomhas. Ní féidir é a chur in ionad an druil féin fanacht ceachtar: tá coimeádán a riamh tháinig ar ais i aon `container ps` scagaire, mar sin ní fheiceann ach an tseiceáil atá leagtha taifeadta é."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That makes it easier to see whether the real issue is Docker, journald, a package cache, or project state."
msgstr "Sin a dhéanann sé níos éasca a fheiceáil an bhfuil an cheist fíor Docker, irisithe, taisce pacáiste, nó stát tionscadail."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That means the bundle is not where logic lives. It is where the architecture becomes a real deployment."
msgstr "Ciallaíonn sé sin nach bhfuil an bundle ina saol loighic. Tá sé nuair a bheidh an ailtireacht a imscaradh fíor."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That pipe **destroys the exit status**: `make test | tee` reports `tee`'s success even when make ends with `Error 2`. You MUST judge such a run by its `📊 per-target wall-clock` table and its `FAILED TARGETS:` line, never by the exit code."
msgstr "Sin píopa **milleann an stádas scoir**: `make test | tee` Tuarascálacha agus tuarascálacha `tee`'s rath fiú nuair a chríochnaíonn a dhéanamh le `Error 2`. MUST tú breitheamh den sórt sin a reáchtáil ag a `📊 per-target wall-clock` tábla agus a `FAILED TARGETS:` líne, riamh ag an cód scoir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That second step exists because a group grant addresses an Open WebUI group id and ``insert_new_group`` assigns it as a fresh UUID, so the id cannot be known while the env is rendered. The task signs in as the native administrator, resolves or creates the group whose name matches the OIDC claim value, and writes the grant through ``POST /api/v1/configs/tool_servers``. It refuses to act when two groups share a name rather than guessing between them."
msgstr "Tá an dara céim mar gheall ar seoltaí deontas grúpa ar Open WebUI grúpa id agus ``insert_new_group`` sannann sé mar UUID úr, mar sin ní féidir an id a dtugtar cé go bhfuil an env a rinneadh. Na comharthaí tasc i mar an riarthóir dúchais, réitíonn nó a chruthaíonn an grúpa a oireann a ainm luach éilimh OIDC, agus scríobhann an deontas tríd ``POST /api/v1/configs/tool_servers``. Diúltaíonn sé gníomhú nuair a roinnt dhá ghrúpa ainm seachas guessing eatarthu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That second step exists because a group grant addresses an Open WebUI group id and `insert_new_group` assigns it as a fresh UUID, so the id cannot be known while the env is rendered. The task signs in as the native administrator, resolves or creates the group whose name matches the OIDC claim value, and writes the grant through `POST /api/v1/configs/tool_servers`. It refuses to act when two groups share a name rather than guessing between them."
msgstr "Tá an dara céim mar gheall ar seoltaí deontas grúpa ar Open WebUI grúpa id agus `insert_new_group` sannann sé mar UUID úr, mar sin ní féidir an id a dtugtar cé go bhfuil an env a rinneadh. Na comharthaí tasc i mar an riarthóir dúchais, réitíonn nó a chruthaíonn an grúpa a oireann a ainm luach éilimh OIDC, agus scríobhann an deontas tríd `POST /api/v1/configs/tool_servers`. Diúltaíonn sé gníomhú nuair a roinnt dhá ghrúpa ainm seachas guessing eatarthu."

