msgstr "An bhfuil PostgreSQL Tá bunachar sonraí tacaíocht suas ag na róil cúltaca lárnach; Is é an toirt sócmhainní cúltaca-réidh de réir choinbhinsiún."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Pull Request MUST be linked to the related work item in [project.infinito.nexus](https://project.infinito.nexus/) and back."
msgstr "An MUST Iarratas Tarraing a nascadh leis an mír oibre a bhaineann i [project.infinito.nexus](https://project.infinito.nexus/) agus ar ais."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Python helper is intentionally self-contained and unit-testable"
msgstr "Is é an cúntóir Python d'aon ghnó féinchoinneáil agus aonad-intestable"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The REST API answers ``inputs: null`` for a finished workflow_dispatch, so the inputs are recovered from the run itself: short ones from the title (``config_from_title``), the long ones from a called job's log (``inputs_from_jobs``), which the title truncates."
msgstr "An REST API Freagraí scríofa ``inputs: null`` ar feadh críochnaithe workflow_dispatch, mar sin na hionchuir a aisghabháil ón rith féin: cinn gearr ón teideal (``config_from_title``), na cinn fada ó logáil post ar a dtugtar (``inputs_from_jobs``), a teascann an teideal."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Root CA private key is generated **unencrypted** (automation-friendly). Protect file permissions."
msgstr "Tá eochair phríobháideach Root CA a ghintear **neamhchriptithe** (uathoibriú-chairdiúil). Ceadanna comhad a chosaint."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The SPOT declaration with the scope's override merged over it."
msgstr "Chuir an dearbhú pacáistithe le ró-bhród an raon feidhme le chéile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The SPOT is ``meta/services.yml.<primary_entity>.architectures``, next to ``modes``: both state what the role CAN do, which is why the deploy matrix narrows a row by them. ``meta/tests.yml`` is the other kind of statement - what CI should skip exercising - and an image that exists for one architecture only is not a testing preference."
msgstr "Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil ``meta/services.yml.<primary_entity>.architectures``, in aice le ``modes``: an dá stát cad a dhéanann an ról CAN, agus sin an fáth cúngaíonn an maitrís imscaradh a chéile acu. ``meta/tests.yml`` Is é an cineál eile ráitis - cad ba chóir CI skip a fheidhmiú - agus íomhá atá ann le haghaidh ailtireacht amháin nach bhfuil ach rogha tástála."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The SPOT is ``meta/services.yml.<primary_entity>.modes.<mode>.enabled``. A missing ``modes`` block, a missing ``<mode>`` entry, or a missing ``enabled`` key all mean the role participates in that mode (default ``True``)."
msgstr "Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil ``meta/services.yml.<primary_entity>.modes.<mode>.enabled``. A iarraidh ``modes`` bloc, ar iarraidh ``<mode>`` iontráil, nó ar iarraidh ``enabled`` eochair chiallaíonn go léir an ról páirt sa mhodh sin (cineál gas: in airde ``True``)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The SPOT is parsed with a plain-string line parser instead of PyYAML: the env build runs during bootstrap (make install-system-python) before any Python dependency exists, so this module must stay stdlib-only. Only plain ``KEY: \"value\"`` entries can be read this way; a Jinja expression or a missing key is a hard error."
msgstr "Tá an phatrún parsáil le parsálaí líne plain-teorann in ionad PyYAML: ritheann an env thógáil le linn buataisítrap (a dhéanamh shuiteáil-chóras-python) roimh aon spleáchas Python ann, mar sin ní mór an modúl seo fanacht stdlib-amháin. Ach simplí ``KEY: \"value\"`` Is féidir le hiontrálacha a léamh ar an mbealach seo; Is earráid chrua é léiriú Jinja nó eochair ar iarraidh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The SSE session travels through the shared Redis channel layer, so the stream and the message POST may land on different replicas."
msgstr "Taistealaíonn an seisiún SSE tríd an gcomhroinnt Redis ciseal cainéal, mar sin d'fhéadfadh an sruth agus an teachtaireacht POST talamh ar macasamhailí éagsúla."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The SSO (``sociallogin``) and LDAP (``user_ldap``) login surfaces are covered by the OIDC/LDAP Playwright specs (requirements 017/018)."
msgstr "An SSO (``sociallogin``) agus LDAP (``user_ldap``) dromchlaí logáil isteach clúdaithe ag an OIDC /LDAP specs Playwright (riachtanais na gcustaiméirí 017/ Baile018)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The SSO (`sociallogin`) and LDAP (`user_ldap`) login surfaces are covered by the OIDC/LDAP Playwright specs (requirements 017/018)."
msgstr "An SSO (`sociallogin`) agus LDAP (`user_ldap`) dromchlaí logáil isteach clúdaithe ag an OIDC /LDAP specs Playwright (riachtanais na gcustaiméirí 017/ Baile018)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The SSO back-channel pin, added automatically. On an onion deployment the OIDC endpoints handed to an application are public ``.onion`` authorities. That is right for the browser, which reaches them through Tor, but unroutable for the application's own server-side calls (code-to-token exchange, JWKS, userinfo): a container resolves ``.onion`` through Tor's resolver, not through DNS. Pinning the provider to a reachable address sends those calls over the local network to the proxy that already serves the vhost. Skipped unless the application has SSO enabled and the provider vhost is an ``.onion`` name, so it is a no-op on clearnet."
msgstr "Chuir an SSO bioráin ar ais-chainéil, go huathoibríoch. Ar imscaradh oinniún, is iad na pointí deiridh OIDC a thugtar d'iarratas poiblí ``.onion`` údaráis. Is é sin ceart don bhrabhsálaí, a shroicheann iad trí Tor, ach unroutable le haghaidh glaonna freastalaí-taobh an iarratais féin (cód-le-chomhartha malartú, JWKS, userinfo): réitíonn coimeádán ``.onion`` trí réiteoir Tor ar, ní trí DNS. Pinning an soláthraí chuig seoladh reachable cuireann na glaonna thar an líonra áitiúil chuig an seachfhreastalaí a fhreastalaíonn cheana féin ar an vhost. Scipeáil mura bhfuil an t-iarratas SSO cumasaithe agus is é an soláthraí vhost an ``.onion`` ainm, mar sin tá sé aon-op ar clearnet."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Sphinx configuration, extensions and generators live in [web-app-docs](../../roles/web-app-docs/). Deploy that role to build and serve the site."
msgstr "An chumraíocht Sphinx, síntí agus gineadóirí beo i [web-app-docs](../../roles/web-app-docs/). Déan an ról sin a thógáil agus a sheirbheáil ar an suíomh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The URL reachability check emits warning annotations for HTTP `429`, `500`, and `503` (rate-limited or temporarily unavailable) via [`utils.annotations.message`](../../../../utils/annotations/message.py)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The URL reachability check skips template placeholders and reserved local or example hosts such as `localhost` and `*.example`."
msgstr "An URL reachability seiceáil skips lonnaitheoirí teimpléad agus in áirithe áitiúil nó mar shampla hóstach ar nós `localhost` agus `*.example`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The URL reachability check treats HTTP `401`, `403`, and `405` as reachable (auth-gated or method-restricted servers, not dead links)."
msgstr "Déileálann an URL seiceáil reachability HTTP `401`, `403`, agus `405` mar reachable (freastalaithe auth-gated nó modh- srianta, naisc nach marbh)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The URL reachability check treats read and connect timeouts as warnings."
msgstr "Déileálann an URL seiceáil reachability léamh agus timeouts ceangal mar rabhaidh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The YAML key is the semantic short name. Each entry value MAY carry ``name`` (the docker volume name); when absent and ``type`` is ``volume``, callers default the docker name to the semantic key."
msgstr "Is é an eochair YAML an t-ainm gearr shéimeantach. Gach luach iontrála ``name`` (an t-ainm toirt docker); nuair a bheidh sé as láthair agus ``type`` Is maith liom ``volume``, callers réamhshocraithe an t-ainm docker leis an eochair shéimeantach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Zammad helpdesk role completes its single-sign-on schema unification, with the variant matrix and Playwright test suite brought in line with the new shape."
msgstr "An bhfuil Zammad Críochnaíonn ról deisce cabhrach a aon-chomhartha-ar aontú scéimre, leis an maitrís athraitheach agus sraith tástála Playwright thabhairt i gcomhréir leis an cruth nua."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The [GitHub Actions self-hosted runner](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/hosting-your-own-runners/managing-self-hosted-runners/about-self-hosted-runners) is an agent that runs GitHub Actions workflow jobs on your own infrastructure instead of GitHub-hosted machines."
msgstr "An bhfuil [GitHub Gníomhartha rádala féin-óstáil](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/hosting-your-own-runners/managing-self-hosted-runners/about-self-hosted-runners) Is gníomhaire a ritheann GitHub Gníomhartha poist sreabhadh oibre ar do bhonneagar féin in ionad meaisíní GitHub-óstach."

msgid "The [`apps/`](apps/) subtree is split by verb (the user intent) and scope:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The [`bundles/`](bundles/) subtree mirrors the same axes for inventory bundles (`fresh.sh` ≈ initialize, `update.sh` ≈ update)."
