msgid "The [`container/`](container/) subtree holds the in-container halves invoked by the host wrappers and follows the same verb/scope layout; see [container/](container/README.md)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The [alias](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/alias) repository is the RECOMMENDED way to define CLI shortcuts so frequently used commands do not have to be retyped. The effective repository is the `INFINITO_ALIAS_REPOSITORY` value in the generated `.env`."
msgstr "An bhfuil [ailias](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/alias) Is é an stór an bealach MEASNDED a shainiú shortcuts CLI sin a úsáidtear go minic nach bhfuil orduithe a retyped. Is é an stór éifeachtach an `INFINITO_ALIAS_REPOSITORY` luach sa ghintear `.env`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The [lint.md](testing/lint.md) page covers repository-wide code quality expectations such as diff quality, maintainability, and conventions."
msgstr "An bhfuil [lint.md](testing/lint.md) Clúdaíonn leathanach ionchais chaighdeán cód ar fud an stór ar nós diff cáilíochta, inchothaitheacht, agus coinbhinsiúin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The [per-role meta layout](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md) already lists `addons`, `plugins`, and `modules` among the keys *inlined* under the primary service entity. This requirement promotes that concept to a first-class, per-file `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml` topic (one file per addon, file root IS the addon spec), the same move requirement 011 made for `meta/info.yml` and requirement 008/009 made for other meta topics."
msgstr "An bhfuil [in aghaidh an leagan amach meta-ról](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md) liostaí cheana féin `addons`, `plugins`, agus `modules` i measc na heochracha *inlined* faoin eintiteas seirbhíse príomha. Cuireann an ceanglas seo an coincheap sin chun an chéad aicme, in aghaidh an-chomhaid `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml` ábhar topaic (comhad amháin in aghaidh an addon, comhad fhréamh IS an spec addon), an riachtanas céanna bogadh 011 déanta as `meta/info.yml` agus ceanglas 008/ Baile009 déanta le haghaidh topaicí meta eile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `.onion` is a **deploy-time input**: a CLI helper mints the v3 key offline during inventory build, vaults it, and sets `DOMAIN_PRIMARY`. It must NOT be a runtime fact — `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` is consumed at build time (LDAP base, CA, applications cache). The role restores the minted key into the hidden-service volume before Tor starts."
msgstr "An bhfuil `.onion` Is maith liom é **ionchur imscaradh-am**: a cúntóir CLI mints an v3 eochair as líne le linn tógáil fardal, bogha sé, agus leagann `DOMAIN_PRIMARY`. Ní mór é a bheith FACT runtime — `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` a chaitear ag am a thógáil (bonn LDAP, CA, iarratais taisce). An ról restores an eochair minted isteach an méid i bhfolach-seirbhíse sula Tosaíonn Tor."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `@playwright/test` version pinned into the rendered `package.json` comes from `playwright.version` in `roles/test-e2e-playwright/meta/services.yml` via the `image_version` filter. That YAML value is the single source of truth for the Playwright version."
msgstr "An bhfuil `@playwright/test` leagan pinned isteach sa rinneadh `package.json` thagann ó `playwright.version` i `roles/test-e2e-playwright/meta/services.yml` tríd an `image_version` scagaire. Is é sin luach YAML an fhoinse amháin na fírinne don leagan Playwright."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `API.cloudflare.api_token` value (declared in `group_vars/all/18_api.yml`, read via `lookup('api', 'cloudflare.api_token')`) must contain a valid Cloudflare API Token.   This token is used for all DNS operations and ACME (SSL/TLS certificate) challenges that require access to your Cloudflare-managed domains."
msgstr "An bhfuil `API.cloudflare.api_token` luach (a dhearbhú in `group_vars/all/18_api.yml`, léamh trí `lookup('api', 'cloudflare.api_token')`) ní mór go bhfuil Cloudflare bailí API Token. Tá an comhartha a úsáidtear le haghaidh gach oibríochtaí DNS agus ACME (Deimhniú SSL / TLS) dúshláin a éilíonn rochtain ar do fearainn Cloudflare-bhainistithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `Bash(*)` allow grants broad access to the `docker` CLI (alongside every other shell command) under the assumption that no production containers share the host. Non-mutating-image subcommands (`rm`, `kill`, `stop`, `system prune`, `volume rm`, `cp`) can disrupt or destroy container state. Under test-only usage, the blast radius is bounded to ephemeral state that can be recreated from the compose stack."
msgstr "An bhfuil `Bash(*)` cead a thabhairt deontais rochtain leathan ar `docker` Slí an Atlantaigh (taobh le gach ordú bhlaosc eile) faoin toimhde nach roinneann aon choimeádáin táirgeachta an t-óstach. Neamh-mutating-image subcommands (`rm`, `kill`, `stop`, `system prune`, `volume rm`, `cp`) Is féidir cur isteach nó scrios staid coimeádán. Faoi úsáid tástála-amháin, tá an ga soinneáin faoi cheangal a stát ephemeral is féidir a athchruthú as an Stack chumadh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `Bash(*)` allow lets the agent run any Makefile target without prompting. The `Makefile` is checked into git and reviewed on every pull request, so targets themselves are trusted. Every action a target performs still runs inside the sandbox."
msgstr "An bhfuil `Bash(*)` ligean ligeann an gníomhaire reáchtáil aon sprioc Makefile gan leideanna. An bhfuil `Makefile` a sheiceáil isteach git agus athbhreithniú ar gach iarratas tarraingt, mar sin spriocanna iad féin iontaofa. Gach gníomh a dhéanann sprioc ritheann fós taobh istigh den bhosca gainimh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The `Corefile.tmpl` MUST be the source of truth. It is rendered to `Corefile` by [coredns.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/development/coredns.py), which substitutes its `${VAR}` placeholders in-process, using values from `.env` (generated from [default.env](../../default.env), overridable through the CLI's environment)."
msgstr "An bhfuil `Corefile.tmpl` MUST a bheith ar an fhoinse na fírinne. Tá sé a rinneadh `Corefile` ag an [coredns.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/development/coredns.py), a ionadaíonn a `${VAR}` sealbhóirí áite i-próiseas, ag baint úsáide as luachanna ó `.env` (a ghintear ó [default.env](../../default.env), overridable trí thimpeallacht an CLI)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `GitHub Actions self-hosted runner <https://docs.github.com/en/actions/hosting-your-own-runners/managing-self-hosted-runners/about-self-hosted-runners>`__ is an agent that runs GitHub Actions workflow jobs on your own infrastructure instead of GitHub-hosted machines."
msgstr "An bhfuil `GitHub Actions self-hosted runner <https://docs.github.com/en/actions/hosting-your-own-runners/managing-self-hosted-runners/about-self-hosted-runners>`__ Is gníomhaire a ritheann GitHub Gníomhartha poist sreabhadh oibre ar do bhonneagar féin in ionad meaisíní GitHub-óstach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `Makefile` is the human-facing command surface for the repo. It MUST expose stable targets that people and CI are meant to run directly."
msgstr "An bhfuil `Makefile` Is é an dromchla orduithe daonna-facing don repo. MUST sé spriocanna cobhsaí a nochtadh go bhfuil daoine agus CI i gceist a reáchtáil go díreach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `OIDC` tree is a lazy group_var: it resolves in the consuming role's context, so the issuer family-aligns to that consumer (clearnet page → clearnet issuer, onion page → onion issuer). Inventory overrides therefore live under `OIDC_OVERRIDE:` — an inventory-level `OIDC:` block would shadow the lazy resolution and is rejected by a constructor assert."
msgstr "An bhfuil `OIDC` Is crann leisciúil group_var: réitíonn sé i gcomhthéacs an róil Tógann, mar sin an t-eisitheoir teaghlaigh ailínigh leis an tomhaltóir sin (leathanach glan → eisitheoir glan, leathanach oinniún → eisitheoir oinniún). overrides Fardal dá bhrí sin beo faoi `OIDC_OVERRIDE:` — leibhéal fardail `OIDC:` Bheadh bloc scáth an réiteach leisciúil agus diúltaíodh ag dearbhú tógálaí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `Options` rule is what keeps a swarm host with NFS-backed volumes on the live copy (see [NFS-backed volumes](#nfs-backed-volumes)): such a volume is a separate filesystem, so a snapshot of the data root would capture it as an empty directory and the backup would succeed while holding nothing. The declaration is checked rather than the mount table, because docker mounts those volumes lazily and unmounts them when the last container stops."
msgstr "An bhfuil `Options` riail cad a choimeádann óstach swarm le méideanna NFS-aiseolas ar an chóip beo (féach ar [NFS-aiseolas méideanna](#nfs-backed-volumes)): Is méid den sórt sin córas comhaid ar leith, mar sin bheadh léargas ar an fhréamh sonraí a ghabháil mar eolaire folamh agus go mbeadh an cúltaca rathúil agus a bhfuil rud ar bith. Déantar an dearbhú a sheiceáil seachas an tábla mount, mar gheall ar mounts docker na méideanna seo go lazily agus unmounts iad nuair a stopann an coimeádán deireanach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `RUNNER_DISTRIBUTION` variable selects distro-specific package installation tasks (Debian, Ubuntu, Arch Linux, or Fedora/EL). The role is designed to be driven by the `make runner-ci-deploy` target; see the end-to-end guide below."
