# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `all` mode honors a per-interpreter stamp at `build/install-lint-<hash>.stamp` (the suffix is the first 8 chars of `sha256(sys.executable)`, so host and container track independently even though `build/` is bind-mounted). Stamp dependencies are [lint.sh](../../../scripts/install/lint.sh) and [pyproject.toml](../../../pyproject.toml). Group-targeted invocations always run and never touch the stamp."
msgstr "An bhfuil `all` modh onóracha stampa per-interpreter ag `build/install-lint-<hash>.stamp` (is é an iarmhír an chéad 8 cars `sha256(sys.executable)`, mar sin óstach agus rian coimeádán go neamhspleách cé `build/` tá sé feistithe). Tá spleáchais Stampa [lint.sh](../../../scripts/install/lint.sh) agus [pyproject.toml](../../../pyproject.toml). Invocations Group-targeted reáchtáil i gcónaí agus ní i dteagmháil leis an stampa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `applications` lookup is the ONLY supported runtime entry point for merged application configuration."
msgstr "An bhfuil `applications` Is Lookup an AMHÁIN tacaíocht pointe iontrála runtime do chumraíocht iarratas cumaisc."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `ask` rules on `docker run*` / `docker build*` / `docker push*` / `docker login*` only catch the outermost invocation. Because the project uses Docker-in-Docker (for example `docker exec <helper-container> docker run ...`), a `docker run` invoked inside an exec'd helper container bypasses the ask-gate. The helper container has its own Docker daemon or a bind-mounted host socket, so the inner `docker run` executes directly."
msgstr "An bhfuil `ask` rialacha maidir le `docker run*` / Baile `docker build*` / Baile `docker push*` / Baile `docker login*` ach an sonrascadh is forimeallaí a ghabháil. Toisc go n-úsáideann an tionscadal Docker-i-Docker (mar shampla `docker exec <helper-container> docker run ...`), a `docker run` agairt taobh istigh de seachbhóthar coimeádán cúntóir exec'd an iarraidh-gheata. Tá an coimeádán cúntóir a daemon Docker féin nó soicéad óstach ceangal-mounted, mar sin an istigh `docker run` fhorghníomhú go díreach."

