# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `biber` and `administrator` Playwright personas are gated on `services.sso.enabled`. When SSO is off, [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) renders `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`. Two reasons:"
msgstr "An bhfuil `biber` agus `administrator` Playwright personas atá gated ar `services.sso.enabled`. Nuair a bhíonn SSO as, [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) custom `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` agus `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`. Dhá chúis:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `biber` and `administrator` personas always end on a verified unauthenticated landing via the in-app logout button."
msgstr "An bhfuil `biber` agus `administrator` personas deireadh i gcónaí ar a fhíorú tuirlingthe unauthenticated tríd an cnaipe logout in-app."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The `biber` persona MUST drive at least one role-specific interaction that a regular end-user would perform (post a message, open a settings tab, browse a content list, submit a form, …). Specs supply this via the `biberInteraction` callback on `runBiberFlow(page, { biberInteraction })`. There is NO generic default. A generic \"click any link\" assertion tests nothing role-specific, so the helper is a no-op until the spec provides a callback."
msgstr "An bhfuil `biber` MUST persona thiomáint ar a laghad ról-shonrach idirghníomhaíocht go mbeadh úsáideoir deiridh rialta a dhéanamh (post teachtaireacht, oscailt cluaisín suímh, brabhsáil liosta ábhar, foirm a chur isteach,...). Specs sholáthar seo tríd an `biberInteraction` callback ar `runBiberFlow(page, { biberInteraction })`. Níl aon mhainneachtain cineálach ann. cineálach \"cliceáil ar nasc\" tástálacha dearbhú aon ról-sonrach, mar sin tá an cúntóir aon-uair go dtí go soláthraíonn an spec callback."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `biber` persona logs in through OIDC without trouble; what it cannot do is log out. Decidim's sign-out is a `data-method` link inside the account dropdown, so the role's own tests navigate to `/users/sign_out` directly rather than clicking a button the shared helper could find."
msgstr "An bhfuil `biber` logaí persona i trí OIDC gan deacracht; cad nach féidir é a dhéanamh ná logáil amach. Is cinnte go bhfuil comhartha-amach `data-method` nasc taobh istigh den dropdown cuntas, mar sin an ról tástálacha féin nascleanúint a dhéanamh `/users/sign_out` go díreach seachas cliceáil cnaipe d'fhéadfadh an cúntóir roinnte teacht."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `build-ci-images` stage uses [call-images-build-ci.yml](../../../../.github/workflows/call-images-build-ci.yml) to build Docker images for the target distributions (`arch`, `debian`, `ubuntu`, `fedora`, `centos`). These images are consumed by all subsequent test jobs."
msgstr "An bhfuil `build-ci-images` úsáidí stáitse [glao-íomhánna-tógáil-ci.yml](../../../../.github/workflows/call-images-build-ci.yml) a thógáil íomhánna Docker do na dáiltí sprioc (`arch`, `debian`, `ubuntu`, `fedora`, `centos`). Déantar na híomhánna seo a chaitheamh ag gach post tástála ina dhiaidh sin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `bundles=` make arg (comma-separated bundle names) is REQUIRED for both entry points. The compose-deploy recipe sets the resulting `bundles` env var read by these scripts."
msgstr "An bhfuil `bundles=` a dhéanamh ar g (ainmneacha cuachta atá deighilte) Is REQUIRED don dá phointe iontrála. Leagann an t-oideas cumadóireachta an toradh `bundles` env var léamh ag na scripteanna."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `cache` decision is exposed via `Profile.cache_stack_enabled()` in [profile.py](../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/profile.py). When active:"
msgstr "An bhfuil `cache` Tá cinneadh nochta trí `Profile.cache_stack_enabled()` i [profile.py](../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/profile.py). Nuair atá sé gníomhach:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `cli.contributing.mirror.cleanup` module deletes GHCR container packages filtered by prefix and visibility. Use it to remove stale private mirror packages that were pushed before the repository switched to `GITHUB_TOKEN`-based authentication (which now makes packages public automatically)."
msgstr "An bhfuil `cli.contributing.mirror.cleanup` scriosann modúl pacáistí coimeádán GHCR scagtha ag réimír agus infheictheacht. Bain úsáid as chun pacáistí scátháin phríobháideacha stale a bhrúíodh roimh an stór a athrú `GITHUB_TOKEN`fíordheimhnithe -bhunaithe (a dhéanann anois pacáistí poiblí go huathoibríoch)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `code-quality-gate` requires linting, code tests, and security checks to all pass before deploy tests are triggered."
msgstr "An bhfuil `code-quality-gate` Éilíonn linting, tástálacha cód, agus seiceálacha slándála chun gach pas sula tástálacha imscaradh spreagtha."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `context_agent` and `contextagentmcp` services in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) render only while `mcp.enabled` is true. The first runs `ghcr.io/nextcloud/context_agent`, listens on its internal port for AppAPI only, and shares `credentials.context_agent_app_secret` with the ExApp registration as `APP_SECRET`. The second is the adapter sidecar, built from the staged `svc-ai-mcp-adapter` context, read-only with every capability dropped, and it is the only MCP endpoint clients are given."
msgstr "An bhfuil `context_agent` agus `contextagentmcp` seirbhísí i [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) a dhéanamh ach amháin le linn `mcp.enabled` Is fíor. An chéad Ritheann `ghcr.io/nextcloud/context_agent`, éisteann ar a port inmheánach le haghaidh AppAPI amháin, agus scaireanna `credentials.context_agent_app_secret` leis an clárú ExApp mar `APP_SECRET`. Is é an dara an taobhcharr adapter, tógtha as an stáitse `svc-ai-mcp-adapter` comhthéacs, léigh-amháin le gach cumas thit, agus is é an t-aon chliaint endpoint MCP a thugtar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `dashboard` service in `meta/services.yml` is only a consumer tile pointing at MIG's canonical domain; it does not host MIG. The role's contract is fully carried by the reachability, canonical-domain and content-type scenarios in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`, plus the guest persona. The path back to the generic personas is an authenticated MIG surface, which upstream does not have."
msgstr "An bhfuil `dashboard` service india `meta/services.yml` ach tíl tomhaltóra dírithe ar MIG's fearainn Canonical; nach bhfuil sé ina óstach MIG. Tá conradh an róil á chur i gcrích go hiomlán ag an reachability, Canonical-domain agus cásanna de chineál ábhar i `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`, móide an persona aoi. Is é an cosán ar ais go dtí an personas cineálach fíordheimhnithe MIG dromchla, nach bhfuil sruth ag."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `default:` points at the central `API` block in [group_vars/all/18_api.yml](../../../../../group_vars/all/18_api.yml), so an operator fills the provider in one place while the role keeps the shape the value must have."
msgstr "An bhfuil `default:` pointí ag an lárnach `API` bloc i [group_vars/all/18_api.yml](../../../../../group_vars/all/18_api.yml), mar sin líonann oibreoir an soláthraí in aon áit amháin agus coimeádann an ról an cruth ní mór an luach a bheith."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `deploy` router target and `make compose-exec` / `make network-trust-ca` helpers."
msgstr "An bhfuil `deploy` sprioc ródaire agus `make compose-exec` / Baile `make network-trust-ca` Cúntóirí."

