msgstr "An bhfuil `utils/` MUST crann bhfuil modúil cúntóir Python agus pacáistí cúntóir amháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `vars/main.yml` of the role MUST define the variables referenced in `args:` by reading them from `meta/services.yml` through the `lookup('config', ...)` filter. This keeps `meta/services.yml` as the single source of truth."
msgstr "An bhfuil `vars/main.yml` an ról MUST shainiú na hathróga tagairt i `args:` ag léamh iad ó `meta/services.yml` tríd an `lookup('config', ...)` scagaire. Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil `meta/services.yml` mar an fhoinse amháin na fírinne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `version:` MUST stay pinned to an exact Playwright version and distro pair such as `v1.59.1-noble`. You MUST NOT switch this to a mutable tag such as `latest`, because mutable upstream tags are more vulnerable to CDN propagation delays and make flaky CI failures much harder to reason about."
msgstr "An bhfuil `version:` MUST fhan pinned le leagan Playwright cruinn agus péire distro nós `v1.59.1-noble`. NÍ MÓR duit athrú seo le chlib mutable nós `latest`, toisc go bhfuil níos leochailí tags sruth mutable do mhoilleanna iomadú CDN agus a dhéanamh teipeanna CI flaky i bhfad níos deacra ar chúis faoi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `🛡️ Trusted` label flips the build source to the PR head and unlocks the Docker Hub credentials; without it the safe base merge ref is built with no organization secrets. Restrict who may set the label via repository label permissions / branch protection so only maintainers can grant it."
msgstr "An bhfuil `🛡️ Trusted` smeach lipéad an fhoinse a thógáil go dtí an ceann PR agus unlocks an credentials Docker Hub; gan é an bonn sábháilte a chumasc ref tógtha le haon rúin eagraíocht. Srianta a fhéadfaidh a shocrú ar an lipéad trí cheadanna lipéad stór / cosaint brainse ionas gur féidir ach choimeádaithe dheonú air."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `🧩 Subset` label must exist in the repository's label set and is applied through the PR labels UI. Both the `pull_request` and `pull_request_target` events carry a `labeled` trigger, so adding it starts a fresh run."
msgstr "An bhfuil `🧩 Subset` Ní mór lipéad a bheith ann i sraith lipéad an stór agus tá sé i bhfeidhm tríd an UI lipéad PR. An dá an `pull_request` agus `pull_request_target` imeachtaí a dhéanamh `labeled` spreagadh, mar sin a chur leis thosaíonn sé ar reáchtáil úr."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The access token paired with `DOCKERHUB_USERNAME`."
msgstr "An rochtain chomhartha péireáilte le `DOCKERHUB_USERNAME`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The action masks its own result: the fact is the whole rendered tree with every application's credentials, so it never reaches a log regardless of `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS`."
msgstr "Déanann an gníomh a thoradh féin: is é an bhfíric an crann iomlán a rinneadh le gach dintiúir iarratais, mar sin ní shroicheann sé logáil beag beann ar `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The active window has a default retention of 7 entries. A higher count is fine for short bursts of releases, but the active changelog SHOULD stay short enough that scrolling it is cheap."
msgstr "Tá an fhuinneog gníomhach a choinneáil réamhshocraithe 7 iontrálacha. Tá comhaireamh níos airde fíneáil do bursts gearr de eisiúintí, ach an athrú gníomhach SHOULD fanacht gearr go leor go bhfuil scrollaigh sé saor."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The actual app deploy runs inside a **sealed throwaway Docker daemon** and is torn down on exit, so the host's own stack is never touched. Several runners can share one host (or coexist with other workloads) safely."
msgstr "Ritheann an app iarbhír imscaradh taobh istigh **séalaithe caith Docker daemon** agus tá sé torn síos ar an slí amach, mar sin tá an óstach Stack féin riamh i dteagmháil léi. Is féidir le roinnt rádóirí óstach amháin a roinnt (nó cómhaireachtáil le ualach oibre eile) go sábháilte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The adapter `digest` pins nothing today. All ten `implementation: adapter` roles carry the identical placeholder `sha256:` followed by sixty-four zeros, the schema only checks that prefix, and nothing outside the tests reads the field: the running image is resolved through `lookup('container_image', …)` from `services.mcp-adapter.image`. The immutable-source guarantee is therefore declared and not in force, so a lint that rejects a placeholder digest MUST land together with real digests rather than before them."
msgstr "An adapter `digest` bioráin aon rud inniu. Gach deich mbliana `implementation: adapter` róil a dhéanamh ar an sealbhóirí áite comhionann `sha256:` ina dhiaidh sin seasca a ceathair nialais, an scéimre seiceálacha ach go réimír, agus aon rud lasmuigh de na tástálacha léann an réimse: Tá an íomhá ag rith réiteach trí `lookup('container_image', …)` ó `services.mcp-adapter.image`. Dá bhrí sin, dearbhaítear an ráthaíocht foinsí neamh-infhíoraithe agus ní i bhfeidhm, mar sin lint a dhiúltaíonn talamh MUST do shealbhóir áite mar aon le díolamaí fíor seachas os a gcomhair."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The adapter is what bounds that. [`files/mcp/tools.json`](./files/mcp/tools.json) names the nine read tools of `calendar`, `contacts` and `files` — the three categories whose upstream `is_available` is unconditional, so the set does not vary with which optional apps a deployment installs. `svc-ai-mcp-adapter` refuses any tool outside that list and any tool marked `mutating` while `mutating_tools_enabled` is false, and it refuses to start at all if the contract's `schema_sha256` does not match the file. The refusal happens in the sidecar, so it holds for every client regardless of what each renders locally."
msgstr "Is é an adapter cad bounds sin. [`files/mcp/tools.json`](./files/mcp/tools.json) ainmneacha na naoi uirlisí a léamh `calendar`, `contacts` agus `files` — na trí chatagóir a bhfuil a ré reatha `is_available` go bhfuil sé neamhchoinníollach, mar sin ní athraíonn an tacar lena n-aipeanna roghnacha a shuiteáil imscaradh. `svc-ai-mcp-adapter` diúltaíonn aon uirlis lasmuigh den liosta sin agus aon uirlis marcáilte `mutating` le linn `mutating_tools_enabled` bréagach, agus diúltaíonn sé tosú ar chor ar bith má tá an conradh ar `schema_sha256` Ní mheaitseáil leis an gcomhad. Tarlaíonn an diúltú sa sidecar, mar sin tá sé do gach cliant beag beann ar cad a dhéanann gach háit."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The adapter is what bounds that. ```files/mcp/tools.json`` <./files/mcp/tools.json>`__ names the nine read tools of ``calendar``, ``contacts`` and ``files`` — the three categories whose upstream ``is_available`` is unconditional, so the set does not vary with which optional apps a deployment installs. ``svc-ai-mcp-adapter`` refuses any tool outside that list and any tool marked ``mutating`` while ``mutating_tools_enabled`` is false, and it refuses to start at all if the contract’s ``schema_sha256`` does not match the file. The refusal happens in the sidecar, so it holds for every client regardless of what each renders locally."
msgstr "Is é an adapter cad bounds sin. ```files/mcp/tools.json`` <./files/mcp/tools.json>`__ names the nine read tools of ``calendar``, ``contacts`` and ``files`` — the three categories whose upstream ``is_available`` is unconditional, so the set does not vary with which optional apps a deployment installs. ``svc-ai-mcp-adapter`` refuses any tool outside that list and any tool marked ``mutating`` while ``mutating_tools_enabled`` is false, and it refuses to start at all if the contract’s ``schema_sha256`` Ní mheaitseáil leis an gcomhad. Tarlaíonn an diúltú sa sidecar, mar sin tá sé do gach cliant beag beann ar cad a dhéanann gach háit."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The adapter presents `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` to the provider in the header named by `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_AUTH_HEADER` (default `Authorization`), formatted by `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_AUTH_FORMAT` (default `Bearer {key}`, where `{key}` is the credential)."
msgstr "Cuireann an adapter `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` chuig an soláthraí sa header ainmnithe ag `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_AUTH_HEADER` (cineál gas: in airde `Authorization`), formáidithe ag `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_AUTH_FORMAT` (cineál gas: in airde `Bearer {key}`, i gcás `{key}` Is é an dintiúir)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The adapter presents ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY`` to the provider in the header named by ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_AUTH_HEADER`` (default ``Authorization``), formatted by ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_AUTH_FORMAT`` (default ``Bearer {key}``, where ``{key}`` is the credential)."
msgstr "Cuireann an adapter ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY`` chuig an soláthraí sa header ainmnithe ag ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_AUTH_HEADER`` (cineál gas: in airde ``Authorization``), formáidithe ag ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_AUTH_FORMAT`` (cineál gas: in airde ``Bearer {key}``, i gcás ``{key}`` Is é an dintiúir)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The admin UI sits behind Keycloak"
msgstr "Suíonn an Chomhéadain admin taobh thiar Keycloak"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The admin assertion MUST additionally prove admin authorisation (admin panel, management menu, \"Users\" / \"Settings\" / \"Administration\" link visible in the DOM). A scenario that lands on the same surface as `biber` and stops there MUST NOT claim admin coverage."
msgstr "An dearbhú admin MUST chomh maith a chruthú údarú admin (painéal admin, roghchlár bainistíochta, \"Users\" / Baile \"Settings\" / Baile \"Administration\" nasc le feiceáil sa DOM). Cás go tailte ar an dromchla céanna mar `biber` agus stopann ann NÍ MÓR éileamh clúdach admin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The administrator is provisioned as an `XWiki.XWikiUsers` object without a `password` property (see [`templates/xml/user/xwikiusers_object.xml.j2`](./templates/xml/user/xwikiusers_object.xml.j2)), and every privileged operation of the role authenticates as the built-in `superadmin` with `credentials.superadminpassword`. Neither credential is the Keycloak secret the shared persona helpers submit, and `biber` has no XWiki user page at all — only the administrator page is created ([`tasks/03_administrator.yml`](./tasks/03_administrator.yml)) — while the OIDC group mapping stays commented out in [`templates/xwiki.properties.j2`](./templates/xwiki.properties.j2). [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) therefore declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`. The Keycloak coupling is instead proven through XWiki's own login action by the addon spec [`files/playwright/addons/oidc-authenticator.spec.js`](./files/playwright/addons/oidc-authenticator.spec.js)."
msgstr "Tá an riarthóir ar fáil mar `XWiki.XWikiUsers` réad gan `password` home insurance (féach ar [`templates/xml/user/xwikiusers_object.xml.j2`](./templates/xml/user/xwikiusers_object.xml.j2)), agus gach oibríocht phribhléid an ról fhíordheimhnithe mar an-tógtha i `superadmin` le `credentials.superadminpassword`. Níl dintiúir an Keycloak rún a chur faoi bhráid na gcúntóirí persona roinnte, agus `biber` Níl aon XWiki leathanach úsáideora ar chor ar bith - ach an leathanach riarthóir cruthaithe ([`tasks/03_administrator.yml`](./tasks/03_administrator.yml)) — cé go bhfuil an mhapáil ghrúpa OIDC tar éis trácht a dhéanamh uirthi [`templates/xwiki.properties.j2`](./templates/xwiki.properties.j2). [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) dá bhrí sin, dearbhaíonn `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` agus `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`. An Keycloak Tá cúplála cruthaithe ina ionad sin XWiki's gníomh logáil isteach féin ag an spec addon [`files/playwright/addons/oidc-authenticator.spec.js`](./files/playwright/addons/oidc-authenticator.spec.js)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The administrator is provisioned as an ``XWiki.XWikiUsers`` object without a ``password`` property (see ```templates/xml/user/xwikiusers_object.xml.j2`` <./templates/xml/user/xwikiusers_object.xml.j2>`__), and every privileged operation of the role authenticates as the built-in ``superadmin`` with ``credentials.superadminpassword``. Neither credential is the Keycloak secret the shared persona helpers submit, and ``biber`` has no XWiki user page at all — only the administrator page is created (```tasks/03_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/03_administrator.yml>`__) — while the OIDC group mapping stays commented out in ```templates/xwiki.properties.j2`` <./templates/xwiki.properties.j2>`__. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The Keycloak coupling is instead proven through XWiki’s own login action by the addon spec ```files/playwright/addons/oidc-authenticator.spec.js`` <./files/playwright/addons/oidc-authenticator.spec.js>`__."
msgstr "Tá an riarthóir ar fáil mar ``XWiki.XWikiUsers`` réad gan ``password`` home insurance (féach ar ```templates/xml/user/xwikiusers_object.xml.j2`` <./templates/xml/user/xwikiusers_object.xml.j2>`__), and every privileged operation of the role authenticates as the built-in ``superadmin`` with ``credentials.superadminpassword``. Neither credential is the Keycloak secret the shared persona helpers submit, and ``biber`` has no XWiki user page at all — only the administrator page is created (```tasks/03_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/03_administrator.yml>`__) — while the OIDC group mapping stays commented out in ```templates/xwiki.properties.j2`` <./templates/xwiki.properties.j2>`__. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The Keycloak coupling is instead proven through XWiki’s own login action by the addon spec ```files/playwright/addons/oidc-authenticator.spec.js`` <./files/playwright/addons/oidc-authenticator.spec.js>`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The administrator journey is covered bespoke in ``files/playwright/auth.spec.js``, which drives the native form and the ``module=Login&action=logout`` sign-out. The same file owns the deny-probe proving biber cannot reach the admin surface — the provider-side assertion the persona helpers deliberately no longer duplicate. The path back to the generic personas is a Keycloak client for Matomo plus group-driven user provisioning."
msgstr "Tá an turas riarthóir clúdaithe bespoke i ``files/playwright/auth.spec.js``, a thiomáineann an fhoirm dúchais agus an ``module=Login&action=logout`` síniú amach. Is leis an gcomhad céanna nach féidir leis an biber deny-probe chruthú a bhaint amach ar an dromchla admin - an soláthraí-taobh dhearbhú na cúntóirí persona d'aon ghnó a thuilleadh dúblach. Is é an cosán ar ais go dtí an personas cineálach Keycloak do chliaint do Matomo móide soláthar úsáideoirí grúpa-tiomáinte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The administrator journey is covered bespoke in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``: the integrated OIDC path is proven at the STS ``AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity`` tier, and the LDAP variant additionally drives the Console form login and logout. The path back to the generic administrator persona is a Console build that surfaces the configured IdP on its login form."
msgstr "Tá an turas riarthóir clúdaithe bespoke i ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``: tá an cosán comhtháite OIDC cruthaithe ag an STS ``AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity`` sraith, agus an leagan LDAP thiomáineann chomh maith leis an bhfoirm Console logáil isteach agus logout. Is é an cosán ar ais go dtí an persona riarthóir cineálach a thógáil Console go dromchlaí an IdP chumraithe ar a fhoirm logáil isteach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The administrator journey is covered bespoke in `files/playwright/auth.spec.js`, which drives the native form and the `module=Login&action=logout` sign-out. The same file owns the deny-probe proving biber cannot reach the admin surface — the provider-side assertion the persona helpers deliberately no longer duplicate. The path back to the generic personas is a Keycloak client for Matomo plus group-driven user provisioning."
msgstr "Tá an turas riarthóir clúdaithe bespoke i `files/playwright/auth.spec.js`, a thiomáineann an fhoirm dúchais agus an `module=Login&action=logout` síniú amach. Is leis an gcomhad céanna nach féidir leis an biber deny-probe chruthú a bhaint amach ar an dromchla admin - an soláthraí-taobh dhearbhú na cúntóirí persona d'aon ghnó a thuilleadh dúblach. Is é an cosán ar ais go dtí an personas cineálach Keycloak do chliaint do Matomo móide soláthar úsáideoirí grúpa-tiomáinte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The administrator journey is covered bespoke in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`: the integrated OIDC path is proven at the STS `AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity` tier, and the LDAP variant additionally drives the Console form login and logout. The path back to the generic administrator persona is a Console build that surfaces the configured IdP on its login form."
msgstr "Tá an turas riarthóir clúdaithe bespoke i `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`: tá an cosán comhtháite OIDC cruthaithe ag an STS `AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity` sraith, agus an leagan LDAP thiomáineann chomh maith leis an bhfoirm Console logáil isteach agus logout. Is é an cosán ar ais go dtí an persona riarthóir cineálach a thógáil Console go dromchlaí an IdP chumraithe ar a fhoirm logáil isteach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The advertised tool contract matches what the hub serves"
msgstr "Cluichí an conradh uirlis a fógraíodh cad a fhreastalaíonn ar an mol"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The agent MAY bind listening sockets on `localhost` (e.g. `make compose-up`, `python -m http.server`, dev servers). Required for any local end-to-end testing."
msgstr "Ceanglaíonn an gníomhaire MAY soicéid éisteachta ar `localhost` (e.g. `make compose-up`, `python -m http.server`, freastalaithe dev). Riachtanach le haghaidh aon tástáil deiridh-le-deireadh áitiúil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The agent MAY write to the paths listed in `sandbox.filesystem.allowWrite`. All other paths are read-only by default."
msgstr "An gníomhaire MAY scríobh chuig na cosáin atá liostaithe i `sandbox.filesystem.allowWrite`. Gach cosáin eile a léamh-amháin de réir réamhshocraithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The agent MUST NOT create any git commit until every Acceptance Criterion in this document is checked off (`- [x]`)."
msgstr "NÍ MÓR an gníomhaire a chruthú aon tiomantas git go dtí go ndéantar gach Critéar Glacthas sa doiciméad seo a sheiceáil amach (`- [x]`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The agent MUST NOT interrupt work to ask about tier changes. Recommendations appear as a single line at the start of the next response after the threshold is crossed."
msgstr "NÍ MÓR an gníomhaire isteach obair a iarraidh faoi athruithe sraith. Tá moltaí le feiceáil mar líne amháin ag tús an chéad fhreagra eile tar éis an tairseach a thrasnú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The agent MUST NOT repeat this notice within the same conversation."
msgstr "NÍ MÓR an gníomhaire arís an fógra seo laistigh den chomhrá céanna."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The agent MUST NOT run `git checkout`, `git switch`, or any other command that changes `HEAD`, stages files, or modifies the working tree. `git push` operates on refs by name and does not require `<branch>` to be checked out. The push goes to the local `origin` remote."
msgstr "An gníomhaire NACH rith `git checkout`, `git switch`, nó aon ordú eile a athraíonn `HEAD`, comhaid céimeanna, nó athraíonn an crann oibre. `git push` oibríonn sé ar aife de réir ainm agus ní gá `<branch>` a sheiceáil amach. Téann an brú go dtí an áitiúil `origin` iargúlta."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The agent MUST execute this requirement **autonomously** once Proposed Decisions are confirmed. Open clarifications only when a decision is genuinely ambiguous and would otherwise block progress; default to the intent already captured in this document and proceed."
msgstr "An gníomhaire MUST fhorghníomhú an riachtanas seo **go neamhspleách** nuair a dheimhnítear cinntí atá beartaithe. Ní soiléirithe oscailte ach amháin nuair a bhíonn cinneadh fíor ambiguous agus go gcuirfeadh sé bac ar dhul chun cinn; mainneachtain an intinn a gabhadh cheana féin sa doiciméad seo agus dul ar aghaidh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The agent MUST execute this requirement **autonomously**. Open clarifications only when a decision is genuinely ambiguous and would otherwise block progress; default to the intent already captured in this document and proceed. Avoid back-and-forth questions on choices already resolved in [Confirmed Decisions](#confirmed-decisions)."
msgstr "An gníomhaire MUST fhorghníomhú an riachtanas seo **go neamhspleách**. Ní soiléirithe oscailte ach amháin nuair a bhíonn cinneadh fíor ambiguous agus go gcuirfeadh sé bac ar dhul chun cinn ar shlí eile; mainneachtain an intinn a gabhadh cheana féin sa doiciméad seo agus dul ar aghaidh. Seachain ar ais-agus-forth ceisteanna ar roghanna réiteach cheana féin i [Cinntí Daingnithe](#confirmed-decisions)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The agent can do anything the granted devices allow. A GPIO or I2C grant means it can drive whatever is wired to those pins; a video grant means it can watch the room; a serial grant means it can talk to whatever sits on the bus. The allowlist is the entire boundary, which is why an empty one is refused and why the device must be dedicated, single-tenant and network-segmented."
msgstr "Is féidir leis an ngníomhaire aon rud a cheadú na feistí a deonaíodh. GPIO nó mé2Ciallaíonn deontas C féidir é a thiomáint is cuma cad atá sreangaithe leis na bioráin; ciallaíonn deontas físeáin is féidir leis féachaint ar an seomra; ciallaíonn deontas sraitheach féidir é a labhairt le cibé suíonna ar an mbus. Is é an liosta an teorainn ar fad, agus sin an fáth go bhfuil duine folamh a dhiúltú agus cén fáth nach mór an gléas a thiomnú, aon-tionónta agus líonra-segmented."

msgid "The agent holds no model credential: it calls `http://agent-broker:<port>/llm/v1`, and the broker relays the call to LiteLLM with the broker's own virtual key and the owner in the OpenAI `user` field, and logs a `relay` event with owner, platform, path and upstream status."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The agent images run on arm64"
msgstr "Na híomhánna gníomhaire a reáchtáil ar lámh64"

msgid "The agent speaks the Anthropic Messages API, which the LiteLLM gateway serves alongside its OpenAI routes. The role writes ``~/.claude/settings.json`` with an ``env`` block carrying the gateway URL, the workstation’s key and the model aliases to use, so every request leaves the machine through the gateway and is accounted there."
msgstr ""

