# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The allowlist covers the `Bash(*)` wildcard plus the non-Bash tools (`Read`, `Edit`, `Write`, `WebSearch`) and per-domain `WebFetch` entries (the wildcard form is inert, see row below). The real gating for Bash lives in the `ask` and `deny` lists below: mutating `gh`/`docker`/`git` shapes land in `ask`, and structurally destructive shapes (`rm -rf*`, `sudo*`, shell loops, `git push --force*`, mutating `gh api` verbs, etc.) are blocked outright by `deny`. The sandbox (`allowWrite`, `denyRead`, `allowedDomains`) bounds the blast radius of everything that does execute."
msgstr "Clúdaíonn an liosta ligin `Bash(*)` cárta fiáin móide na huirlisí neamh-Bash (`Read`, `Edit`, `Write`, `WebSearch`) agus per-domain `WebFetch` iontrálacha (tá an fhoirm cárta fiáin iert, féach ar a chéile thíos). An gating fíor do Bash saol sa `ask` agus `deny` liostaí thíos: `gh`/ Baile`docker`/ Baile`git` cruthanna talún i `ask`, agus cruthanna struchtúrtha millteach (`rm -rf*`, `sudo*`, lúba bhlaosc, `git push --force*`, mutating `gh api` briathra, etc.) atá bac ar dheis ag `deny`. An bosca gainimh (`allowWrite`, `denyRead`, `allowedDomains`) bounds an ga soinneáin de gach rud a dhéanann fhorghníomhú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The anonymous volume cleanup service."
msgstr "An tseirbhís glanta toirte gan ainm."

# translated-by: libretranslate
