# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The classic failure shape (`DNS [OK]`, `TCP [OK]`, `TLS [FAIL] TimeoutError after 8s`) is an __MTU mismatch__, not a TLS-layer bug. Small packets (TCP-SYN, DNS replies) survive; the larger TLS-ServerHello with the certificate chain is dropped silently because the path MTU is below the bridge MTU and ICMP-needs-frag is filtered upstream. When `auth.docker.io` is OK but `ghcr.io` / `registry-1.docker.io` time out, the chain-length difference between hosts (Cloudflare-fronted ≈ small chain, GitHub/AWS ≈ large chain) confirms MTU as the cause rather than a blanket TLS block."
msgstr "An cruth teip clasaiceach (`DNS [OK]`, `TCP [OK]`, `TLS [FAIL] TimeoutError after 8s`) Tá an MTU mismatch__, ní bug TLS-ciseal. Pacáistí beaga (TCP-SYN, freagraí DNS) maireachtáil; Tá an TLS-ServerHello níos mó leis an slabhra deimhniú thit go ciúin toisc go bhfuil an MTU cosán faoi bhun an MTU droichead agus ICMP-needs-frag scagadh sruth. Nuair a bheidh `auth.docker.io` Is ceart go leor ach `ghcr.io` / Baile `registry-1.docker.io` am amach, an difríocht slabhra-fad idir hóstach (Cloudflare-fronted slabhra beag, GitHub / AWS slabhra mór) Deimhníonn MTU mar an chúis seachas blaincéad TLS bloc."

