# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The double-login is UX-hostile (creds typed twice) and the second hop silently bypasses any 2FA Keycloak enforced on the first hop — anyone with the LDAP password can reach the app even when WebAuthn/OTP is required at the IdP. Friendica's stock `saml` addon (already on disk under `/var/www/html/addon/saml/`) supports a SAML2 AuthnRequest → IdP-initiated SSO with auto-account-creation, which collapses the chain to a single 2FA-gated round-trip."
msgstr "Is é an dúbailte-login UX-óstach (creds clóscríofa faoi dhó) agus seachnaíonn an dara hop go ciúin aon 2FA EN Keycloak i bhfeidhm ar an chéad hop - Is féidir le duine ar bith leis an focal faire LDAP teacht ar an app fiú nuair a WebAuthn / OTP ag teastáil ag an IdP. stoc Friendica `saml` foirm duille: líneach (cheana féin ar an diosca faoi `/var/www/html/addon/saml/`) tacú le SAML2 AuthnRequest → IdP-initiated SSO le uathoibríoch-cuntas-creation, a collapses an slabhra le amháin 2FA-gated babhta-turas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The drill owns the **lifecycle** and nothing else. Every restore is `python3 -m cli.administration.recover`, the same command an operator runs after a real loss, so the drill exercises that tool instead of a second implementation of it."
msgstr "Is leis an druil na **saolré** agus aon rud eile. Tá gach ais `python3 -m cli.administration.recover`, ritheann an t-ordú céanna oibreoir tar éis caillteanas fíor, mar sin cleachtaí an druil uirlis in ionad an dara cur i bhfeidhm de."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The drill proves the `svc-bkp-*` chain forward through the DEPLOYED systemd units (nfs on the export host, volume + secrets on the manager when the app's include closure pulls those roles in, remote pull + device sync on the backup host) and every `recover.py` back (device -> local root -> NFS export, docker volume and host secrets into the live system paths), with marker files that must survive the whole loop: the matrix update pass boots the recovered stack and `verify_recovered_marker.sh` asserts the marker on the live volume. It reuses the round-1 stack instead of spinning a dedicated cluster, and skips cleanly when the app declares no NFS-flagged volume. The backup host is started by `routine/01_bootstrap.sh` (drill profile) and receives its two roles via `extend_inventory`; the pull trust (backup keypair) and the device mount/target/source come from `utils/tests/swarm/write/extras.py`, while `remote-2-local.backup_providers` is derived per round by `utils/tests/swarm/backup_repos.py` from the same placements `extend_inventory` turns into inventory groups, and reaches the deploy through the provisioner's host_vars merge."
msgstr "Cruthaíonn an druil an `svc-bkp-*` slabhra ar aghaidh trí na haonaid córasaithe DEPLOYED (nfs ar an óstach onnmhairithe, toirt + rúin ar an mbainisteoir nuair a áirítear an app dúnadh pulls na róil i, iargúlta tarraingt + gléas sync ar an óstach cúltaca) agus gach `recover.py` ar ais ar ais (gléas - lí fréamhacha áitiúil - lí NFS onnmhairiú, toirt docker agus rúin óstach isteach na cosáin córas beo), le comhaid marcóir nach mór maireachtáil ar an lúb ar fad: pas maitrís buataisí an chairn ghnóthú agus `verify_recovered_marker.sh` Dearbhaíonn an marcóir ar an toirt beo. Reuses sé an babhta-1 Stack in ionad sníomh braisle tiomnaithe, agus scipeanna cleanly nuair a dhearbhaíonn an app aon toirt NFS-flagged. Tá an óstach cúltaca tús ag `routine/01_bootstrap.sh` (Próifíl druileáil) agus faigheann sé a dhá ról trí `extend_inventory`; an t-iontaobhas tarraingt (eochaircheap cúltaca) agus an gléas mount/target/source teacht ó `utils/tests/swarm/write/extras.py`, cé `remote-2-local.backup_providers` díorthaithe in aghaidh an bhabhta ag `utils/tests/swarm/backup_repos.py` ó na socrúcháin chéanna `extend_inventory` casadh i ngrúpaí fardal, agus sroicheann an imscaradh tríd an tsoláthróir host_vars merge."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The drill runs whenever the app declares an NFS-flagged volume (`PRIMARY_NFS_VOLUME`); apps without one skip it, since there is nothing to prove a restore against."
msgstr "Ritheann an druil aon uair a dhearbhaíonn an app toirt NFS-flagged (`PRIMARY_NFS_VOLUME`); apps gan ceann skip é, ós rud é nach bhfuil aon rud a chruthú ar ais i gcoinne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The dump recreates roles and databases, which an application role may not do, so the credentials are the instance's superuser rather than an app's."
msgstr "Athchruthaíonn an dumpáil róil agus bunachair shonraí, nach bhféadfadh ról an iarratais a dhéanamh, mar sin is iad na dintiúir an cás superuser seachas app."

