# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The lid switch is a hardware component on laptops that triggers power state changes (sleep, hibernate, lock) when the lid is closed. On Linux, systemd's `logind` daemon manages lid switch events via `/etc/systemd/logind.conf`. The [`setup-hibernate`](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/setup-hibernate) tool provides hibernation support configuration."
msgstr "Is comhpháirt crua-earraí é an lasc lid ar ríomhairí glúine a chuireann athruithe stáit cumhachta i bhfeidhm (codlata, hibernate, glas) nuair a dhúntar an clúdach. Ar Linux, córasach `logind` Daemon Bainistíonn imeachtaí athrú clúdach trí `/etc/systemd/logind.conf`. An [`setup-hibernate`](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/setup-hibernate) Soláthraíonn uirlis cumraíocht tacaíocht hibernation."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The lid switch is a hardware component on laptops that triggers power state changes (sleep, hibernate, lock) when the lid is closed. On Linux, systemd’s ``logind`` daemon manages lid switch events via ``/etc/systemd/logind.conf``. The ```setup-hibernate`` <https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/setup-hibernate>`__ tool provides hibernation support configuration."
msgstr "Is comhpháirt crua-earraí é an lasc lid ar ríomhairí glúine a chuireann athruithe stáit cumhachta i bhfeidhm (codlata, hibernate, glas) nuair a dhúntar an clúdach. Ar Linux, systemd’s ``logind`` Daemon Bainistíonn imeachtaí athrú clúdach trí ``/etc/systemd/logind.conf``. An ```setup-hibernate`` <https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/setup-hibernate>` Soláthraíonn uirlis cumraíocht tacaíocht hibernation."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The lint (`tests/lint/ansible/roles/meta/test_info.py`) rejects any other top-level key so the file does not become a dumping ground."
msgstr "An lint (`tests/lint/ansible/roles/meta/test_info.py`) Diúltaíonn aon eochair eile ar leibhéal barr mar sin nach bhfuil an comhad a bheith ina talamh dumpála."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The lint test in ``tests/lint/repository/settings/test_claude_sorted.py`` requires every hand-curated array to stay ASCII-sorted ascending so diffs stay reviewable and merge conflicts stay minimal. Tools that auto-extend the file (e.g. permission auto-allowlists) tend to append unsorted; this script puts everything back in order."
msgstr "An tástáil lint i ``tests/lint/repository/settings/test_claude_sorted.py`` Éilíonn gach sraith lámh-curated chun fanacht ASCII-sorted dul suas mar sin diffs fanacht inathbhreithnithe agus coimhlintí chumasc fanacht íosta. Uirlisí go auto-extend an comhad (e.g. cead auto-allowlists) claonadh a chur i gceangal unsorted; cuireann an script gach rud ar ais in ord."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The lint test that fails when a requirement file is fully checked off ([tests/lint/repository/documentation/test_requirements_completeness.py](../../../tests/lint/repository/documentation/test_requirements_completeness.py)) still lives here. It now imports the archive primitives from `pkgmgr.actions.archive`, pulled in via the `dev` extra in [pyproject.toml](../../../pyproject.toml)."
msgstr "An tástáil lint go mainneoidh nuair a dhéantar comhad ceanglas a sheiceáil go hiomlán as ([tests/lint/repository/documentation/test_requirements_completeness.py](../../../tests/lint/repository/documentation/test_requirements_completeness.py)) fós ina chónaí anseo. allmhairí sé anois an primitives cartlann ó `pkgmgr.actions.archive`, tarraingthe isteach tríd an `dev` breise i [pyproject.toml](../../../pyproject.toml)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The list below was produced by grepping each `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js` for `biber|BIBER`. A role appears under \"missing\" iff it has a Playwright spec, no biber references, AND its policy classification (next column) says one is expected. Each checkbox MUST be closed by reading the spec end to end, deciding whether the role is in scope, and then either adding the biber scenario (and the env keys) OR documenting in the commit message why the role is exempt and removing it from this list."
msgstr "Rinneadh an liosta thíos a tháirgeadh trí grepping gach `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js` le haghaidh `biber|BIBER`. Tá ról le feiceáil faoi \"missing\" iff tá sé spec Playwright, aon tagairtí biber, AGUS a aicmiú beartais (An chéad cholún eile) deir go bhfuil duine ag súil leis. Gach MUST bosca seiceála a dhúnadh ag léamh an deireadh spec chun deiridh, cinneadh a dhéanamh an bhfuil an ról i raon feidhme, agus ansin ceachtar cur leis an cás biber (agus na heochracha env) NÓ doiciméadú sa teachtaireacht tiomantas cén fáth go bhfuil an ról díolmhaithe agus é a bhaint as an liosta seo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The list below was produced by grepping each role's `meta/services.yml` for an `ldap` block with `enabled` set to something other than `false`. Each checkbox MUST be closed by reading the spec end to end, deciding whether the role exposes a test-drivable LDAP auth surface, and then either adding the LDAP scenario OR documenting in the commit message why the role is exempt (e.g. the LDAP integration is consumer-side only, with no Playwright- reachable login UI)."
msgstr "Rinneadh an liosta thíos a tháirgeadh trí grepping gach ról `meta/services.yml` le haghaidh `ldap` bloc le `enabled` a leagtar le rud éigin eile seachas `false`. Gach bosca seiceála MUST a dhúnadh ag léamh an deireadh spec chun deireadh a chur, cinneadh a dhéanamh an nochtann an ról a thástáil-tiomáinte LDAP dromchla auth, agus ansin an cás LDAP nó doiciméadú sa teachtaireacht tiomantas cén fáth go bhfuil an ról díolmhaithe (e.g. Is é an comhtháthú LDAP tomhaltóirí-taobh amháin, gan aon Chomhéadain logáil isteach Playwright- reachable)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
