msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The merged map is what the inventory ALSO bakes into host_vars, so feeding the same dict into `CombinedResolver(services_overrides=...)` eliminates the topology-vs-host_vars drift that variant-blind resolution produced."
msgstr "Is é an léarscáil cumaisc cad a bhácálann an ALSO fardal isteach host_vars, mar sin bheathú an deacht céanna isteach `CombinedResolver(services_overrides=...)` eliminates an topology-vs-host_vars sruth go réiteach athraitheach dall a tháirgtear."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The metrics endpoint needs a server-generated token that cannot be pre-seeded into a static scrape config from the inventory. Same pattern as `web-app-gitea`. Gives the `openbao_core_unsealed` gauge."
msgstr "Riachtanais an metrics endpoint le chomhartha freastalaí-ghinithe nach féidir a réamh-síolú isteach i rabhsáil statach config as an fhardal. patrún céanna mar `web-app-gitea`. Tugann an `openbao_core_unsealed` tomhas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The minimum env set for any spec following the persona flows is `APP_BASE_URL`, `CANONICAL_DOMAIN`, and `LOGOUT_URL`. `DASHBOARD_BASE_URL` is rendered only by the dashboard role's own spec, because consumer personas enter at `APP_BASE_URL` directly. Specs that gate on auth additionally read at least one of `OIDC_ISSUER_URL`, `KEYCLOAK_BASE_URL`, plus the persona credentials `ADMIN_USERNAME` / `ADMIN_PASSWORD` and `BIBER_USERNAME` / `BIBER_PASSWORD`. Specs that exercise integrations (Matomo, Discourse, Email, Prometheus, …) read the integration-specific keys defined in [Agent `playwright.env.j2`](../../../../agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md)."
msgstr "Is é an sraith íosta env d'aon spec tar éis sreabhadh persona `APP_BASE_URL`, `CANONICAL_DOMAIN`, agus `LOGOUT_URL`. `DASHBOARD_BASE_URL` Is é a rinneadh ach amháin ag an ról Painéal na nIonstraimí ar spec féin, mar gheall ar personas tomhaltóirí isteach ag `APP_BASE_URL` go díreach. Specs a gheata ar auth léamh chomh maith ar a laghad ar cheann de `OIDC_ISSUER_URL`, `KEYCLOAK_BASE_URL`, móide na dintiúir persona `ADMIN_USERNAME` / Baile `ADMIN_PASSWORD` agus `BIBER_USERNAME` / Baile `BIBER_PASSWORD`. Specs a fheidhmiú integrations (Matomo, Discourse, Ríomhphost, Prometheus, ...) léamh na heochracha comhtháthú-sonrach a shainmhínítear i [Gníomhaire `playwright.env.j2`](../../../../agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mirror workflow runs as stage 8 of the CI pipeline. See [ci.md](../git/pipeline.md). It runs in parallel with the DNS tests and MUST complete before deploy tests start."
msgstr "Ritheann an sreabhadh oibre scátháin mar chéim 8 den phíblíne CI. Féach ar [ci.md](../git/pipeline.md). Ritheann sé i gcomhthráth leis na tástálacha DNS agus MUST iomlán sula dtosaíonn tástálacha imscaradh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The mirrors file is generated into the inventory directory. The inventory creator applies mirror image overrides to host variables via `cli/administration/inventory/provision/mirror_overrides.py`, which reads `mirrors.yml.applications` and writes `applications.{role}.services.{service}.image` (and `.version`) into host vars subject to the per-service `mirror_policy`."
msgstr "Tá an comhad scátháin a ghintear isteach ar an eolaire fardal. Cuireann an cruthaitheoir fardal overrides íomhá scáthán athróg óstáil via `cli/administration/inventory/provision/mirror_overrides.py`, a léann `mirrors.yml.applications` agus scríobhann `applications.{role}.services.{service}.image` (agus `.version`) i vars óstach faoi réir an per-service `mirror_policy`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mode is read as ``compose_mode_force or DEPLOYMENT_MODE`` rather than the bare cluster mode, because ``container_networks`` resolves attachments through that same effective mode: a role with an override must not lose its pin and its overlay at once."
msgstr "Léann an modh mar ``compose_mode_force or DEPLOYMENT_MODE`` seachas an modh braisle lom, mar gheall ar ``container_networks`` réitíonn ceangaltáin tríd an modh céanna éifeachtach: ní mór ról le ródaire chailleadh a bioráin agus a overlay ag an am céanna."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mode selection is a *filter*, not an axis: ``--modes swarm`` keeps the rows whose role can be deployed as a swarm stack, ``--modes \"compose swarm\"`` keeps the rows at least one of the two can take. The shared filter is mode-clause + INFINITO_WHITELIST + INFINITO_BLACKLIST, the order is INFINITO_DISCOVERY_SORT, whose first key sorts clones last (one representative per dna cluster stays ahead of the budget cut, so redundant same-service-set variants fall behind it first), and the lifecycle envelope is INFINITO_LIFECYCLES."
msgstr "Is é an rogha modh *scagaire scagaire*, ní ais: ``--modes swarm`` coimeádann na sraitheanna ar féidir a ról a imscaradh mar Stack swarm, ``--modes \"compose swarm\"`` coimeádann na sraitheanna ar a laghad ar cheann de na dhá is féidir a ghlacadh. Is é an scagaire roinnte mód-clause + INFINITO_WHITELIST + + + + INFINITO_BLACKLIST, Is é an t-ordú INFINITO_DISCOVERY_SORT, a bhfuil an chéad chineál clones eochair seo caite (Fanann ionadaí amháin in aghaidh an bhraisle dna roimh an ghearradh buiséid, mar sin titim iomarcach leaganacha céanna-seirbhíse taobh thiar de na chéad sé), agus is é an clúdach saolré INFINITO_LIFECYCLES."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mode sequence defaults to `compose swarm` and is overridable with `modes=\"compose swarm\"`. The order is always compose first, so the cheaper mode fails fast before the expensive swarm rebuild. Append `k8s` here once that mode exists."
msgstr "Na mainneachtainí ord mód a `compose swarm` agus tá sé overridable le `modes=\"compose swarm\"`. Is é an t-ordú a chumadh i gcónaí ar dtús, mar sin theipeann ar an modh níos saoire go tapa roimh an rebuild Swarm daor. Amharc ar gach eolas `k8s` anseo uair amháin go bhfuil an modh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mode the guide would replay *app* in, or ``''`` when it cannot."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The module is deliberately free of deploy-runtime imports: the CI selection resolves its closure on a runner that has no inventory, no container and no `INFINITO_SRC_DIR`."
msgstr "Tá an modúl saor in aisce d'aon turas ó allmhairí imscartha: réitíonn roghnú CI a dhúnadh ar rádala nach bhfuil fardal, gan aon choimeádán agus gan aon `INFINITO_SRC_DIR`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mount MUST be available before Docker starts. Otherwise the daemon may fall back to the system drive or fail to start cleanly."
msgstr "An MUST mount a bheith ar fáil sula dtosaíonn Docker. Seachas sin d'fhéadfadh an daemon titim ar ais go dtí an tiomáint córas nó theipeann a thosú go glan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The name never holds a space: the ``whitelist`` and ``priority`` workflow inputs are space-separated lists, so a display name with a space in it would make a two-role list unparseable."
msgstr "An t-ainm riamh i seilbh spás: an ``whitelist`` agus ``priority`` Tá ionchuir sreabhadh oibre liostaí spás-scartha, mar sin bheadh ainm taispeáint le spás ann a dhéanamh liosta dhá-role unparseable."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The name of the matching role directory."
msgstr "Ainm an eolaire ról meaitseáil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The names in declaration order, aliases substituted."
msgstr "Cuirtear na hainmneacha in ord dearbhaithe, ailiases in ionad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The names payload is stored under in THIS generation."
msgstr "Stóráiltear pá-ualach na n-ainmneacha faoin ghlúin seo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The naming conventions below are additionally checked locally by the lint test [test_branch_name.py](../../../../tests/lint/repository/naming/test_branch_name.py), which fails `make test-lint` when the checked-out branch uses an unknown prefix (e.g. `feat/` instead of `feature/`) or a non-kebab-case description."
msgstr "Déantar na coinbhinsiúin ainmniúcháin thíos a sheiceáil go háitiúil leis an tástáil lint [test_branch_name.py](../../../../tests/lint/repository/naming/test_branch_name.py), a mhainníonn `make test-lint` nuair a úsáideann an brainse a sheiceáil amach réimír anaithnid (e.g. `feat/` in ionad `feature/`) nó tuairisc ar chás neamhchúitimh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The narrow case is what a deploy job actually sees, because the matrix hands every row exactly one kind. Reading that narrowness as a demand would turn every condition the applying step tolerates into a red row on every deploy: a loop device it could not claim, a pool another job still holds. The run's own input decides instead."
msgstr "Is é an cás caol cad a fheiceann post imscaradh iarbhír, mar gheall ar na lámha maitrís gach chéile go díreach cineál amháin. Léitheoireacht go mbeadh cúngacht mar éileamh dul gach coinníoll an chéim i bhfeidhm fhulaingt isteach i ndiaidh a chéile dearg ar gach imscaradh: gléas lúb nach bhféadfadh sé a éileamh, tá post eile a chomhthiomsú fós. Cinneann ionchur an reáchtáil féin ina ionad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The next `make compose-deploy mode=update apps=web-app-hugo` will pull the image, restart nginx, and serve the freshly rendered output."
msgstr "An chéad cheann eile `make compose-deploy mode=update apps=web-app-hugo` Beidh tarraingt ar an íomhá, atosú nginx, agus freastal ar an aschur úr a rinneadh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The next stage in the pipeline MUST NOT execute when the previous stage classified the plugin as `incompatible`."
msgstr "An chéad chéim eile sa phíblíne NÍ MÓR fhorghníomhú nuair a rangaíodh an chéim roimhe an breiseán mar `incompatible`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The nfs-server uses the userspace `nfs-ganesha` (`ganesha`) flavor in every runtime; `services.nfs-server.flavor` in `roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/meta/services.yml` is the SPOT, and `kernel` is a per-inventory override. Ganesha is packaged for the `Debian` and `RedHat` os families only. Kernel `nfsd` in a privileged DinD node is wedge-prone: the export can be present yet the controller mount returns ENOENT, and `exportfs` can stick in D-state. If a swarm step hangs at `Reload NFS exports` from a stuck kernel-NFS mount, you MUST recover with `make swarm-clean` on the host; see the NFS gotcha in [Roundtrip Loop](roundtrip.md). You MUST NOT fall back to a compose-only sweep while swarm is blocked."
msgstr "Úsáideann an nfs-freastalaí an spás úsáideora `nfs-ganesha` (`ganesha`) blas i ngach runtime; `services.nfs-server.flavor` i `roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/meta/services.yml` is é an phatrún, agus `kernel` Is override per-fardail. Tá Ganesha pacáistithe don `Debian` agus `RedHat` os teaghlaigh amháin. Uisce agus Séarachas `nfsd` i nód phribhléid DinD ding-prone: Is féidir leis an onnmhairiú a bheith i láthair go fóill an rialtóir mount tuairisceáin ENOENT, agus `exportfs` Is féidir bata i D-stáit. Má hangs céim swarm ag `Reload NFS exports` ó mount Eithne-NFS bhfostú, MUST tú a ghnóthú le `make swarm-clean` ar an óstach; féach ar an gotcha NFS i [Seirbhís do Chustaiméirí](roundtrip.md). NÍ MÓR duit titim ar ais go dtí an cuma-amháin agus tá swarm bac."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The nightly timers (volume 01:00, nfs 01:30, secrets 01:45, device 02:00, remote pull 00:30) run independently of every step above and never fire during a lab run."
msgstr "An timers oíche (toirt 01:00, nfs 01:30, rúin 01:45, gléas 02:00, tarraingt iargúlta 00:30) reáchtáil go neamhspleách ar gach céim thuas agus ní tine le linn reáchtáil saotharlainne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The node hidden service exposes Mailu's mail ports in addition to `80`, via extra `HiddenServicePort` entries: `HiddenServicePort 25`, `587`, `465`, `143`, `993` → Mailu's local front binds on `127.0.0.1`. Mailu is then reachable at `<node>.onion` for SMTP/submission/IMAP."
msgstr "Léirigh an tseirbhís i bhfolach nód Mailu's calafoirt phost chomh maith `80`, trí breise `HiddenServicePort` iontrálacha: `HiddenServicePort 25`, `587`, `465`, `143`, `993` → → Mailu's ceangail tosaigh áitiúil ar `127.0.0.1`. Tá Mailu ansin reachable ag `<node>.onion` le haghaidh SMTP/submission/IMAP."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The number of discarded translations; their entries stay unchanged."
msgstr "Líon na n-aistriúchán a scriosadh; a n-iontrálacha fanacht gan athrú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The number of dumps replayed."
msgstr "Athsheoladh líon na dumpaí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The oauth2 ACL in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) blacklists only `/login`, and `sys-svc-proxy` renders a blacklist as *expose everything by default, then protect the listed paths*. The helper lands on `/`, which is public, so the proxy never intercepts it and the Keycloak round trip never starts."
msgstr "Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil2 ACL i [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) blacklists ach amháin `/login`, agus `sys-svc-proxy` déanann blacklist mar *gach rud a nochtadh de réir réamhshocraithe, ansin na cosáin atá liostaithe a chosaint*. Na tailte cúntóir ar `/`, atá poiblí, mar sin an seachfhreastalaí riamh intercepts sé agus an Keycloak turas bhabhta Tosaíonn riamh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The oauth2 ACL in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ blacklists only ``/login``, and ``sys-svc-proxy`` renders a blacklist as *expose everything by default, then protect the listed paths*. The helper lands on ``/``, which is public, so the proxy never intercepts it and the Keycloak round trip never starts."
msgstr "Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil2 ACL i ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ blacklists only ``/login``, and ``sys-svc-proxy`` renders a blacklist as *expose everything by default, then protect the listed paths*. The helper lands on ``/``, atá poiblí, mar sin an seachfhreastalaí riamh intercepts sé agus an Keycloak turas bhabhta Tosaíonn riamh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The offered modes are already narrowed by the run's ``--modes`` input, the onion states by its ``--tor`` input and the two pools by ``--distros`` and ``--filesystem``, so this catches a pin that fights the role, the variant, or the run's own axes with one check each."
msgstr "Na modhanna atá ar fáil a chaolú cheana féin ag an reáchtáil ar ``--modes`` ionchur, na stáit oinniún ag a ``--tor`` ionchur agus an dá linnte ag ``--distros`` agus ``--filesystem``, mar sin gabhálacha seo bioráin go troideanna an ról, an leagan, nó aiseanna an reáchtáil féin le seiceáil amháin gach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The official Baserow SSO feature is Enterprise-only. This role instead gates the community image with the shared Keycloak oauth2-proxy and installs a small trusted-header bridge in the Baserow backend. The bridge trusts the identity headers injected by nginx after oauth2-proxy authentication and converts them into native Baserow JWT refresh/access tokens for the frontend."
msgstr "The official Baserow Is gné SSO Fiontraíocht-amháin. An ról seo ina ionad sin geataí an íomhá pobail leis an roinnte Keycloak riachtanais uisce: measartha2-proxy agus cuireann sé droichead beag iontaofa-ceann sa Baserow siar. iontaobhais an droichead na headers aitheantais instealladh ag nginx tar éis oauth2-proxy fíordheimhnithe agus athraíonn iad i dúchais Baserow JWT tokens refresh / rochtain don tosaigh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The official installer is **downloaded at runtime** and verified before execution:"
msgstr "Is é an suiteálaí oifigiúil **íoslódáil ag runtime** agus a fhíorú roimh fhorghníomhú:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The offset a run was given, as written. ``None`` reads ``INFINITO_CI_OFFSET``; :func:`offset_index` decides what it means."
msgstr "Tugadh an fritháireamh a reáchtáil, mar atá scríofa. ``None`` léamha ``INFINITO_CI_OFFSET``; :func:`offset_index` chinneann cad a chiallaíonn sé."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The one accepted ``--set`` key shape for a credential override."
msgstr "Ghlac an ceann ``--set`` cruth eochair do override credential."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The one-shot smoke mail the msmtp prefix puts in front of a probe."
msgstr "An deataigh aon-lámhaigh phost cuireann an réimír msmtp os comhair probe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion axis of the CI deploy matrix: what it may do, and to which rows."
msgstr "An ais oinniún an maitrís CI imscaradh: cad is féidir é a dhéanamh, agus a sraitheanna."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion identity (key files) is minted/reused by ``cli.administration.inventory.onion``; this provisioner is the single spot that writes the resulting address into ``applications.svc-net-tor.services.tor.node`` of the host_vars — so consumers read it via ``lookup('config', 'svc-net-tor', 'services.tor.node')`` with no env indirection."
msgstr "Féiniúlacht oinniún (comhaid eochair) Tá mionaithe / athúsáid ag ``cli.administration.inventory.onion``; Is é an soláthróir an láthair amháin a scríobhann an seoladh mar thoradh air isteach ``applications.svc-net-tor.services.tor.node`` de na host_vars – mar sin léann tomhaltóirí é ``lookup('config', 'svc-net-tor', 'services.tor.node')`` gan aon indírigh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion key is minted offline during inventory build (``cli.administration.inventory.onion``) and stored in the inventory, so the address is stable across redeploys and restorable from a backup."
msgstr "Tá an eochair oinniún minted as líne le linn a thógáil fardal (``cli.administration.inventory.onion``) agus a stóráil san fhardal, mar sin tá an seoladh cobhsaí ar fud ath-imlonnú agus soscrios ó cúltaca."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion key is minted offline during inventory build (`cli.administration.inventory.onion`) and stored in the inventory, so the address is stable across redeploys and restorable from a backup."
msgstr "Tá an eochair oinniún minted as líne le linn a thógáil fardal (`cli.administration.inventory.onion`) agus a stóráil san fhardal, mar sin tá an seoladh cobhsaí ar fud ath-imlonnú agus soscrios ó cúltaca."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion state is spelled `+clearnet` rather than `-tor` because a role id may itself end in `-tor`."
msgstr "Tá an stát oinniún litrithe `+clearnet` seachas seachas `-tor` toisc go bhféadfadh ról id féin deireadh i `-tor`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion state spells out as ``+tor``/``+clearnet`` rather than as a ``-tor`` suffix: a role id may itself end in ``-tor`` (``svc-net-tor``), and a suffix that eats the tail of a role name selects a different role in silence."
msgstr "An stát oinniún spells amach mar ``+tor``/ Baile``+clearnet`` seachas mar ``-tor`` iarmhír: d'fhéadfadh ról id féin deireadh i ``-tor`` (``svc-net-tor``), agus iarmhír a itheann an eireaball ainm ról roghnaíonn ról difriúil i tost."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion states one *mode* is worth running for a priority row."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The only account that form accepts is Checkmk's built-in `cmkadmin`, whose password comes from `credentials.cmk_password` (`CMK_PASSWORD` in the container env) — a site-local secret unrelated to the Keycloak credentials the personas use. No Checkmk user is provisioned for a non-admin identity at all. With SSO enabled both personas run through the header-auth chain."
msgstr "Is é an t-aon chuntas go nglacann an fhoirm Checkmk's tógtha isteach `cmkadmin`, a thagann a focal faire ó `credentials.cmk_password` (`CMK_PASSWORD` sa choimeádán env) — rún áitiúil láithreáin nach mbaineann leis an Keycloak dintiúir an duine a úsáid. Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil Checkmk Tá úsáideoir ar fáil le haghaidh aitheantais neamh-riaracháin ar chor ar bith. Le SSO cumasaithe araon personas reáchtáil tríd an slabhra header-auth."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The only account that form accepts is Checkmk’s built-in ``cmkadmin``, whose password comes from ``credentials.cmk_password`` (``CMK_PASSWORD`` in the container env) — a site-local secret unrelated to the Keycloak credentials the personas use. No Checkmk user is provisioned for a non-admin identity at all. With SSO enabled both personas run through the header-auth chain."
msgstr "Is é an t-aon chuntas go nglacann an fhoirm Checkmks-tógtha i ``cmkadmin``, a thagann a focal faire ó ``credentials.cmk_password`` (``CMK_PASSWORD`` sa choimeádán env) — rún áitiúil láithreáin nach mbaineann leis an Keycloak dintiúir an duine a úsáid. Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil Checkmk Tá úsáideoir ar fáil le haghaidh aitheantais neamh-riaracháin ar chor ar bith. Le SSO cumasaithe araon personas reáchtáil tríd an slabhra header-auth."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The operator MUST review the staged diff and message before committing."
msgstr "MUST an t-oibreoir athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar an diff stáitse agus teachtaireacht roimh cion."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The orchestrator and the push entry workflow (`entry-push-latest.yml`) cancel in-progress runs on every ref except `main`, which no automatic trigger cancels. A `pull_request_target` run inherits `refs/heads/main` as its ref, so the orchestrator does not cancel there either; per-PR supersession is handled by the entry workflow's own `pr-ci-*` group. See [configuration.md](../../tools/github/actions/configuration.md)."
msgstr "An t-imreoir agus an sreabhadh oibre iontrála bhrú (`entry-push-latest.yml`) a chur ar ceal i-progress ritheann ar gach ref ach amháin `main`, nach gcuireann aon truicir uathoibríoch ar ceal. Amharc ar gach eolas `pull_request_target` a reáchtáil hoidhreachtaí `refs/heads/main` mar a athshocrú, mar sin ní chuireann an t-eolaire ar ceal ann; déantar ollseisiún per-PR a láimhseáil ag an sreabhadh oibre iontrála féin `pr-ci-*` grúpa. Féach ar [configuration.md](../../tools/github/actions/configuration.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The orchestrator runs the following stages in order:"
msgstr "Ritheann an t-eolaire na céimeanna seo a leanas chun:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The orchestrator's `wait-fork-prereq-run` job **skips the wait** for the privileged fork images."
msgstr "An t-imreoir `wait-fork-prereq-run` post office **skips an fanacht** do na híomhánna forc phribhléid."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The order in `ORDERED_HANDLERS` MUST respect data dependencies. Example: `infinito_container` runs after `passthrough` so it can read the resolved `INFINITO_DISTRO`."
msgstr "An t-ordú i `ORDERED_HANDLERS` MUST urramú spleáchais sonraí. Sampla: `infinito_container` Ritheann tar éis `passthrough` ionas gur féidir é a léamh ar an réiteach `INFINITO_DISTRO`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The order is a precondition, not a preference. `baudolo-restore --empty` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays in the next; a booting consumer recreates it in between and the dump's own `CREATE TABLE` fails — which is how zammad turned this drill red with `relation \"ar_internal_metadata\" already exists`. The chain refuses the replay while a consumer runs, so a drill that got the order wrong would fail loudly instead of flaking."
msgstr "Is réamhchoinníoll é an t-ordú, ní rogha. `baudolo-restore --empty` réamh-ghlanann an scéimre i seisiún psql amháin agus replays sa chéad cheann eile; tomhaltóir tosaithe recreates sé i idir agus an dump's féin `CREATE TABLE` go mainneoidh - cé chomh zammad iompaigh an druil dearg le `relation \"ar_internal_metadata\" already exists`. Diúltaíonn an slabhra an replay agus ritheann tomhaltóir, mar sin bheadh druil a fuair an t-ordú mícheart theipeann os ard in ionad scealóga."

msgid "The order of those mocks is load-bearing and the router is not what reads it. `AI_AGENT_MODEL` takes `AI_MOCK_ALIASES | first`, so the mock declared first becomes the agent broker's model and its window becomes the context the broker gates platforms on. Declaring the 4096 mock first withheld `hermes`, whose `min_context` is 64000, and the broker's CLI test failed with the reason spelled out. The widest mock therefore leads. A sharper fix would be to have `AI_AGENT_MODEL` pick the mock with the largest declared context instead of the first one, which would make the order irrelevant."
msgstr ""

