msgid "The pinned image runs on arm64"
msgstr "Ritheann an íomhá pinned ar lámh64"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The pinned release is inference-only; an MCP-capable one may be selected only after source inspection proves per-server routes, exact tool allowlists and the credential lifecycle."
msgstr "Is é an scaoileadh pinned tátal-amháin; Is féidir le MCP-capable amháin a roghnú ach amháin tar éis go gcruthóidh iniúchadh foinse bealaí in aghaidh an-freastalaí, chead liostaí uirlis cruinn agus an saolré credential."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The pins are parsed by hand instead of through ``utils.cache.yaml`` because every ``lint-*`` target depends on ``install-lint``, which bootstraps the toolchain on a bare interpreter -- PyYAML is not installed yet at that point, and importing it here fails the whole lint stage with ``ModuleNotFoundError``. ``_parse_pins`` therefore only understands the two-level shape this one file uses; ``tests/unit/python/utils/install/lint/test_pinned_versions.py`` cross-checks it against PyYAML so the two readings cannot drift apart."
msgstr "Na bioráin atá parsed de láimh in ionad trí ``utils.cache.yaml`` mar gheall ar gach ``lint-*`` ag brath ar sprioc ar ``install-lint``, a buataisítraps an toolchain ar ateangaire lom - nach bhfuil PyYAML suiteáilte go fóill ag an bpointe sin, agus a allmhairiú theipeann anseo an chéim lint iomlán le ``ModuleNotFoundError``. ``_parse_pins`` Dá bhrí sin, ní thuigeann ach an cruth dhá leibhéal seo a úsáideann an comhad amháin; ``tests/unit/python/utils/install/lint/test_pinned_versions.py`` cros-seiceáil sé i gcoinne PyYAML mar sin ní féidir leis an dá léamh sruth óna chéile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The pins are read by ``utils/install/lint/pinned.py``, which every lint installer calls:"
msgstr "Na bioráin a léamh ag ``utils/install/lint/pinned.py``, a glaonna gach suiteálaí lint:"

