msgid "The pipeline owns three responsibilities for one Nextcloud plugin (app):"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The placement rule is per check. The catalog \"Position\" column uses these labels."
msgstr "Tá an riail socrúcháin in aghaidh na seiceála. An chatalóg \"Position\" Úsáideann colún na lipéid."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The plain image tag becomes a manifest list. Anything that inspects the tag expecting a single image manifest sees an index instead."
msgstr "Is é an chlib íomhá plain liosta follasach. Rud ar bith a iniúchadh ar an chlib ag súil le léiriú íomhá amháin Feiceann innéacs ina ionad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The plain-scalar rule is deliberately narrower than YAML's: a plain scalar must start with a letter, an underscore or a slash, and may then carry only ``[A-Za-z0-9_./+@:-]`` and spaces. That excludes every leading character PyYAML's implicit resolvers key off, so no accepted plain scalar can come back as an int, float, bool, timestamp or null."
msgstr "Is é an riail plain-scalar d'aon ghnó níos cúinge ná YAML: ní mór scalar plain tús a chur le litir, underscore nó Slais, agus d'fhéadfadh a dhéanamh ansin ach amháin ``[A-Za-z0-9_./+@:-]`` agus spásanna. Ní áirítear gach príomh-charachtar réiteoirí intuigthe PyYAML ar eochair amach, mar sin ní féidir aon scalar glacadh plain teacht ar ais mar orlach, snámhphointe, bool, amstamp nó neamhní."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The plan runs the same pipeline the deploy jobs discover through (``cli.meta.ci.matrix``), so what the table shows and what CI deploys cannot diverge. One row per ``role#variant`` candidate in global query order, with the chunk it falls into and the axes it was assigned."
msgstr "Ritheann an plean an phíblíne chéanna na poist imscaradh amach tríd (``cli.meta.ci.matrix``), mar sin cad a léiríonn an tábla agus cad nach féidir CI imscaradh éagsúil. Sraith amháin in aghaidh an ``role#variant`` iarrthóir in ord cheist domhanda, leis an smután thagann sé isteach agus na haiseanna sannadh é."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The platform MUST NOT deploy one all-powerful OpenAPI-to-MCP process holding administrator credentials for every application. It MUST provide one reusable, immutable adapter implementation but instantiate it once per provider application or per equally isolated trust domain. Each adapter instance MUST attach only to the provider's existing local network, receive only that provider's least-privileged credential, expose a distinct MCP endpoint, and remain addressable by the provider's `application_id`."
msgstr "NÍ MÓR an t-ardán imscaradh amháin OpenAPI-go-MCP próiseas a bhfuil dintiúir riarthóir do gach iarratas. MUST sé a chur ar fáil ar cheann reusable, cur i bhfeidhm adapter immutable ach toirtigh sé uair amháin in aghaidh an t-iarratas soláthraí nó in aghaidh an chomh fearainn muinín iargúlta. Gach cás adapter MUST ag gabháil ach amháin le líonra áitiúil an tsoláthraí atá ann cheana féin, a fháil ach amháin go bhfuil an soláthraí ar a laghad-privileged dintiúir, nochtadh ar leith MCP endpoint, agus fanacht i ngleic ag an soláthraí ar `application_id`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The platform already reserves a user key per role, so `hermes` and `openclaw` existed as accounts, non-privileged and each with its own mailbox, before either role claimed one. Claiming the key is what turns a reservation into an identity the agent may authenticate as, and gives the account its description."
msgstr "Forchoimeádann an t-ardán eochair úsáideora in aghaidh an róil cheana féin, mar sin `hermes` agus `openclaw` ann mar chuntais, neamh-privileged agus gach ceann acu lena bhosca poist féin, sular éiligh ceachtar ról ceann. Is é an eochair a athrú cad a tharlaíonn áirithint i bhféiniúlacht féadfaidh an gníomhaire a fhíordheimhniú mar, agus tugann sé an cuntas a chur síos."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The play used to consume a task file per group, generated at setup time. The order is derived from data that already lives in the roles, so it is resolved here instead and read through the `group_roles` lookup."
msgstr "An spraoi a úsáidtear chun ithe comhad tasc in aghaidh an ghrúpa, a ghintear ag am thus. Tá an t-ordú a dhíorthaítear ó shonraí a bhfuil cónaí orthu cheana féin sna róil, mar sin tá sé réiteach anseo ina ionad sin agus a léamh tríd an `group_roles` cuma."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The play's variable scope. Only the subset that `_stable_variables_signature` reads influences the key."
msgstr "Raon feidhme athróg an dráma. Ach an fo-thacar go `_stable_variables_signature` léann tionchar an eochair."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The play-scoped carrier of the rendered applications payload: the fact name `_INFINITO_APPLICATIONS_RENDERED`, `merged_applications_cache_key`, and the reader `get_merged_applications` consults before it renders."
msgstr "An t-iompróir play-scoped de na pálasta iarratais a rinneadh: an t-ainm `_INFINITO_APPLICATIONS_RENDERED`, `merged_applications_cache_key`, agus an léitheoir `get_merged_applications` dul i gcomhairle sula ndéanann sé."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The play-scoped carrier: fact name, `merged_applications_cache_key`, and the reader that serves the carried payload."
msgstr "An t-iompróir play-scoped: ainm fíoras, `merged_applications_cache_key`, agus an léitheoir a fhreastalaíonn ar an pálasta iompar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The playbook is designed for developers who require Docker in their local development environments. It simplifies the process of Docker installation and configuration, making it straightforward for developers to start containerizing their applications without the complexities often encountered in a server or production environment."
msgstr "Tá an leabhar súgartha deartha d'fhorbróirí a éilíonn Docker ina dtimpeallachtaí forbartha áitiúla. Simplíonn sé an próiseas suiteála agus cumraíocht Docker, rud a chiallaíonn sé simplí d'fhorbróirí chun tús a chur coimeádán a n-iarratas gan na castachtaí minic a bhíonn i dtimpeallacht freastalaí nó táirgthe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The plugin answers ``initialize`` without credentials, because that call is capability negotiation and carries no data. Everything after it is guarded: an unauthenticated ``tools/list`` is refused and returns no tool inventory."
msgstr "Na freagraí breiseán ``initialize`` gan dintiúir, toisc go bhfuil an glaoch idirbheartaíocht cumas agus déanann aon sonraí. Gach rud tar éis é a chosaint: aineolach ``tools/list`` diúltaíodh agus tuairisceáin aon fhardal uirlis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The plugin answers `initialize` without credentials, because that call is capability negotiation and carries no data. Everything after it is guarded: an unauthenticated `tools/list` is refused and returns no tool inventory."
msgstr "Na freagraí breiseán `initialize` gan dintiúir, toisc go bhfuil an glaoch idirbheartaíocht cumas agus déanann aon sonraí. Gach rud tar éis é a chosaint: aineolach `tools/list` diúltaíodh agus tuairisceáin aon fhardal uirlis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The plugin lives in the `system` plugin group so it can intercept every request via `onAfterInitialise`. It MUST run BEFORE the Joomla local form-login plugin in the system event chain so the redirect short-circuits any local-account authentication attempt. System plugins are ordered alphabetically. `keycloak` ranks before `users`, which is the typical local-form gate."
msgstr "Saol an breiseán sa `system` grúpa breiseán ionas gur féidir é a idircheapadh gach iarratas via `onAfterInitialise`. MÓR é a reáchtáil BEFORE an Joomla breiseán foirm-login áitiúil sa slabhra ócáid córas mar sin an athdhíriú gearr-chuaird aon iarracht fíordheimhnithe cuntas áitiúil. Breiseáin Córas a ordú aibítre. `keycloak` céimeanna roimh `users`, a bhfuil an geata tipiciúil áitiúil-form."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The plugin needs to be manually activated in the admin interface. would be nice if this is automatized as well"
msgstr "Ní mór an breiseán a ghníomhachtú de láimh sa chomhéadan admin. bheadh deas má tá sé seo uathoibriú chomh maith"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The plugin reads its runtime config from the Joomla container's environment, so the same plugin code works against any Keycloak realm without manual reconfiguration through the Joomla admin UI."
msgstr "Léann an breiseán a config runtime ón Joomla coimeádán timpeallacht, mar sin oibríonn an cód breiseán céanna i gcoinne aon Keycloak realm gan reconfiguration láimhe tríd an Joomla Chomhéadain admin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The plugin trusts the Keycloak-issued ID token. The `jumbojett/openid-connect-php` library validates the JWT signature against the realm's JWKS, so the issuer URL MUST be reachable from the Joomla container at the time the user authenticates."
msgstr "Iontaobhais an breiseán an Keycloakchomhartha aitheantais eisithe. An bhfuil `jumbojett/openid-connect-php` bailíochtaíonn leabharlann an síniú JWT i gcoinne JWKS an réimse, mar sin an URL eisitheoir MUST a bheith insroichte ó Joomla coimeádán ag an am fíoraíonn an t-úsáideoir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The plugin's PHP dependencies (`jumbojett/openid-connect-php`) are vendored at deploy time inside the Joomla container. Composer is baked into the role's custom image by `roles/web-app-joomla/files/Dockerfile`. The role-side `tasks/08_oidc_plugin.yml` copies the plugin source into the container, runs `composer install --no-dev`, and installs the plugin via the Joomla CLI:"
msgstr "Braitheann an breiseán ar PHP (`jumbojett/openid-connect-php`) a dhíol ag am imscaradh taobh istigh den Joomla coimeádán. Tá múirín bácáilte isteach sa ról ar íomhá saincheaptha ag `roles/web-app-joomla/files/Dockerfile`. An ról-thaobh `tasks/08_oidc_plugin.yml` cóipeanna an fhoinse breiseán isteach sa choimeádán, Ritheann `composer install --no-dev`, agus installs an breiseán tríd an Joomla CLI:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The plugin's built-in fallback computed from `DOMAIN_PRIMARY`, the `web-app-mailu` group, the `no-reply` user, and related inputs."
msgstr "An breiseán tógtha-i fallback ríomh ó `DOMAIN_PRIMARY`, an `web-app-mailu` grúpa, an `no-reply` úsáideoir, agus ionchuir a bhaineann."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The point is to make the safe path the natural path."
msgstr "Is é an pointe a dhéanamh ar an cosán sábháilte an cosán nádúrtha."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The point: an assistant with real reach into the home, but the agent runtime stays isolated and the Pi host stays untouched. Capabilities come through MCP tools, not host access."
msgstr "An pointe: cúntóir le fíor teacht isteach sa bhaile, ach fanann an gníomhaire runtime iargúlta agus fanann an óstach Pi untouched. Tagann cumais trí uirlisí MCP, gan rochtain óstach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The policy `.hcl` templates are rendered to the host config directory and mounted at `/openbao/policies/`, deliberately **outside** `/openbao/config/`: the server parses every file in its config directory as server configuration, so a policy file there breaks startup."
msgstr "An beartas `.hcl` teimpléid a dhéantar ar an eolaire choigiltis óstach agus suite ag `/openbao/policies/`, d'aon ghnó **taobh amuigh** `/openbao/config/`: parses an freastalaí gach comhad ina eolaire config mar chumraíocht freastalaí, mar sin comhad polasaí sosanna ann tosaithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The pool's ``size`` bounds the slice docker hands the bridge, so the gateway is derived from that slice rather than from the enclosing supernet - they agree only while the pool starts on a slice boundary."
msgstr "An linn snámha ``size`` teorainneacha an docker slice lámha an droichead, mar sin tá an geata a dhíorthaítear ón slice seachas ón supernet enclosing - aontaíonn siad ach amháin nuair a thosaíonn an linn snámha ar theorainn slice."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The port is the single source of truth ``svc-net-tor services.tor.ports.local.socks``; only the host varies by caller context (loopback for host-network consumers, ``host.docker.internal`` for a bridged sibling container, ``0.0.0.0`` for the daemon bind)."
msgstr "Is é an calafort an fhoinse amháin na fírinne ``svc-net-tor services.tor.ports.local.socks``; ní hionann ach an t-óstach trí chomhthéacs glaoiteora (athsheoladh do thomhaltóirí brú-líonra, ``host.docker.internal`` le haghaidh coimeádán deartháireacha, ``0.0.0.0`` don daemon ceangal)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The post-login assertion MUST prove the session is real, in this order of preference: a user-menu or persona-name string visible in the DOM, a navigation element only rendered for authenticated users, a URL pattern unique to authenticated state. Stopping at a 2xx status code or a static text snippet that exists logged-out as well MUST NOT count as a session check."
msgstr "An dearbhú iar-login MUST chruthú go bhfuil an seisiún fíor, san ord seo de rogha: teaghrán úsáideora-menu nó persona-ainm le feiceáil sa DOM, eilimint nascleanúint a rinneadh ach amháin d'úsáideoirí fíordheimhnithe, patrún URL uathúil stát fíordheimhnithe. Stopadh ag 2xx cód stádas nó snippet téacs statach atá logáilte amach chomh maith NÍ MÓR chomhaireamh mar sheiceáil seisiún."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The precedence is:"
msgstr "Is é an tosaíocht:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The prefixed form is byte-identical to the container's ``.Config.Image`` after deploy, so it can be matched against a running container exactly."
msgstr "Tá an fhoirm chomhfhreagraigh leis an gcoimeádán ``.Config.Image`` tar éis imscaradh, ionas gur féidir é a mheaitseáil i gcoinne coimeádán ag rith go díreach."

msgid "The primary checkout's path, or ``repo_root`` when git cannot say."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary objective of this role is to provide a straightforward and efficient method for setting up Java, specifically JDK 11, on personal computers or development environments. This setup is essential for developers who work with Java or run applications that require the Java runtime environment."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an róil seo modh simplí agus éifeachtúil a chur ar fáil chun cur ar bun Java, go sonrach JDK 11, ar ríomhairí pearsanta nó timpeallachtaí forbartha. Tá an thus riachtanach d'fhorbróirí a oibríonn le Java nó iarratais a reáchtáil a éilíonn an Java timpeallacht runtime."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to automate the process of swapfile creation, ensuring that the system has sufficient swap space to handle memory-intensive tasks and maintain overall performance."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná próiseas cruthaithe babhtála a uathoibriú, ag cinntiú go bhfuil spás leordhóthanach ag an gcóras chun tascanna diana cuimhne a láimhseáil agus feidhmíocht fhoriomlán a choinneáil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to configure WireGuard on a client by setting appropriate MTU values on network interfaces. This ensures a stable and optimized VPN connection."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná WireGuard a chumrú ar chliant trí luachanna iomchuí MTU a shocrú ar chomhéadan líonra. Cinntíonn sé seo nasc VPN cobhsaí agus optamaithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to enable proper routing and connectivity for a WireGuard client situated behind a firewall or NAT device. By adapting iptables rules, it ensures that the client can communicate effectively with external networks."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná ródú agus nascacht chuí a chumasú do chliant WireGuard atá suite taobh thiar de bhalla dóiteáin nó gléas NAT. Trí rialacha iptables a oiriúnú, cinntíonn sé gur féidir leis an gcliant cumarsáid éifeachtach a dhéanamh le líonraí seachtracha."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to enhance system performance by ensuring that Docker volumes are stored on the most appropriate storage medium, optimizing both speed and capacity."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná feidhmíocht an chórais a fheabhsú trína chinntiú go stóráiltear méideanna Docker ar an meán stórála is oiriúnaí, agus an dá luas agus an cumas a bharrfheabhsú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to enhance the security of the system by ensuring that a valid SSH key is available for the [root user](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superuser). By automating the generation and output of the public key, it reduces manual intervention and helps maintain a secure configuration for administrative access."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an róil seo slándáil an chórais a fheabhsú trína chinntiú go bhfuil eochair bailí SSH ar fáil don [duille dath glas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superuser). Trí ghiniúint agus aschur an eochair phoiblí a uathoibriú, laghdaíonn sé idirghabháil láimhe agus cabhraíonn sé le cumraíocht slán a choimeád le haghaidh rochtain riaracháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to enhance the security of the system by ensuring that a valid SSH key is available for the `root user <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superuser>`__. By automating the generation and output of the public key, it reduces manual intervention and helps maintain a secure configuration for administrative access."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an róil seo slándáil an chórais a fheabhsú trína chinntiú go bhfuil eochair bailí SSH ar fáil don `root user <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superuser>`__. Trí ghiniúint agus aschur an eochair phoiblí a uathoibriú, laghdaíonn sé idirghabháil láimhe agus cabhraíonn sé le cumraíocht slán a choimeád le haghaidh rochtain riaracháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to ensure that Docker-based services remain operational. By automatically monitoring container health, it enables administrators to react quickly to failures, reducing downtime and preventing unnoticed service degradation."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná a chinntiú go bhfanfaidh seirbhísí Docker-bhunaithe i bhfeidhm. Trí fhaireachán a dhéanamh go huathoibríoch ar shláinte an choimeádáin, cuireann sé ar chumas riarthóirí freagairt go tapa ar theipeanna, ag laghdú downtime agus ag cosc díghrádú seirbhíse gan choinne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to ensure that all Docker Compose services are restarted consistently, resolving issues that may arise from partial restarts. This helps maintain overall service stability and minimizes downtime."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an róil seo a chinntiú go bhfuil gach Docker Compose seirbhísí atosú go seasta, saincheisteanna a d'fhéadfadh teacht chun cinn ó restarts páirteach réiteach. Cuidíonn sé seo a choimeád ar bun cobhsaíocht seirbhíse foriomlán agus laghdaíonn downtime."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to ensure that disk space remains within safe limits by automating cleanup tasks, thereby improving system performance and stability."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná a chinntiú go bhfanann spás diosca laistigh de theorainneacha sábháilte trí thascanna glantacháin a uathoibriú, rud a fheabhsaíonn feidhmíocht agus cobhsaíocht an chórais."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to ensure that the target system has a reliable sudo configuration. By installing the [sudo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudo) package and deploying a standard sudoers file, the role facilitates proper administrative access and minimizes potential security risks."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná a chinntiú go bhfuil cumraíocht iontaofa ag an gcóras sprioc. Trí shuiteáil an [taiseachas aeir: fliuch](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudo) pacáiste agus a imscaradh comhad sudoers caighdeánach, éascaíonn an ról rochtain riaracháin cuí agus laghdaíonn sé rioscaí slándála féideartha."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to ensure that the target system has a reliable sudo configuration. By installing the `sudo <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudo>`__ package and deploying a standard sudoers file, the role facilitates proper administrative access and minimizes potential security risks."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná a chinntiú go bhfuil cumraíocht iontaofa ag an gcóras sprioc. Trí shuiteáil an `sudo <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudo>`__ pacáiste agus a imscaradh comhad sudoers caighdeánach, éascaíonn an ról rochtain riaracháin cuí agus laghdaíonn sé rioscaí slándála féideartha."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to guarantee that an SSH client is available on the system before executing any SSH-related operations, such as key generation, remote access, or automated provisioning."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná a ráthú go bhfuil cliant SSH ar fáil ar an gcóras sula ndéanann sé aon oibríochtaí a bhaineann le SSH, mar shampla príomhghiniúint, rochtain iargúlta, nó soláthar uathoibrithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to maintain optimal backup storage by automatically removing outdated backup versions when disk usage exceeds a specified threshold."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná stóráil cúltaca is fearr a choinneáil trí leaganacha cúltaca as dáta a bhaint go huathoibríoch nuair a théann úsáid diosca thar tairseach sonraithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to maintain optimal performance of Btrfs file systems by automating balancing tasks, ensuring efficient storage allocation and performance."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná feidhmíocht optamach na gcóras comhaid Btrfs a choimeád trí thascanna cothromaíochta a uathoibriú, leithdháileadh agus feidhmíocht éifeachtach stórála a áirithiú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to prevent storage bloat caused by unused Docker images, volumes, and build artifacts. Regular pruning ensures:"
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná bloat stórála a chosc de bharr íomhánna Docker neamhúsáidte, toirteanna, agus déantáin a thógáil. Cinntíonn bearradh rialta:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to provide a centralized mechanism for service failure notifications. By integrating with both the Telegram and Email notifier roles, it delivers reliable alerts through multiple channels, enhancing overall system observability and responsiveness."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná meicníocht láraithe a sholáthar le haghaidh fógraí teipe seirbhíse. Trí chomhtháthú leis an dá na róil Telegram agus r-phost notifier, seachadann sé foláirimh iontaofa trí bhealaí éagsúla, feabhas a chur ar inbhraiteacht córas foriomlán agus freagrúlacht."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to provide a comprehensive solution for automated email notifications in a systemd environment. By integrating with msmtp and customizable templates, it delivers clear and timely alerts about service failures, thereby enhancing system reliability."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo réiteach cuimsitheach a chur ar fáil le haghaidh fógraí ríomhphoist uathoibrithe i dtimpeallacht chórasach. Trí chomhtháthú le msmtp agus teimpléid customizable, seachadann sé foláirimh soiléir agus tráthúil faoi teipeanna seirbhíse, rud a chuireann feabhas ar iontaofacht an chórais."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to provide a reliable installation of the Python package manager, pip, ensuring that subsequent Python package installations can proceed without issues."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná suiteáil iontaofa a chur ar fáil don bhainisteoir pacáiste Python, pip, ag cinntiú gur féidir le suiteálacha pacáiste Python ina dhiaidh sin dul ar aghaidh gan saincheisteanna."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to provide a reusable mechanism for scheduling recurring tasks on a system. By creating and managing a systemd timer unit, the role ensures that specified services are automatically started at defined intervals, enhancing system automation and reliability."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná meicníocht ath-inúsáidte a chur ar fáil chun cúraimí athfhillteacha a chur ar chóras. Trí aonad lasc ama sistéamaí a chruthú agus a bhainistiú, cinntíonn an ról go dtosófar ar sheirbhísí sonraithe go huathoibríoch ag eatraimh shainithe, feabhas a chur ar uathoibriú córais agus ar iontaofacht."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to provide a robust solution for automated Telegram notifications in a systemd environment. By integrating with Telegram’s Bot API and using customizable message templates, it delivers clear and timely alerts about service failures, thereby enhancing system observability and reliability."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo réiteach láidir a sholáthar le haghaidh fógraí teileagram uathoibrithe i dtimpeallacht chórasach. Trí chomhtháthú le Bot Telegram ar API agus ag baint úsáide as teimpléid teachtaireacht customizable, seachadann sé foláirimh soiléir agus tráthúil faoi theipeanna seirbhíse, rud a chuireann le inbhraiteacht córas agus iontaofacht."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to provide a secure and dedicated administrator account solely for running local administration tasks. This approach minimizes security risks associated with using the root account and enforces best practices in user privilege management."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an róil seo cuntas riarthóra slán agus tiomanta a chur ar fáil ach amháin chun tascanna riaracháin áitiúla a reáchtáil. Laghdaíonn an cur chuige seo rioscaí slándála a bhaineann leis an gcuntas fréimhe a úsáid agus cuireann sé na cleachtais is fearr i mbainistiú pribhléide úsáideora i bhfeidhm."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to safeguard system stability during maintenance by preventing conflicts with running services. It ensures that maintenance operations proceed only when the environment is ready."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an ról seo ná cobhsaíocht an chórais a chosaint le linn cothabhála trí choinbhleachtaí le seirbhísí reatha a chosc. Cinntíonn sé nach dtéann oibríochtaí cothabhála ar aghaidh ach amháin nuair a bhíonn an timpeallacht réidh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary purpose of this role is to set up and manage a Wireguard VPN configuration on the host. By automating package installation and configuration file deployment, it ensures that the VPN service is enabled with optimal network settings for secure connectivity."
msgstr "Is é príomhchuspóir an róil seo ná bunú agus bainistiú a dhéanamh ar Wireguard cumraíocht VPN ar an óstach. De réir uathoibriú suiteáil pacáiste agus imscaradh comhad chumraíocht, cinntíonn sé go bhfuil an tseirbhís VPN chumas le suímh líonra is fearr is féidir le haghaidh nascacht slán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The primary service entry is the role entity name returned by `get_entity_name`."
msgstr "Is é an iontráil phríomhsheirbhís ná ainm an eintitis ról a thugtar ar ais ag `get_entity_name`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The private helpers (``_resolve_round_include`` and friends) are re-exported below because unit tests historically patch them under this package path. New tests SHOULD patch the submodule path directly (e.g. ``inventory.legacy_resolver._resolve_round_include``)."
msgstr "Cúntóirí príobháideacha (``_resolve_round_include`` agus cairde) ath-onnmhairithe thíos mar gheall ar tástálacha aonad paiste stairiúil iad faoin cosán pacáiste. tástálacha nua paiste SHOULD an cosán submodule díreach (e.g. ``inventory.legacy_resolver._resolve_round_include``)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The privileged `pull_request_target` build switches its **build source** from the base merge ref to the **raw PR head** (`head.repo.full_name` @ `head.sha`)."
msgstr "An phribhléid `pull_request_target` tógáil lasca a **foinse tógála** ón mbonn a chumasc ref chun an **ceann PR amh** (`head.repo.full_name` Cuntas deimhnithe `head.sha`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The probe runs inside the systemd unit, not at deploy time, because the set of docker volumes changes between deploys and a volume added afterwards would be an empty stub inside a snapshot. It refuses unless all of the following hold for the docker data root reported by ``docker info``:"
msgstr "Ritheann an probe taobh istigh den aonad córasach, ní ag am a imscaradh, toisc go mbeadh an sraith de athruithe toirt docker idir imscaradh agus toirt breise ina dhiaidh sin stub folamh taobh istigh de snapshot. Diúltaíonn sé ach amháin má tá gach ceann acu seo a leanas le haghaidh an fhréamh sonraí docker a thuairiscigh ``docker info``:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The probe runs inside the systemd unit, not at deploy time, because the set of docker volumes changes between deploys and a volume added afterwards would be an empty stub inside a snapshot. It refuses unless all of the following hold for the docker data root reported by `docker info`:"
msgstr "Ritheann an probe taobh istigh den aonad córasach, ní ag am a imscaradh, toisc go mbeadh an sraith de athruithe toirt docker idir imscaradh agus toirt breise ina dhiaidh sin stub folamh taobh istigh de snapshot. Diúltaíonn sé ach amháin má tá gach ceann acu seo a leanas le haghaidh an fhréamh sonraí docker a thuairiscigh `docker info`:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The probe therefore builds a **throwaway** btrfs on a loop device and puts a stub on `PATH` in place of the docker daemon. The host's real data root is never touched, and no state survives the run."
msgstr "Dá bhrí sin, cuireann an probe a **caith amach** btrfs ar ghléas lúb agus cuireann stub ar `PATH` in áit an daemon docker. Ní dhéantar teagmháil le fréamh sonraí fíor an óstach, agus ní mhaireann aon stát an rith."

msgid "The probe's own check was vacuous beside this: it compared a declared window against an estimated demand, both produced by this deployment, so it structurally could not observe a declaration the backend does not honour. It now also reads `usage.prompt_tokens` from the answer, the one number in the exchange that the backend produced."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The probe; with prefixes it is wrapped so ``test`` renders CMD-SHELL."
msgstr "An probe; le réimeanna tá sé fillte mar sin ``test`` déanann CMD-SHELL."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The producer [build_ldap_role_entries](../../../../roles/svc-db-openldap/filter_plugins/build_ldap_role_entries.py) also emits a per-application `groupOfNames` container `cn=<application_id>,ou=roles,...` whose `member` attribute references every role group of that application, so an LDAP-only consumer can still navigate the hierarchy. Keycloak does not rely on those containers; it reconstructs `/roles/<application_id>/<role_name>` via per-application mappers (see below)."
msgstr "An táirgeoir [build_ldap_role_entries](../../../../roles/svc-db-openldap/filter_plugins/build_ldap_role_entries.py) scaoileann freisin iarratas in aghaidh an `groupOfNames` coimeádán `cn=<application_id>,ou=roles,...` a bhfuil a `member` tagairtí tréith gach grúpa ról an iarratais sin, mar sin is féidir le tomhaltóir LDAP-amháin nascleanúint a dhéanamh fós ar an ordlathas. Ní Keycloak ag brath ar na coimeádáin sin; reconstructs sé `/roles/<application_id>/<role_name>` trí léarscáileoirí in aghaidh an iarratais (féach thíos:)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The production-safe path MUST follow Mattermost's documented Agents and MCP deployment guidance."
msgstr "An cosán a tháirgeadh-sábháilte MUST leanúint Mattermost'Gníomhairí doiciméadaithe agus treoir imscaradh MCP."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The project tree's full path list (one walk per process) and per-file UTF-8 contents (`read_text`). Used by lint/integration tests and CLI tools that scan the repo."
msgstr "Liosta iomlán cosán an chrainn tionscadail (siúlóid amháin in aghaidh an phróisis) agus in aghaidh an comhad UTF-8 Tuilleadh eolais (`read_text`). Úsáidte ag tástálacha lint / slánú agus uirlisí CLI a scanadh an repo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The project's environment is owned by a single generator, not scattered across shell modules. Every variable is documented INLINE next to its definition with a one-line `# ...` comment above the key. This page is just a map of where to look."
msgstr "Tá timpeallacht an tionscadail faoi úinéireacht ag gineadóir amháin, nach bhfuil scaipthe ar fud modúil bhlaosc. Tá gach athróg doiciméadaithe INLINE in aice lena sainmhíniú le aon-líne `# ...` trácht os cionn an eochair. Tá an leathanach seo ach léarscáil de nuair a chuardach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The project-owned plugin is unaudited: endpoint, transport, auth and tool scope are unverified in source."
msgstr "Tá an breiseán atá faoi úinéireacht an tionscadail a fuarthas amach: endpoint, iompar, auth agus raon feidhme uirlis unverified sa fhoinse."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The project-owned server passes ownership, licence, pinning and read-only default, but its HTTP transport serves one session per process, which upstream asserts in `src/test/transport.test.ts` at `v0.3.1`; the deploy probe alone would leave it restart-required."
msgstr "Gabhann an freastalaí faoi úinéireacht an tionscadail úinéireacht, ceadúnas, pinning agus a léamh-amháint, ach feidhmíonn a iompar HTTP seisiún amháin in aghaidh an phróisis, a dhearbhaíonn sruth in `src/test/transport.test.ts` ag an `v0.3.1`; bheadh an probe imscaradh amháin fhágáil sé restart-riachtanach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The project-owned server requires an active browser tab and plugin connection and can execute powerful design-context operations. Record `interactive_browser_session`; only an experimental user-initiated integration with a pinned server and isolated session may proceed."
msgstr "Éilíonn an freastalaí faoi úinéireacht tionscadail cluaisín bhrabhsálaí gníomhach agus nasc plugin agus is féidir a fhorghníomhú oibríochtaí dearadh-comhthéacs cumhachtach. Taifead agus Taifead `interactive_browser_session`; Is féidir ach comhtháthú úsáideora-initiated turgnamhach le freastalaí pinned agus seisiún iargúlta ar aghaidh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The prompt tracks a category stack: typing a bare category name cd's into it, ``..`` walks one level up, ``/`` returns to root, path tokens with ``/`` or ``..`` navigate, ``infinito [path]`` jumps absolute, ``ls`` lists the current folder, everything else runs with the current path prepended."
msgstr "Na rianta pras RatánComment catagóir: clóscríobh catagóir lom ainm cd isteach é, ``..`` siúlóidí leibhéal amháin suas, ``/`` tuairisceáin ar fhréamh, comharthaí cosán le ``/`` nó ``..`` nascleanúint a dhéanamh, ``infinito [path]`` jumps iomlán, ``ls`` liostaí an fillteán atá ann faoi láthair, ritheann gach rud eile leis an cosán atá ann faoi láthair prepended."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The propagation chain has four hops:"
msgstr "Tá ceithre hop sa slabhra iomadú:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The protection rules enforced on `main` are documented in [branch.md](../../tools/github/branch/security.md)."
msgstr "Na rialacha cosanta arna bhforfheidhmiú `main` doiciméadú i [branch.md](../../tools/github/branch/security.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The provider credential is whatever ``mcp.credential`` declares: ``owner`` names the principal, ``source`` where its secret lives (``token_store`` or the role's own ``credentials``), ``key`` the entry. No provider inherits the administrator's token."
msgstr "Is é an dintiúir soláthraí is cuma cad ``mcp.credential`` dearbhaíonn: ``owner`` ainmneacha an príomhoide, ``source`` áit a bhfuil a saol rúnda (``token_store`` nó an ról féin ``credentials``), ``key`` an iontráil. No soláthraí hoidhreacht an riarthóir chomhartha."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The provision CLI parses the JSON and forwards the per-app index as `--variant <N>` to each `infinito administration inventory credentials` subprocess call."
msgstr "An fhoráil CLI parses an JSON agus ar aghaidh an t-innéacs per-app mar `--variant <N>` le gach ceann `infinito administration inventory credentials` glaoch subprocess."

msgid "The proxy config used to grow a loop per source, so the rule for \"how is this alias called\" lived in four places that drifted apart: the LM Studio branch published no context window although its README promised one, and a mock needed a fifth branch. Here the sources meet once, the template renders one loop, and every shape is a unit test instead of a rendered fixture."
msgstr ""

msgid "The proxy filters methods and paths, not request bodies. `POST /volumes/create` stays on the allowlist because the broker creates a volume per agent, and a local-driver volume with `o=bind,device=/` is a host bind mount that arrives as a volume. Fields such as `Privileged`, `PidMode` or `CapAdd` on `containers/create` are likewise unfiltered. The isolation therefore holds against a compromised **agent**, which reaches no socket at all, not against a compromised **broker**."
msgstr ""

msgid "The public entry point of three layers, each importable on its own:"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The published (host) port is ``ports.local.<proto>`` when declared, else ``ports.public.<proto>``; the container port is ``ports.internal.<proto>``."
msgstr "Foilsíodh é (óstach óstach) Is maith liom é ``ports.local.<proto>`` nuair a dhearbhaítear, eile ``ports.public.<proto>``; Is é an calafort coimeádán ``ports.internal.<proto>``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The published image is multi-arch, but only `linux/amd64` has been exercised."
msgstr "Is é an íomhá a foilsíodh il-arch, ach amháin `linux/amd64` a fheidhmiú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this folder is to keep domain logic in one predictable place so different plugins, helpers, and automation paths can rely on the same behavior. Rather than being tied to one feature, the code here supports the broader shape of how domains are interpreted, normalized, collected, and reused across the project. 🧭"
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an fillteán seo a choinneáil loighic fearainn in aon áit intuartha sin plugins éagsúla, Cúntóirí, agus is féidir le cosáin uathoibriú brath ar an iompar céanna. Seachas a bheith ceangailte le gné amháin, tacaíonn an cód anseo an cruth níos leithne ar conas fearainn a léiriú, normalaithe, bailithe, agus athúsáid ar fud an tionscadail. 🧭"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the configuration of cloud-integrated user directories by ensuring that common folders like `Downloads`, `Music`, and `Workspaces` are transparently redirected into a centralized cloud structure. This makes it easier to maintain sys-bkp-friendly, cloud-ready setups for homelab and professional workflows."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná cumraíocht na stiúrthóireachtaí úsáideoirí scamall-chomhtháite a uathoibriú trína chinntiú gur mhaith le fillteáin chomhchoiteanna `Downloads`, `Music`, agus `Workspaces` atreorú go trédhearcach i struchtúr scamall láraithe. Seo a dhéanann sé níos éasca a choimeád ar bun sys-bkp-chairdiúil, setups scamall-réidh do saotharlann bhaile agus sreabhadh oibre gairmiúla."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the configuration of cloud-integrated user directories by ensuring that common folders like ``Downloads``, ``Music``, and ``Workspaces`` are transparently redirected into a centralized cloud structure. This makes it easier to maintain sys-bkp-friendly, cloud-ready setups for homelab and professional workflows."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná cumraíocht na stiúrthóireachtaí úsáideoirí scamall-chomhtháite a uathoibriú trína chinntiú gur mhaith le fillteáin chomhchoiteanna ``Downloads``, ``Music``, agus ``Workspaces`` atreorú go trédhearcach i struchtúr scamall láraithe. Seo a dhéanann sé níos éasca a choimeád ar bun sys-bkp-chairdiúil, setups scamall-réidh do saotharlann bhaile agus sreabhadh oibre gairmiúla."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the deployment of a full-featured RetroArch environment, reducing manual setup and improving reproducibility across gaming setups."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná imscaradh iomlán a uathoibriú RetroArch timpeallacht, laghdú thus láimhe agus a fheabhsú atáirgtheacht ar fud setups cearrbhachais."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the installation and configuration of Git for personal computers. By leveraging a custom git-configurator, it sets up essential Git settings such as merge options, rebase preferences, user information, and GPG signing, ensuring a consistent environment for version control operations."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná suiteáil agus cumraíocht a uathoibriú Git do ríomhairí pearsanta. Trí git-configurator saincheaptha a ghiaráil, cuireann sé bunriachtanach Git socruithe cosúil le roghanna a chumasc, roghanna atosú, faisnéis úsáideora, agus síniú GPG, timpeallacht comhsheasmhach a áirithiú le haghaidh oibríochtaí rialaithe leagan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the installation and configuration of LibreOffice along with its language support on personal computers. This ensures that users have a consistent and fully functional office suite environment across their systems."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná suiteáil agus cumraíocht a uathoibriú LibreOffice chomh maith lena tacaíocht teanga ar ríomhairí pearsanta. Cinntíonn sé seo go bhfuil timpeallacht oifige atá comhsheasmhach agus feidhmiúil go hiomlán ag úsáideoirí ar fud a gcórais."

msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the installation and update process for Infinito.Nexus-related applications or other managed packages using ``pkgmgr``. It simplifies package handling and enforces best practices for package deployment in automated environments."
msgstr ""

msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the installation and update process for Infinito.Nexus-related applications or other managed packages using `pkgmgr`. It simplifies package handling and enforces best practices for package deployment in automated environments."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the installation of Git in a consistent and idempotent manner. It is especially useful in environments where Git is a prerequisite for further automation or development tasks."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná suiteáil a uathoibriú Git ar bhealach comhsheasmhach agus idempotent. Tá sé úsáideach go háirithe i dtimpeallachtaí ina Git Is réamhriachtanas le haghaidh tascanna breise uathoibriú nó forbartha."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the installation of fakeroot so that users can simulate superuser operations without requiring elevated privileges. This is particularly useful in development environments and during package building processes."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná suiteáil bréige a uathoibriú ionas gur féidir le húsáideoirí oibríochtaí superuser a insamhail gan pribhléidí ardaithe a bheith ag teastáil. Tá sé seo úsáideach go háirithe i dtimpeallachtaí forbartha agus le linn próisis tógála pacáiste."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the provisioning of SSH agent capabilities and synchronize the `.ssh` directory from a Git repository. This enables users to access private repositories or authenticate with remote servers immediately after login."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná soláthar cumais gníomhaire SSH a uathoibriú agus sioncrónú an `.ssh` web development Git stór. Cuireann sé seo ar chumas úsáideoirí rochtain a fháil ar stórtha príobháideacha nó a fhíordheimhniú le freastalaithe iargúlta díreach tar éis logáil isteach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the provisioning of SSH agent capabilities and synchronize the ``.ssh`` directory from a Git repository. This enables users to access private repositories or authenticate with remote servers immediately after login."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná soláthar cumais gníomhaire SSH a uathoibriú agus sioncrónú an ``.ssh`` web development Git stór. Cuireann sé seo ar chumas úsáideoirí rochtain a fháil ar stórtha príobháideacha nó a fhíordheimhniú le freastalaithe iargúlta díreach tar éis logáil isteach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the provisioning of a development-ready environment by ensuring the GCC toolchain is properly installed and available."
msgstr "Is é an cuspóir atá leis an ról seo ná timpeallacht forbartha a chur ar fáil a uathoibriú trí chinntiú GCC toolchain suiteáilte i gceart agus ar fáil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the provisioning of a secure Chromium environment in a consistent and maintainable way. It reduces manual configuration steps and guarantees that critical browser extensions are enforced, making it ideal for both production and personal deployments."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná soláthar slán a uathoibriú Chromium timpeallacht ar bhealach comhsheasmhach agus inchothaithe. Laghdaíonn sé céimeanna cumraíochta láimhe agus ráthaíochtaí go bhfuil síntí bhrabhsálaí criticiúil i bhfeidhm, rud a chiallaíonn sé oiriúnach do tháirgeadh agus imscaradh pearsanta araon."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to automate the setup of a lightweight SMTP client that acts as a sendmail replacement. By configuring msmtp, the role facilitates direct email sending using your SMTP server credentials, making it a simple yet effective solution for system notifications and other email-based communications."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo a uathoibriú an thus de cliant SMTP lightweight a ghníomhaíonn mar athsholáthair seoltaí. De réir a chumrú msmtp, éascaíonn an ról ríomhphost díreach a sheoladh ag baint úsáide as do dintiúir freastalaí SMTP, rud a chiallaíonn sé réiteach simplí fós éifeachtach le haghaidh fógraí córas agus cumarsáid ríomhphoist-bhunaithe eile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to enforce a consistent and predictable lid switch behavior across power states, improving usability on laptops that otherwise behave unpredictably when the lid is closed."
msgstr "Is é an cuspóir atá leis an ról seo ná iompar lid comhsheasmhach agus intuartha a fhorfheidhmiú ar fud stáit chumhachta, feabhas a chur ar inúsáidteacht ar ríomhairí glúine a iompraíonn ar shlí eile go neamhthuartha nuair a dhúntar an clúdach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to enhance and customize the GNOME desktop environment by managing shell extensions. It simplifies the process of installing and configuring extensions, thereby improving productivity and desktop functionality."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná an timpeallacht deisce GNOME a fheabhsú agus a shaincheapadh trí leathnú bhlaosc a bhainistiú. Simplíonn sé an próiseas a shuiteáil agus a chumrú síntí, rud a fheabhsú táirgiúlacht agus feidhmiúlacht deisce."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to enhance the security of your backup system by providing a dedicated user with strict command restrictions. This controlled environment limits the potential damage from a compromised backup account while still allowing efficient backup operations."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo slándáil do chóras cúltaca a fheabhsú trí úsáideoir tiomanta a sholáthar le srianta ordú dian. An timpeallacht rialaithe teorainneacha an damáiste féideartha ó chuntas cúltaca comhréiteach agus fós ag ligean oibríochtaí cúltaca éifeachtach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to ensure that GNOME Terminal is installed and properly configured on Arch Linux systems, providing users with a robust and fully featured terminal emulator that integrates seamlessly with the GNOME desktop."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an róil seo a chinntiú go GNOME Terminal suiteáilte agus a chumrú i gceart ar chórais Arch Linux, ag soláthar úsáideoirí le emulator críochfort láidir agus go hiomlán le feiceáil a chomhtháthaíonn seamlessly leis an deisce GNOME."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to ensure uninterrupted workflow by keeping the desktop active during long-running tasks or presentations. By automatically starting caffeine-ng, it prevents unwanted screen locking or sleep modes on GNOME systems."
msgstr "Is é an cuspóir atá leis an ról seo ná sreabhadh oibre gan bhriseadh a chinntiú trí na cúraimí nó na láithreoireachtaí deisce atá gníomhach le linn na tréimhse fada a choinneáil. Trí dheireadh a chur go huathoibríoch Caiféin-ng, cuireann sé cosc ar ghlais scáileáin nach dteastaíonn nó modhanna codlata ar chórais GNOME."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to externalise the static-IP DNS resolver out of large multi-service stacks (such as mail) into a single-service stack. Keeping the static-IP allocation in a trivial 1-service / 1-network stack avoids the swarm VIP-allocation deadlock that a 13-service / 4-network stack triggers, and lets consumer roles stay stateless and unpinned."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo a sheachtrú an statach-IP réiteoir DNS as cruacha il-seirbhíse mór (mar phost) i Stack aon-seirbhíse. Ag coinneáil an static-IP leithdháileadh i fánach 1-seirbhíse / seirbhíse / 1-network Stack seachnaíonn an Swarm VIP-allocation deadlock go 13-seirbhíse / seirbhíse / 4-network Stack triggers, agus ligeann róil tomhaltóirí fanacht stateless agus gan choinne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide a **generic, reusable Git pull primitive** for other roles in the Infinito.Nexus ecosystem."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an róil seo ná soláthar **cineálach, ath-inúsáidte Git tarraingt primitive** do róil eile sna Infinito.Nexus éiceachóras."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide a central E2E test primitive that can be executed at the end of a deployment (for example, as a post task), without hardcoding tests in the runner itself."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an róil seo ná E lárnach a sholáthar2E tástáil primitive is féidir a fhorghníomhú ag deireadh an imscaradh (mar shampla, mar phost tasc), gan tástálacha crua-chódú sa dara háit féin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide a complete GNOME desktop experience by orchestrating multiple sub-roles. This simplifies deployment and management by ensuring that all key components are installed and configured in a consistent, system-wide manner."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná taithí iomlán deisce GNOME a chur ar fáil trí fho-ráillí il a eagrú. Simplíonn sé seo imscaradh agus bainistíocht trína chinntiú go bhfuil na comhpháirteanna eochair suiteáilte agus cumraithe ar bhealach comhsheasmhach, ar fud an chórais."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide a hands-off, production-ready Odoo ERP deployment that integrates seamlessly with the Infinito.Nexus platform. Organizations can leverage Odoo's comprehensive business management capabilities while benefiting from centralized authentication, backup, monitoring, and security features."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná lámha a chur ar fáil, a tháirgeadh-réidh Odoo ERP imscaradh a chomhtháthaíonn seamlessly leis an Infinito.Nexus ardán. Is féidir le heagraíochtaí a ghiaráil cumais bainistíochta gnó cuimsitheach Odoo agus leas a bhaint as fíordheimhnithe láraithe, cúltaca, monatóireacht, agus gnéithe slándála."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide a hands-off, production-ready Odoo ERP deployment that integrates seamlessly with the Infinito.Nexus platform. Organizations can leverage Odoo’s comprehensive business management capabilities while benefiting from centralized authentication, backup, monitoring, and security features."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná lámha a chur ar fáil, a tháirgeadh-réidh Odoo ERP imscaradh a chomhtháthaíonn seamlessly leis an Infinito.Nexus ardán. Is féidir le heagraíochtaí a ghiaráil cumais bainistíochta gnó cuimsitheach Odoo agus leas a bhaint as fíordheimhnithe láraithe, cúltaca, monatóireacht, agus gnéithe slándála."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide a reliable, configurable, and secure PhpMyAdmin deployment out-of-the-box. It minimizes the need for manual setup, and integrates smoothly with other Infinito.Nexus infrastructure roles."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo a chur ar fáil iontaofa, configurable, agus slán PhpMyAdmin imscaradh lasmuigh den bhosca. Laghdaíonn sé an gá atá le thus lámhleabhar, agus comhtháthaíonn sé go réidh le eile Infinito.Nexus róil bhonneagair."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide an automated, idempotent installation of GNU Make, ensuring that the tool is available system-wide for building software. It is ideal for developers and system administrators who require a reliable build system."
msgstr "Is é an cuspóir atá leis an ról seo ná suiteáil uathoibrithe, inmharthana de chuid GNU Make a chur ar fáil, ag cinntiú go bhfuil an uirlis ar fáil ar fud an chórais le haghaidh bogearraí tógála. Tá sé oiriúnach d'fhorbróirí agus riarthóirí córais a dteastaíonn córas tógála iontaofa uathu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide an effortless way to deploy a PostgreSQL database via Docker. It minimizes manual interventions while ensuring that your database is configured securely and reliably for both production and development scenarios."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo bealach effortless a chur ar fáil chun imscaradh PostgreSQL bunachar sonraí trí Docker. Íoslaghdaíonn sé idirghabhálacha láimhe agus a chinntiú go bhfuil do bhunachar sonraí a chumrú go daingean agus go hiontaofa le haghaidh cásanna táirgthe agus forbartha araon."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide an effortless way to deploy a Qdrant vector database via Docker. It minimizes manual interventions while ensuring that the engine is configured securely and reliably for both production and development scenarios."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo bealach effortless a chur ar fáil chun imscaradh Qdrant bunachar sonraí veicteoir trí Docker. Laghdaíonn sé idirghabhálacha láimhe agus ag cinntiú go bhfuil an t-inneall cumraithe go daingean agus go hiontaofa le haghaidh cásanna táirgthe agus forbartha araon."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide an effortless way to deploy a central Elasticsearch engine via Docker so that application roles stay stateless, unpinned and NFS-shareable in swarm while the engine keeps its on-disk index state node-local. See [docs/architecture/central-engines.md](../../docs/architecture/central-engines.md)."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an róil seo bealach effortless a chur ar fáil chun imscaradh lárnach Elasticsearch inneall via Docker ionas go mbeidh róil iarratais fanacht gan stát, gan íoc agus NFS-roinnte i swarm agus coimeádann an t-inneall a ar-dísc stáit innéacs node-áitiúil. Féach ar [docs/architecture/central-engines.md](../../docs/architecture/central-engines.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide an effortless way to deploy a central Elasticsearch engine via Docker so that application roles stay stateless, unpinned and NFS-shareable in swarm while the engine keeps its on-disk index state node-local. See `docs/architecture/central-engines.md <../../docs/architecture/central-engines.md>`__."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an róil seo bealach effortless a chur ar fáil chun imscaradh lárnach Elasticsearch inneall via Docker ionas go mbeidh róil iarratais fanacht gan stát, gan íoc agus NFS-roinnte i swarm agus coimeádann an t-inneall a ar-dísc stáit innéacs node-áitiúil. Féach ar `docs/architecture/central-engines.md <../../docs/architecture/central-engines.md>`__."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide an effortless way to run a shared Typesense engine via Docker while giving each consumer its own isolated, scoped credential. It minimizes manual interventions while keeping engine on-disk state node-local (it cannot live on NFS)."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo bealach effortless a chur ar fáil a reáchtáil roinnte Typesense inneall trí Docker agus a thabhairt do gach tomhaltóir a scoite amach féin, dintiúir raon feidhme. Íoslaghdaíonn sé idirghabhálacha láimhe agus inneall a choinneáil ar an stát nód-áit áitiúil (ní féidir leis maireachtáil ar NFS)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to provide automated healing for Docker Compose environments, minimizing manual recovery effort and reducing downtime."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná leigheas uathoibrithe a chur ar fáil le haghaidh Docker Compose timpeallachtaí, íoslaghdú iarracht a ghnóthú láimhe agus downtime a laghdú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to reduce the complexity of setting up OpenProject with modern production-ready defaults. By combining Docker Compose and Ansible automation, it enables a hands-off setup for both small teams and larger internal infrastructures."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an róil seo ná castacht a bhaineann le bunú a laghdú OpenProject le táirgeadh-réidh nua-aimseartha mainneachtainí. Trí chéile Docker Compose agus uathoibriú Ansible, cuireann sé ar fáil lámha-uaire le haghaidh foirne beaga agus bonneagair inmheánacha níos mó."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to simplify the installation of Kevin's Package Manager, reducing manual steps and ensuring a consistent setup across environments. Ideal for developers and system administrators, it helps integrate repository management seamlessly into your automation workflows."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an róil seo ná suiteáil Bhainisteoir Pacáiste Kevin a shimpliú, céimeanna láimhe a laghdú agus socrú comhsheasmhach a chinntiú ar fud na timpeallachtaí. Ideal d'fhorbróirí agus riarthóirí córais, cuidíonn sé a chomhtháthú bainistíocht stór seamlessly isteach i do sreabhadh oibre uathoibrithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to simplify the installation of Kevin’s Package Manager, reducing manual steps and ensuring a consistent setup across environments. Ideal for developers and system administrators, it helps integrate repository management seamlessly into your automation workflows."
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an róil seo ná suiteáil Bhainisteoir Pacáiste Kevin a shimpliú, céimeanna láimhe a laghdú agus socrú comhsheasmhach a chinntiú ar fud timpeallachtaí. Ideal d'fhorbróirí agus riarthóirí córais, cuidíonn sé a chomhtháthú bainistíocht stór seamlessly isteach i do sreabhadh oibre uathoibrithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to unify shell environment setup across Bash and Zsh. It minimizes duplication and confusion by encouraging the use of `.profile` for shared configuration such as environment variables and agent settings."
msgstr "Is é an cuspóir atá leis an ról seo ná cur isteach ar thimpeallacht sliogáin ar fud Bash agus Zsh. Laghdaíonn sé dúbailt agus mearbhall trí úsáid a spreagadh `.profile` do chumraíocht roinnte ar nós athróg comhshaoil agus suímh gníomhaire."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of this role is to unify shell environment setup across Bash and Zsh. It minimizes duplication and confusion by encouraging the use of ``.profile`` for shared configuration such as environment variables and agent settings."
msgstr "Is é an cuspóir atá leis an ról seo ná cur isteach ar thimpeallacht sliogáin ar fud Bash agus Zsh. Laghdaíonn sé dúbailt agus mearbhall trí úsáid a spreagadh ``.profile`` do chumraíocht roinnte ar nós athróg comhshaoil agus suímh gníomhaire."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The purpose of tthis role is to simplify the deployment and management of a personal or professional portfolio. By focusing on usability and a clean presentation, the role helps you:"
msgstr "Is é cuspóir an ról seo ná imscaradh agus bainistiú punainne pearsanta nó ghairmiúil a shimpliú. Trí dhíriú ar inúsáidteacht agus cur i láthair glan, cabhraíonn an ról leat:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The push entry synchronizes the current repository's `main` branch from the configured source repository before CI policy and deploy discovery run. The default source is `infinito-nexus/core`, and `CI_SYNC_MAIN_SOURCE_REPOSITORY` MAY override or disable the sync as documented in [configuration.md](../../tools/github/actions/configuration.md). This sync **force-overwrites** the local `main`, so on a synced repository you MUST NOT work directly in `main`; use a `feature/**`, `fix/**`, or `hotfix/**` branch and treat `main` as a read-only mirror."
msgstr "Sioncrónaíonn an iontráil bhrú an stór reatha ar `main` brainse ón stór foinse cumraithe roimh bheartas CI agus reáchtáil fionnachtana imscaradh. Is é an fhoinse réamhshocraithe `infinito-nexus/core`, agus `CI_SYNC_MAIN_SOURCE_REPOSITORY` MAY override nó disable an sync mar atá doiciméadaithe i [configuration.md](../../tools/github/actions/configuration.md). An sync **force-overwrites** an áitiúil `main`, mar sin ar stór synced tú NACH obair go díreach i `main`; úsáid `feature/**`, `fix/**`, nó `hotfix/**` brainse agus a chóireáil `main` mar scáthán léite amháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The qualifier in parentheses is OPTIONAL. Use it only when two workflows share the same category and subject."
msgstr "Is é an qualifier i lúibíní OPTIONAL. Bain úsáid as ach amháin nuair a roinneann dhá shreabhadh oibre an chatagóir agus an t-ábhar céanna."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The raw ``run-name:`` string declared by the manual CI workflow."
msgstr "An t-amhras ``run-name:`` teaghrán dhearbhú ag an sreabhadh oibre CI lámhleabhar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The reason is reviewability and tooling. Extracted assets get proper syntax highlighting, linting, and diffing. Inline heredocs and multi-line `query:` or `command:` blocks hide all three and make the task file harder to read."
msgstr "Is é an chúis léirmheasability agus tooling. Sócmhainní Sliocht fháil syntax cuí béim, linting, agus diffing. Inlíne heredocs agus il-líne `query:` nó `command:` bloic cheilt gach trí agus a dhéanamh ar an comhad tasc níos deacra a léamh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The reason is the endpoint's own shape: Baserow's `MCPEndpoint` carries no scope column, so the endpoint key grants every tool the backend implements — including the three write tools — with no way to narrow it. The adapter is what narrows it, by serving four read tools and refusing every other name."
msgstr "Is é an chúis cruth féin an endpoint: Baserow ar `MCPEndpoint` Déanann aon cholún raon feidhme, mar sin tugann an eochair endpoint gach uirlis na huirlisí cúltaca - lena n-áirítear na trí uirlisí scríobh - gan aon bhealach a caolú. Is é an adapter cad a chaolaíonn sé, trí fhreastal ceithre uirlisí a léamh agus diúltú gach ainm eile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The reason is the endpoint’s own shape: Baserow’s ``MCPEndpoint`` carries no scope column, so the endpoint key grants every tool the backend implements — including the three write tools — with no way to narrow it. The adapter is what narrows it, by serving four read tools and refusing every other name."
msgstr "Is é an chúis an endpoint ar cruth féin: Baserow ar ``MCPEndpoint`` Déanann aon cholún raon feidhme, mar sin tugann an eochair endpoint gach uirlis na huirlisí cúltaca - lena n-áirítear na trí uirlisí scríobh - gan aon bhealach a caolú. Is é an adapter cad a chaolaíonn sé, trí fhreastal ceithre uirlisí a léamh agus diúltú gach ainm eile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The recommended way to disable IPv6 for local development is via Make:"
msgstr "An bealach molta chun IPv a dhíchumasú6 le haghaidh forbairt áitiúil trí Déan:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The reconciliation stage MUST run before the end-to-end tests that read the converged state, and MUST NOT sit behind a task that a red test aborts. Placed in the destructor stage it ran after the Playwright suite, and `any_errors_fatal` meant any failing role skipped reconciliation entirely, so the suite asserted a state nothing had produced yet."
msgstr "An chéim athmhuintearas MUST reáchtáil roimh na tástálacha deireadh-le-deireadh a léamh ar an stát converged, agus NACH MUST suí taobh thiar de tasc go aborts tástála dearg. Áitithe sa chéim destructor rith sé tar éis an tsraith Playwright, agus `any_errors_fatal` Chiallaigh aon ról gan staonadh athmhuintearas go hiomlán, mar sin dhearbhaigh an tsraith rud ar bith stáit a táirgeadh go fóill."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The redeploy is NEVER the verification. \"The gate/reinstall has to run anyway\" or \"the next deploy will validate it\" is FORBIDDEN as a justification."
msgstr "Is é an redeploy NEVER an fíorú. \"Tá an geata / athshuiteáil a reáchtáil ar aon nós\" nó \"Beidh an chéad imscaradh eile a bhailíochtú\" Is FORBIDDEN mar údar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The redundancy cut does not follow the axes. `covered_by` is a role-level claim discovery computes from the service closure, so the row that covers a cut row now usually lands on a different distribution: on a full sweep, 6 of 44 cut rows share their coverer's distro. The cut therefore asserts that the services were exercised, not that they were exercised on that row's distribution. Reaching a cut row on its own axes means naming it on the priority line, which is what `⭐` exists for."
msgstr "Ní leanann an gearrtha iomarcaíochta na haiseanna. `covered_by` Is éard atá i gceist le fionnachtain ar leibhéal róil ón dúnadh seirbhíse, mar sin is gnách go dtéann an tsraith a chlúdaíonn sraith gearrtha ar dháileadh difriúil: ar scuab iomlán, 6 de 44 sraitheanna gearrtha a roinnt distro a chlúdachóir. Dearbhaíonn an gearrtha dá bhrí sin gur feidhmíodh na seirbhísí, ní go bhfeidhmíodh iad ar dháileadh an tsraith sin. A bhaint as a chéile gearrtha ar a haiseanna féin ciallaíonn ainmniú sé ar an líne tosaíochta, a bhfuil cad é `⭐` ann do."

msgid "The remaining reproductions of Jev, [open-alternative-jev](https://github.com/ikermoel/open-alternative-jev) on any open-weights model and OpenJev on DiffusionGemma 26B-A4B, are not used."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The remaining variables match the requirements of the delegated script. See its `README.md` for details."
msgstr "Na hathróga atá fágtha comhoiriúnach le riachtanais an script tarmligthe. Féach ar a `README.md` le haghaidh sonraí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The render runs once per play. The constructor stage parks the payload and its cache key in the host fact `_INFINITO_APPLICATIONS_RENDERED`, and every task's worker process (Ansible forks one per task) serves that payload instead of rendering again. See [applications.md](../artefact/files/plugins/lookup/applications.md) for the carrier contract."
msgstr "Ritheann an rindreáil uair amháin in aghaidh an dráma. Páirceanna an chéim tógálaí an pálasta agus a eochair taisce i ndáiríre óstach `_INFINITO_APPLICATIONS_RENDERED`, agus gach tasc ar phróiseas oibrí (Forks inchreidte amháin in aghaidh an tasc) freastal ar an pálasta in ionad a dhéanamh arís. Féach ar [applications.md](../artefact/files/plugins/lookup/applications.md) don chonradh iompróra."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The renderable path"
msgstr "An cosán rindreáilte"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The rendered `Corefile` is build artefact and MUST stay in `.gitignore`."
msgstr "An rinneadh `Corefile` tá déantúsaÃ agus fanacht MÓR a thógáil i `.gitignore`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The rendered fragment MUST start at the ``groups:`` item level (two-space indented ``- name: <group>`` entries), because it is concatenated into the single ``groups:`` list of the Prometheus rule file."
msgstr "Tosaíonn an MUST ilroinnte a rinneadh ag ``groups:`` leibhéal na míre (dhá spás fleasctha ``- name: <group>`` iontrálacha), toisc go bhfuil sé concatenated isteach an singil ``groups:`` liosta de na Prometheus comhad riail."

msgid "The replay is a second deploy on the same runner, so the row it picks must be one the guide can actually deploy: the role has to be invokable, because that is what makes the documentation build give it a Production block, and the guide's own mode (``compose`` for a role that ships a stack, ``host`` for one installed onto the machine) has to be a mode the role runs and tests."
msgstr ""

msgid "The replay rides along on a deploy row of the sweep instead of holding a job of its own. [guide.py](../../../../../utils/roles/guide.py) marks one row per role:"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The replay used to be a job of its own, picking one random role per run. It rides on a deploy row instead: the role's smallest variant among the rows this sweep actually deploys, marked with ``instructions`` (the mode the replay runs in) and a 📖 in the job title. :mod:`utils.roles.guide` decides which variant that is; this module is what turns the decision into matrix entries."
msgstr "An replay a úsáidtear a bheith ina phost ar a chuid féin, ag piocadh ról randamach amháin in aghaidh an reáchtáil. rides sé ar a chéile imscaradh ina ionad sin: an ról ar leagan is lú i measc na sraitheanna seo sweep i ndáiríre imscaradh, marcáilte le ``instructions`` (an modh ritheann an replay i) agus a 📖 sa teideal poist. :mod:`utils.roles.guide` chinneann a mhalairt is é sin; Is é an modúl seo cad a tharlaíonn an cinneadh i iontrálacha maitrís."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The repo treats `biber` as the canonical non-admin RBAC fixture: the user is provisioned by `roles/svc-db-openldap` and exposed to specs via the `lookup('users', 'biber')` filter. ~19 role specs already consume `BIBER_USERNAME` / `BIBER_PASSWORD` from `roles/<role>/templates/playwright.env.j2` and drive at least one non-admin scenario (typically: SSO login via Keycloak, land on the expected post-login surface, optionally assert that admin-only UI is absent)."
msgstr "An repo déileálann `biber` mar an daingneán Canonical neamh-admin RBAC: tá an t-úsáideoir ar fáil ag `roles/svc-db-openldap` agus nochta do specs tríd an `lookup('users', 'biber')` scagaire. ~19 specs ról ithe cheana féin `BIBER_USERNAME` / Baile `BIBER_PASSWORD` ó `roles/<role>/templates/playwright.env.j2` agus a thiomáint ar a laghad cás amháin neamh-admin (de ghnáth: SSO logáil isteach via Keycloak, talamh ar an dromchla iar-login ag súil, a dhearbhú go bhfuil Chomhéadain admin-amháin as láthair)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The repository already contains a modular environment test suite at [scripts/tests/workspace/](../../../scripts/tests/workspace/README.md). The commands from that suite are explained here as the intended end-to-end flow."
msgstr "Tá sraith tástála comhshaoil modúlach ag an stór cheana féin ag [scripts/tests/workspace/ Baile](../../../scripts/tests/workspace/README.md). Mínítear na horduithe ón tsraith sin anseo mar an sreabhadh deiridh atá beartaithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The repository already deploys role-level extension units, but each role spells the same concept differently and stores it in a different place:"
msgstr "An stór imscaradh cheana féin aonaid síneadh ról-leibhéal, ach gach ról spells an coincheap céanna difriúil agus siopaí sé in áit éagsúla:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The repository lint suite checks for `templates/Dockerfile.j2` files automatically:"
msgstr "Seiceálacha seomra lint stór le haghaidh `templates/Dockerfile.j2` comhaid go huathoibríoch:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The repository no longer maintains a generated `05_applications.yml` artifact. Keeping defaults close to the owning role reduces duplication and avoids stale generated state."
msgstr "Ní choinníonn an stór a ghintear a thuilleadh `05_applications.yml` Déantán. Laghdaíonn mainneachtainí a choinneáil gar don ról féin dúbailt agus seachnaíonn stát a ghintear stale."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The repository prefers many focused parts over one giant playbook."
msgstr "Is fearr leis an stór codanna dírithe go leor thar aon leabhar súgartha ollmhór."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The repository snapshot evaluated for this requirement contains 172 roles with a literal `application_id` and 18 role-local `mcp:` blocks. The audit below classifies every one of those 172 roles exactly once. The snapshot is planning evidence, not a second runtime registry: implemented surfaces remain authoritative in each role's `meta/services.yml`, while a generated lint test MUST prove that every current `application_id` still has a disposition."
msgstr "Tá an snapshot stór meastóireacht ar an gceanglas seo 172 róil le litriúil `application_id` agus 18 ról-áitiúil `mcp:` bloic. Rangaíonn an t-iniúchadh thíos gach ceann de na 172 róil go díreach uair amháin. Is é an pictiúr fianaise pleanála, ní clárlann dara runtime: dromchlaí i bhfeidhm fós údarásach i ngach ról `meta/services.yml`, MUST tástála lint a ghintear, cé go bhfuil gach reatha `application_id` tá fós diúscairt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The repository working tree stays clean (no `vendor/` checked in) and the host MUST NOT need a PHP or Composer installation."
msgstr "Fanann an stór crann oibre glan (Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil `vendor/` seiceáil isteach) agus an MUST óstach NACH gá PHP nó suiteáil Composer."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The repository working tree. Required for any code change."
msgstr "An crann stór oibre. Riachtanach le haghaidh aon athrú cód."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The requirements archive helper that used to live here has moved to [kpmx](https://pypi.org/project/kpmx/) so every kpmx-managed repository can rely on the same archival convention."
msgstr "Tá an cúntóir cairte a úsáidtear chun cónaí anseo tar éis bogadh go dtí [Déan teagmháil linn](https://pypi.org/project/kpmx/) mar sin is féidir le gach stór kpmx-bhainistithe brath ar an gcoinbhinsiún cartlainne céanna."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The rescue-diagnostics artifact one deploy job uploads."
msgstr "An tarrthála-diagnóisic Déantán amháin uaslódáil poist imscaradh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The resolved block replaces the mapping rather than being written into it. ``_build_role_base_config`` parks the YAML cache's own object under ``mcp``, so an in-place write would inject these keys into every later raw read of ``meta/mcp.yml``."
msgstr "Tagann an bloc réitithe in ionad na mapála seachas é a scríobh isteach ann. ``_build_role_base_config`` páirceanna an taisce YAML ar réad féin faoi ``mcp``, mar sin bheadh scríobh in-áit instealladh na heochracha isteach gach léamh ina dhiaidh sin amh ``meta/mcp.yml``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The result MUST be visually appealing and pleasant for humans to look at."
msgstr "An toradh MUST a achomharc amhairc agus taitneamhach do dhaoine chun breathnú ar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The result MUST feel like one coherent brand theme, not a collection of unrelated overrides."
msgstr "An toradh MUST bhraitheann cosúil le téama branda comhtháite amháin, ní bailiúchán de overrides neamhghaolmhara."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The result feeds the web-svc-mirror privacy proxy: the mirror's nginx vhost whitelists exactly these hosts as proxy upstreams, and the body-filter rewrite maps `https://<host>/...` to `<mirror>/<host>/...` in served HTML."
msgstr "Fothaí an toradh na web-svc-mirror seachfhreastalaí príobháideachta: an scáthán nginx vhost whitelists díreach na hóstach mar upstreams seachfhreastalaí, agus an comhlacht-scagair athscríobh léarscáileanna `https://<host>/...` go dtí `<mirror>/<host>/...` i HTML sheirbheáil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The result is a complete, reproducible domain rollout in a single playbook task."
msgstr "Is é an toradh iomlán, reproducible bhfearann rolladh amach i tasc playbook amháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The result is canonical_domains_map(applications, DOMAIN_PRIMARY). Per-app domain declarations live in `applications.<app>.domains` (canonical/aliases) and flow through the regular applications-merge pipeline."
msgstr "Is é an toradh canonical_domains_map(iarratais, DOMAIN_PRIMARY). Per-app dearbhuithe fearainn beo i `applications.<app>.domains` (Canonical/aliasess) agus sreabhadh tríd an píblíne iarratais a chumasadh go rialta."

msgid "The result is immutable and one source message is masked once per target language, so the same string arrives dozens of times per run."
msgstr ""

msgid "The result is stored on the stack host and rendered back into `model_info.traits.speed` on the same deploy, so the gateway restarts once with the numbers it just produced. A re-measured rate that moved less than 10% keeps its stored value, because no two runs measure the same machine and an unclamped result would restart the gateway for nothing. A model the measurement could not reach keeps its stored rate rather than losing it, so one bad minute does not unrank a model against its peers."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The resulting snippets cover every shared provider in the variant's closure, so the deploy stage finds the required `applications.<provider>.secrets.credentials` block in the inventory and `lookup('config', '<provider>', 'secrets.credentials.<key>')` succeeds."
msgstr "Clúdaíonn na snippets mar thoradh ar gach soláthraí roinnte i dúnadh an leagan, mar sin faigheann an chéim imscaradh an gá `applications.<provider>.secrets.credentials` bloc san fhardal agus `lookup('config', '<provider>', 'secrets.credentials.<key>')` éiríonn."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The resume offset a retrigger computes names a `role#variant` and carries no axes, because every axis rotates with the sweep number and a retrigger receives a fresh one."
msgstr "An atosú fhritháireamh ainmneacha retrigger computes `role#variant` agus déanann aon aiseanna, toisc go rothlaíonn gach ais leis an uimhir scuabtha agus faigheann retrigger ceann úr."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The returned token names a place in the ranking, so it carries no axes, and neither does the membership test behind it (:func:`proven_rows`): the source run recorded its combinations under its own sweep number and the retrigger gets a fresh one, so comparing them row by row is the only comparison that survives the rotation."
msgstr "Na hainmneacha chomhartha ar ais áit sa rangú, mar sin déanann sé aon aiseanna, agus ní dhéanann an tástáil bhallraíocht taobh thiar de (:func:`proven_rows`): an reáchtáil foinse a thaifeadadh a teaglaim faoina uimhir scuabtha féin agus faigheann an retrigger ceann úr, mar sin i gcomparáid leo as a chéile trí chéile é an comparáid ach amháin a mhaireann an rothlú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The reusable generator logic lives in `utils/domains/list.py`"
msgstr "Tá an loighic gineadóir reusable ina chónaí i `utils/domains/list.py`"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The reverse closure is fail-safe: any seed that is not modellable in the resolver (no `application_id` and not referenced by any role's `run_after`) MUST trigger a fall-back to a full deploy, as MUST any resolver runtime error. The closure MUST NOT silently shrink the deploy matrix on partial information. The variant narrowing follows the same rule: a role reached only through a `run_after` edge (which the round closure does not follow) keeps every variant, and so does a seed role itself, whose own files changed."
msgstr "Tá an dúnadh droim ar ais theipeann-sábháilte: aon síol nach bhfuil insamhalta sa réiteoir (Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil `application_id` agus gan tagairt ag aon ról `run_after`) MUST tús a chur le titim ar ais go dtí imscaradh iomlán, mar MUST aon earráid runtime réiteora. NÍ MÓR an dúnadh Laghdaigh an maitrís imscaradh ar eolas páirteach. Leanann an leagan cúngú an riail chéanna: ról bainte amach ach amháin trí `run_after` méid bláth: beag (nach leanann an dúnadh babhta) coimeádann gach leagan, agus mar sin a dhéanann ról síol féin, a bhfuil a comhaid féin athrú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The reverse closure is implemented in [affected resolver](../../../../cli/meta/roles/applications/resolution/affected/__main__.py) and invoked from [affected_roles.sh](../../../../scripts/meta/resolve/diff/affected_roles.sh). The workflow glue lives in [effective_whitelist.sh](../../../../scripts/github/resolve/effective_whitelist.sh)."
msgstr "Tá an dúnadh droim ar ais i bhfeidhm i [a bhfuil tionchar acu ar réiteach](../../../../cli/meta/roles/applications/resolution/affected/__main__.py) agus agairt ó [affected_roles.sh](../../../../scripts/meta/resolve/diff/affected_roles.sh). Tá an gliú sreabhadh oibre ina chónaí i [effective_whitelist.sh](../../../../scripts/github/resolve/effective_whitelist.sh)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The right choice should be easiest."
msgstr "Ba chóir go mbeadh an rogha ceart éasca."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role MUST NOT solve internal connectivity by globally disabling SSRF protection for all flow authors. If the exact pinned Flowise release cannot keep `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=true` for internal service DNS, the MCP workspace MUST be admin-only, egress MUST be restricted to a fixed-target MCP proxy, redirects MUST be disabled, DNS resolution MUST be revalidated at connection time, and network policy MUST prevent access to loopback, link-local metadata, unrelated application networks, and the container control plane."
msgstr "An ról NACH MUST réiteach nascacht inmheánach ag cosaint SSRF disabling ar fud an domhain do gach údair sreabhadh. Má tá an pinned cruinn Flowise Ní féidir scaoileadh choinneáil `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=true` do DNS seirbhíse inmheánach, an MCP workspace MUST a bheith admin-amháin, egress MUST a theorannú do seasta-target MCP seachfhreastalaí, Redirects MUST a bheith faoi mhíchumas, MUST réiteach DNS a athluacháil ag am nasc, agus beartas líonra MUST cosc rochtain ar lúbadh, meiteashonraí nasc-áitiúil, líonraí iarratais neamhghaolmhara, agus an eitleán rialaithe coimeádán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role MUST build its own Flowise image from the pinned npm package. The published `flowiseai/flowise` tags `3.1.3`, `3.1.4` and `latest` all ship the `flowise` package at version 3.1.2, which serves none of the `custom-mcp-servers`, `mcp-server` or `mcp-endpoint` routes; upstream's Dockerfile runs an unpinned `npm install -g flowise` whose layer the release CI reuses across builds. The deployed version therefore MUST come from `npm install -g flowise@<version>`, and the served route set MUST be verified rather than inferred from the tag."
msgstr "An ról MUST thógáil a chuid féin Flowise íomhá ón bpacáiste npm pinned. Foilsíodh é `flowiseai/flowise` tags `3.1.3`, `3.1.4` agus `latest` gach long an `flowise` pacáiste ag leagan 3.1.2, a fhreastalaíonn ar aon cheann de na `custom-mcp-servers`, `mcp-server` nó `mcp-endpoint` bealaí; Ritheann Dockerfile upstream ar neamhthuilleamaí `npm install -g flowise` a bhfuil ciseal an scaoileadh CI reuses ar fud na tógálacha. An leagan imscaradh dá bhrí sin MUST teacht ó `npm install -g flowise@<version>`, agus an bealach a sheirbheáil MUST a fhíorú seachas inferred as an chlib."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role MUST deploy cleanly under all four variants on a fresh box. V1 (ansible all-on) MUST additionally pass the biber + administrator Playwright personas plus the new `test-element-call` + `test-bridge-roster` specs."
msgstr "An ról MUST imscaradh go glan faoi gach ceithre leagan ar bhosca úr. VV VV1 (ansible all-on) MUST pas a fháil chomh maith leis an biber + riarthóir Playwright personas móide an nua `test-element-call` + + + + `test-bridge-roster` specs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role MUST deploy cleanly under all three variants on a fresh box. V1 (sso + ldap) and V3 (ldap-only) additionally MUST pass the biber + administrator Playwright personas."
msgstr "An ról MUST imscaradh go glan faoi gach trí leagan ar bhosca úr. VV VV1 (sso + ldap) agus V3 (taiseachas aeir: fliuch) chomh maith MUST pas a fháil ar an biber + riarthóir Playwright personas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role MUST follow the standard role-meta layout described in [layout.md](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md) (`meta/services.yml`, `meta/secrets.yml`, `meta/volumes.yml`, `meta/variants.yml`, `meta/info.yml`, `meta/main.yml`). [web-app-openproject](../../roles/web-app-openproject/) is the closest structural model — it combines PostgreSQL, a Redis `cache` service, background workers, an internal proxy, Keycloak SSO and LDAP — and SHOULD be used as the primary reference; [web-app-taiga](../../roles/web-app-taiga/) and [web-app-confluence](../../roles/web-app-confluence/) are secondary references."
msgstr "An ról MUST lean an leagan amach ról-meta caighdeánach cur síos ar i [layout.md](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md) (`meta/services.yml`, `meta/secrets.yml`, `meta/volumes.yml`, `meta/variants.yml`, `meta/info.yml`, `meta/main.yml`). [web-app-openproject](../../roles/web-app-openproject/) Is é an tsamhail struchtúrach is gaire - le chéile sé PostgreSQL, a Redis `cache` seirbhís, oibrithe cúlra, seachvótálaí inmheánach, Keycloak SSO agus LDAP - agus SHOULD a úsáid mar thagairt bunscoile; [web-app-taiga](../../roles/web-app-taiga/) agus [web-app-confluence](../../roles/web-app-confluence/) is tagairtí tánaisteacha iad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role MUST template `sites/{{ canonical_domain }}/site_config.json` (or the equivalent common-site-config layer) so Frappe's three Redis logical roles all point at the shared `svc-db-redis` instance with distinct DB numbers:"
msgstr "An ról MUST teimpléad `sites/{{ canonical_domain }}/site_config.json` (nó an ciseal coiteann-config coibhéiseach) mar sin Frappe ar trí Redis róil loighciúil gach pointe ag an roinnte `svc-db-redis` mar shampla le huimhreacha DB ar leith:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role abstracts package management operations using ``pkgmgr``. It ensures the package manager itself is updated once per run and provides idempotent installation and update routines for specified packages."
msgstr "An ról achomaireachtaí oibríochtaí bainistíochta pacáiste ag baint úsáide as ``pkgmgr``. Cinntíonn sé go bhfuil an bainisteoir pacáiste féin cothrom le dáta uair amháin in aghaidh an reáchtáil agus soláthraíonn sé suiteáil idempotent agus gnáthaimh cothrom le dáta le haghaidh pacáistí sonraithe."

