# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is waiting and availability checks. Build, release, and resource-specific lifecycle operations should stay in their dedicated directories."
msgstr "Tá raon feidhme an fhillteáin seo ag fanacht agus seiceálacha infhaighteachta. Ba cheart oibríochtaí saolré a thógáil, a scaoileadh, agus a bhaineann go sonrach le hacmhainní fanacht ina gcuid stiúrthóireachtaí tiomnaithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script **prefers `/mnt`** when it is a separate partition (classic `ubuntu-latest` layout with `/dev/sdb` mounted at `/mnt`) and falls back to `/` otherwise. Current public runners no longer expose a separate `/mnt`, so the swapfile lands on `/` and must not starve the root filesystem."
msgstr "An script **fearr `/mnt`** nuair is laindéal ar leith é (clasaiceach `ubuntu-latest` leagan amach le `/dev/sdb` suite ag `/mnt`) agus titim ar ais go dtí `/` ar shlí eile. Ní nochtann rádóirí poiblí reatha ar leith a thuilleadh `/mnt`, mar sin na tailte swapfile ar `/` agus ní mór a starve an córas comhaid fhréamh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script first starts the role's deployed backup unit (a fresh differential generation of the live material), then mirrors each present subtree back to its fixed system path (`rsync -a --delete`): `secrets` into `/var/lib/infinito/secrets`, `ca` into `/etc/<domain>/ca`, `acme` into `/etc/letsencrypt`, `certbot` into `/etc/certbot`. `--no-safety-backup` skips the pre-recover unit run. The `node` subtree (ssh host keys + machine-id) is restored only with `--restore-node-identity`, because overwriting the running machine-id / ssh host keys changes the host's identity mid-flight — do it on a fresh host after total loss."
msgstr "Tosaíonn an script an ról aonad cúltaca imscaradh (glúin úr difreálach den ábhar beo), ansin scátháin gach fochrainn faoi láthair ar ais go dtí a cosán córas seasta (`rsync -a --delete`): `secrets` isteach i `/var/lib/infinito/secrets`, `ca` isteach i `/etc/<domain>/ca`, `acme` isteach i `/etc/letsencrypt`, `certbot` isteach i `/etc/certbot`. `--no-safety-backup` skips an t-aonad réamh-aisghabháil reáchtáil. An bhfuil `node` cineál gas: in airde (eochracha óstach ssh + meaisín-id) ar ais ach amháin le `--restore-node-identity`, toisc go n-athraíonn róscríobh na heochracha óstach meaisín-id / ssh féiniúlacht an óstach lár-eitilt - é a dhéanamh ar óstach úr tar éis caillteanas iomlán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script first starts the role’s deployed backup unit (a fresh differential generation of the live material), then mirrors each present subtree back to its fixed system path (``rsync -a --delete``): ``secrets`` into ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets``, ``ca`` into ``/etc/<domain>/ca``, ``acme`` into ``/etc/letsencrypt``, ``certbot`` into ``/etc/certbot``. ``--no-safety-backup`` skips the pre-recover unit run. The ``node`` subtree (ssh host keys + machine-id) is restored only with ``--restore-node-identity``, because overwriting the running machine-id / ssh host keys changes the host’s identity mid-flight — do it on a fresh host after total loss."
msgstr "Tosaíonn an script an ról aonad cúltaca imscaradh (glúin úr difreálach den ábhar beo), ansin scátháin gach fochrainn faoi láthair ar ais go dtí a cosán córas seasta (``rsync -a --delete``): ``secrets`` isteach i ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets``, ``ca`` isteach i ``/etc/<domain>/ca``, ``acme`` isteach i ``/etc/letsencrypt``, ``certbot`` isteach i ``/etc/certbot``. ``--no-safety-backup`` skips an t-aonad réamh-aisghabháil reáchtáil. An bhfuil ``node`` cineál gas: in airde (eochracha óstach ssh + meaisín-id) ar ais ach amháin le ``--restore-node-identity``, mar gheall ar overwriting an reáchtáil meaisín-id / eochracha óstach ssh athruithe ar an óstach féiniúlacht lár-eitilt - é a dhéanamh ar óstach úr tar éis caillteanas iomlán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script must stay free of every shell ``$``: the compose and swarm render paths launder dollars differently (a ``$pid`` reached the container as ``\"\"`` and crash-looped the sidecar on a sh syntax error). The bucket bootstrap therefore polls ``/status`` from a backgrounded subshell while ``exec`` makes the server PID 1; the poll loop dies with the container and readiness is gated by the consumer's bounded wait."
msgstr "Ní mór don script fanacht saor ó gach bhlaosc ``$``: déanann na cosáin launder dollar a chumadh agus a mhionnú go héagsúil (a ``$pid`` shroich an coimeádán mar ``\"\"`` agus tuairteála-looped an sidecar ar earráid sh syntax). An buicéad buataisítrap dá bhrí sin vótaíochtaí ``/status`` ó subshell chúlra agus ``exec`` a dhéanann an freastalaí PID 1; básann an lúb vótaíochta leis an gcoimeádán agus tá ullmhacht gated ag fanacht faoi cheangal an tomhaltóra."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script opens the LUKS device (interactive passphrase prompt; `--passphrase-stdin` for automation), mounts it, picks the newest device snapshot across every machine hash (a fresh host after total loss has a new machine id), mirrors it into the target (`rsync -a --delete`) and unmounts/closes the device again. No pre-recover service backup runs: the device itself is the backup this role maintains. Afterwards restore individual applications from the backup root with the matching role's `recover.py` (`svc-bkp-volume-2-local` for docker volumes, `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local` for NFS exports)."
msgstr "Osclaíonn an script an gléas LUKS (pras passphrase idirghníomhach; `--passphrase-stdin` do uathoibriú), mounts sé, picks an pictiúr gléas is nuaí ar fud gach meaisín hash (ina óstach úr tar éis an caillteanas iomlán tá id meaisín nua), scátháin sé isteach sa sprioc (`rsync -a --delete`) agus unmounts / Dúnann an gléas arís. Ritheann aon cúltaca seirbhíse réamh-aisghabháil: Is é an gléas féin an cúltaca Coinníonn an ról seo. Ina dhiaidh sin ar ais iarratais aonair ón fhréamh cúltaca leis an ról meaitseáil ar `recover.py` (`svc-bkp-volume-2-local` do toirteanna docker, `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local` le haghaidh onnmhairí NFS)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script opens the LUKS device (interactive passphrase prompt; ``--passphrase-stdin`` for automation), mounts it, picks the newest device snapshot across every machine hash (a fresh host after total loss has a new machine id), mirrors it into the target (``rsync -a --delete``) and unmounts/closes the device again. No pre-recover service backup runs: the device itself is the backup this role maintains. Afterwards restore individual applications from the backup root with the matching role’s ``recover.py`` (``svc-bkp-volume-2-local`` for docker volumes, ``svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`` for NFS exports)."
msgstr "Osclaíonn an script an gléas LUKS (pras passphrase idirghníomhach; ``--passphrase-stdin`` do uathoibriú), mounts sé, picks an pictiúr gléas is nuaí ar fud gach meaisín hash (ina óstach úr tar éis an caillteanas iomlán tá id meaisín nua), scátháin sé isteach sa sprioc (``rsync -a --delete``) agus unmounts / Dúnann an gléas arís. Ritheann aon cúltaca seirbhíse réamh-aisghabháil: Is é an gléas féin an cúltaca Coinníonn an ról seo. Ina dhiaidh sin ar ais iarratais aonair ón fhréamh cúltaca leis an ról meaitseáil ar ``recover.py`` (``svc-bkp-volume-2-local`` do toirteanna docker, ``svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`` le haghaidh onnmhairí NFS)."

