msgid "The sidecar authenticates a Gitea token"
msgstr "Fíoraíonn an taobhcharr Gitea minicíocht uisce: flúirseach"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar creates its consumer's bucket itself at startup because a swarm stack's converge gate blocks before any post-deploy task could create it, deadlocking consumers that hard-fail on a missing bucket (e.g. the OpenTalk controller). The stock entrypoint routes every argv through ``weed`` (``sh`` as a command would become ``weed sh``), so the template overrides it with ``sh -c``; the server itself is still launched via ``/entrypoint.sh`` to keep its /data chown, privilege drop, and default server args."
msgstr "Cruthaíonn an taobhcharr buicéad a thomhaltóra féin ag an am tosaithe toisc go bhféadfadh bloic geata scuabtha Stack swarm roimh aon tasc iar-imscartha é a chruthú, tomhaltóirí a deadlocking go crua-fail ar buicéad ar iarraidh (e.g. an OpenTalk rialtóir rialtóir). Na bealaí iontrála stoc gach argv trí ``weed`` (``sh`` mar a bheadh ordú a bheith ``weed sh``), mar sin overrides an teimpléad sé le ``sh -c``; Tá an freastalaí féin a seoladh fós tríd ``/entrypoint.sh`` a choinneáil ar a chown / sonraí, titim phribhléid, agus args freastalaí réamhshocraithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar is never routed publicly. A bearerless probe of `/mcp` on the public vhost is answered with an SSO redirect, never with an MCP response."
msgstr "Ní dhéantar an taobhcharr a rianú go poiblí. A probe bearerless de `/mcp` ar an vhost poiblí freagraítear le atreorú SSO, riamh le freagra MCP."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar is never routed publicly. A bearerless probe of ``/mcp`` on the public vhost is answered with an SSO redirect, never with an MCP response."
msgstr "Ní dhéantar an taobhcharr a rianú go poiblí. A probe bearerless de ``/mcp`` ar an vhost poiblí freagraítear le atreorú SSO, riamh le freagra MCP."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar is reachable on the container network only, so a client probes it from inside the stack:"
msgstr "Is é an sidecar reachable ar an líonra coimeádán amháin, mar sin probes cliant sé ó taobh istigh den chairn:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar oauth2-proxy admits only the LibreTranslate administrator RBAC group and whitelists just the machine API paths (`/translate`, `/detect`, …); see [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml). Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under [Single sign-on](#single-sign-on) above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`. The `administrator` and `guest` personas run unconditionally."
msgstr "An oauth sidecar2-proxy admhaíonn ach an LibreTranslate riarthóir grúpa RBAC agus whitelists ach an meaisín API cosáin (`/translate`, `/detect`, ...); féach [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml). Laistigh den aip, tá údarú API-key-tier amháin agus decoupled as an IdP, mar atá doiciméadaithe faoi [Sínigh aonair ar](#single-sign-on) thuas. Tá cuairteoir neamh-admin dá bhrí sin aon seisiún Chomhéadain a thiomáint, mar sin [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) a dhearbhú `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`. An `administrator` agus `guest` personas reáchtáil gan choinníoll."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar oauth2-proxy admits only the LibreTranslate administrator RBAC group and whitelists just the machine API paths (``/translate``, ``/detect``, …); see ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under `Single sign-on <#single-sign-on>`__ above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run unconditionally."
msgstr "An oauth sidecar2-proxy admhaíonn ach an LibreTranslate riarthóir grúpa RBAC agus whitelists ach an meaisín API cosáin (``/translate``, ``/detect``, ...); féach ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under `Sínigh aonair ar <#single-sign-on>`__ above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas reáchtáil gan choinníoll."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar reads its upstream credential from an ``upstream.env`` file rather than from the compose environment, because the app password does not exist when the stack is first rendered. ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through ``svc-ai-mcp-adapter``\\ ’s ``rebuild.yml``: ``compose up`` resolves ``env_file`` while creating the container, which a restart would not."
msgstr "Léann an sidecar a chreidiúnacht suas le sruth ó ``upstream.env`` comhad seachas ón timpeallacht chumadh, toisc nach bhfuil an focal faire app ann nuair a bhíonn an chairn a rinneadh ar dtús. ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through ``svc-ai-mcp-adapter``\\ ’s ``rebuild.yml``: ``compose up`` resolves ``env_file`` agus a chruthú ar an gcoimeádán, nach mbeadh atosú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar reads its upstream credential from an `upstream.env` file rather than from the compose environment, because the app password does not exist when the stack is first rendered. [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through `svc-ai-mcp-adapter`'s `rebuild.yml`: `compose up` resolves `env_file` while creating the container, which a restart would not."
msgstr "Léann an sidecar a chreidiúnacht suas le sruth ó `upstream.env` comhad seachas ón timpeallacht chumadh, toisc nach bhfuil an focal faire app ann nuair a bhíonn an chairn a rinneadh ar dtús. [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) scríobhann go comhad tar éis an mint agus recreates an sidecar trí `svc-ai-mcp-adapter`'s `rebuild.yml`: `compose up` an t-eolas úsáideach `env_file` agus a chruthú ar an gcoimeádán, nach mbeadh atosú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar starts with `-r` (read-only) and a scope list covering user, repository, issue, pull request, search, file, branch, tag, commit and release."
msgstr "Tosaíonn an sidecar le `-r` (léamh amháin) agus liosta raon feidhme a chlúdaíonn úsáideoir, stór, eisiúint, iarraidh tarraingthe, cuardaigh, comhad, brainse, tag, tiomantas agus scaoileadh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar starts with ``-r`` (read-only) and a scope list covering user, repository, issue, pull request, search, file, branch, tag, commit and release."
msgstr "Tosaíonn an sidecar le ``-r`` (léamh amháin) agus liosta raon feidhme a chlúdaíonn úsáideoir, stór, eisiúint, iarraidh tarraingthe, cuardaigh, comhad, brainse, tag, tiomantas agus scaoileadh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The single `make compose-deploy` target resolves one or more bundles into the role groups declared under `all.children` and feeds them into the standard local deploy flow when `bundles=<csv>` is set. The resolver is [`utils.inventory.bundle_apps`](../../utils/inventory/bundle_apps.py); it deduplicates across bundles and preserves declaration order."
msgstr "An singil `make compose-deploy` réiteach sprioc amháin nó níos mó bundles isteach sa rólghrúpaí dearbhaithe faoi `all.children` agus feeds iad isteach sa sruth áitiúil caighdeánach nuair a `bundles=<csv>` Tá leagtha. Is é an réiteach [`utils.inventory.bundle_apps`](../../utils/inventory/bundle_apps.py); deduplicates sé thar bundles agus caomhnaíonn ordú dearbhaithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The single-database dumps, and the cluster dumps, which name their instance in the file name and go through ``baudolo-restore cluster``."
msgstr "Na dumpaí bunachar sonraí aonair, agus na dumpaí braisle, a ainmníonn a n-áit in ainm an chomhaid agus dul tríd ``baudolo-restore cluster``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The single-token `gh * <verb>*` patterns above only match when the third token starts with the verb. Compound names like `item-create` or `mark-template` slip through because the third token is the full compound, not the bare verb. These rules close that gap for Projects v2 mutations namespace-wide."
msgstr "An singil-chomhartha `gh * <verb>*` patrúin thuas mheaitseáil ach amháin nuair a thosaíonn an tríú chomhartha leis an briathar. Ainmneacha cumaisc mhaith `item-create` nó `mark-template` duillín tríd toisc go bhfuil an tríú chomhartha an cumaisc iomlán, ní an briathar lom. Dúnann na rialacha seo an bhearna do Thionscadail v2 sócháin ar fud an ainmspás."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The size is the config blob plus every layer blob, i.e. what a pull moves over the wire. A multi-platform index is resolved to the ``os_name``/``architecture`` manifest first."
msgstr "Is é an méid an blob config móide gach blob ciseal, i.e. cad a ghluaiseann tarraingt thar an sreang. Tá innéacs il-ardán réiteach leis an ``os_name``/ Baile``architecture`` a léiriú ar dtús."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The skill writes `.claude/settings.json` / `.claude/settings.local.json`, which is the source of truth for the permission model itself: allow/ask/deny rules, sandbox scope, env vars, and hook commands that run on every tool event. Auto-allowing it creates a privilege-escalation path where the agent can grant itself arbitrary new `allow` entries, install hooks that run arbitrary shell, or widen `sandbox.filesystem.allowWrite` / shrink `denyRead`, all without ever prompting. Sandbox write-scope does not stop this because `.` is in `allowWrite`. A single wildcard entry (`update-config*`) covers every current and future invocation shape in one rule."
msgstr "Scríobhann an scil `.claude/settings.json` / Baile `.claude/settings.local.json`, a bhfuil an fhoinse na fírinne don mhúnla cead féin: allow/ask/deny rialacha, raon feidhme bosca gainimh, env vars, agus orduithe Hook a reáchtáil ar gach ócáid uirlis. Cruthaíonn sé cosán pribhléid-scagáil nuair is féidir leis an ngníomhaire féin treallach nua a dheonú `allow` iontrálacha, crúcaí a reáchtáil bhlaosc treallach a shuiteáil, nó a leathnú `sandbox.filesystem.allowWrite` / Laghdaigh `denyRead`, go léir gan spreagadh riamh. Ní Sandbox scríobh-scóip stop seo mar gheall ar `.` Tá sé i `allowWrite`. iontráil cárta fiáin amháin (`update-config*`) Clúdaíonn sé gach cruth invocation reatha agus sa todhchaí i riail amháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The slug comes from :func:`axes.artifact_slug`, the same call the matrix entry carries into the workflow, so the name this looks for and the name CI uploads cannot drift apart."
msgstr "Tagann an sluga ó :func:`axes.artifact_slug`, an glaoch céanna a dhéanann an iontráil maitrís isteach sa sreabhadh oibre, mar sin an t-ainm Breathnaíonn sé seo agus ní féidir leis an ainm uaslódáil CI sruth óna chéile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The software's identity: its repository, read from the group_vars SPOT, its author and address."
msgstr "Féiniúlacht na bogearraí: a stór, léamh as an group_vars an t-údar agus a sheoladh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The source code of this software is publicly available for transparency, learning, and private use."
msgstr "Tá an cód foinse na bogearraí seo ar fáil go poiblí le haghaidh trédhearcacht, foghlama, agus úsáid phríobháideach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The source run read a window of the ranking, starting where *carried* put it (:func:`carried_index`) and stopping at its budget. Only the green part of that window is newly settled, so the answer is the last row of the leading run of *successful* rows behind the window's start, as a selection token -- a token still names the same row after the ranking shifts, a row count does not."
msgstr "An reáchtáil foinse léamh fuinneog an rangú, ag tosú i gcás *a iompar* chuir sé é (:func:`carried_index`) agus ag stopadh ar a bhuiséad. Níl ach an chuid glas den fhuinneog sin socraithe le déanaí, mar sin is é an freagra an tsraith dheireanach den phríomh-rúcht *rathúil* sraitheanna taobh thiar de thús na fuinneoige, mar chomhartha rogha - a chomhartha ainmneacha fós ar an tsraith chéanna tar éis na shifts rangú, ní comhaireamh as a chéile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The source run's ``priority`` input, whole."
msgstr "An foinse reáchtáil ar ``priority`` ionchur, iomlán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The spec MUST be at `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`. The role-relative path is the SPOT constant `ROLE_FILE_PLAYWRIGHT_SPEC` in [mapping.py](../../../../../utils/roles/mapping.py); registered as optional on `ROLE_TYPE_APPLICATION`, disallowed elsewhere."
msgstr "An MUST spec a bheith ag `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`. Is é an cosán ró-ghaol an tairiseach `ROLE_FILE_PLAYWRIGHT_SPEC` i [mapping.py](../../../../../utils/roles/mapping.py); cláraithe mar roghnach ar `ROLE_TYPE_APPLICATION`, dícheadú in áit eile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The split means contributors do not need to extend the allowlist for every new shell command: `Bash(*)` already covers them, and sandbox confinement bounds the blast radius. The `deny` list catches the small set of operations whose blast radius is destructive even within the sandbox. For example, `rm -rf .` would still erase the working tree and `.git/` because `.` is writable under `allowWrite`, so the `rm -rf*` deny rule closes that gap."
msgstr "Ní gá do na rannchuiditheoirí acmhainne scoilt an deisliosta a leathnú do gach ordú bhlaosc nua: `Bash(*)` Clúdaíonn siad cheana féin, agus greamaíonn gaibhniú bosca gainimh an ga soinneáin. An bhfuil `deny` liosta gabhálacha an tsraith beag oibríochtaí a bhfuil ga soinneáin millteach fiú laistigh den bhosca gainimh. Mar shampla, `rm -rf .` bheadh fós scrios an crann oibre agus `.git/` mar gheall ar `.` Is inscríofa faoi `allowWrite`, mar sin an `rm -rf*` Dúnann riail deny an bhearna sin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The stack deploy modes the CI test-deploy matrix (get_role_skip) covers."
msgstr "Na modhanna cruach imscaradh an CI maitrís tástála-imlonrach (get_role_skip) clúdaigh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The stack provides on-prem data storage, a local AI-adjacent service, centralized identity, and secure exposure through a reverse proxy. This bundle is a skeleton activation map."
msgstr "Soláthraíonn an Stack stóráil sonraí ar-ionad, seirbhís AI-adjacent áitiúil, aitheantas láraithe, agus nochtadh slán trí seachfhreastalaí droim ar ais. Is é seo an bundle léarscáil gníomhachtaithe creatlach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The stage a role is invoked in (deepest matching category wins)."
msgstr "Tá an chéim ról agairt i (Bhuaigh catagóir meaitseála is doimhne)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The staging dir exists and contains a non-empty `.env`."
msgstr "An dir staging ann agus tá neamh-empty `.env`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The standard OIDC `sub` claim is permitted as an alternative when the application explicitly requires a UUID-shaped identifier and stores its own mapping table. In that case the role MUST document the deviation in its README."
msgstr "An OIDC caighdeánach `sub` Tá éileamh ceadaithe mar mhalairt nuair a éilíonn an t-iarratas go sainráite aitheantóir UUID-chruthach agus siopaí a tábla mapála féin. Sa chás sin, doiciméadaíonn an ról MUST an diall ina README."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The steps, and the repos whose manifest could not be read. A repo that cannot state its layout is skipped rather than guessed at, but it must not take the others with it: recovering two repos of three beats recovering none because one manifest is corrupt."
msgstr "Na céimeanna, agus an repos nach bhféadfaí a léiriú a léamh. A repo nach féidir a lua go bhfuil a leagan amach skipped seachas guessed ag, ach ní mór é a chur ar na daoine eile leis: aisghabháil dhá stór de thrí buillí ais aon cheann toisc go bhfuil léiriú amháin truaillithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The stored bearer still authenticates"
msgstr "An marcóir stóráilte fíordheimhnithe fós"

