msgstr "Déanann an fochrainn an taobh ósta `apps/` briathar struchtúr le briathar agus raon feidhme de réir raon feidhme:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The subtree splits by user intent (the verb) and scope:"
msgstr "Roinneann an fochrann le hintinn an úsáideora (an briathar) agus raon feidhme:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The swarm deploy chain across both flavors:"
msgstr "An slabhra swarm imscaradh ar fud an dá blasanna:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The swarm path applies the same cut through the `blocked` parameter of `applications_if_group_and_all_deps`; `disable` roles are cut from the dep walk, so orphaned providers never enter the provisioned inventory and `swarm_deploy_targets` (bounded by inventory presence) cannot re-add them."
msgstr "Baineann an cosán muc an gearrtha céanna tríd an `blocked` paraiméadar de `applications_if_group_and_all_deps`; `disable` róil a ghearradh as an siúlóid dep, mar sin ní soláthraithe dílleachtaithe isteach ar an fardal ar fáil agus `swarm_deploy_targets` (faoi cheangal ag láithreacht fardal) Ní féidir iad a athchur."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The swarm-test nfs-server serves shared storage from userspace `nfs-ganesha` (the `ganesha` flavor of `svc-storage-nfs-server`, the default in every runtime), which runs inside the privileged DinD node and never touches the host kernel `nfsd`, so an interrupted export cannot wedge the host. The `kernel` flavor is a per-inventory override for real hosts, where `nfsd` is not shared across clusters. If a swarm step ever hangs at `Reload NFS exports` from a stuck kernel-NFS mount, you MUST recover with `make swarm-clean` on the host (needs sudo): it removes what the docker CLI can, then runs `umount -f -l /var/lib/infinito` + `exportfs -ua` + `systemctl restart docker`. The no-sudo sandbox only prints those commands, so the host recovery is mandatory and the sweep MUST stop until it is done; never fall back to compose-only."
msgstr "Feidhmíonn an nfs-freastalaí tástála muc stóráil roinnte ó spás úsáideora `nfs-ganesha` (an `ganesha` blas de blas `svc-storage-nfs-server`, an réamhshocraithe i ngach runtime), a ritheann taobh istigh den nód DinD phribhléid agus ní baint leis an eithne óstach `nfsd`, mar sin ní féidir le honnmhairiú isteach ding an óstach. An bhfuil `kernel` Is blas override per-ardaitheoir do hóstach fíor, áit a bhfuil `nfsd` nach bhfuil roinnte ar fud braislí. Má hangs céim swarm riamh ag `Reload NFS exports` ó mount Eithne-NFS bhfostú, MUST tú a ghnóthú le `make swarm-clean` ar an óstach (riachtanais uisce: measartha): cuireann sé cad is féidir leis an CLI Docker, ansin ritheann `umount -f -l /var/lib/infinito` + + + + `exportfs -ua` + + + + `systemctl restart docker`. An bosca gainimh no-sudo priontaí ach na orduithe, mar sin tá an aisghabháil óstach éigeantach agus an sweep MUST stad go dtí go bhfuil sé déanta; riamh titim ar ais go dtí chumadh-amháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sweep's ordered candidate rows: priority line first, then the regular line, each annotated with the modes it offers and whether it is priority."
msgstr "Sraitheanna iarrthóir ordaithe an sweep ar: líne tosaíochta ar dtús, ansin an líne rialta, gach anótáilte leis na modhanna a thairgeann sé agus cibé an bhfuil sé tosaíocht."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sync pass is the whole disaster drill against the host this role deploys on (`BKP_TEST_IS_STACK_HOST`), in one sequence: back up, seed the marker, back up again so the tested generation carries it, take every project down, restore through the recover chain, require the marker and every recorded container back, and finally let the host's own container health service judge."
msgstr "Is é an pas sync an druil tubaiste ar fad i gcoinne an óstach an ról seo imscaradh ar (`BKP_TEST_IS_STACK_HOST`), in ord amháin: ar ais suas, síol an marcóir, ar ais suas arís mar sin déanann an ghlúin a tástáladh é, gach tionscadal síos, ar ais tríd an slabhra ais, a cheangal ar an marcóir agus gach coimeádán a taifeadadh ar ais, agus ar deireadh in iúl an ósta ar féin deimhniúcháin seirbhíse sláinte coimeádán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The systemd services installed by `svc.sh` require a host with a real init system. Registration, service install, and service start are skipped when `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true`; the role can be fully deployed in DinD (binary extraction and `.env` file work). The nested `deploy-fresh-purged-apps` call in `test.sh` is also skipped when `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true` — in DinD, `make up` does not start the package-cache proxy (`cache_stack_enabled()` returns false in CI), so apt inside the fresh container cannot resolve the proxy hostname and package installs fail. Structural checks (binary + `.env`) are sufficient proof of a correct deploy in DinD; the full end-to-end deploy only runs on a real host."
msgstr "Na seirbhísí córasaithe suiteáilte ag `svc.sh` a cheangal ar óstach le córas init fíor. Clárú, suiteáil seirbhíse, agus tús seirbhíse a skipped nuair `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true`; is féidir an ról a imscaradh go hiomlán i DinD (eastóscadh dénártha agus `.env` obair comhad). An neadaithe `deploy-fresh-purged-apps` glaoch ar `test.sh` Tá skipped freisin nuair `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true` — in DinD, `make up` Ní thosaíonn an seachfhreastalaí pacáiste-cache (`cache_stack_enabled()` tuairisceáin bréagach i CI), mar sin ní féidir apt taobh istigh den choimeádán úr a réiteach an hostname seachfhreastalaí agus a shuiteáil pacáiste theipeann. Seiceálacha struchtúracha (dénártha + `.env`) go bhfuil cruthúnas leordhóthanach ar imscaradh ceart i DinD; Ritheann an deireadh-le-deireadh iomlán ach amháin ar óstach fíor."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The table below summarizes common Ansible plugin types and their conventional directory names."
msgstr "Achoimre ar an tábla thíos cineálacha breiseán Ansible coitianta agus a n-ainmneacha eolaire traidisiúnta."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The table lives in its own ``## Roles Overview 🧩`` section directly above ``## Use it online 🚀`` in the root README.md and is fully regenerated on every run; every other section stays untouched. Rows are the invokable roles, sorted ascending by the Entity column."
msgstr "Tá cónaí ar an tábla ina chuid féin ``## Roles Overview 🧩`` alt díreach os cionn ``## Use it online 🚀`` sa fhréamh README.md agus tá sé athghiniúint go hiomlán ar gach reáchtáil; fhanann gach alt eile untouched. Tá Rows na róil invokable, curtha in eagar ag an colún Aonán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The target refuses to drop a worktree with uncommitted changes. Show the operator that status and let them decide; only add `force=true` when they explicitly ask for it, because it discards the changes."
msgstr "Diúltaíonn an sprioc crann oibre a scaoileadh le hathruithe neamhchumtha. Taispeáin an t-oibreoir a stádas agus lig dóibh cinneadh a dhéanamh; ach cuir `force=true` nuair a iarrann siad go sainráite air, toisc go ndéanann sé na hathruithe a scriosadh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The target subtree must already exist; the script refuses to create export subtrees implicitly."
msgstr "Ní mór an fochrann sprioc ann cheana féin; diúltaíonn an script a chruthú fochrainn onnmhairithe intuigthe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The task sits in `tasks/stages/01_constructor.yml` after the `networks`, `design` and `service_provider` merges, after the `add_host` placements and after the token store, so the payload renders with the same `group_names`, `groups` and user records a role would see. Moving it earlier bakes stale values into the play."
msgstr "Suíonn an tasc i `tasks/stages/01_constructor.yml` tar éis an `networks`, `design` agus `service_provider` cumaisc, tar éis an `add_host` socrúcháin agus tar éis an siopa dearbhán, mar sin déanann an pálasta leis an gcéanna `group_names`, `groups` agus taifid úsáideora a bheadh ról a fheiceáil. Bogadh é níos luaithe bhácúis luachanna stale isteach sa spraoi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The template maps the generated palette to semantic variables such as `--color-01-solid-primary`, `--color-01-link-primary`, grayscale steps, and `--color-rgb-01-*`."
msgstr "An teimpléad léarscáileanna an pailéad a ghintear le hathróga shéimeantach ar nós `--color-01-solid-primary`, `--color-01-link-primary`, céimeanna grayscale, agus `--color-rgb-01-*`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The tested envelope 🧪"
msgstr "An clúdach tástála 🧪"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The theme MUST be bundled with the source repository (either checked in under ``themes/`` or referenced as a Hugo Module via ``go.mod``). V1 does not support a separate theme override."
msgstr "An téama MUST a cuachta leis an stór foinse (seiceáil isteach faoi ``themes/`` nó tagairt mar Hugo Modúl trí ``go.mod``). V1 ní thacaíonn sé le ró-bhród téama ar leith."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The theme MUST be bundled with the source repository (either checked in under `themes/` or referenced as a Hugo Module via `go.mod`). V1 does not support a separate theme override."
msgstr "An téama MUST a cuachta leis an stór foinse (seiceáil isteach faoi `themes/` nó tagairt mar Hugo Modúl trí `go.mod`). V1 ní thacaíonn sé le ró-bhród téama ar leith."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The three `API_*_KEY` entries are read as `${{ secrets.X || vars.X }}`, so a secret of the same name wins and the variable is the fallback. Prefer the secret: a repository **variable is not masked**, and the development inventory sets `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS: false`, so a key supplied as a variable can be printed by a task that echoes its own arguments."
msgstr "Na trí `API_*_KEY` iontrálacha a léamh mar `${{ secrets.X || vars.X }}`, mar sin tá rún de na bua ainm céanna agus is é an athróg an fallback. Tabhair an rún: stór **nach bhfuil athróg masced**, agus na tacair fardal forbartha `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS: false`, mar sin is féidir eochair ar fáil mar athróg a phriontáil ag tasc go macalla a argóintí féin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The three `svc-bkp-*` repository rows come from `backup_repos.repo_placements`. `utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py` calls `backup_repos.backup_provider_ips`, which resolves the same two closures and returns the nodes as IPs, to build `svc-bkp-remote-2-local.services.remote-2-local.backup_providers`."
msgstr "Na trí `svc-bkp-*` sraitheanna stór teacht ó `backup_repos.repo_placements`. `utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py` Glaoigh orainn `backup_repos.backup_provider_ips`, a réitíonn an dá dúnadh céanna agus tuairisceáin na nóid mar IPs, a thógáil `svc-bkp-remote-2-local.services.remote-2-local.backup_providers`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The three candidates that vendor documentation claimed were probed against running instances on 2026-08-27, and each is filed below on what the deployed artefact actually offers rather than on the claim:"
msgstr "Bhí na trí iarrthóirí a doiciméadú díoltóir éileamh probed i gcoinne cásanna a reáchtáil ar 2026- - - - -08- - - - -27, agus tá gach comhdaíodh thíos ar an méid a thairgeann an déantáin imscaradh iarbhír seachas ar an éileamh:"

msgid "The title a role presents itself under."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The title renders these as glyphs, so recovering one means translating a symbol back into a value; the log holds the word the operator picked. Reading it there keeps the retrigger honest even if the title's marker changes shape."
msgstr "Tugann an teideal seo mar glyphs, mar sin a ghnóthú ciallaíonn amháin aistriú siombail ar ais i luach; Tá an logáil an focal an t-oibreoir a roghnaíodh. Léitheoireacht Coinníonn sé ann an retrigger macánta fiú má athraíonn an teideal cruth marcóir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The title's priority segment is the cross-check, not the source: it proves a priority line existed even when truncation mangled it, so an empty log read is a broken reader -- expired logs, a moved Inputs block, an inlined orchestrator -- rather than a run dispatched without one."
msgstr "Is é deighleog tosaíochta an teidil an chros-seiceáil, ní an fhoinse: cruthaíonn sé líne tosaíochta ann fiú nuair a mangled teasctha é, mar sin is léitheoir briste é logáil folamh a léamh - logaí in éag, bloc Ionchuir ar athraíodh a ionad, ceolfhoireann inlined - seachas reáchtáil seolta gan ceann amháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token as an operator would have written it, for error messages."
msgstr "Bheadh an dearbhán mar oibreoir scríobh sé, le haghaidh teachtaireachtaí earráide."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token can name a row this ranking no longer has -- the role was removed, a variant was dropped, the filters moved. The start is then the first row the source run got green, which lies inside the same window and so never falls behind it. A run with nothing green and an unresolvable token leaves no anchor at all and starts at the head."
msgstr "Is féidir leis an dearbhán a rá as a chéile go bhfuil an rangú a thuilleadh - baineadh an ról, thit leagan, bhog na scagairí. Is é an tús ansin an chéad as a chéile fuair an sruth foinse glas, a luíonn taobh istigh den fhuinneog céanna agus mar sin ní thiteann taobh thiar de. A reáchtáil le rud ar bith glas agus gan réiteach chomhartha duilleoga aon ancaire ar chor ar bith agus a thosaíonn ag an ceann."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token each entry carries is the one the deployment issued, not the signed-in caller's own, so reaching an MCP tool server is a grant separate from signing in. The env renders `config.access_grants: []`, which `has_connection_access` reads as administrator-only, and [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) then narrows each entry to the serving role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "Is é an dearbhán gach iontráil an ceann an t-imscaradh a eisíodh, ní an sínithe-i callaire féin, mar sin a bhaint amach ar fhreastalaí uirlis MCP deontas ar leith ó síniú isteach. Déanann an env `config.access_grants: []`, a, `has_connection_access` léann mar riarthóir-amháin, agus [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) ansin caolaíonn gach iontráil chuig an ról ag freastal ar `mcp` Grúpa RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token each entry carries is the one the deployment issued, not the signed-in caller’s own, so reaching an MCP tool server is a grant separate from signing in. The env renders ``config.access_grants: []``, which ``has_connection_access`` reads as administrator-only, and ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ then narrows each entry to the serving role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "Is é an dearbhán gach iontráil an ceann an t-imscaradh a eisíodh, ní an sínithe-i callaire féin, mar sin a bhaint amach ar fhreastalaí uirlis MCP deontas ar leith ó síniú isteach. Déanann an env ``config.access_grants: []``, a, ``has_connection_access`` léann mar riarthóir-amháin, agus ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ then narrows each entry to the serving role’s ``mcp`` Grúpa RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token lifetime is bounded to one hour, and a new token is minted on every workflow run."
msgstr "Tá an saol chomhartha faoi cheangal uair an chloig, agus déantar chomhartha nua a mhionú ar gach sreabhadh oibre."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token lives in the store under the user named by the provider's ``mcp.credential.owner``, keyed by the provider's own ``application_id``. Spelling that out at each call site repeated the owner resolution, the two ``.get`` fallbacks and the trim in eighteen places, so a role that read it slightly differently read a different thing."
msgstr "An comhartha saol sa siopa faoin úsáideoir ainmnithe ag an soláthraí ``mcp.credential.owner``, eochairithe ag an soláthraí féin ``application_id``. Díol go amach ag gach suíomh glao arís agus arís eile an réiteach úinéir, an dá ``.get`` fallbacks agus an Baile Átha Troim in ocht n-áiteanna déag, mar sin ról a léamh sé beagán difriúil a léamh rud éagsúla."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token owner; tool calls run with that account's Mattermost permissions"
msgstr "An t-úinéir chomhartha; glaonna uirlis reáchtáil leis an gcuntas sin Mattermost irl - Library Service"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token owner; tool calls run with that account’s Mattermost permissions"
msgstr "An t-úinéir chomhartha; glaonna uirlis reáchtáil leis an gcuntas sin Mattermost irl - Library Service"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token store at ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets/tokens.yml`` survives compose+volumes purges. Matrix-deploy variant transitions wipe an app's persistent state but the stale token would otherwise be reused on the next round (for example matomo's API probe in ``sys-front-inj-matomo``, whose token-empty guard never fires while the prior round's token is still present). The purge orchestrator invokes this module to drop the matching ``users.<user>.tokens.<app_id>`` entries alongside the entity-level wipe."
msgstr "An siopa chomhartha ag ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets/tokens.yml`` maireachtáil chumadh + toitíní purges. Athruithe Maitrís-deploy wipe staid leanúnach app ach bheadh an chomhartha stale a athúsáid ar shlí eile ar an chéad bhabhta eile (mar shampla matomo ar API probe i ``sys-front-inj-matomo``, a bhfuil a garda chomhartha-empty riamh tinte agus tá an bhabhta roimhe ar chomhartha fós i láthair). An ceoltóir purge agairt an modúl chun titim ar an meaitseáil ``users.<user>.tokens.<app_id>`` iontrálacha taobh leis an wipe leibhéal an eintitis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token store is written on `STACK_HOST` while every `lookup('users').tokens` reader executes on the Ansible controller. In compose the two are one machine; in swarm they are not, so a provider that mints and persists its credential still resolves to an empty bearer for every client. The store therefore has to reach the controller as well."
msgstr "Tá an siopa chomhartha scríofa ar `STACK_HOST` le linn gach `lookup('users').tokens` léitheoir fhorghníomhú ar an rialtóir Ansible. I chumadh go bhfuil an dá meaisín amháin; i swarm nach bhfuil siad, mar sin soláthraí go mints agus leanann a credential réitíonn fós le settings folamh do gach cliant. Tá an siopa dá bhrí sin a bhaint amach ar an rialtóir chomh maith."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The top-level `compose.yml` is scoped to **local development and CI testing only**. It MUST NOT be used to deploy or run a live Infinito.Nexus stack. Production deployments MUST go through the Ansible roles and their own rendered compose files under `roles/<role>/templates/`."
msgstr "An leibhéal barr `compose.yml` go bhfuil raon feidhme **forbairt áitiúil agus tástáil CI amháin**. NÍ MÓR é a úsáid chun cónaí a imscaradh nó a reáchtáil Infinito.Nexus Stack. Imscaradh táirgeachta MUST dul tríd na róil Ansible agus a gcuid féin a rinneadh comhaid a chumadh faoi `roles/<role>/templates/`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The top-level `env` block sets process environment variables for every Claude Code session. It is currently used to disable GPG signing for agent-created commits via the additive `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` mechanism:"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The top-level node MUST be a YAML list. A non-list root is a hard error."
msgstr "An nód barrleibhéil MUST bheith ina liosta YAML. Is earráid chrua é fréimhe neamhliosta."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The trade-off is that `deny` now carries the full weight of \"what the agent must never do from the shell\". New destructive patterns MUST be added to `deny`. They can no longer be caught implicitly by an absent `allow` entry."
msgstr "Is é an trádáil-uaire go `deny` anois déanann an meáchan iomlán \"cad ní mór don ghníomhaire a dhéanamh as an bhlaosc\". patrúin nua millteach MUST a chur leis `deny`. Ní féidir iad a ghabháil a thuilleadh intuigthe ag as láthair `allow` iontráil."

msgid "The transitive fields (``services`` / ``consumed_by`` and their counts) are the BFS closure capped at ``max_level``; the ``*_direct`` fields are always the one-hop neighbours. ``weight`` is the sum of the four numeric columns. ``dna`` is a hash of the role's own name unioned with its embedded services (sorted), so two roles covering the same service set share a dna. ``siblings`` are the other roles sharing that dna; ``clone`` is True for every row of a dna group except the heaviest one (ties broken by name), so sorting clones last keeps one representative per service set ahead of the budget cut. ``random`` is a per-row 6-digit nonce, rolled fresh per invocation, so tie order deliberately varies between runs. ``variant`` is the ``meta/variants.yml`` index this row was computed against, or ``None`` for a whole-role row. ``id`` and ``covered_by`` are set by the CLI after sorting: ``id`` is the row's numeric position in sort order (1-based), and ``covered_by`` is the ``id`` of the first earlier (green) row of a DIFFERENT role that embeds this row, or the sentinel ``0`` when this row is itself green (no real ``id`` is 0). Two variants of the same role never cover each other. ``row`` is the 1-based line number in the final rendered output (assigned last, after filtering), so it stays sequential even when sorting by ``covered_by`` scrambles ``id``. ``variants`` is the number of ``meta/variants.yml`` variants of the role in whole-role mode; under ``--variant`` each row already is a single variant, so it is ``1``. ``lifecycle`` is the role's ``meta/services.yml`` lifecycle stage (alpha/beta/pre/…). ``compose`` / ``swarm`` are True when the CI test-deploy matrix exercises the role in that mode, honouring the discovery skip logic: invokable + lifecycle in the tested envelope + the role's ``skip`` list. Under ``--variant`` ``swarm`` is per-variant (every variant deploys, so it tracks the role-level ``swarm`` and ``stack``). ``stack`` is True when the role renders its own container stack (ships a ``templates/*compose*.yml.j2``); host-only roles (backup, wireguard, swapfile) and pure service-injectors are False. ``swarm`` implies ``stack``: a role with no compose template of its own is never a swarm stack-deploy target, so ``swarm`` is forced False when ``stack`` is False. ``host`` mirrors the primary entity's ``modes.host.enabled`` flag (default True) for non-stack roles, and is forced False for a stack role: it marks invokable roles that configure the host instead of shipping a stack. ``test_compose`` / ``test_swarm`` / ``test_host`` duplicate the mode columns minus the role's ``meta/tests.yml`` ``skip`` list: ``modes`` states where a role RUNS, ``skip`` deactivates TESTING a mode, and CI discovery filters on these ``test_*`` columns. ``integrated`` is False when the row's direct service map keeps no foreign provider enabled (the role deploys isolated): per variant on variant rows, from the base ``meta/services.yml`` on whole-role rows."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The translatable core strings are `galaxy_info.description` in every `roles/*/meta/main.yml` (266 roles), `title` and `description` of every node in [categories.yml](../../meta/categories.yml), the key and `description` of every entry in [menu_categories.yml](../../roles/web-app-dashboard/vars/menu_categories.yml), and the logout panel strings. Role titles are product names and MUST NOT be translated."
msgstr "Is iad na teaghráin croí translatable `galaxy_info.description` i ngach `roles/*/meta/main.yml` (266 Róil), `title` agus `description` de gach nód i [categories.yml](../../meta/categories.yml), an eochair agus `description` de gach iontráil i [menu_categories.yml](../../roles/web-app-dashboard/vars/menu_categories.yml), agus na teaghráin painéal logout. Tá teidil Ról ainmneacha táirge agus NACH MÓR a aistriú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The translatable strings core ships, keyed by the ``msgctxt`` of their source."
msgstr "Na teaghráin inaistrithe croí-longa, keyed ag an ``msgctxt`` dá bhfoinse."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The trigger is **group membership**, not a per-role flag."
msgstr "Is é an truicir **ballraíocht ghrúpa**, ní bratach per-role."

msgid "The trigger validates on its own before it dispatches, and refuses the whole run when a token cannot deploy on this branch. That refusal is not about deploy minutes: `call-orchestrator.yml` runs the same check as its first job and every other job needs it, so a bad token never reaches a chunk. It reaches the branch's concurrency group, which `entry-manual-steer.yml` declares with `cancel-in-progress`, so the doomed dispatch cancels the run currently in flight before failing its own validation."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The trivial static passthroughs live in two collector files: `passthrough.py` (always emitted) and `gha_passthrough.py` (emitted only when `ctx.on_gha` is true)."
msgstr "An passthroughs statach fánach beo i dhá comhad bailitheoir: `passthrough.py` (i gcónaí astaítear) agus `gha_passthrough.py` (astaítear ach amháin nuair `ctx.on_gha` Is fíor)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The trusted build additionally receives the Docker Hub mirror credentials (passed only when the label is present); untrusted builds mirror anonymously."
msgstr "Faigheann an tógáil iontaofa chomh maith na dintiúir scáthán Docker Hub (a rith ach amháin nuair a bhíonn an lipéad i láthair); Tógann untrusted scáthán gan ainm."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The two deploy-test workflows listed in the `Infrastructure tests` table of [workflows.md](../../tools/github/actions/workflows.md) (compose and swarm modes) run in parallel once DNS and mirroring have completed. Both cover all deployment types (`INFINITO_DISCOVER_ALL`, lifecycle-filtered to the `INFINITO_LIFECYCLES` envelope), not just the `web-*` server scope."
msgstr "An dá shreabhadh oibre tástála imscaradh atá liostaithe sa `Infrastructure tests` tábla de [workflows.md](../../tools/github/actions/workflows.md) (modhanna a chumadh agus a mhúscailt) reáchtáil i gcomhthráth uair amháin DNS agus scáthán curtha i gcrích. Clúdaíonn an dá chineál imscaradh (`INFINITO_DISCOVER_ALL`, saolré-scagtha leis an `INFINITO_LIFECYCLES` clúdach clúdach), ní hamháin ar an `web-*` raon feidhme freastalaí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The two host-qualified forms, then the bare ``/`` for a target the upstream expressed as an absolute path."
msgstr "An dá fhoirm ósta cáilithe, ansin an lom ``/`` le haghaidh sprioc an sruth in iúl mar cosán iomlán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The two inputs a retrigger decides itself rather than carrying over."
msgstr "An dá ionchur a retrigger chinneann féin seachas iompar ar láimh."

msgid "The two lanes run at the same time because they run on different machines. The CI run is remote; the local loop is this host."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The two measured inputs resolve in a fixed order: an inventory override (`RESOURCE_HOST_CPUS_OVERRIDE` / `RESOURCE_HOST_MEM_MB_OVERRIDE`), then the host's own hardware facts, then a probe of the machine this plugin runs on. The probe only applies to a target reached over the local connection, because a lookup executes on the Ansible controller: probing for a remote host would report the controller's hardware. That case raises and names the override to set."
msgstr "An dá ionchur tomhaiste réiteach in ord seasta: override fardal (`RESOURCE_HOST_CPUS_OVERRIDE` / Baile `RESOURCE_HOST_MEM_MB_OVERRIDE`), ansin an óstach fíricí crua-earraí féin, ansin probe an meaisín ritheann an breiseán ar. Ní bhaineann an probe ach le sprioc bainte amach thar an nasc áitiúil, mar gheall ar fhorghníomhú Lookup ar an rialtóir Ansible: Bheadh probing do óstach iargúlta tuairisc crua-earraí an rialaitheora. Ardaíonn an cás sin agus ainmneacha an override a shocrú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The two mutual-exclusion guards (*tests/integration/iam/oauth2_oidc/test_mutual_exclusive.py*, *test_acl_mutual_exclusive.py*) — obsolete under the single-block schema."
msgstr "An dá gardaí frith-eisiaimh (*tests/integration/iam/oauth2_oidc/test_mutual_exclusive.py*, *test_acl_mutual_exclusive.py*) - i léig faoin scéimre aon-bhloc."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The unified `# noqa` / `# nocheck` syntax that suppresses individual checks across the infinito-nexus test suite."
msgstr "An aontaithe `# noqa` / Baile `# nocheck` syntax a chuireann bac ar sheiceálacha aonair ar fud an tsraith tástála infinito-nexus."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The unified schema supports:"
msgstr "Tacaíonn an scéimre aontaithe:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The universal-logout service ([web-svc-logout](../../../../../roles/web-svc-logout/)), when attached to a deployment, injects JavaScript that auto-detects every logout control across the role tree and rewrites it to redirect through Keycloak's end-session endpoint. Persona scenarios therefore do NOT branch on whether universal-logout is active: they always click the role's own logout button. The injected JS handles the redirect when active, the click clears the local session when not, and the post-click assertion (`assertUnauthenticatedLanding`) is identical in both cases."
msgstr "An tseirbhís uilíoch-logout ([web-svc-logout](../../../../../roles/web-svc-logout/)), nuair a ghabhann sé le himscaradh, instealladh JavaScript go auto-detects gach rialú logout ar fud an crann ról agus athscríobh sé a atreorú trí Keycloak's críochphointe an tseisiúin. Dá bhrí sin, ní féidir le cásanna Duine a bheith ina bhrainse ar cibé an bhfuil logáil uilíoch gníomhach: cliceáil ar an ról i gcónaí cnaipe logála féin. Láimhseálann an JS instealladh an atreorú nuair gníomhach, soiléiríonn an cliceáil an seisiún áitiúil nuair nach bhfuil, agus an dearbhú iar-chliceáil (`assertUnauthenticatedLanding`) Tá sé comhionann sa dá chás."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The upstream `oauth2-proxy` MUST set `X-Forwarded-User` (or `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`) and `X-Forwarded-Email` on every request that reaches the broker. Without `X-Forwarded-User`, the broker returns HTTP 401, there is no anonymous fallback by design."
msgstr "An sruth `oauth2-proxy` MUST leagtha `X-Forwarded-User` (nó `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`) agus `X-Forwarded-Email` ar gach iarratas a shroicheann an bróicéir. Gan Sreang `X-Forwarded-User`, tuairisceáin an bróicéir HTTP 401, níl aon fallback gan ainm ag dearadh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The upstream server is stdio-oriented and broadly mutating over a cache several applications share."
msgstr "Is é an freastalaí upstream stdio-dhírithe agus go ginearálta mutating thar taisce roinnt iarratais."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The upstream server is stdio-oriented and broadly mutating. Keep `stdio_only_and_shared_cache` unless an isolated instance, prefix-scoped ACL principal, pinned bridge, and exact read-only tool list are supplied. Prefer using Redis as an internal agent-memory backend rather than a user-visible server."
msgstr "Is é an freastalaí upstream stdio-dhírithe agus go ginearálta mutating. Coinnigh orainn `stdio_only_and_shared_cache` mura soláthraítear cás iargúlta, príomhoide ACL réamhscóipthe, droichead pinned, agus liosta uirlise léite amháin. Prefer ag baint úsáide as Redis mar chúlscríbhinn gníomhaire inmheánach seachas freastalaí úsáideoir-visible."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The user is a direct member of the expected group (not only a parent OU)."
msgstr "Is é an t-úsáideoir ina bhall díreach den ghrúpa ag súil leis (ní amháin OU tuismitheoir)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The user is created idempotently (safe to run multiple times)."
msgstr "Tá an t-úsáideoir a cruthaíodh idempotently (sábháilte a reáchtáil amanna éagsúla)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The userland tools are baked into every distro image by [filesystem.sh](../../scripts/install/filesystem.sh); the kernel side comes from the host."
msgstr "Tá na huirlisí úsáide bácáilte i ngach íomhá distro ag [filesystem.sh](../../scripts/install/filesystem.sh); Tagann an taobh eithne ón óstach."

msgid "The v3 address is ``base32(PUBKEY || CHECKSUM || VERSION)`` where ``CHECKSUM = SHA3-256(\".onion checksum\" || PUBKEY || VERSION)[:2]`` and ``VERSION = 0x03`` (see spec.torproject.org/address-spec). Tor stores the *expanded* ed25519 secret key ``clamp(SHA512(seed)[:32]) || SHA512(seed)[32:]`` in ``hs_ed25519_secret_key``; the public key ``clamp(SHA512(seed)[:32]) * B`` equals the standard ed25519 public key, so it is taken straight from ``cryptography`` without needing scalar multiplication."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The value a row draws from *pool* this sweep: a plain rotation over the row's global position, so consecutive rows spread across the pool and consecutive sweeps move every row on to the next value."
msgstr "Tarraingíonn an luach as a chéile ó *linn snámha linn snámha* an sweep: rothlú plain thar an tsraith seasamh domhanda, sraitheanna chomh as a chéile scaipthe ar fud an linn snámha agus sweeps as a chéile bogadh gach chéile ar aghaidh go dtí an chéad luach eile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The value as it now stands in the file, or \"\" when it was removed."
msgstr "An luach mar a sheasann sé anois sa chomhad, nó \"\" nuair a baineadh é."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The value can be adjusted or overridden via inventory, group vars, or host vars if needed."
msgstr "Is féidir an luach a choigeartú nó a shárú trí fhardal, vars grúpa, nó vars óstach más gá."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The value is always double-quoted in the output. That makes the emit safe for YAML edge cases like `restart: no` (bare `no` would otherwise parse as a boolean) without burdening the caller with quoting rules."
msgstr "Tá an luach i gcónaí dúbailte luaite san aschur. Sin a dhéanann an astaíonn sábháilte do chásanna imeall YAML cosúil `restart: no` (lom `no` bheadh ar shlí eile parse mar boolean) gan ualach a chur ar an nglacadóir le rialacha luaite."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The value must mirror how the backed-up group is keyed. `all` treats every matched run as one instance — correct for `global-ci-<repo>-<ref_name>`, which spans both `entry-push-latest.yml` and `entry-manual-steer.yml`, so a push must be able to reap a manual sweep. `event` keeps one instance per event name — correct for `pr-ci-<repo>-<event_name>-pr-<number>`. Grouping any finer than the real key spares a run the group would have reaped: per-workflow grouping leaves the manual sweep alive, because it is the newest run of its own workflow."
msgstr "Ní mór don luach scáthán a dhéanamh ar an gcaoi a bhfuil an grúpa cúlaithe bunaithe. `all` déileálann gach reáchtáil mheaitseáil mar shampla amháin - ceart le haghaidh `global-ci-<repo>-<ref_name>`, a théann trasna an dá `entry-push-latest.yml` agus `entry-manual-steer.yml`, mar sin ní mór a bhrú a bheith in ann a reap sweep láimhe. `event` coimeádann cás amháin in aghaidh an ainm ócáid - ceart le haghaidh `pr-ci-<repo>-<event_name>-pr-<number>`. Ag grúpáil aon níos fearr ná an fíor-eochair spártha a reáchtáil go mbeadh an grúpa reaped: fágann grúpáil per-workflow an scuab láimhe beo, toisc go bhfuil sé an reáchtáil is nua dá sreabhadh oibre féin."

msgid "The value name, or None when no allowed value cleared *minimum*. None is a real answer: the measurement cannot carry a pin, and the caller leaves that axis to the rotation instead of guessing it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The values one axis may draw from this run."
msgstr "Is féidir leis na luachanna ais amháin a tharraingt as an rith."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The variant of *app* that carries the replay, and the mode it runs in."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The variant only affects inventory generation; the Ansible deploy itself reads `applications.<app>` overrides from the variant-resolved inventory and MUST NOT consult variant data at runtime."
msgstr "Bíonn tionchar ag an leagan ach ar ghiniúint fardail; léann an Infheicthe féin `applications.<app>` overrides ón bhfardal athraitheach agus NACH MUST i gcomhairle le sonraí athraitheacha ag runtime."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The variant override is baked as a real boolean into the inventory, so the shared-service auto-include picks it up at build time. Variant 0 therefore pulls `web-app-discourse` into the include set. Variant 1 does not."
msgstr "Tá an override athraitheach bácáilte mar boolean fíor isteach san fhardal, mar sin an auto-seirbhíse roinnte-áirítear picks sé suas ag am a thógáil. Amharc ar gach eolas 0 dá bhrí sin pulls `web-app-discourse` san áireamh sraith. Amharc ar gach eolas 1 nach bhfuil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The variant that enables the fewest services, as the matrix writes it; the lowest index wins a tie, and ``''`` means none qualifies."
msgstr "An leagan a chuireann ar chumas na seirbhísí is lú, mar a scríobhann an maitrís é; Bhuaigh an t-innéacs is ísle comhionannas vótaí, agus ``''`` ciallaíonn aon cháilíonn."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The verb folder name expresses the deploy intent. The script name expresses the scope."
msgstr "Léiríonn an t-ainm fillteán focal an intinn imscaradh. Léiríonn ainm an script an raon feidhme."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The version is read from roles/<application_id>/files/package-lock.json, so the URL is always the exact pinned, lockfile-reproducible version."
msgstr "Tá an leagan a léamh ó róil /<application_id>/ comhaid / pacáiste-lock.json, mar sin tá an URL i gcónaí ar an pinned cruinn, glas comhad-laghdaithe leagan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The vhost is identified by the ``domains.canonical`` key that carries the domain, which is the same key ``server.status_codes`` uses. A domain that is not canonical, or a key that declares nothing, falls back to the declared ``default``."
msgstr "Tá an vhost aitheanta ag an ``domains.canonical`` eochair a dhéanann an bhfearann, a bhfuil an eochair chéanna ``server.status_codes`` úsáidí. Fearann nach bhfuil Canonical, nó eochair a dhearbhaíonn rud ar bith, titim ar ais go dtí an dearbhaithe ``default``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The vocabulary a package plan is written in."
msgstr "Tá an stór focal plean pacáiste scríofa i."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The volume repo contributes a database step after its file steps: the dumps have to land once the volumes are back and while the consumers are still down, which is where the caller has them."
msgstr "Cuireann an repo toirt céim bhunachar sonraí tar éis a chéimeanna comhaid: ní mór na dumpaí a thabhairt i dtír nuair a bhíonn na méideanna ar ais agus cé go bhfuil na tomhaltóirí fós síos, a bhfuil i gcás ina bhfuil an glaoiteoir iad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The warning MUST name the role, the addon id, and the failing step so the operator can act without reading raw task output."
msgstr "An rabhadh MUST ainm an ról, an id addon, agus an chéim ag teip ionas gur féidir leis an oibreoir gníomhú gan léamh aschur tasc amh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The wget half stays proxy-aware on purpose: busybox wget rejects ``--proxy=off``, and this flavor exists for images where which tool ships is unknown, so hardening it there would break the very case it covers."
msgstr "An wget leath tréimhsí seachfhreastalaí-aware ar na críche: bosca gnóthach Diúltaíonn wget ``--proxy=off``, agus tá an blas le haghaidh íomhánna ina bhfuil longa uirlis anaithnid, mar sin hardening sé go mbeadh briseadh an cás an-chlúdaíonn sé."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The wildcard in the namespace slot collapses 21 mutating verbs across `gh issue/pr/release/repo/ruleset/run/cache/gist/label/project/…` into a single rule per verb. Future namespaces that ship the same verb (e.g. a hypothetical `gh discussion lock`) are caught automatically. Explicit per-namespace lists rot as the `gh` CLI grows."
msgstr "Titeann an cárta fiáin sa sliotán ainmspás 21 briathra mutating ar fud `gh issue/pr/release/repo/ruleset/run/cache/gist/label/project/…` i riail amháin in aghaidh an bhriathar. Spásanna ainmneacha sa todhchaí a long an briathar céanna (e.g. hipitéiseach `gh discussion lock`) a ghabháil go huathoibríoch. Liostaí eisiach per-namespace lobhadh mar `gh` Fásann CLI."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The window's start is the floor: with nothing green behind it the answer is the start itself, never the head. Walking back to the head is what made every retrigger redeploy the whole stretch its predecessors had already proven."
msgstr "Is é tús na fuinneoige an t-urlár: le rud ar bith glas taobh thiar de go bhfuil an freagra an tús féin, riamh an ceann. Ag siúl ar ais go dtí an ceann a rinne gach retrigger ath-imlonnú an stráice ar fad a bhí cruthaithe cheana féin a réamhtheachtaithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The wiring block sits behind a ``file_exists`` guard on ``extensions/VisualEditorPlus/vendor/autoload.php``, because ``LocalSettings.php`` is rendered before the extensions are installed and ``VisualEditorPlus`` fatals until its composer step has run."
msgstr "Suíonn an bloc sreangú taobh thiar de ``file_exists`` garda ar ``extensions/VisualEditorPlus/vendor/autoload.php``, mar gheall ar ``LocalSettings.php`` a rinneadh roimh na síntí suiteáilte agus ``VisualEditorPlus`` básanna go dtí go bhfuil a chéim cumadóir rith."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The wiring block sits behind a `file_exists` guard on `extensions/VisualEditorPlus/vendor/autoload.php`, because `LocalSettings.php` is rendered before the extensions are installed and `VisualEditorPlus` fatals until its composer step has run."
msgstr "Suíonn an bloc sreangú taobh thiar de `file_exists` garda ar `extensions/VisualEditorPlus/vendor/autoload.php`, mar gheall ar `LocalSettings.php` a rinneadh roimh na síntí suiteáilte agus `VisualEditorPlus` básanna go dtí go bhfuil a chéim cumadóir rith."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The wiring that makes this work is purely in the `services` declaration, not in `run_after`:"
msgstr "Is é an sreangú a dhéanann an obair seo amháin sa `services` dearbhú, nach bhfuil i `run_after`:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The workaround used here is the **GitLab OAuth2 provider** (`MM_GITLABSETTINGS_*`), which is generic enough to work with any OIDC-compatible identity provider including Keycloak. This provides true SSO: user accounts are automatically created in Mattermost on first login."
msgstr "Is é an workaround a úsáidtear anseo an **GitLab Uisce agus Séarachas2 soláthróir** (`MM_GITLABSETTINGS_*`), atá cineálach go leor chun oibriú le haon soláthraí aitheantais OIDC-comhoiriúnach lena n-áirítear Keycloak. Soláthraíonn sé seo SSO fíor: cuntais úsáideora a cruthaíodh go huathoibríoch i Mattermost ar an gcéad logáil isteach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The workaround used here is the **GitLab OAuth2 provider** (``MM_GITLABSETTINGS_*``), which is generic enough to work with any OIDC-compatible identity provider including Keycloak. This provides true SSO: user accounts are automatically created in Mattermost on first login."
msgstr "Is é an workaround a úsáidtear anseo an **GitLab Uisce agus Séarachas2 soláthróir** (``MM_GITLABSETTINGS_*``), atá cineálach go leor chun oibriú le haon soláthraí aitheantais OIDC-comhoiriúnach lena n-áirítear Keycloak. Soláthraíonn sé seo SSO fíor: cuntais úsáideora a cruthaíodh go huathoibríoch i Mattermost ar an gcéad logáil isteach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The workflow-driven jobs additionally require the `BOT_APP_CLIENT_ID` and `BOT_APP_PRIVATE_KEY` repository secrets, see [secrets.md](secrets.md). Without those secrets, runs fail at the token-minting step and no PR is opened."
msgstr "Éilíonn na poist sreabhadh oibre freisin ar an `BOT_APP_CLIENT_ID` agus `BOT_APP_PRIVATE_KEY` rúin stór, féach [secrets.md](secrets.md). Gan na rúin, ritheann theipeann ar an chéim chomhartha-minting agus ní oscail PR."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The workload form only changes step 6: a stack that carries services gets `docker stack rm`, a role whose compose renders none gets its compose project stopped on every node. `has_swarm_service` decides by asking the deployed stack. Every other step operates on volumes, the NFS export and the deployed backup units, independent of the orchestrator."
msgstr "Ní athraíonn an fhoirm ualach oibre ach céim 6: Stack a dhéanann seirbhísí faigheann `docker stack rm`, ról a bhfuil a chumadh rindreáil fhaigheann aon cheann a tionscadal a chumadh stop ar gach nód. `has_swarm_service` chinneann trí iarraidh ar an chairn imscaradh. Feidhmíonn gach céim eile ar imleabhair, ar onnmhairiú an NFS agus ar na haonaid cúltaca imscaradh, neamhspleách ar an gceolaire."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The worst entry point (``entry-*.yml``) adds its own jobs to the same run before calling the orchestrator; that overhead is subtracted too."
msgstr "An pointe iontrála is measa (``entry-*.yml``) Cuireann a chuid post féin leis an rith céanna roimh glaoch ar an orchestrator; go bhfuil forchostais dhealú freisin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The wp-discourse plugin install in [roles/web-app-wordpress/tasks/addons/wp-discourse.yml](../../../roles/web-app-wordpress/tasks/addons/wp-discourse.yml) does `container exec discourse rake api_key:create_master[...]` during the WordPress play. The Discourse container therefore has to exist by the time WordPress runs."
msgstr "An breiseán wp-discourse shuiteáil i [roles/web-app-wordpress/tasks/addons/wp-discourse.yml](../../../roles/web-app-wordpress/tasks/addons/wp-discourse.yml) a dhéanann `container exec discourse rake api_key:create_master[...]` le linn an WordPress imirt. An bhfuil Discourse coimeádán dá bhrí sin, tá a bheith ann ag an am WordPress Ritheann."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The writable ``secrets.credentials`` node of one application block."
msgstr "An inscríofa ``secrets.credentials`` nód de bhloc iarratais amháin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The writer a handler picks decides how long a value lives. Both kinds are registered in `default.env` and both are visible to the lints; they differ only in whether the generated `.env` remembers what the environment said."
msgstr "Cinneann an scríbhneoir a picks láimhseálaí cé chomh fada agus a saol luach. Tá an dá chineál cláraithe i `default.env` agus tá an dá le feiceáil ar na lints; tá siad difriúil ach amháin i cibé an bhfuil an ghintear `.env` cuimhin cad a dúirt an timpeallacht."

msgid "Then dispatch:"
