# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role refreshes the package index and upgrades every installed package on the host. ``tasks/main.yml`` reads ``ansible_facts['distribution']`` and dispatches to one of three task files grouped by package-manager family. Debian and Ubuntu both use ``apt``, Fedora and CentOS both use ``dnf``, so each pair shares a single task file. A separate ``unsupported.yml`` fails loudly with a clear message when a host runs a distribution that this role does not yet cover."
msgstr "Refreshes an ról seo an t-innéacs pacáiste agus uasghrádú gach pacáiste suiteáilte ar an óstach. ``tasks/main.yml`` léamha ``ansible_facts['distribution']`` agus seolta chuig ceann de thrí comhad tasc grúpáilte ag teaghlach pacáiste-bainisteoir. Debian agus Ubuntu araon úsáid ``apt``, Fedora agus CentOS araon úsáid ``dnf``, mar sin scaireanna gach péire comhad tasc amháin. A ar leith ``unsupported.yml`` teipeann os ard le teachtaireacht soiléir nuair a ritheann óstach dáileadh nach bhfuil an ról seo a chlúdach go fóill."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role refreshes the package index and upgrades every installed package on the host. `tasks/main.yml` reads `ansible_facts['distribution']` and dispatches to one of three task files grouped by package-manager family. Debian and Ubuntu both use `apt`, Fedora and CentOS both use `dnf`, so each pair shares a single task file. A separate `unsupported.yml` fails loudly with a clear message when a host runs a distribution that this role does not yet cover."
msgstr "Refreshes an ról seo an t-innéacs pacáiste agus uasghrádú gach pacáiste suiteáilte ar an óstach. `tasks/main.yml` léamha `ansible_facts['distribution']` agus seolta chuig ceann de thrí comhad tasc grúpáilte ag teaghlach pacáiste-bainisteoir. Debian agus Ubuntu araon úsáid `apt`, Fedora agus CentOS araon úsáid `dnf`, mar sin scaireanna gach péire comhad tasc amháin. A ar leith `unsupported.yml` teipeann os ard le teachtaireacht soiléir nuair a ritheann óstach dáileadh nach bhfuil an ról seo a chlúdach go fóill."

