# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Trusted fork PRs: a maintainer-applied *trusted-pr* label runs a fork PR as deliberately released code — the orchestrator skips the fork-prerequisite wait and the privileged *pull_request_target* build switches its source from the base merge ref to the raw PR head, while the built image keeps the merge-SHA tag so every downstream consumer is unchanged. The label is the only switch (applying a label is collaborator-only on GitHub, so fork authors cannot grant it), build-orchestration scripts always come from the base repository, and both unlabeled fork PRs and same-repository PRs are untouched. See [the fork-PR pipeline](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md) and [the contributor fork workflow](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pull-request.md)."
msgstr "Forc PRanna Iontaofa: a maintainer-feidhmithe *iontaofa-pr* Ritheann lipéad PR forc mar a scaoileadh d'aon ghnó cód - skips an ceolfhoireann an fanacht forc-réamhriachtanas agus an phribhléid *pull_request_target* a thógáil lasca a fhoinse as an bonn a chumasc ref chuig an ceann PR amh, agus coimeádann an íomhá tógtha an chlib merge-SHA mar sin tá gach tomhaltóir downstream gan athrú. Is é an lipéad an t-aon athrú (Is lipéad a chur i bhfeidhm comhoibritheach-amháin ar GitHub, mar sin ní féidir le húdair forc é a dheonú), a thógáil-orchestration scripteanna teacht i gcónaí as an stór bonn, agus an dá PRanna forc neamhlipéadaithe agus PRanna céanna-taisce atá untouched. Féach ar [an píblíne forc-PR](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md) agus [sreabhadh oibre an rannchuiditheora](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pull-request.md)."

