# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "What still blocks it is the transport. `server.py` speaks streamable HTTP upstream: `post_upstream` POSTs JSON-RPC to one URL and reads the reply, optionally SSE-framed. Baserow serves the older HTTP+SSE transport, where the client opens the stream and posts to the endpoint that stream announces — the shape `roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.py` implements for `transport: sse` (\"the stream is the response channel and the endpoint it announces is the request channel\"). Fronting Baserow therefore needs that client transport in the adapter, or evidence that Baserow 2.3.3 also accepts a plain streamable-HTTP POST, which only a running instance can settle. A second consequence is waiting behind it: `web-app-n8n` speaks only `sse`, so it drops out of `allowed_consumers` the moment the surface becomes `streamable_http`."
msgstr "Cad bloic fós go bhfuil sé an t-iompar. `server.py` Labhraíonn sruthú HTTP upstream: `post_upstream` POSTs JSON-RPC le URL amháin agus léann an freagra, roghnach SSE-fráma. Feidhmíonn Baserow an níos sine HTTP + SSE iompair, áit a osclaíonn an cliant an sruth agus na poist go dtí an pointe deiridh a fhógraíonn sruth - an cruth `roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.py` uirlisí le haghaidh `transport: sse` (\"is é an sruth an cainéal freagartha agus an pointe deiridh a fhógraíonn sé gurb é an cainéal iarratais\"). Tosaigh Baserow dá bhrí sin, ní mór go n-iompar cliant san adapter, nó fianaise go Baserow 2.3.3 Glacann sé freisin le POST simplí sruthlaithe-HTTP, nach féidir ach cás reatha a réiteach. Tá an dara iarmhairt ag fanacht taobh thiar de: `web-app-n8n` Labhraíonn ach amháin `sse`, mar sin titeann sé amach as `allowed_consumers` faoi láthair éiríonn an dromchla `streamable_http`."

