# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When a host runs Docker Swarm with NFSv4-backed shared volumes (see [svc-storage-nfs-server](../svc-storage-nfs-server/) and [svc-storage-nfs-client](../svc-storage-nfs-client/)), this role **does not capture them** - provided some host is in the [svc-bkp-nfs-2-local](../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/) inventory group. The lookup checks that group, not whether the role's last run actually succeeded, so a cluster whose export repository has never been deployed keeps that assumption unverified. The `backup_volume` lookup asks the same `swarm_nfs_backed()` predicate that drives the compose rewrite (`utils/storage/nfs.py`) and hands every export-backed volume to baudolo's `--volumes-no-backup-required`. Their single capture is then the export host's repository, which reads the same bytes from the server's own filesystem - no NFS round trip, no second copy racing the `link-dest` target."
msgstr "Nuair a ritheann óstach Docker Swarm le NFSv4-backed méideanna roinnte (féach ar [svc-storage-nfs-server](../svc-storage-nfs-server/) agus [svc-storage-nfs-client](../svc-storage-nfs-client/)), an ról seo **nach ghabháil leo** - ar choinníoll go bhfuil roinnt óstach sa [svc-bkp-nfs-2-local](../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/) grúpa fardal. Seiceálann an Lookup an grúpa sin, ní cibé acu an bhfuil an ról ar siúl go deireanach éirigh iarbhír, mar sin tá braisle a bhfuil stór onnmhairithe riamh imscaradh Coinníonn sin toimhde unverified. An bhfuil `backup_volume` lookup iarrann an gcéanna `swarm_nfs_backed()` preideacáid a thiomáineann an athscríobh chumadh (`utils/storage/nfs.py`) agus lámha gach imleabhar onnmhairithe-tacaíocht le baudolo ar `--volumes-no-backup-required`. Is é a ghabháil amháin ansin an óstach onnmhairithe stór, a léann an bytes céanna ó chóras comhad an fhreastalaí féin - gan aon turas bhabhta NFS, aon dara cóip rásaíocht an `link-dest` sprioc."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When a host runs Docker Swarm with NFSv4-backed shared volumes (see `svc-storage-nfs-server <../svc-storage-nfs-server/>`__ and `svc-storage-nfs-client <../svc-storage-nfs-client/>`__), this role **does not capture them** - provided some host is in the `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local <../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/>`__ inventory group. The lookup checks that group, not whether the role’s last run actually succeeded, so a cluster whose export repository has never been deployed keeps that assumption unverified. The ``backup_volume`` lookup asks the same ``swarm_nfs_backed()`` predicate that drives the compose rewrite (``utils/storage/nfs.py``) and hands every export-backed volume to baudolo’s ``--volumes-no-backup-required``. Their single capture is then the export host’s repository, which reads the same bytes from the server’s own filesystem - no NFS round trip, no second copy racing the ``link-dest`` target."
msgstr "Nuair a ritheann óstach Docker Swarm le NFSv4-backed méideanna roinnte (féach ar `svc-storage-nfs-server <../svc-storage-nfs-server/>`__ agus `svc-storage-nfs-client <../svc-storage-nfs-client/>`__), an ról seo **nach ghabháil leo** - ar choinníoll go bhfuil roinnt óstach sa `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local <../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/>`__ grúpa fardal. Na seiceálacha Lookup an grúpa sin, ní cibé acu an bhfuil an ról ar reáchtáil caite éirigh iarbhír, mar sin le braisle a bhfuil riamh stór onnmhairithe a imscaradh Coinníonn sin toimhde unverified. An bhfuil ``backup_volume`` lookup iarrann an gcéanna ``swarm_nfs_backed()`` preideacáid a thiomáineann an athscríobh chumadh (``utils/storage/nfs.py``) agus lámha gach onnmhairiú-tacaíocht toirte a baudolo ar ``--volumes-no-backup-required``. Is é a ghabháil amháin ansin an óstach onnmhairithe stór, a léann an bytes céanna ó chóras comhad an fhreastalaí féin - aon turas bhabhta NFS, aon dara cóip rásaíocht an ``link-dest`` sprioc."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When a local deploy fails, you MUST validate the proposed fix inside a sidecar against the same image via `make compose-inner-run` (or `make compose-exec` against the live container) BEFORE starting another deploy, whenever the failure is reproducible there. The reproducible-there set includes: a container that crashes at startup, a misconfigured env var, an image-side bug, an in-container script that fails, or any failure whose root cause was traced to runtime state of the container. The only exception is failures that genuinely depend on multi-container or post-deploy state (network neighbours, persistent volumes, post-deploy Ansible hooks) — call that out explicitly in the iteration narrative."
msgstr "Nuair a theipeann ar imscaradh áitiúil, MUST tú a bhailíochtú an shocrú atá beartaithe taobh istigh de sidecar i gcoinne an íomhá chéanna tríd `make compose-inner-run` (nó `make compose-exec` i gcoinne an coimeádán beo) BEFORE ag tosú imscaradh eile, aon uair a bhíonn an teip a laghdú ann. Áirítear leis an sraith ath-inúsáidte: coimeádán a tuairteála ag tosaithe, a var misconfigured env, íomhá-taobh, ar script in-ina bhfuil go mainneoidh, nó aon teip a bhfuil a chúis fhréamh rianú go staid runtime an choimeádáin. Is é an t-aon eisceacht teipeanna a bhraitheann i ndáiríre ar il-coimeádaí nó stát iar-imlonnaithe (líonra comharsana, méideanna leanúnacha, crúcaí Ansible iar-imlonnú) — glaoigh ar an scéal éirithe."

