msgid "You MUST describe only the current state of the subject. You MUST NOT carry historical context, migration notes, or comparisons to former implementations into documentation. Phrases such as \"this replaces X\", \"previously X did Y\", \"formerly known as X\", \"the legacy X\", or \"after the refactor\" MUST NOT appear in documentation. Readers arrive in the present and need to know how the subject works now, not how it used to work. Historical context belongs in commit messages, pull request descriptions, and changelogs, where it is anchored to a point in time and ages gracefully. Documentation that carries history rots as soon as the next refactor lands."
msgstr "MUST tú cur síos ach an staid reatha an ábhair. NÍ MÓR duit comhthéacs stairiúil, nótaí imirce, nó comparáidí a chur i bhfeidhm iar i ndoiciméadacht. Frásaí ar nós \"Gabhann sé seo X\", \"roimhe seo rinne X Y\", \"ar a dtugtar X\", \"an oidhreacht X\", nó \"tar éis an fhreagróra\" NÍ MÓR le feiceáil i ndoiciméadacht. Léitheoirí teacht i láthair agus is gá a fhios conas a oibríonn an t-ábhar anois, ní conas a úsáidtear é a bheith ag obair. Baineann comhthéacs Stairiúil i teachtaireachtaí tiomanta, cur síos ar iarraidh a tharraingt, agus changelogs, áit a bhfuil sé ar ancaire go pointe in am agus aoiseanna gracefully. Doiciméadú a iompraíonn rótair stair chomh luath agus is na tailte eile refactor."

