# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] Any role whose `meta/services.yml` declares `ldap.enabled` (literal `true` or the dynamic `\"{{ 'svc-db-openldap' in group_names }}\"` form per [test_dynamic_flags.py](../../tests/integration/roles/meta/services/test_dynamic_flags.py)) AND ships an authenticated Playwright spec MUST include at least one scenario that drives the role's **LDAP-bind login path** end-to-end. The test MUST NOT route through Keycloak: it MUST hit whatever in-app LDAP auth surface the role exposes (Joomla core LDAP plugin, Jenkins LDAP security realm, OpenCloud LDAP basic-auth driver, Mattermost AD/LDAP login, etc.)."
msgstr "[ ] Aon ról a bhfuil a `meta/services.yml` a dhearbhú `ldap.enabled` (foirm duille: líneach `true` nó an dinimiciúil `\"{{ 'svc-db-openldap' in group_names }}\"` foirm in aghaidh an [test_dynamic_flags.py](../../tests/integration/roles/meta/services/test_dynamic_flags.py)) Agus longa ar spec Playwright fíordheimhnithe I measc ar a laghad cás amháin a thiomáineann an ról ar **cosán logáil isteach LDAP-bind** deireadh-le-deireadh. NÍ MÓR an tástáil bealach tríd Keycloak: MUST sé buailte cibé in-app LDAP auth dromchla nochtann an ról (Joomla croí breiseán LDAP, Jenkins LDAP réimse slándála, OpenCloud LDAP tiománaí bunúsach-auth, Mattermost Logáil isteach AD/LDAP, etc.)."

