# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[`roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.sh`](../../roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.sh) proves the endpoint answers its declared contract, not that any particular client can route to it: it runs in a throwaway container joined to the *provider's* own network, because an `expose:`-only endpoint resolves nowhere else. Per-client routing is therefore still unproven by any test. Measured by hand on compose, Open WebUI resolves `baserow` to `192.168.206.4` and `homeassistant` to `192.168.79.2`, both distinct from the wildcard address, so the topology carries those two pairs; Swarm is unmeasured. [`isolation.sh`](../../roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/isolation.sh) does cover the adapter half, counting networks inside the sidecar for every `implementation: adapter` provider."
msgstr "[`roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.sh`](../../roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.sh) go gcruthóidh na freagraí endpoint a chonradh dearbhaithe, ní gur féidir le haon chliant ar leith bealach chuige: ritheann sé i gcoimeádán throwaway isteach ar an *soláthróir* líonra féin, mar gheall ar `expose:`-ach endpoint réitíonn aon áit eile. Dá bhrí sin, níl aon tástáil ar ródú cuí fós. Tomhaiste de láimh ar chumadh, Open WebUI an t-eolas úsáideach `baserow` go dtí `192.168.206.4` agus `homeassistant` go dtí `192.168.79.2`, idir ar leith ó sheoladh an chárta fiáin, mar sin déanann an topology an dá péirí; Tá Swarm gan thomhas. [`isolation.sh`](../../roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/isolation.sh) a chlúdaíonn an leath adapter, líonraí comhaireamh taobh istigh den sidecar do gach `implementation: adapter` soláthraí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[`roles/web-app-flowise/vars/main.yml`](../../roles/web-app-flowise/vars/main.yml) currently computes discovery data but no task registers it. [`roles/web-app-flowise/templates/env.j2`](../../roles/web-app-flowise/templates/env.j2) disables `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK` globally when MCP servers are present, and [`roles/web-app-flowise/files/playwright/test-mcp.js`](../../roles/web-app-flowise/files/playwright/test-mcp.js) proves only that an anonymous chatflow call is rejected."
msgstr "[`roles/web-app-flowise/vars/main.yml`](../../roles/web-app-flowise/vars/main.yml) faoi láthair computes sonraí fionnachtana ach aon tasc cláir sé. [`roles/web-app-flowise/templates/env.j2`](../../roles/web-app-flowise/templates/env.j2) riachtanais uisce: measartha `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK` ar fud an domhain nuair a bhíonn freastalaithe MCP i láthair, agus [`roles/web-app-flowise/files/playwright/test-mcp.js`](../../roles/web-app-flowise/files/playwright/test-mcp.js) go gcruthaíonn sé ach go ndiúltaítear glao comhrá gan ainm."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[`roles/web-app-openwebui/tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](../../roles/web-app-openwebui/tasks/utils/mcp.yml) and [`roles/web-app-openwebui/files/python/provision_mcp_grants.py`](../../roles/web-app-openwebui/files/python/provision_mcp_grants.py) can resolve or create an Open WebUI group by its path-like name and then write the generated group identifier into `access_grants`. This is the correct deployment-controlled mechanism, but application-specific Keycloak membership, last-group revocation, and restart reconciliation remain mandatory gaps."
msgstr "[`roles/web-app-openwebui/tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](../../roles/web-app-openwebui/tasks/utils/mcp.yml) agus [`roles/web-app-openwebui/files/python/provision_mcp_grants.py`](../../roles/web-app-openwebui/files/python/provision_mcp_grants.py) is féidir a réiteach nó a chruthú Open WebUI grúpa ag a ainm cosáin-mhaith agus ansin scríobh an t-aitheantóir grúpa a ghintear isteach `access_grants`. Is é seo an mheicníocht cheart rialaithe imlonnaithe, ach an t-iarratas-sonrach Keycloak ballraíocht, ceiliúradh grúpa deireanach, agus restart athmhuintearas fós bearnaí éigeantach."

