# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[pr.sh](../../../../../scripts/github/update/open/pr.sh) reads `APP_SLUG` from the environment and resolves the App's bot user via `gh api /users/<slug>[bot]`. The resolved login and numeric user ID are written into `git config user.name` and `git config user.email` in the `<id>+<slug>[bot]@users.noreply.github.com` form that GitHub accepts for verified commits. When `APP_SLUG` is unset, the script falls back to the `github-actions[bot]` identity. That branch is reached only when the script is invoked outside the workflow, for example a local smoke test where the caller has set `GH_TOKEN` to something other than an App token."
msgstr "[pr.sh](../../../../../scripts/github/update/open/pr.sh) léamha `APP_SLUG` ón gcomhshaol agus réitíonn an t-úsáideoir bot App trí `gh api /users/<slug>[bot]`. Tá an logáil isteach agus ID úsáideora uimhriúil scríofa isteach `git config user.name` agus `git config user.email` sa `<id>+<slug>[bot]@users.noreply.github.com` foirm go nglacann GitHub le haghaidh tiomantais fhíorú. Nuair a bheidh `APP_SLUG` Is unset, titeann an script ar ais go dtí an `github-actions[bot]` aitheantas. Tá an brainse sin bainte amach ach amháin nuair a bhíonn an script agairt taobh amuigh den sreabhadh oibre, mar shampla tástáil deataigh áitiúil i gcás ina bhfuil an glaoiteoir leagtha `GH_TOKEN` le rud éigin seachas comhartha."

