# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`FORCE_CANCEL_AFTER_SECONDS` turns the cancel into an escalation. A cancel request does not stop a running step: the runner asks it to end, and a step that ignores the signal keeps going until its own `timeout-minutes`, which is 350 for a deploy. The concurrency group holds the newer run on `pending` until the occupant is *terminal*, not until it is cancel-requested, so a superseded sweep can block its branch for hours after being told to stop -- measured at eight minutes and counting, with ten deploy jobs untouched. After the wait, every run that is still not `completed` gets [`force-cancel`](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-runs), which bypasses the conditions that keep it alive. The skipped cleanup steps are the price, and for a run that has already been superseded its artefacts are of no use to anyone. Leave the variable unset to cancel and walk away, which is what a closed pull request and a deleted branch want."
msgstr "`FORCE_CANCEL_AFTER_SECONDS` casadh an cealú isteach i escalation. Ní chuireann iarratas ar ceal stad céim ag rith: iarrann an dara háit é a chríochnú, agus céim a neamhaird Coinníonn an comhartha ag dul go dtí a chuid féin `timeout-minutes`, atá 350 le haghaidh imscaradh. Tá an grúpa concurrency reáchtáil níos nuaí ar `pending` go dtí go bhfuil an t-áititheoir *críochfort*, ní go dtí go bhfuil sé ar ceal-requested, mar sin is féidir sweep áit bloc a brainse ar feadh uair an chloig tar éis a insint chun stop a chur -- thomhas ag ocht nóiméad agus comhaireamh, le deich post imscaradh untouched. Tar éis an fanacht, gach reáchtáil nach bhfuil fós `completed` faigheann [`force-cancel`](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-runs), a sheachnaíonn na coinníollacha a choinneáil beo. Is iad na céimeanna cleanup skipped an praghas, agus le haghaidh a reáchtáil go bhfuil curtha in ionad cheana féin a déantáin nach bhfuil aon úsáid do dhuine ar bith. Fág an unset athróg a chur ar ceal agus siúl ar shiúl, a bhfuil cad a iarraidh tarraingt dúnta agus brainse a scriosadh ag iarraidh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Fider <https://getfider.com/>`__ is an open-source community feedback and voting platform that allows teams to collect, prioritize, and track feature requests and ideas."
msgstr "`Fider <https://getfider.com/>`__ is aiseolais pobail foinse oscailte agus ardán vótála a ligeann d'fhoirne a bhailiú, tús áite, agus rian iarratais gné agus smaointe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`FusionDirectory <https://www.fusiondirectory.org/>`__ is a web-based LDAP administration tool that manages users, groups, and other directory objects through a pluggable interface. The application stores all of its data in an external LDAP directory, which makes it the natural front-end for the project’s ``svc-db-openldap`` backend."
msgstr "`FusionDirectory <https://www.fusiondirectory.org/>`__ Is uirlis riaracháin LDAP gréasán-bhunaithe a bhainistíonn úsáideoirí, grúpaí, agus rudaí eolaire eile trí comhéadan pluggable. Déanann an t-iarratas gach ceann dá chuid sonraí in eolaire LDAP seachtrach, rud a fhágann go bhfuil sé an ceann tosaigh nádúrtha don tionscadal ``svc-db-openldap`` siar."

