msgstr "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona agus na dearbhuithe bonnlíne reáchtáil gan choinníoll."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` agus ritheann i ngach leagan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` in every matrix variant, because the shared persona helper cannot drive this role’s sign-in in any of them. Three independent reasons, each sufficient on its own:"
msgstr "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` i ngach malairt maitrís, toisc nach féidir leis an gcúntóir persona roinnte tiomáint an ról seo comhartha-in in aon cheann acu. Trí chúis neamhspleách, gach leor ar a chuid féin:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``adapter``:         immutable source contract of a repository-owned adapter. ``category_allowlist`` suits an upstream that switches whole categories and offers no per-tool filter, where a tool allowlist would be unenforceable; ``mcp_passthrough`` fronts an upstream that already speaks MCP instead of translating REST. ``upstream_path`` names that upstream where it lives on the application's own vhost, so the proxy can hide it: reaching it directly walks past the allowlist the adapter exists to enforce. A provider whose upstream is a separate sidecar declares ``upstream_network`` instead and has nothing to hide there."
msgstr "``adapter``: conradh foinse immutable adapter faoi úinéireacht stór. ``category_allowlist`` oireann an sruth atá ag athrú catagóirí ar fad agus cuireann sé aon scagaire in aghaidh an-ol, i gcás ina mbeadh deisliosta uirlis a bheith unenforceable; ``mcp_passthrough`` os comhair srutha a labhraíonn MCP cheana féin in ionad an REST a aistriú. ``upstream_path`` ainmneacha go upstream áit a bhfuil sé ina chónaí ar vhost an t-iarratas féin, mar sin is féidir leis an seachfhreastalaí cheilt é: a bhaint amach go díreach siúlóidí anuas ar an liosta an adapter ann a fhorfheidhmiú. Soláthróir a bhfuil a sruth faoi seach Dearbhaíonn sidecar ar leith ``upstream_network`` ina ionad sin agus níl aon rud a cheilt ann."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``aliases``: list of DNS aliases. Default: ``[entity_name]`` for shared_net, ``[]`` for default_net"
msgstr "``aliases``: liosta de ailiases DNS. Réamhshocrú: ``[entity_name]`` le haghaidh shared_net, ``[]`` le haghaidh default_net"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``allowed`` (default ``True``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MAY be present for a role of this type. Set ``allowed: False`` to forbid the file/entry on roles of this type so the lint layer can surface the offence with a precise reason."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible_facts`` only carries ``docker0`` once the daemon has run, and the daemon config is written before that on a fresh node - facts are gathered at play start, and nothing re-gathers them after the install. Reading the fact alone therefore yields nothing on the very run that has to emit the address, which leaves the inner containers pointed at the clearnet resolver and the DinD DNS check failing on a domain only the node dnsmasq knows."
msgstr "``ansible_facts`` ach iompraíonn ``docker0`` nuair a bheidh an daemon reáchtáil, agus tá an daemon config scríofa roimh sin ar nód úr - fíricí a bailíodh ag tús a imirt, agus rud ar bith ath-gathers iad tar éis an shuiteáil. Léitheoireacht an bhfíric ina n-aonar dá bhrí sin táirgeann rud ar bith ar an reáchtáil an- go bhfuil a astú an seoladh, a fhágann na coimeádáin istigh Léirigh ag an réiteoir glan agus an DinD DNS seiceáil ag teip ar fhearann ach an dnsmasq nód fhios."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default)"
msgstr "``ansible`` (cineál gas: in airde)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default) wraps `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD runs ~70 upstream sub-roles to deliver Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Element Call, and Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD by commit, renders an MDAD inventory from ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, and disables MDAD’s bundled Traefik / Postgres / Redis so the central Infinito services back the stack."
msgstr "``ansible`` (cineál gas: in airde) timfhilleadh `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). Ritheann MDAD ~70 fo-ráillí upstream a sheachadadh Synapse, Element, gach droichead tacaíocht, Element Call, agus Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus bioráin MDAD trí chimiú, cuireann fardal MDAD ó ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, agus disables MDAD cuachta Traefik / Iarmhairtí / Redis mar sin na seirbhísí Infinito lárnach ar ais ar an Stack."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` is the public S3 endpoint and is reachable without SSO gating."
msgstr "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` Is é an S poiblí3 endpoint agus is reachable gan SSO gating."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` is read from the play variables unless given as ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` names the block instead of ``ports``, for Discourse's launcher file, whose ``expose:`` list is what becomes ``docker run -p`` there."
msgstr "``application_id`` léamh ó na hathróga spraoi mura dtugtar mar ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` ainmneacha an bloc in ionad ``ports``, le haghaidh Discourse's comhad seoltaí, a bhfuil ``expose:`` Is maith liom é ``docker run -p`` ann."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` of the client doing the discovery."
msgstr "``application_id`` an chliaint ag déanamh an fionnachtana."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Raon feidhme Baile Cúnta an dearbhán don chuntas a mhionaithe é. Cuireann an t-imscaradh seo é don riarthóir, mar sin tagann glao mar an riarthóir whoever d'iarr an cliant. Nochtú Aonán teorainneacha fós ar an teacht. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` Grúpa RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds glaoch ag an gcuntas mbaineann an chomhartha leis. Tugann an t-imscaradh seo léargas pearsanta ar an gcuntas riarthóra, mar sin tagann glaonna le cearta an chuntais sin cibé duine a d'iarr. Reaching an freastalaí uirlis gated ar an ról ar ``mcp`` Grúpa RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: an API Tá dearbhán a eisiúint i gcoinne an chuntais riarthóir, mar sin gach glaoch a dhéanann an cuntas cearta is cuma cé a d'iarr an cliant. Reaching an freastalaí uirlis gated ar an ról ar ``mcp`` Grúpa RBAC, is deontas ar leith ó riaradh Jenkins."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: déantar an dearbhán rochtana pearsanta a mhionú i gcoinne an ``root`` cuntas agus a stóráil faoin ``administrator`` eochair, mar sin déanann gach glaoch go cuntas cearta is cuma a d'iarr an cliant. Reaching an freastalaí uirlis gated ar an ról ar ``mcp`` Grúpa RBAC, is deontas ar leith ó riaradh GitLab."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: eisítear an dearbhán seirbhíse gréasáin i gcoinne an chuntais riarthóra, mar sin déanann glao cearta an chuntais sin beag beann ar cé a d'iarr an cliant. Déantar na feidhmeanna atá ceangailte a léamh-amháin, a chuireann de cheangal ar na cearta sin a dhéanamh anseo. Reaching an freastalaí uirlis gated ar an ról ar ``mcp`` Grúpa RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. Tagann glaoch ar Baserow mar an t-úinéir endpoint beag beann ar a d'iarr an cliant, agus sroicheann ach an spás oibre amháin go bhfuil cuntas. Is é sin an dara ceangal faoi cheadú an adapter, ní ionad é."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` Grúpa RBAC, ar deontas ar leith é ó bheith i seilbh Nextcloud cuntas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject``:    identity MCP calls execute as. ``user`` and ``oidc`` additionally require a ``delegation`` block, because a rendered deployment bearer is a service account no matter what the metadata claims."
msgstr "``auth_subject``: glaonna MCP aitheantais fhorghníomhú mar. ``user`` agus ``oidc`` a cheangal chomh maith le ``delegation`` bloc, toisc go bhfuil iompróir imscaradh a rinneadh cuntas seirbhíse is cuma cad iad na héilimh meiteashonraí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_type: bearer`` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "``auth_type: bearer`` leis an chomhartha ó na sonraí fionnachtana"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth``:            authentication scheme guarding the endpoint."
msgstr "``auth``: scéim fíordheimhnithe ag cosaint an deireadhphointe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auto`` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated ``btrfs``/``zfs`` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the ``.baudolo-*`` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "``auto`` comhairle agus ní theipeann ar an aonad - tá gach diúltú logáilte isteach ar an iris mar ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, mar sin seiceáil ann má tá óstach tú ag súil a snapshot nach bhfuil. Amharc ar gach eolas ``btrfs``/ Baile``zfs`` go mainneoidh an t-aonad ina ionad sin, a bhfuil an pointe a rá é. Roimh gach snapshot cuireann an seoltóir na ``.baudolo-*`` duilleoga a maraíodh taobh istigh den fhréamh sonraí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``backend``: ``cloud`` or ``chezmoi``"
msgstr "``backend``: ``cloud`` nó ``chezmoi``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``base_dir`` (string): base directory for CA files"
msgstr "``base_dir`` (teaghrán): eolaire bonn do chomhaid CA"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays the dump in the next, so a consumer that boots in between recreates the schema and the replay dies on its own ``CREATE TABLE``. Hence the refusal while a consumer is up."
msgstr "``baudolo-restore --empty`` réamh-ghlanann an scéimre i seisiún psql amháin agus replays an dumpáil sa chéad cheann eile, mar sin le tomhaltóir go buataisí i idir recreates an scéimre agus bás an replay ar a chuid féin ``CREATE TABLE``. Dá réir sin an diúltú agus tomhaltóir suas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bench new-site`` uses the central MariaDB’s ``root`` to create the per-site DB on first deploy."
msgstr "``bench new-site`` úsáidí an lárnach MariaDB’s ``root`` a chruthú ar an DB per-site ar an gcéad imscaradh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``biber`` only ever exists inside EspoCRM through OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run in every variant."
msgstr "``biber`` ach riamh ann taobh istigh EspoCRM trí OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas reáchtáil i ngach leagan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bond`` states how tightly a role couples to the service it declares: ``>= 1`` keeps the partner on the same host, ``< 1`` lets it live on its own. The value sits on the consumer's side of the relation, so the pair is directed and the two directions of one pair need not agree."
msgstr "``bond`` a deir cé chomh docht le lánúineacha ról don tseirbhís a dhearbhaíonn sé: ``>= 1`` coimeádann an comhpháirtí ar an óstach céanna, ``< 1`` ligeann sé beo ar a chuid féin. Suíonn an luach ar thaobh an tomhaltóra den ghaol, mar sin tá an péire dírithe agus ní gá an dá threo de péire amháin aontú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **parent** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` apex)"
msgstr "``c.wiki.example.com`` → → **tuismitheoir an linbh** ``wiki.example.com`` (móide móide ``example.com`` a chur ar fáil)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ca_cert_host`` is where sys-ca-selfsigned provisions the root CA on the host. The container-side bind-mount targets live in the ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) and reach the standalone runtime scripts as env vars and CLI arguments."
msgstr "``ca_cert_host`` i gcás ina sys-ca-selfsigned forálacha an fhréamh CA ar an óstach. Tá na spriocanna ceangail taobh an choimeádáin ina gcónaí sa ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars Plandaí faoi dhíon (``inject_cert_container`` / Baile ``inject_wrapper_container``) agus teacht ar na scripteanna runtime standalone mar vars env agus argóintí CLI."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``central_mariadb_root_password``: The root password for the MariaDB server."
msgstr "``central_mariadb_root_password``: An focal faire fréimhe don MariaDB freastalaí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``cert_host`` (string): host path to Root CA certificate"
msgstr "``cert_host`` (teaghrán): cosán óstach ar dheimhniú Root CA"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``classification``:  what this role is in the MCP audit. Required."
msgstr "``classification``: cad é an ról seo san iniúchóireacht MCP. Riachtanach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``comments`` is the parsed per-key comment map from default.env (see :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dynamic keys carry their comments via each handler's ``COMMENT`` constant. ``custom.env`` overrides run last (see :func:`apply_custom_env`)."
msgstr "``comments`` Is é an léarscáil tráchta parsed in aghaidh an-eochair ó default.env (féach ar :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Déanann eochracha Dinimiciúla a gcuid tuairimí trí gach láimhseálaí ``COMMENT`` tairiseach. ``custom.env`` overrides reáchtáil deireanach (féach ar :func:`apply_custom_env`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose build`` re-bakes the static output whenever the cloned content changes, so deploys are content-driven without any runtime build step."
msgstr "``compose build`` ath-bakes an t-aschur statach aon uair a athraíonn an t-ábhar cloned, mar sin tá imscaradh ábhar-tiomáinte gan aon chéim a thógáil runtime."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` (deprecated)"
msgstr "``compose`` (bláthanna cumhra: cumhráin)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` is the in-repo Docker Compose stack. It remains installable but receives no new features."
msgstr "``compose`` Is é an in-repo Docker Compose Stack. Tá sé fós insuite ach faigheann aon gnéithe nua."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` or ``swarm`` to pin every image to that track, ``rotate`` to split the images across both."
msgstr "``compose`` nó ``swarm`` chun bioráin gach íomhá go dtí an rian, ``rotate`` a scoilt na híomhánna ar fud an dá."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``composer install`` failed."
msgstr "``composer install`` theip."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``config.access_grants: []``, administrator-only rather than public"
msgstr "``config.access_grants: []``, riarthóir-amháin seachas poiblí"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer_not_allowed`` is a decision and simply narrows the result. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` and ``tools_unenforceable`` mean the provider did authorize this consumer and the connection still cannot be rendered, so they abort the run instead of disappearing quietly: a client that silently ends up with fewer tools than the deployment declared is indistinguishable from one that works."
msgstr "``consumer_not_allowed`` Is cinneadh agus go gcúngaíonn sé an toradh. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` agus ``tools_unenforceable`` chiallaíonn go raibh an soláthraí údar an tomhaltóir seo agus an nasc nach féidir a dhéanamh fós, mar sin abort siad an reáchtáil in ionad a imíonn siad go ciúin: cliant a chríochnaíonn go ciúin suas le huirlisí níos lú ná an t-imscaradh dearbhaithe indistinguishably ó cheann go n-oibríonn."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer``: optional override"
msgstr "``consumer``: override roghnach"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``container system prune -a -f`` to remove unused Docker resources."
msgstr "``container system prune -a -f`` acmhainní Docker neamhúsáidte a bhaint."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``core`` for every language but the source language, ``docs`` for the languages LibreTranslate supports."
msgstr "``core`` do gach teanga ach an teanga foinse, ``docs`` do na teangacha LibreTranslate tacaíochtaí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential_missing`` is the one authorized rejection that does not abort, because a provider deploying later in the same play has not written its secret yet. That exemption ends at the reconciliation stage, which runs once every provider has: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` treats it as fatal there."
msgstr "``credential_missing`` Is é an diúltú amháin údaraithe nach bhfuil abort, toisc nach bhfuil soláthraí imscaradh ina dhiaidh sin sa spraoi céanna scríofa a rún go fóill. Tagann deireadh leis an díolúine sin ag céim an athmhuintearais, a ritheann uair amháin gach soláthraí: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` déileálann sé marfach ann."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential``:      which principal the provider authenticates as, and where its secret is read from. Replaces the administrator token path."
msgstr "``credential``: cén príomhoide a fhíoraíonn an soláthraí mar, agus i gcás ina bhfuil a rún a léamh ó. Replaces an cosán chomhartha riarthóir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, sent as ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"
msgstr "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, sheoladh mar ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``custom.env`` is the operator's untracked override file; its values win over static defaults AND handler-computed values."
msgstr "``custom.env`` Is é an t-oibreoir comhad override untracked; a luachanna bua thar mainneachtainí statach agus luachanna handler-computed."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_name``: The name of the initial database to create."
msgstr "``database_name``: Ainm an bhunachar sonraí tosaigh a chruthú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_password``: The password for the database user."
msgstr "``database_password``: An focal faire don úsáideoir bunachar sonraí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_username``: The username for the database user."
msgstr "``database_username``: An ainm úsáideora don úsáideoir bunachar sonraí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``days`` (int): certificate validity"
msgstr "``days`` (taiseachas aeir: fliuch): bailíocht deimhnithe"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``default-address-pools`` is where docker takes that address from, so the declaration answers before the daemon exists and answers identically afterwards. That also keeps daemon.json byte-identical across passes, which the fact-derived value could not: it appeared only from the second run on and restarted the container runtime under a live stack."
msgstr "``default-address-pools`` nuair a thógann docker an seoladh sin ó, mar sin na freagraí dearbhú roimh an daemon ann agus freagraí céanna ina dhiaidh sin. Go gcoinníonn freisin daemon.json byte-identical ar fud Gabhann, a bhfuil an luach fíor-derived Ní fhéadfadh: sé le feiceáil ach amháin ón dara reáchtáil ar agus atosú an runtime coimeádán faoi chairn beo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``delegation``:      recorded proof, at one exact upstream version, that per-user token acquisition, refresh, audience binding and revocation exist."
msgstr "``delegation``: cruthúnas taifeadta, ag leagan amháin sruth cruinn, go bhfuil fáil chomhartha in aghaidh an úsáideora, athnuachan, lucht féachana ceangailteach agus cúlghairm ann."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``deployment`` restricts to roles present anywhere in ``groups``, which is what a container-network consumer can actually reach; ``all`` returns every declaring role, deployed or not."
msgstr "``deployment`` srian le róil i láthair in áit ar bith i ``groups``, a bhfuil cad is féidir le tomhaltóir coimeádán-líonra a bhaint amach iarbhír; ``all`` tuairisceáin gach ról dhearbhú, imscaradh nó nach bhfuil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dest``: destination path (required for ``cloud``)"
msgstr "``dest``: cosán scríbe (ag teastáil le haghaidh ``cloud``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``direction``:       whether the role exposes MCP, consumes it, or both."
msgstr "``direction``: an nochtann an ról MCP, ídíonn sé, nó iad araon."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``discourse``: the WP->Discourse post round-trip scenario. Disabling Discourse skips it; front-page reachability and CSP baselines stay active."
msgstr "``discourse``: an WP-Discourse post cás babhta-turas. Díchumasú Discourse skips sé; tosaigh-leathanach reachability agus CSP baselines fanacht gníomhach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``docker_name``    the explicit ``name:`` field (alias for ``name``"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``domains``: canonical and alias domains"
msgstr "``domains``: fearainn Canonical agus ailias"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_apply`` (default: ``true``): run ``doli pull`` after adding mappings"
msgstr "``dotlinker_apply`` (cineál gas: in airde ``true``): reáchtáil ``doli pull`` tar éis mapaí a chur leis"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (cineál gas: in airde ``doli``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_config_path`` (default: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_config_path`` (cineál gas: in airde ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_package_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_package_name`` (cineál gas: in airde ``doli``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_replace`` (default: ``true``): pass ``--replace`` to ``doli add``"
msgstr "``dotlinker_replace`` (cineál gas: in airde ``true``): pas ``--replace`` go dtí ``doli add``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_user`` (required): user to run ``doli`` as"
msgstr "``dotlinker_user`` (ag teastáil): úsáideoir a reáchtáil ``doli`` mar atá"

msgid "``dsk-gnt-cursor`` and ``dsk-gnt-pi`` carry no entry in that map. Cursor is a full editor rather than an extension, and neither vendor publishes an extension on Open VSX, so there is nothing to install into Code for them. Both agents are used from their own binary."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``enabled`` (bool)"
msgstr "``enabled`` (taiseachas aeir: fliuch)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``endpoint``:        connection metadata for clients (server roles only)."
msgstr "``endpoint``: meiteashonraí nasc do chliaint (róil freastalaí amháin)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``enforced`` onions every capable row, ``disabled`` none, ``exclusive`` drops the rows that cannot take one, ``auto`` rotates."
msgstr "``enforced`` oinniúin gach sraith ann, ``disabled`` aon cheann, ``exclusive`` titeann na sraitheanna nach féidir a ghlacadh ar cheann, ``auto`` rothlú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entries_only=true`` returns those strings as a list instead of the rendered block, for a container that is not described by a compose file at all: ``web-app-discourse`` is built by discourse_docker's ``launcher``, whose only argument surface is ``docker_args:`` in its ``app.yml``, so it needs ``--add-host=<entry>`` lines."
msgstr "``entries_only=true`` tuairisceáin na teaghráin mar liosta in ionad an bloc a rinneadh, le haghaidh coimeádán nach bhfuil cur síos ag comhad a chumadh ar chor ar bith: ``web-app-discourse`` tógtha ag discourse_docker's ``launcher``, a bhfuil ach dromchla argóint ``docker_args:`` ina ``app.yml``, mar sin riachtanais sé ``--add-host=<entry>`` línte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entries`` is a list of dotted-path facts about the file's content. Each entry carries the same ``mandatory`` and ``allowed`` semantics described above and adds a ``marker`` flag (default ``False``): ``marker: True`` declares the path as the type marker for the surrounding type entry. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` walks every ``marker: True`` entry; each marker that resolves to a non-empty value in the role's file adds the surrounding type to the role's type set. ``application_id`` for ``application`` and ``system_service_id`` for ``system-service`` are the canonical markers."
msgstr "``entries`` Is liosta de na fíricí dotted-path mar gheall ar an comhad ábhar. Déanann gach iontráil mar an gcéanna ``mandatory`` agus ``allowed`` shéimeasúir cur síos thuas agus cuireann sé ``marker`` bratach bratach (cineál gas: in airde ``False``): ``marker: True`` Dearbhaíonn an cosán mar an marcóir cineál don iontráil cineál máguaird. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` siúlóidí gach ``marker: True`` iontráil; Cuireann gach marcóir a réitíonn le luach neamh-empty i gcomhad an ról an cineál mórthimpeall ar an ról atá leagtha cineál. ``application_id`` le haghaidh ``application`` agus ``system_service_id`` le haghaidh ``system-service`` Is iad na marcóirí Canonical."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` declares a ``run-name:`` that interpolates the dispatch inputs. Once a run has started, that title is the only record of them: the REST API answers ``inputs: null`` for a workflow_dispatch run. Anything that wants to know what a run was dispatched with therefore parses the title — and parsing it against a hand-copied format would drift the moment the workflow changes, silently and without a failing test."
msgstr "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` Dearbhaíonn a ``run-name:`` a idirshuíomh na hionchuir seolta. Nuair a bheidh tús le reáchtáil, is é an teideal sin an t-aon taifead orthu: an REST API Freagraí scríofa ``inputs: null`` ar feadh workflow_dispatch reáchtáil. Rud ar bith atá ag iarraidh a fháil amach cad a bhí seolta a reáchtáil le dá bhrí sin parses an teideal - agus parsáil sé i gcoinne formáid lámh-copied bheadh sruth an nóiméad na hathruithe sreabhadh oibre, go ciúin agus gan tástáil teip."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ephemeral`` publishes the container port on a host port docker picks, for a service addressed only through the compose network."
msgstr "``ephemeral`` Foilsíonn an calafort coimeádán ar phioc docker port óstach, le haghaidh seirbhíse a dtugtar aghaidh air ach tríd an líonra a chumadh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposed`` is an explicit per-service opt-in (default false) that makes the service reachable over the node onion: its port gets a dedicated ``HiddenServicePort``. Because ``applications`` is the variant-merged config (base ``meta/services.yml`` deep-merged with the round's ``meta/variants.yml`` override), a service is forwarded only in the variant/config where it sets ``exposed: true`` — which is exactly what lets the two DB variants be tested over Tor (v0 exposed -> reachable, v1 not -> refused)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposure``:        who may reach the endpoint."
msgstr "``exposure``: a d'fhéadfadh teacht ar an gcríochphointe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``extra_hosts=``, whatever the call site needs on top: a peer's overlay VIP, or a partner service reachable only on the host."
msgstr "``extra_hosts=``, is cuma cad is gá ar an suíomh glaonna ar bharr: a piaraí forleagan VIP, nó seirbhís comhpháirtíochta reachable ach amháin ar an óstach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``false`` while MCP servers are discovered"
msgstr "``false`` cé go bhfuil freastalaithe MCP amach"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``family`` is the ``os_family`` ansible reports for the host. Callers that have facts (the action plugin) pass it, so distributions outside the CI matrix - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - still resolve through their family. Callers without facts (lints, the availability test) omit it and the family is derived from :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, which only covers the default matrix."
msgstr "``family`` Is é an ``os_family`` tuarascálacha inghlactha don óstach. Glaoiteoirí go bhfuil fíricí (an breiseán gníomh) pas a fháil é, mar sin dáiltí lasmuigh den maitrís CI - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - réiteach fós trína dteaghlach. Glaoiteoirí gan fíricí (lints, an tástáil infhaighteachta) omit é agus an teaghlach a dhíorthaítear ó :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, a chlúdaíonn ach an maitrís réamhshocraithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` serves the filer web UI behind an admin-only oauth2-proxy."
msgstr "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` freastal ar an Chomhéadain gréasáin filer taobh thiar de admin-amháin oauth2-proxy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (run on the deploy host) completes the first-run wizard (seeds the break-glass admin), installs both plugins via Jellyfin’s own ``/Packages`` installer, writes the plugin configs, and restarts."
msgstr "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (reáchtáil ar an óstach imscaradh) Críochnaíonn an chéad-reáchtáil draoi (síolta an admin bhriseadh-gloine), installs an dá plugins via Jellyfins féin ``/Packages`` suiteálaí, scríobhann an breiseán configs, agus atosú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/playwright.config.js``: shared Playwright configuration"
msgstr "``files/playwright.config.js``: cumraíocht Playwright roinnte"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/python/policy.py`` validates it at startup. A contract missing a limit, carrying an empty allowlist, naming a wildcard path or lacking a pinned schema hash is refused before the process serves anything."
msgstr "``files/python/policy.py`` bailíochtaíonn sé ag tosaithe. Tá conradh ar iarraidh teorainn, ag iompar an allowlist folamh, ainmniú cosán cárta fiáin nó nach bhfuil schema pinned diúltaíodh roimh an bpróiseas feidhmíonn rud ar bith."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``flags``: list of flags to AND. Default: ``[enabled, shared]``"
msgstr "``flags``: liosta bratacha chuig agus. Réamhshocrú: ``[enabled, shared]``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``flavor`` picks the probe shape (see utils/docker/healthcheck/); each flavor brings its own interval, timeout, retries and start_period, and any of those may be overridden next to it. Without a ``flavor`` the entry must carry an explicit ``test`` argv. ``port_key`` selects another entry below ``ports.internal`` for services that expose their probe on a second port."
msgstr "``flavor`` Pioc an cruth probe (féach ar utils/docker/healthcheck/ Baile); Tugann gach blas a eatramh féin, timeout, retries agus start_period, agus d'fhéadfadh aon cheann de na a shárú in aice leis. Gan ``flavor`` ní mór an iontráil a dhéanamh go sainráite ``test`` Argv. ``port_key`` roghnaigh iontráil eile thíos ``ports.internal`` do sheirbhísí a nochtadh a probe ar an dara calafort."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``force_regen`` (bool): if true, remove and regenerate key/cert"
msgstr "``force_regen`` (taiseachas aeir: fliuch): más fíor, eochair / teastais a bhaint agus a athghiniúint"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``forward[A]`` is the list of provider roles that ``A`` directly depends on (services it embeds). ``reverse[B]`` is the list of roles that directly depend on ``B`` (consumers that embed ``B``)."
msgstr "``forward[A]`` Is é an liosta de na róil soláthraí go ``A`` ag brath go díreach ar (seirbhísí leabú sé). ``reverse[B]`` Is é liosta na róil atá ag brath go díreach ar ``B`` (tomhaltóirí a leabú ``B``)."

msgid "``galaxy_info.author`` is where a role records who implemented it, so that is where the names are read. A role may credit more than one person, comma separated."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``getent`` honours nsswitch and cannot address a server, so on its own it cannot say which of the resolvers in resolv.conf refused. Where the distro ships a query tool, ask every nameserver directly; where it does not, the per-name verdicts still stand on their own."
msgstr "``getent`` onóracha nswitch agus ní féidir aghaidh a thabhairt ar fhreastalaí, mar sin ar a chuid féin ní féidir é a rá cé acu de na réiteoirí i resolv.conf dhiúltaigh sé. Nuair a long an distro uirlis cheist, a iarraidh ar gach nameserver go díreach; i gcás nach bhfuil sé, na fíorasc per-ainm seasamh fós ar a gcuid féin."

msgid "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` is the single source of truth for host paths. The env layer (utils/env/handlers, exported by scripts/meta/env/load.sh) derives the ``INFINITO_*`` env keys from it; a set env wins so callers can override. When a tool runs outside that layer, e.g. a bare ``subprocess`` that does not inherit the env build, the value is read straight from the group_vars SPOT, so there is still no hardcoded literal default."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``host_alias=true``, which pins ``host.docker.internal`` at whatever reaches the host in the effective mode. A container that must talk to a service the host publishes -- msmtp relaying through the swarm ingress on :587, for instance -- needs the alias, and it must not hardcode ``host-gateway`` because that breaks under swarm for the reason below."
msgstr "``host_alias=true``, a bioráin ``host.docker.internal`` ag cibé sroicheann an t-óstach sa mhodh éifeachtach. A coimeádán a chaithfidh labhairt le seirbhís a fhoilsíonn an óstach - msmtp Relaying tríd an ingress swarm ar:587, mar shampla - ní mór na ailias, agus ní mór é a cruachód ``host-gateway`` toisc go sosanna faoi mhionn ar an gcúis thíos."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, own network only"
msgstr "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, líonra féin amháin"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` on the shared MCP overlay"
msgstr "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` ar an overlay MCP roinnte"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``implementation``:  how the surface is provided, ordered by precedence."
msgstr "``implementation``: conas a sholáthraítear an dromchla, d'ordaigh roimh ré."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``in_container`` exists because one template serves two consumers. The host's /root/.msmtprc is read by the host and loopback is right for it; the copy mounted at /etc/msmtprc is read inside a container, where 127.0.0.1 is that container's own loopback and nothing listens on it. Such a service must also emit ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` so the alias resolves."
msgstr "``in_container`` ann mar feidhmíonn teimpléad amháin dhá thomhaltóirí. Is é an óstach / root / .msmtprc léamh ag an ósta agus lúb ais ceart chun é; an chóip suite ag / srl / mtprc léamh taobh istigh coimeádán, áit a bhfuil 127.0.0.1 Is é sin coimeádán ar ais féin agus aon rud éisteann ar sé. Ní mór seirbhís den sórt sin a astú freisin ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` mar sin réitíonn an ailias."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``indent=0`` collapses everything to the left edge - useful when the lookup is rendered into top-level YAML (no service wrapper)."
msgstr "``indent=0`` collapses gach rud ar an imeall chlé - úsáideach nuair a bhíonn an Lookup a rinneadh i YAML leibhéal barr (aon fhillteán seirbhíse)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ingress`` (default) emits the short ``\"host:published:container\"`` string; ``host`` emits the long block with ``mode: host``, which is what an edge role needs in swarm so the client address survives the hop."
msgstr "``ingress`` (cineál gas: in airde) astaíonn an gearr ``\"host:published:container\"`` teaghrán; ``host`` astaíonn an bloc fada le ``mode: host``, a bhfuil an méid is gá ról imeall i swarm mar sin maireann an seoladh cliant an hop."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``internal`` (default) reads ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` reuses the published port, for services that cannot remap (STUN/TURN, media relays)."
msgstr "``internal`` (cineál gas: in airde) léamha ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` reuses an calafort foilsithe, le haghaidh seirbhísí nach féidir a athléamh (STUN / TURN, Relays meáin)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``internal``, container network only"
msgstr "``internal``, líonra coimeádán amháin"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``kas`` (Kubernetes agent server, workspaces), ``pages``, ``registry`` and ``mailroom`` are not deployed; ``gitlab.yml`` disables them."
msgstr "``kas`` (freastalaí gníomhaire Kubernetes, spásanna oibre), ``pages``, ``registry`` agus ``mailroom`` gan iad a imscaradh; ``gitlab.yml`` disables iad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key_bits`` (int): RSA key size"
msgstr "``key_bits`` (taiseachas aeir: fliuch): RSA méid eochair"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key_host`` (string): host path to Root CA private key"
msgstr "``key_host`` (teaghrán): cosán óstach do Root CA eochair phríobháideach"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key`` names the pinned key and defaults to ``version``; an entity with several pins declares a list of such blocks. The types are ``git_tags`` (repository), ``registry_tags`` (image), ``npm`` (package), ``http_regex`` (url, pattern) and ``script`` (path, run with the current version and printing the latest one)."
msgstr "``key`` ainmneacha an eochair pinned agus mainneachtainí a ``version``; eintiteas le roinnt bioráin Dearbhaíonn liosta de na bloic sin. Tá na cineálacha ``git_tags`` (stór lárnach), ``registry_tags`` (íomhá íomhá), ``npm`` (pacáiste pacáiste), ``http_regex`` (url, patrún) agus ``script`` (cosán, reáchtáil leis an leagan reatha agus a phriontáil an ceann is déanaí)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key``: services.<key>.* lookup base. Default: provides or entity_name"
msgstr "``key``: seirbhísí.<key>.* bonn lookup. Réamhshocrú: Soláthraíonn nó entity_name"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``kind``: ``services_flags`` (default) | ``database`` | ``mcp_client`` | ``web_facing`` | ``onion_sso``. ``mcp_client`` admits a role only when its ``mcp.direction`` is ``client`` or ``both`` AND it declares ``services.<own-entity>.mcp_consumer: true`` without the provider refusing it through ``mcp_consumer: false`` on that same entry, so a provider's network carries the clients it admitted rather than every client in the deployment. Being a client is not an admission: without the second condition one admission anywhere reaches every provider that opens its overlay."
msgstr "``kind``: ``services_flags`` (cineál gas: in airde) Amharc ar gach eolas ``database`` Amharc ar gach eolas ``mcp_client`` Amharc ar gach eolas ``web_facing`` Amharc ar gach eolas ``onion_sso``. ``mcp_client`` ligeann ról ach amháin nuair a ``mcp.direction`` Is maith liom ``client`` nó ``both`` Agus dearbhaíonn sé ``services.<own-entity>.mcp_consumer: true`` gan an soláthraí diúltú é tríd ``mcp_consumer: false`` ar an iontráil chéanna, mar sin déanann líonra soláthraí na cliaint admhaigh sé seachas gach cliant san imscaradh. A bheith ina cliant nach ligean isteach: gan an dara coinníoll sroicheann amháin isteach in áit ar bith gach soláthraí a osclaíonn a forleagan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``last`` seeds the OCI pagination cursor: only tags sorting lexically after it are returned. Repos like GitLab CNG carry tens of thousands of commit-sha tags before the ``v*`` release tags, so an unseeded scan exhausts ``max_pages`` without ever reaching them."
msgstr "``last`` síolta an cúrsóir tosaithe OCI: ach clibeanna sórtáil le chéile tar éis é a chur ar ais. Is maith liom GitLab CNG a iompar na mílte clibeanna tiomantas-cruth os comhair na ``v*`` tags scaoileadh, mar sin sceite scanadh unseed ``max_pages`` gan riamh iad a bhaint amach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``latest`` is the last commit of the default branch. It is built at start and rebuilt whenever a fetch finds a new commit; the previous build stays online until the new one replaces it."
msgstr "``latest`` Is é an tiomantas deireanach den bhrainse réamhshocraithe. Tá sé tógtha ag tús agus atógáil aon uair a fhaigheann beir tiomantas nua; an tógáil roimhe tréimhsí ar líne go dtí go ionad an ceann nua é."

msgid "``laya``, ``torch`` or ``onnx``; the role refuses anything else"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ldap``: the three RBAC scenarios additionally depend on LDAP group sync; disabling LDAP skips them alongside OIDC."
msgstr "``ldap``: na trí cásanna RBAC ag brath chomh maith ar sync grúpa LDAP; disabling LDAP skips iad taobh OIDC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ldapauth`` is the only path that materialises a ``friendica.user`` row, so its enablement derives directly from the ``ldap`` service flag. The oauth2-proxy ``sso`` gate in front of the vhost is a front-door auth gate, not an addon bridge, and stays in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. The LDAP login path is covered by the existing LDAP Playwright spec (requirement 018), so no addon-specific spec is added."
msgstr "``ldapauth`` Is é an cosán amháin go materialises a ``friendica.user`` as a chéile, mar sin tagann a cumasú go díreach ó na ``ldap`` bratach seirbhíse. Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil2-proxy ``sso`` geata os comhair an vhost Is geata tosaigh-door auth, ní droichead addon, agus tréimhsí i ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`. Tá an cosán logála isteach LDAP clúdaithe ag an spec LDAP Playwright atá ann cheana (ceanglas 018), mar sin tá aon spec addon-sonrach leis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``libaacs`` (AACS decryption library)"
msgstr "``libaacs`` (AACS leabharlann decryption)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``libbluray`` (Blu-ray playback support library)"
msgstr "``libbluray`` (leabharlann tacaíochta athsheinm Blu-ray)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lifecycle``  — maturity marker filtered by ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."
msgstr "``lifecycle`` - marcóir aibíochta arna scagadh ag ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``limits``:          the request, response, timeout, concurrency, pagination and stream ceilings the surface enforces."
msgstr "``limits``: an t-iarratas, an fhreagairt, an t-am, an concurrency, an tógáil agus na huasteorainneacha sruth an dromchla i bhfeidhm."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale-gen`` only re-runs when the template changes"
msgstr "``locale-gen`` ach ath-ritheann nuair a athraíonn an teimpléad"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale.conf``: sets ``LANG`` and ``LANGUAGE`` environment variables"
msgstr "``locale.conf``: Leagann ``LANG`` agus ``LANGUAGE`` internet marketing"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale.gen``: uncomment or specify the locales you need"
msgstr "``locale.gen``: uncomment nó na locales de dhíth ort a shonrú"

msgid "``lookup('guide_role', application_id)`` picks the first invokable app the round deployed beside ``application_id``. Invokability comes from :func:`utils.roles.validation.invokable.list_invokable_app_ids`, so no caller re-derives it from role-name prefixes."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('users', user_key).authorized_keys`` (list; may be empty)"
msgstr "``lookup('users', user_key).authorized_keys`` (liosta; d'fhéadfadh a bheith folamh)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('users', user_key).username`` (defaults to ``user_key``)"
msgstr "``lookup('users', user_key).username`` (riachtanais uisce: measartha ``user_key``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``lookup('volume', application_id)`` — return the WHOLE canonical registry as a dict keyed by semantic name. Useful for tasks that loop over every declared volume (e.g. NFS subdir pre-creation). Returns ``{}`` for roles with no meta/volumes.yml."
msgstr "``lookup('volume', application_id)`` — an clárlann Canonical WHOLE a thabhairt ar ais mar dict arna eochaircheapadh de réir ainm shéimeantach. Úsáideacha le haghaidh tascanna a lúb thar gach toirt dearbhaithe (e.g. NFS subdir réamh-creidiú). Tuairisceáin ``{}`` do róil gan aon meta/volumes.yml."

