# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``networks.internet.dns`` arrives through ``-e @inventories/...`` and is read straight out of ``variables``, which hands back whatever the file contains. While that was a literal address nobody noticed; an expression there reached the daemon as its own source text and docker refused the config with ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."
msgstr "``networks.internet.dns`` Tagann trí ``-e @inventories/...`` agus tá sé a léamh díreach amach as ``variables``, a lámha ar ais cibé an bhfuil an comhad. Cé go raibh seoladh litriúil aon duine faoi deara; léiriú ann shroich an daemon mar a téacs foinse féin agus docker dhiúltaigh an config leis ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
