msgstr "``new_text_or_None`` Is maith liom ``None`` nuair a athrú rud ar bith."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``nfs``            NFS opt-in (bool or dict), ``None`` if absent"
msgstr "``nfs`` NFS rogha isteach (bool nó deacht), ``None`` má bhíonn sé as láthair"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``noqa`` and ``nocheck`` are accepted as synonyms (case-insensitive) by this parser. By repo convention every project rule from ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` MUST use ``nocheck:`` because ``# noqa: <code>`` is also parsed by ruff as a flake8 directive and triggers ``invalid-noqa-code`` warnings on every project-specific rule key. ``noqa:`` is reserved for real flake8 / ruff codes (``E402``, ``F401``, …). The ``direct-yaml`` lint enforces the convention by hard-rejecting the ``noqa:`` form."
msgstr "``noqa`` agus ``nocheck`` Glactar leis mar comhchiallaigh (cás-íogair) ag an parsálaí. De réir repo coinbhinsiún riail gach tionscadal ó ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` Úsáid MUST ``nocheck:`` mar gheall ar ``# noqa: <code>`` Tá parsed freisin ag ruff mar gcáithníní8 Treoir agus truicir ``invalid-noqa-code`` rabhaidh ar gach eochair riail-sonrach tionscadail. ``noqa:`` forchoimeádta le haghaidh calóg fíor8 / Ruff cóid (``E402``, ``F401``, ...). An ``direct-yaml`` lint i bhfeidhm ar an gcoinbhinsiún ag crua-rejecting an ``noqa:`` foirm."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``offset`` moves that start deliberately: it is how an operator reaches the tail without waiting for anything. It defaults to 0, so every run that does not ask for it deploys the same head and can be compared against the last one. This used to be derived from the sweep number instead, which bought tail coverage at the price of the head -- chunk 0 began wherever the arithmetic pointed, the rows that matter most ran only every few sweeps, and no two runs were comparable."
msgstr "``offset`` bogann a thosaíonn d'aon turas: is é an chaoi a sroicheann oibreoir an t-eireaball gan fanacht le rud ar bith. Réamhshocrú 0, mar sin gach reáchtáil nach bhfuil a iarraidh ar sé imscaradh an ceann céanna agus is féidir a chur i gcomparáid i gcoinne an ceann deireanach. Úsáidtear é seo le díorthú ón uimhir scuabtha ina ionad sin, a cheannaigh clúdach eireaball ar phraghas an chinn - smután 0 thosaigh cibé áit a dúirt an arithmetic, na sraitheanna go ábhar ar siúl ach gach scuab cúpla, agus ní raibh aon dá ritheann inchomparáide."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``oidc-authenticator`` and ``ldap-authenticator`` are mutually exclusive auth backends (only one may be enabled; see ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` carries only the installer coordinate."
msgstr "``oidc-authenticator`` agus ``ldap-authenticator`` Tá cúlchríocha auth frithpháirteach eisiach (d'fhéadfadh ach duine amháin a chumasú; féach ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` Déanann ach an comhordú suiteálaí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``oidc``: baseline admin OIDC round-trip plus the three RBAC scenarios (subscriber/editor/administrator)."
msgstr "``oidc``: bonnlíne admin OIDC babhta-turas móide na trí cásanna RBAC (subscriber/editor/administrator)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``openssl_conf_host`` (string): host path for generated openssl.cnf"
msgstr "``openssl_conf_host`` (teaghrán): cosán óstach do ghintear openssl.cnf"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``out`` itself lives under the dump dir (both derive from INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), so the walk must skip its own output subtree or copytree recurses into the growing destination until ENAMETOOLONG."
msgstr "``out`` féin ina chónaí faoi dir dumpála (an dá dhíorthaíonn ó INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), mar sin ní mór don siúlóid a fo-chrann aschur féin nó cóipchrann recurses isteach sa cheann scríbe atá ag fás go dtí ENAMETOOLONG."

