msgstr "``path`` an oidhreacht ``path:`` réimse, ``''`` má bhíonn sé as láthair"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``phpunit/phpunit`` declares ``_PHPUNIT_EXTENSIONS`` as platform requirements and Composer refuses to resolve the vendor tree without them, so they are part of the toolchain rather than of the suite consuming it. A distro ships them as packages separate from the interpreter, which is why a present ``php`` binary does not imply they are there."
msgstr "``phpunit/phpunit`` a dhearbhú ``_PHPUNIT_EXTENSIONS`` mar riachtanais ardán agus Diúltaíonn Composer a réiteach ar an crann díoltóir gan iad, mar sin tá siad mar chuid den toolchain seachas an tsraith Tógann sé. A distro longa iad mar pacáistí ar leith ón ateangaire, agus sin an fáth a láthair ``php`` Ní dénártha le tuiscint go bhfuil siad ann."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``playwright.spec.js`` — orchestrator: TLS baseline, project creation, image asset upload, and the ``guest``/``biber``/``administrator`` personas. The ``biber`` / ``administrator`` personas are declared blocked via ``PERSONA_*_BLOCKED`` (mirroring ``web-app-taiga``): Penpot’s in-app “OpenID” entry and SPA user-menu logout aren’t driveable by the generic persona helper, so both users’ real auth is exercised by the dedicated login companions above."
msgstr "``playwright.spec.js`` — orchestrator: TLS baseline, chruthú tionscadail, uaslódáil sócmhainní íomhá, agus ``guest``/ Baile``biber``/ Baile``administrator`` duine. An bhfuil ``biber`` / Baile ``administrator`` personas a dhearbhaítear bac trí ``PERSONA_*_BLOCKED`` (scáthán ``web-app-taiga``): Penpot ar in-app “Oscailt” iontráil agus SPA úsáideora-menu logout nach bhfuil in thiomáint ag an duine cineálach cúntóir persona, mar sin tá an dá úsáideoirí’ fíor auth a fheidhmiú ag na companions logáil isteach tiomnaithe thuas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``playwright.version`` in ``meta/services.yml`` is the single source of truth for the default Playwright version; the central ``templates/package.json.j2`` pins it via the ``image_version`` filter."
msgstr "``playwright.version`` i ``meta/services.yml`` Is é an fhoinse amháin na fírinne don leagan Playwright réamhshocraithe; an lárnach ``templates/package.json.j2`` bioráin sé tríd an ``image_version`` scagaire."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``plg_system_keycloak`` is built imperatively inside the Joomla container and speaks OIDC against Keycloak. Its enablement derives directly from the ``sso`` service flag, and its OIDC runtime contract (issuer, client id/secret, redirect/end-session URLs, fallback toggle, and RBAC group paths) lives under the addon’s ``config:`` block, which ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders into the ``JOOMLA_OIDC_*`` plugin environment."
msgstr "``plg_system_keycloak`` tógtha go mór taobh istigh den Joomla coimeádán agus labhraíonn OIDC i gcoinne Keycloak. Tagann a cumasú go díreach ó na ``sso`` bratach seirbhíse, agus a chonradh runtime OIDC (eisitheoir, id cliant/rúnaí, URLanna atreorú/deireadh-seisiún, scoránaigh ar ais, agus bealaí grúpa RBAC) saol faoi na addon ar ``config:`` bloc, a ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders into the ``JOOMLA_OIDC_*`` timpeallacht breiseán."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``poll: 0`` makes a task fire and forget, so its own ``changed_when`` and ``failed_when`` never see an outcome. The outcome only exists once the job is collected with ``async_status``, and collecting it is where the verdict has to be made -- for a whole batch at once, so one run reports every broken job rather than the first."
msgstr "``poll: 0`` a dhéanann tine tasc agus dearmad, mar sin a chuid féin ``changed_when`` agus ``failed_when`` riamh a fheiceáil toradh. Tá an toradh ann ach amháin nuair a bhailítear an post leis ``async_status``, agus é a bhailiú i gcás ina bhfuil an fíorasc a dhéanamh - le haghaidh bhaisc ar fad ag an am céanna, mar sin tuarascálacha reáchtáil amháin gach post briste seachas an chéad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ports.onion`` is a category-keyed map of booleans alongside ``internal`` / ``local`` / ``public``: it names which of a service's already-declared ports should answer on the node onion, and nothing else. The port number comes from ``ports.local`` when that category is declared there and from ``ports.public`` otherwise, which is the precedence ``container_ports`` publishes by, so the forward always targets the port the service is actually reachable on."
msgstr "``ports.onion`` Is léarscáil chatagóir-eochairithe de booleans taobh ``internal`` / Baile ``local`` / Baile ``public``: ainmneacha sé ar chóir go mbeadh calafoirt seirbhíse cheana féin a dhearbhú freagra a thabhairt ar an nód oinniún, agus aon rud eile. Tagann uimhir an chalafoirt ó ``ports.local`` nuair a dhearbhaítear an chatagóir sin ann agus ó ``ports.public`` ar shlí eile, a bhfuil an tosaíocht ``container_ports`` Foilsíonn, mar sin an aghaidh spriocanna i gcónaí ar an gcalafort go bhfuil an tseirbhís reachable iarbhír ar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``priority`` IS the retrigger: it names what failed. ``offset`` is recomputed rather than carried, but from the carried value up: the source run got a stretch behind its own offset green before its budget ran out, so the regular line resumes behind that stretch (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) instead of repeating it, and never falls back behind where that run started. Everything else is carried verbatim, including ``whitelist``, so a retrigger of a scoped run stays inside that scope instead of quietly widening to the whole repository."
msgstr "``priority`` IS an retrigger: ainmneacha sé cad theip. ``offset`` Tá recomputed seachas a rinneadh, ach ón luach a rinneadh suas: an fhoinse reáchtáil fuair stráice taobh thiar de a fhritháireamh glas féin sular rith a bhuiséad amach, mar sin atosaíonn an líne rialta taobh thiar den stráice (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) in ionad athrá é, agus ní thiteann ar ais taobh thiar de nuair a thosaigh an rith. Tá gach rud eile a dhéantar verbatim, lena n-áirítear ``whitelist``, mar sin fanann retrigger de reáchtáil scoped taobh istigh raon feidhme sin in ionad leathnú go ciúin leis an stór ar fad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``provider`` / ``provider_key``: for ``onion_sso``, the app whose"
msgstr "``provider`` / Baile ``provider_key``: le haghaidh ``onion_sso``, an app a"

