# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``relay`` and ``media`` are UDP. ``stun_turn`` and its TLS variant do speak TCP, but the allocation they hand out is a UDP relay address the onion client can never receive on, so forwarding the signalling port buys nothing."
msgstr "``relay`` agus ``media`` Tá UDP. ``stun_turn`` agus a TLS leagan a dhéanamh labhairt TCP, ach is é an leithdháileadh láimh siad amach seoladh sealaíochta UDP ní féidir leis an cliant oinniún a fháil ar, mar sin ar aghaidh an port comharthaíochta cheannach rud ar bith."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``repo`` carries the repository the names come from, defined inline on the entry that needs it: a full definition (``name``/``description``/ ``baseurl``/``gpgkey``) rendered as a yum repo, ``bootstrap_package`` for a repo shipped as a package such as ``epel-release``, ``enable_existing`` to switch on a repo the distro already ships, ``pacman_section`` to uncomment a section of ``pacman.conf`` such as ``multilib``, ``copr``/``ppa`` for a community repository, or ``managed_externally`` when the role sets it up itself."
msgstr "``repo`` Déanann an stór na hainmneacha a thagann ó, inlíne sainithe ar an iontráil a riachtanais sé: sainmhíniú iomlán (``name``/ Baile``description``/ Baile ``baseurl``/ Baile``gpgkey``) a rinneadh mar repo yum, ``bootstrap_package`` le haghaidh repo shipped mar phacáiste ar nós ``epel-release``, ``enable_existing`` a athrú ar repo an distro longa cheana féin, ``pacman_section`` alt de chuid a dhíchóimeáil ``pacman.conf`` den sórt sin ``multilib``, ``copr``/ Baile``ppa`` do stór pobail, nó ``managed_externally`` nuair a leagann an ról suas é féin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``required`` (always installed)"
msgstr "``required`` (suiteáilte i gcónaí)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``required`` (always installed, vendored)"
msgstr "``required`` (suiteáilte i gcónaí, díoltóirithe)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``requirepass`` for the ``default`` (admin) user, sourced from the ``REDIS_PASSWORD`` credential."
msgstr "``requirepass`` do na ``default`` (admin sa Spáinn) úsáideoir, a fháil ón ``REDIS_PASSWORD`` dintiúir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``retries`` counts CONSECUTIVE failures, and a request that leaves the container is load balanced across the service VIP. With N replicas and one of them alive, a round robin never produces more than N-1 failures in a row, so a streak based check is arithmetically blind to losing all but one backend. Chaining ``samples`` requests into a single probe makes one probe cover the whole pool instead."
msgstr "``retries`` chomhaireamh teipeanna CONSECUTIVE, agus iarratas a fhágann go bhfuil an coimeádán ualach cothrom ar fud an tseirbhís VIP. Le N macasamhla agus ceann acu beo, Riamh robin bhabhta Táirgeann níos mó ná N-1 teipeanna i ndiaidh a chéile, mar sin tá seiceáil bunaithe ar streak arithmetically dall a chailliúint go léir ach ceann ar ais. Slabhraí ``samples`` iarratais isteach probe amháin a dhéanann probe amháin a chlúdach an linn snámha ar fad ina ionad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``role`` may be a role name (relative to ``roles/``) or an absolute path to a role directory. Pass ``role_name`` explicitly when ``role`` is an arbitrary path whose basename is not the canonical role name."
msgstr "``role`` a bheith ina ainm ról (i gcoibhneas le ``roles/``) nó cosán iomlán chuig eolaire ról. Pas pas ``role_name`` go sainráite nuair ``role`` Is cosán treallach nach bhfuil a basename an t-ainm ról Canonical."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/<app>/meta/server.yml`` declares ``status_codes`` keyed like ``domains.canonical``; it is the single source of truth for every prober."
msgstr "``roles/<app>/meta/server.yml`` a dhearbhú ``status_codes`` eochair mhaith ``domains.canonical``; is é an fhoinse amháin na fírinne do gach prober."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` Follow `Contributing ``playwright.env.j2`` <../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md>`__ and `Contributing ``playwright.spec.js`` <../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md>`__ while creating them."
msgstr "``roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` Lean muid ar aghaidh `Contributing ``playwright.env.j2`` <../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md>`__ agus `Contributing ``playwright.spec.js`` <../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md>`__ agus iad a chruthú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/sys-lint/meta/services.yml`` is the SPOT for both the repository and the version of every GitHub-release lint tool. Each entry carries the ``repository`` / ``ref`` pair that ``utils.update.repository`` already scans, so the existing ``update-repository-refs`` CI job bumps the pins to the latest semver tag and opens a PR -- the same machinery that keeps ``roles/pkgmgr`` current."
msgstr "``roles/sys-lint/meta/services.yml`` Is é an nóta le haghaidh an stór agus an leagan de gach uirlis lint GitHub-scaoileadh. Déanann gach iontráil ``repository`` / Baile ``ref`` péire go ``utils.update.repository`` scanadh cheana féin, mar sin an reatha ``update-repository-refs`` CI post bumps an bioráin leis an chlib semver is déanaí agus osclaíonn PR - an innealra céanna a choimeádann ``roles/pkgmgr`` reatha."

