msgid "``run_after`` is deliberately NOT read: it is a deploy-ordering hint, not a runtime dependency. The wider cosmos (federation peers, external bridged networks) cannot be derived from metadata and is left for the author to add."
msgstr "``run_after`` NACH d'aon ghnó a léamh: tá sé leid imscaradh-ordú, ní spleáchas runtime. An cosmos níos leithne (piaraí cónaidhme, líonraí droichead seachtrach) Ní féidir a dhíorthaítear ó meiteashonraí agus tá sé fágtha don údar a chur leis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` validates the generated packaging metadata with each ecosystem's native parser. This installer provisions those parsers wherever the platform's package manager can: on Debian (apt) the lint container gets ``dpkg-parsechangelog`` (``dpkg-dev``), ``rpmspec`` (``rpm``) and ``rpmlint``; on Arch (pacman) a dev host gets ``namcap``."
msgstr "``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` bailíochtaíonn na meiteashonraí pacáistithe a ghintear le parsálaí dúchais gach éiceachórais. Forálacha an suiteálaí na parsers cibé áit ar féidir leis an ardán bainisteoir pacáiste: ar Debian (apt apt) faigheann an coimeádán lint ``dpkg-parsechangelog`` (``dpkg-dev``), ``rpmspec`` (``rpm``) agus ``rpmlint``; ar Arch (pacman) faigheann óstach dev ``namcap``."

