# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``tools_unenforceable`` is that same rule applied to the tool policy rather than the connection. A client filters by tool name, so a provider that resolves no callable name gives it nothing to pin and the rendered filter would be empty. That happens two ways, and neither is a working pairing: a surface composed at runtime keeps its contract in ``tools.categories``, which no per-tool filter can express, and a surface that withholds every tool it serves as mutating has nothing left to offer. Advertising either as a configured server would leave an agent wired to a provider it can never call."
msgstr "``tools_unenforceable`` Is é sin an riail chéanna i bhfeidhm ar an mbeartas uirlis seachas an ceangal. Scagairí cliant de réir ainm uirlis, mar sin soláthraí a réitíonn aon ainm callable Tugann sé aon rud a bioráin agus go mbeadh an scagaire a rinneadh a bheith folamh. Tarlaíonn sé sin dhá bhealach, agus ní pairing oibre é: coimeádann dromchla atá comhdhéanta ag runtime a chonradh i ``tools.categories``, nach féidir aon scagaire in aghaidh an-ol a chur in iúl, agus dromchla a choimeádann gach uirlis feidhmíonn sé mar mutating bhfuil aon rud fágtha a thairiscint. Bheadh Fógraíocht ceachtar mar fhreastalaí cumraithe fhágáil gníomhaire wired le soláthraí ní féidir é a ghlaoch."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``tools``:           ``allowlist`` is what a reader may reach and ``writer_allowlist`` what a writer may reach; the deployment renders one contract per role, each with its own bearer, because the gateway tells callers apart by credential and by nothing else. ``allowlist`` is policy, what the platform lets a consumer reach, and is only a constraint where a gateway enforces it. ``upstream_serves`` is the observation: every tool the upstream offers at the deployed version. State it only where it DIFFERS from the allowlist; absence means the two are identical, which is the normal case for a provider that serves exactly what is allowed. The difference between them measures unenforced exposure, and a provider whose difference is non-empty needs a gateway in front. Plus schema hash and mutation policy."
msgstr "``tools``: ``allowlist`` Is é an méid a d'fhéadfadh léitheoir a bhaint amach agus ``writer_allowlist`` cad is féidir le scríbhneoir a bhaint amach; déanann an t-imscaradh conradh amháin in aghaidh an róil, gach ceann acu lena iompróir féin, toisc go insíonn an geata glaoiteoirí ar leith de réir dintiúir agus ag aon rud eile. ``allowlist`` Is beartas, cad a ligeann an t-ardán teacht ar thomhaltóirí, agus tá sé ach srian i gcás ina forfheidhmíonn geata é. ``upstream_serves`` Is é an breathnóireacht: gach uirlis na tairiscintí réamhtheachtach ag an leagan imscaradh. Stát sé ach amháin nuair a DIFFERS sé as an liosta; ciallaíonn easpa an dá bhfuil comhionann, a bhfuil an cás gnáth le haghaidh soláthraí a fheidhmíonn go díreach cad atá ceadaithe. Beartaíonn an difríocht idir iad nochtadh gan choinne, agus soláthraí a bhfuil difríocht nach bhfuil gá le geata os comhair. Plus hash scéimre agus beartas sócháin."

