# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`allow`: pre-authorized. Additionally, `sandbox.autoAllowBashIfSandboxed: true` pre-authorizes any Bash command that runs sandboxed and matches no `deny`/`ask` rule. Agents without an equivalent OS-level sandbox MUST treat unmatched Bash as `ask`."
msgstr "`allow`: réamh-údaraithe. Ina theannta sin, `sandbox.autoAllowBashIfSandboxed: true` réamh-údar aon ordú Bash a ritheann sandboxed agus cluichí aon `deny`/ Baile`ask` riail. Gníomhairí gan bosca gainimh comhionann OS-leibhéal MUST chóireáil Bash unmatched mar `ask`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`allowed_consumers` MUST contain explicit client `application_id` values. Discovery MUST require the provider to allow the consumer and the consumer to support the provider's transport and authentication scheme. Authorized but unrenderable entries MUST fail reconciliation with a machine-readable reason; they MUST NOT disappear silently."
msgstr "`allowed_consumers` MUST bhfuil cliant sainráite `application_id` luachanna. Éilíonn Discovery MUST ar an soláthraí cead a thabhairt don tomhaltóir agus don tomhaltóir tacú le scéim iompair agus fíordheimhnithe an tsoláthraí. Iontrálacha údaraithe ach unrenderable MUST theipeann ar athmhuintearas le cúis meaisín-inléite; MUST siad NACH imíonn siad go ciúin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`allowed_consumers` creates no network edge. A client reaches a provider only when the provider declares a `kind: mcp_client` consumer in its `meta/networks.yml`, or when the client happens to declare that provider as a service for an unrelated reason. Four of twenty providers declare the opening (gitlab, homeassistant, moodle, nextcloud); the other sixteen admit consumers they cannot serve, four of them enabled (baserow, gitea, jenkins, mattermost). Measured: deploying Hermes fails at its own probe with `All connection attempts failed` against `http://prometheusmcp:8080/mcp`, because `hermes` joins `[gitlab, hermes, homeassistant, litellm, moodle]` while `prometheusmcp` joins `[prometheus]` alone, and the adapter sidecar's isolation check asserts exactly that single attachment. Open WebUI reaches Baserow only because it also declares `services.baserow`. Per-pair networks therefore have to replace `kind: mcp_client`, which opens a provider to every client rather than to the admitted one."
msgstr "`allowed_consumers` Cruthaíonn aon imeall líonra. Ní shroicheann cliant soláthraí ach amháin nuair a dhearbhaíonn an soláthraí `kind: mcp_client` tomhaltóirí ina `meta/networks.yml`, nó nuair a tharlaíonn an cliant a dhearbhú go soláthraí mar sheirbhís ar chúis neamhghaolmhar. Ceithre de fiche soláthraithe a dhearbhú an oscailt (gitlab, homeassistant, moodle, nextcloud); an ceann eile déag a ligean isteach tomhaltóirí nach féidir leo freastal ar, ceathrar acu ar chumas (ghrian nochtadh: ghrian go hiomlán). Tomhaiste: go mainneoidh imscaradh Hermes ar a probe féin le `All connection attempts failed` i gcoinne `http://prometheusmcp:8080/mcp`, mar gheall ar `hermes` Uirlisí ilchuspóireacha `[gitlab, hermes, homeassistant, litellm, moodle]` le linn `prometheusmcp` Uirlisí ilchuspóireacha `[prometheus]` ina n-aonar, agus Dearbhaíonn seiceáil leithlisiú an taobhcharr adapter go díreach iatán amháin. Sroicheann WebUI Oscailte Baserow ach amháin toisc go ndearbhaíonn sé freisin `services.baserow`. Tá líonraí Per-pairt dá bhrí sin a chur in ionad `kind: mcp_client`, a osclaíonn soláthraí do gach cliant seachas an ceann admhaigh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`ansible.builtin.package` ships as a documentation-only stub; its logic lives in Ansible's action plugin. The action plugin here executes modules directly, so it must swap this marker for the host's `ansible_facts.pkg_mgr`."
msgstr "`ansible.builtin.package` longa mar stub doiciméadú-amháin; saol a loighic i breiseán gníomh Ansible ar. An breiseán gníomh a fhorghníomhú anseo modúil go díreach, mar sin ní mór é a babhtáil an marcóir don óstach `ansible_facts.pkg_mgr`."

