# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`apt/<distro>.list`: apt sources, one file per `INFINITO_DISTRO`. The matching file is mounted at `/etc/apt/sources.list.d/package-cache.list`. `apt/debian.list` routes apt through `apt-debian`, `apt/ubuntu.list` through `apt-ubuntu`; the pacman/dnf distros get an empty file, because `apt-get update` fails as a whole on a single unreachable source and must not carry a foreign distro's entry."
msgstr "`apt/<distro>.list`: foinsí apt, comhad amháin in aghaidh an `INFINITO_DISTRO`. Tá an comhad meaitseáil suite ag `/etc/apt/sources.list.d/package-cache.list`. `apt/debian.list` bealaí apt trí `apt-debian`, `apt/ubuntu.list` trí mheán `apt-ubuntu`; an pacman / dnf distros fháil comhad folamh, mar gheall ar `apt-get update` go mainneoidh ina n-iomláine ar fhoinse unreachable amháin agus ní mór a sheoladh iontráil distro coigríche."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`apt` (mirrors)"
msgstr "`apt` (scátháin)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`architecture` is an axis of the matrix row, assigned per row by [axes.py](../../../utils/github/variant/axes.py) next to `mode`, `tor`, `distro` and `filesystem`."
msgstr "`architecture` Is ais ar an tsraith maitrís, sannta in aghaidh a chéile de réir [axes.py](../../../utils/github/variant/axes.py) in aice leis `mode`, `tor`, `distro` agus `filesystem`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`ask`: requires per-invocation operator confirmation in the current conversation. A prior confirmation from another conversation MUST NOT be reused."
msgstr "`ask`: Éilíonn deimhniú oibreoir in aghaidh an sonraisc sa chomhrá reatha. A deimhniú roimh ré ó comhrá eile NACH MÓR a athúsáid."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth: none` MUST fail lint unless the endpoint is bound to localhost or an internal-only network and the role README documents why authentication is impossible upstream."
msgstr "`auth: none` MUST theipeann lint mura bhfuil an pointe deiridh faoi cheangal a localhost nó líonra inmheánach-amháin agus na doiciméid README ról cén fáth go bhfuil fíordheimhniú dodhéanta upstream."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth: none` requires `exposure: internal`."
msgstr "`auth: none` Éilíonn `exposure: internal`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: Raon feidhme Baile Cúnta an dearbhán don chuntas a mhionaithe é. Cuireann an t-imscaradh seo é don riarthóir, mar sin tagann glao mar an riarthóir whoever d'iarr an cliant. Nochtú Aonán teorainneacha fós ar an teacht. Tá dul chuig an bhfreastalaí uirlis gated ar an ról ar `mcp` Grúpa RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account's rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: Mattermost bounds glaoch ag an gcuntas mbaineann an chomhartha leis. Tugann an t-imscaradh seo le fios gur féidir rochtain phearsanta a fháil ar chuntas an riarthóra, mar sin tagann glaonna le cearta an chuntais sin cibé duine a d'iarr. Reaching an freastalaí uirlis gated ar an ról ar `mcp` Grúpa RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account's rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: an API chomhartha a eisiúint i gcoinne an chuntais riarthóir, mar sin déanann gach glaoch sin cuntas cearta aon ábhar a d'iarr an cliant. Reaching an freastalaí uirlis gated ar an ról ar `mcp` Grúpa RBAC, is deontas ar leith ó riaradh Jenkins."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: the personal access token is minted against the `root` account and stored under the `administrator` key, so every call carries that account's rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: déantar an dearbhán rochtana pearsanta a mhionú i gcoinne an `root` cuntas agus a stóráil faoin `administrator` eochair, mar sin déanann gach glaoch go cuntas cearta is cuma a d'iarr an cliant. Reaching an freastalaí uirlis gated ar an ról ar `mcp` Grúpa RBAC, is deontas ar leith ó riaradh GitLab."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account's rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: eisítear an dearbhán seirbhíse gréasáin i gcoinne an chuntais riarthóra, mar sin déanann glao cearta an chuntais sin beag beann ar cé a d'iarr an cliant. Déantar na feidhmeanna atá ceangailte a léamh-amháin, a chuireann de cheangal ar na cearta sin a dhéanamh anseo. Reaching an freastalaí uirlis gated ar an ról ar `mcp` Grúpa RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: service_account | administrator` requires an explicit `tools.mutating_tools_enabled: false`."
msgstr "`auth_subject: service_account | administrator` cineál gas: in airde `tools.mutating_tools_enabled: false`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: service_account`. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter's allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "`auth_subject: service_account`. Tagann glaoch ar Baserow mar an t-úinéir endpoint beag beann ar a d'iarr an cliant, agus sroicheann ach an spás oibre amháin go bhfuil cuntas. Is é sin an dara ceangal faoi cheadú an adapter, ní ionad é."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: service_account`: [`tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml) creates the account `NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME` with `occ user:add` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under `mcp.credential.owner`. Every call carries that account's rights, not the administrator's, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "`auth_subject: service_account`: [`tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml) Cruthaíonn an cuntas `NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME` le `occ user:add` má tá sé ar iarraidh, mints an focal faire app i gcoinne an cuntas sin, agus siopaí sé faoi `mcp.credential.owner`. Déanann gach glao cearta an chuntais sin, ní an riarthóir, is cuma a d'iarr an cliant. Reaching an freastalaí uirlis gated ar an ról ar `mcp` Grúpa RBAC, ar deontas ar leith é ó bheith i seilbh Nextcloud cuntas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: user` and `auth: oidc` claim that an MCP call executes with the requesting end user's permissions. A `delegation:` block records the audit that backs the claim; without it, [`test_mcp_schema.py`](../../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_schema.py) rejects the role."
msgstr "`auth_subject: user` agus `auth: oidc` éileamh go bhforghníomhaíonn glao MCP leis na ceadanna úsáideora deiridh iarrtha. Amharc ar gach eolas `delegation:` bloc taifid an t-iniúchadh a chúlann an t-éileamh; gan é, [`test_mcp_schema.py`](../../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_schema.py) Diúltaíonn an ról."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: user` or `auth: oidc` requires a `delegation` block; see [delegation.md](mcp/delegation.md)."
msgstr "`auth_subject: user` nó `auth: oidc` Éilíonn `delegation` bloc; féach [delegation.md](mcp/delegation.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject` MUST be `user` where upstream supports per-user authorization. `service_account` and `administrator` MUST keep mutating tools disabled by default."
msgstr "`auth_subject` MUST a bheith `user` i gcás tacaíochtaí sruth in aghaidh an-úsáideoir údarú. `service_account` agus `administrator` MUST a choinneáil uirlisí mutating faoi mhíchumas de réir réamhshocraithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_type: bearer` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "`auth_type: bearer` leis an chomhartha ó na sonraí fionnachtana"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth` reads `environment` and `tls`."
msgstr "`auth` léamha `environment` agus `tls`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auto` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as `baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>`, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated `btrfs`/`zfs` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the `.baudolo-*` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "`auto` comhairle agus ní theipeann ar an aonad - tá gach diúltú logáilte isteach ar an iris mar `baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>`, mar sin seiceáil ann má tá óstach tú ag súil a snapshot nach bhfuil. Amharc ar gach eolas `btrfs`/ Baile`zfs` go mainneoidh an t-aonad ina ionad sin, a bhfuil an pointe a rá é. Roimh gach snapshot cuireann an seoltóir na `.baudolo-*` duilleoga a maraíodh taobh istigh den fhréamh sonraí."

