# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`enabled`/`shared` are omitted. [`utils/cache/applications.py`](../../../../../utils/cache/applications.py) derives both from the admitted clients as `\"{{ '<client>' in group_names or … }}\"`, and `false` when no client is admitted, so a surface is reachable exactly while a peer that uses it is deployed. Write either key to override that: a value in `meta/variants.yml` wins over one in `meta/mcp.yml`, and both win over the derivation. Do not hand-write a `group_names` gate: it is a second source for the derived fact and drifts when an edge changes."
msgstr "`enabled`/ Baile`shared` a fhágáil ar lár. [`utils/cache/applications.py`](../../../../../utils/cache/applications.py) Tagann an dá ó na cliaint admhaithe mar `\"{{ '<client>' in group_names or … }}\"`, agus `false` nuair nach ligtear isteach aon chliant, mar sin tá dromchla insroichte go díreach agus piaraí a úsáideann é a imscaradh. Scríobh ceachtar eochair a shárú go: luach i `meta/variants.yml` Bhuaigh thar ceann i `meta/mcp.yml`, agus an dá bhuachan thar an derivation. Ná lámh-scríobh `group_names` geata: is dara foinse é don fhíoras agus do na sruthanna a dhíorthaítear nuair a athraíonn imeall."

