# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh api` switches implicitly from GET to POST as soon as a body-flag is present; no explicit `-X`/`--method` is required. Without these ask rules the broad `Bash(*)` allow would let body-carrying `gh api` POSTs through silently. Short forms (`-f`, `-F`), long forms (`--field`, `--raw-field`), and file input (`--input`) are all listed so no spelling slips past. A future gh-CLI body-flag would need to be added here explicitly."
msgstr "`gh api` lasca intuigthe ó GET go POST chomh luath agus is comhlacht brada i láthair; gan aon follasach `-X`/ Baile`--method` ag teastáil. Gan na rialacha a iarraidh ar an leathan `Bash(*)` bheadh cead a ligean comhlacht-iompar `gh api` POSTs trí ciúin. Foirmeacha gearra (`-f`, `-F`), foirmeacha fada (`--field`, `--raw-field`), agus ionchur comhad (`--input`) Tá gach liostaithe mar sin aon duillíní litriú anuas. Bheadh gá le comhlacht G-CLI sa todhchaí a chur leis anseo go sainráite."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh config set editor /tmp/evil.sh` plants a binary that runs the next time any `gh` subcommand opens an editor (e.g. `gh issue create` without `--body`), a deferred-execution backdoor that survives the current session. Persistent CLI config belongs to a deliberate operator decision."
msgstr "`gh config set editor /tmp/evil.sh` plandaí dénártha a ritheann an chéad uair eile aon `gh` subcommand osclaíonn eagarthóir (e.g. `gh issue create` gan `--body`), backdoor iarchurtha-fhorghníomhaithe a mhaireann an seisiún reatha. Persistent CLI config bhaineann le cinneadh oibreoir d'aon ghnó."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh workflow run` does NOT print the new run id. Resolve it by repeating the same list query until the returned databaseId is non-empty AND differs from `<prev-run-id>`. That value is `<run-id>`. Each repeat MUST be a separate tool invocation; no shell loop. Do NOT accept a result equal to `<prev-run-id>`; that would attach the watcher to the stale run and return its old exit status immediately."
msgstr "`gh workflow run` NACH phriontáil ar an id reáchtáil nua. Athsholáthar é trí athdhéanamh an cheist liosta céanna go dtí go bhfuil an bunachar sonraí ar ais neamh-empty agus éagsúil ó `<prev-run-id>`. Is é sin luach `<run-id>`. Gach MUST arís a bheith ina invocation uirlis ar leith; aon lúb bhlaosc. Ná glacadh le toradh comhionann le `<prev-run-id>`; a bheadh ag gabháil leis an watcher leis an reáchtáil stale agus a stádas scoir d'aois ar ais láithreach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh` CLI's cache directory (HTTP response cache + extension metadata). Granted because every `gh` invocation writes cache entries at startup; denying it would require every `gh` call to be wrapped with an `XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/...` env prefix, which adds a shell shape that falls out of sandbox auto-allow and forces per-subcommand allow entries. Auth tokens are **not** stored here (they live in `~/.config/gh/`, which stays read-only). Persistence trade-off is identical to `~/.cache/pip` / `~/.cache/pre-commit`: cache poisoning, if it occurred, would survive reboots, but API auth is server-side so the blast radius is bounded to wrong-output-to-operator."
msgstr "`gh` eolaire taisce CLI (taisce freagra HTTP + meiteashonraí síneadh). Deonaithe mar gheall ar gach `gh` invocation scríobhann iontrálacha taisce ag startup; dhiúltú bheadh sé ag teastáil gach `gh` glaoch a bheith fillte le `XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/...` env réimír, a chuireann cruth bhlaosc a thagann amach as bosca gainimh uathoibríoch agus fórsaí in aghaidh an-subcommand cheadú iontrálacha. Tá comharthaí auth **bláthanna cumhra: aon cumhráin** stóráil anseo (cónaí orthu i `~/.config/gh/`, a fhanann léamh-amháin). Tá trádáil-uaire comhionann le `~/.cache/pip` / Baile `~/.cache/pre-commit`: nimhiú taisce, má tharla sé, Bheadh maireachtáil reboots, ach API auth freastalaí-taobh mar sin tá an ga soinneáin faoi cheangal a mícheart-aschur-go-oibritheoir."

