# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`svc-ai-litellm` already serves an OpenAI-compatible gateway, and `web-app-nextcloud` already binds its `integration_openai` app to that gateway through `tasks/addons/integration_openai.yml`, a `credentials.litellm_api_key` entry and a dedicated Playwright spec. That pattern is implemented once and is not required, described or verified for any other role."
msgstr "`svc-ai-litellm` freastal ar gheata OpenAI-comhoiriúnach cheana féin, agus `web-app-nextcloud` Ceanglaíonn cheana féin a `integration_openai` app chuig an tairseach sin tríd `tasks/addons/integration_openai.yml`, a `credentials.litellm_api_key` iontráil agus spec Playwright tiomanta. Tá an patrún i bhfeidhm uair amháin agus nach bhfuil ag teastáil, cur síos nó a fhíorú le haghaidh aon ról eile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`svc-ai-litellm` pulls `svc-ai-ollama` and `svc-ai-lmstudio` with it, so a consumer that enables the gateway adds roughly 6 GB to its round. Variant 0 is the fallback every higher round lands on, so a heavy shared dependency pinned there appears in every round: with the gateway on variant 0 of `web-app-matrix`, `web-app-mattermost` and `web-app-zammad`, the `web-app-nextcloud` rounds that pin those partners exceed the 64 GB budget guarded by `tests/integration/roles/meta/variants/test_resource_budget.py`."
msgstr "`svc-ai-litellm` Seirbhís do Chustaiméirí `svc-ai-ollama` agus `svc-ai-lmstudio` leis, mar sin a tomhaltóir a chuireann ar chumas an geata Cuireann garbh 6 GB go dtí a bhabhta. Amharc ar gach eolas 0 Is é an fallback gach tailte bhabhta níos airde ar, mar sin spleáchas roinnte trom pinned ann le feiceáil i ngach babhta: leis an geata ar malairt 0 de `web-app-matrix`, `web-app-mattermost` agus `web-app-zammad`, an `web-app-nextcloud` babhtaí a bioráin na comhpháirtithe níos mó ná an 64 buiséad GB cosanta ag `tests/integration/roles/meta/variants/test_resource_budget.py`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`svc-ai-mcp-adapter` carries no MCP surface of its own. It is the adapter runtime a provider role instantiates, so its disposition is `enabler` and it MUST NOT appear in discovery as a provider or a consumer."
msgstr "`svc-ai-mcp-adapter` Déanann aon dromchla MCP dá chuid féin. Is é an runtime adapter ról soláthraí láithreach, mar sin tá a dhiúscairt `enabler` agus NÍ MÓR é le feiceáil i bhfionnachtain mar sholáthraí nó tomhaltóir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`svc-ai-mcp-adapter` validates the platform's OIDC access token, so an adapter-backed provider is the one surface that can declare `auth: oidc` with `auth_subject: user`. Only Open WebUI can consume it:"
msgstr "`svc-ai-mcp-adapter` bailíochtaíonn an t-ardán ar chomhartha rochtana OIDC, mar sin tá soláthraí adapter-tacaíocht an dromchla amháin is féidir a dhearbhú `auth: oidc` le `auth_subject: user`. Ach Open WebUI is féidir é a ithe:"

msgid "`svc-ai-robot` stays out of the platform list. It runs the same agent in embodied mode, which means it drops the isolating runtime on purpose and hands the container the host devices it is meant to drive. A broker platform is defined by the opposite: `runsc`, no host device, no host mount. Serving an embodied agent per user would either break that invariant or ship a robot that cannot reach its hardware."
