# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test.sh` runs two different passes, selected by `ASYNC_ENABLED`. The snapshot probe runs first in both, because it depends on nothing the backup produces."
msgstr "`test.sh` Ritheann dhá Gabhann éagsúla, roghnaithe ag `ASYNC_ENABLED`. Ritheann an probe snapshot ar dtús sa dá, toisc go mbraitheann sé ar aon rud a tháirgeann an cúltaca."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_dotted_path_keys_exist.py` validates that every Jinja dotted path (`FOO.BAR.BAZ`) whose head is in `group_vars/all/` or the consuming role's own `vars`/`defaults` resolves to an existing key in that dict tree, catching typos / renamed / removed sub-keys. Per-line suppression: `# nocheck: dotted-path`."
msgstr "`test_dotted_path_keys_exist.py` bailíochtaíonn go bhfuil gach cosán Jinja dotted (`FOO.BAR.BAZ`) a bhfuil ceann i `group_vars/all/` nó an ról Tógann féin `vars`/ Baile`defaults` réitíonn sé le eochair atá ann cheana féin sa chrann deach sin, ag teacht ar fho-ráillí / athainmnithe / bainte. Sochtadh Per-líne: `# nocheck: dotted-path`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_e2e_playwright_only_roles` (default: `lookup('deployment').running`, every role the round deploys, dependencies included)"
msgstr "`test_e2e_playwright_only_roles` (cineál gas: in airde `lookup('deployment').running`, gach ról an imscartha babhta, spleáchais san áireamh)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_e2e_playwright_skip_roles` (default: `[]`)"
msgstr "`test_e2e_playwright_skip_roles` (cineál gas: in airde `[]`)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_network_create_via_util.py` requires that role tasks creating Docker networks route through the shared utility, never inline `community.docker.docker_network` calls."
msgstr "`test_network_create_via_util.py` Éilíonn go tascanna ról a chruthú gréasáin Docker bealach tríd an fóntais roinnte, riamh inlíne `community.docker.docker_network` glaonna."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_no_inline_multiline_sql.py` caps inline multi-line SQL in Ansible tasks at three lines. Larger statements MUST live in a dedicated `.sql` file under the role's `files/` directory and be loaded explicitly so linters, formatters, and database tooling can operate on them."
msgstr "`test_no_inline_multiline_sql.py` caipíní inlíne SQL il-líne i tascanna Ansible ag trí líne. Ráitis níos mó MUST beo i tiomnaithe `.sql` comhad faoin ról `files/` eolaire agus a luchtú go sainráite mar sin linters, formáideoirí, agus is féidir tooling bunachar sonraí a oibriú orthu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_no_jinja_default_on_spot_path.py` forbids `| default(...)` on Jinja expressions whose path resolves via `group_vars/all/*.yml`. Those keys are loaded unconditionally, so the default is dead code at best and silent SPOT decoupling at worst. Per-line suppression: `# nocheck: spot-default`."
msgstr "`test_no_jinja_default_on_spot_path.py` forbids `| default(...)` ar abairtí Jinja a réitíonn a cosán trí `group_vars/all/*.yml`. Tá na heochracha luchtaithe gan choinníoll, mar sin tá an réamhshocraithe cód marbh ag decoupling fearr agus adh ag is measa. Sochtadh Per-líne: `# nocheck: spot-default`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_no_legacy_get_url_module_usage.py` forbids the unqualified `get_url:` module name; tasks MUST use `ansible.builtin.get_url`."
msgstr "`test_no_legacy_get_url_module_usage.py` cosc a chur ar an neamhcháilithe `get_url:` ainm modúl; tascanna MUST úsáid `ansible.builtin.get_url`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_no_legacy_uri_module_usage.py` forbids the unqualified `uri:` module name; tasks MUST use `ansible.builtin.uri`."
msgstr "`test_no_legacy_uri_module_usage.py` cosc a chur ar an neamhcháilithe `uri:` ainm modúl; tascanna MUST úsáid `ansible.builtin.uri`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_no_literal_no_log.py` forbids literal `no_log: true` / `no_log: false`; every gate MUST flow through the `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS` variable."
msgstr "`test_no_literal_no_log.py` forbids litriúil `no_log: true` / Baile `no_log: false`; gach geata MUST sreabhadh tríd an `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS` athróg."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_no_lookup_config_jinja_default.py` forbids `lookup('config', application_id, 'path') | default(X)`. The two-term `config` lookup raises on a missing key, so the Jinja `default(...)` filter never fires; the fallback MUST be passed as the lookup's third argument instead."
msgstr "`test_no_lookup_config_jinja_default.py` forbids `lookup('config', application_id, 'path') | default(X)`. An dá théarma `config` Ardaíonn lookup ar eochair ar iarraidh, mar sin an Jinja `default(...)` scagaire riamh tinte; an MUST fallback a rith mar an lookup ar an tríú argóint ina ionad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_no_redundant_default_on_module_io.py` forbids `| default(...)` on a task's own `register:` output or input arguments inside its own conditionals, where the value is provably set."
msgstr "`test_no_redundant_default_on_module_io.py` forbids `| default(...)` ar tasc féin `register:` argóintí aschur nó ionchur taobh istigh dá coinníollachtaí féin, i gcás ina bhfuil an luach leagtha go provably."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_no_sh_lc_pipefail.py` requires that every `sh -lc '...'` invocation containing a `|` pipeline starts with `set -o pipefail`, so failures mid-pipeline propagate."
msgstr "`test_no_sh_lc_pipefail.py` Éilíonn go bhfuil gach `sh -lc '...'` sonrasc ina bhfuil `|` Tosaíonn píblíne le `set -o pipefail`, mar sin teipeanna lár-píblíne propagate."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_no_sh_pipefail_in_ansible_tasks.py` requires that Ansible `shell:` tasks stay on Bash and use Bash's `set -o pipefail` form, not the POSIX-`sh` workaround."
msgstr "`test_no_sh_pipefail_in_ansible_tasks.py` Éilíonn go Ansible `shell:` tascanna fanacht ar Bash agus úsáid Bash `set -o pipefail` foirm, ní an POSIX-`sh` workaround."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`test_role_and_group_vars_used.py` scans top-level keys of `roles/<role>/{vars,defaults}/main.yml` and `group_vars/**/*.yml` against every project `.yml` / `.yaml` / `.j2` file. The suppression rule key is `unused-var` (see [suppression.md](../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md))."
msgstr "`test_role_and_group_vars_used.py` scans eochracha barr-leibhéal de `roles/<role>/{vars,defaults}/main.yml` agus `group_vars/**/*.yml` in aghaidh gach tionscadail `.yml` / Baile `.yaml` / Baile `.j2` comhad. Is é an eochair riail faoi chois `unused-var` (féach ar [suppression.md](../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md))."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_run_once_tags.py` requires that every `set_fact` marked `run_once: true` carries the canonical run-once tags so re-runs and `--tags` filters keep the fact populated."
msgstr "`test_run_once_tags.py` Éilíonn go bhfuil gach `set_fact` marcáilte marcáilte `run_once: true` Déanann an Canonical reáchtáil-amháin clibeanna mar sin re-runs agus `--tags` scagairí a choinneáil ar an bhfíric daonra."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_sed_escape.py` requires that any Jinja-templated replacement passed to `sed` flows through the `sed_escape` filter so substitutions with regex metacharacters land literally."
msgstr "`test_sed_escape.py` Éilíonn go rith aon athsholáthair Jinja-templated `sed` sreabhadh tríd an `sed_escape` scagaire mar sin ionadú le talamh metacharachtar regex literally."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_service_shared_consistency.py` enforces that every service whose `meta/services.yml` entry marks it `shared: true` exposes the required role-side bindings, and the inverse: a role consuming the shared form MUST declare the corresponding flag in its `meta/services.yml`."
msgstr "`test_service_shared_consistency.py` forfheidhmiú go bhfuil gach seirbhís a bhfuil a `meta/services.yml` marcanna iontrála é `shared: true` nochtann na ceangail ró-thaobh is gá, agus an inbhéartach: ról Tógann an fhoirm roinnte MUST dhearbhú an bhratach chomhfhreagrach ina `meta/services.yml`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`test_vars_usage_in_yaml.py` scans task-level `vars:` blocks against the same consumer set. The two scanners never overlap because their declaration shapes differ."
msgstr "`test_vars_usage_in_yaml.py` scans tasc-leibhéal `vars:` bloic i gcoinne an leagtha tomhaltóir céanna. Riamh an dá scanóirí forluí toisc go bhfuil a gcuid cruthanna dearbhú difriúil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`tests/lint/...`                           collision/band checks"
msgstr "`tests/lint/...` seiceálacha imbhuailte agus bannaí"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`tests/lint/ansible/roles/meta/test_unpinned_no_engine_volume.py` stays as the guard: an unpinned role must not declare an engine on-disk data volume."
msgstr "`tests/lint/ansible/roles/meta/test_unpinned_no_engine_volume.py` fanacht mar an garda: ní mór ról gan choinne a dhearbhú méid sonraí inneall ar-díreach."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`tls.py`/`tls_common`: onion branch + app-level flavor override + unit tests."
msgstr "`tls.py`/ Baile`tls_common`: brainse oinniún + override blas app-leibhéal + tástálacha aonad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`tls` reads `external` and `TLS_ENABLED`."
msgstr "`tls` léamha `external` agus `TLS_ENABLED`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`tool_objectfs` object-file-storage plugin"
msgstr "`tool_objectfs` breiseán réad-comhad-stóráil"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`tools/list` returns 10 tools: entity control (`HassTurnOn`, `HassTurnOff`), timers, broadcast, to-do list read and write, date and time, and `GetLiveContext` for the current state."
msgstr "`tools/list` data recovery 10 uirlisí: rialú eintiteas (`HassTurnOn`, `HassTurnOff`), timers, craoladh, liosta a dhéanamh léamh agus a scríobh, dáta agus am, agus `GetLiveContext` don stát reatha."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`transport` MUST default to `streamable_http` for server deployments. Stdio MAY exist only for local development and MUST NOT be enabled in a deployed web role by default."
msgstr "`transport` MUST réamhshocraithe a `streamable_http` le haghaidh imscaradh freastalaí. Stdio MAY ann ach amháin le haghaidh forbartha áitiúla agus NACH MÓR a chumasú i ról gréasáin imscaradh de réir réamhshocraithe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`transport` accepts `streamable_http` and `sse` only. A stdio MCP server is a local process the client spawns, so it inherits the client container's filesystem and network with no endpoint to authenticate, no proxy to route through, and nothing for a probe to reach. Every property the other rules rely on (`auth`, `exposure`, `endpoint`) is undefined for it. Clients that support stdio are pinned away from it in their own role: Flowise sets `CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse` so no flow can spawn a command."
msgstr "`transport` Glacann `streamable_http` agus `sse` ach amháin. Is próiseas áitiúil é freastalaí MCP stdio, agus mar sin tá córas comhaid agus líonra an choimeádáin chliaint le gan aon phointe a fhíordheimhniú, gan aon seachfhreastalaí dul tríd, agus aon rud le haghaidh probe chun teacht. Gach maoin na rialacha eile ag brath ar (`auth`, `exposure`, `endpoint`) Tá sé neamhshainithe dó. Cliaint a thacaíonn stdio a pinned amach as é ina ról féin: Leagann Flowise `CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse` ionas gur féidir aon sreabhadh a sceitheadh ordú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`true` (case-insensitive)"
msgstr "`true` (cás-íogair)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`true` = baseline install contract: always installed, MAY omit `enabled`, MUST NOT set `enabled: false`. Also gates install-failure: a failed `required: true` addon hard-fails the play; a failed `required: false` addon warns, is skipped, and the play continues."
msgstr "`true` = conradh suiteála bonnlíne: suiteáilte i gcónaí, MAY omit `enabled`, NÍ MÓR leagan síos `enabled: false`. Chomh maith leis sin geataí shuiteáil-failure: theip `required: true` addon crua-fails an dráma; theip `required: false` addon warns, Tá skipped, agus leanann an spraoi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`true` if the host is in the `web-app-mailu` group, else `false`"
msgstr "`true` má tá an t-óstach sa `web-app-mailu` grúpa, eile `false`"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`true` or `false`; appends `--debug` when true"
msgstr "`true` nó `false`; Aguisíní `--debug` nuair fíor"

msgid "`true` stops an agent after `idle_minutes` without a request; `false` keeps it running"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`true` to allow update PRs (workflow-driven and Dependabot)"
msgstr "`true` a cheadú PRs cothrom le dáta (sreabhadh oibre-tiomáinte agus ag brath)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`true` to keep them for every test (passing runs included); the workflow forwards it as `INFINITO_PLAYWRIGHT_KEEP`"
msgstr "`true` iad a choinneáil le haghaidh gach tástála (Ritheann a rith san áireamh); an sreabhadh oibre ar aghaidh mar `INFINITO_PLAYWRIGHT_KEEP`"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`true` to machine-translate the entries a PR leaves empty or fuzzy, one PR per language"
msgstr "`true` chun meaisín-aistriú na n-iontrálacha PR duilleoga folamh nó fuzzy, PR amháin in aghaidh na teanga"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`true` to run CI on `main` pushes too"
msgstr "`true` a reáchtáil CI ar `main` pushes ró-"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`type:` and `regex:` are enforced by `validate_supplied_value()` in [inventory.py](../../../../../utils/manager/inventory.py) at inventory-creation time, on every path where a value arrives from outside:"
msgstr "`type:` agus `regex:` a fhorfheidhmiú trí `validate_supplied_value()` i [inventory.py](../../../../../utils/manager/inventory.py) ag am fardal-creation, ar gach cosán ina dtagann luach ó taobh amuigh:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`type:` and `regex:` hold an operator-supplied value to the shape the schema declares; a generated one is exempt because the algorithm that produced it is named by the same schema."
msgstr "`type:` agus `regex:` a shealbhú luach oibreoir-sholáthar ar an cruth Dearbhaíonn an scéimre; tá ceann a ghintear díolmhaithe mar gheall ar an algartam a tháirgtear go bhfuil sé ainmnithe ag an scéimre chéanna."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`type` is one of `openapi_allowlist`, `graphql_allowlist`, `named_query`, `s3_prefix`, `prometheus_readonly`, `n8n_workflow`, `resource_readonly`. `graphql_allowlist`, `named_query`, `s3_prefix` and `resource_readonly` additionally require a non-empty `adapter.scope` naming the exact buckets, prefixes, collections or queries reachable. `openapi_allowlist` and `graphql_allowlist` require a checked-in `specification_path` under the role's own `files/`."
msgstr "`type` Is é ceann de na `openapi_allowlist`, `graphql_allowlist`, `named_query`, `s3_prefix`, `prometheus_readonly`, `n8n_workflow`, `resource_readonly`. `graphql_allowlist`, `named_query`, `s3_prefix` agus `resource_readonly` a cheangal chomh maith le neamh-empty `adapter.scope` ainmniú na buicéid bheacht, réimeanna, bailiúcháin nó fiosruithe reachable. `openapi_allowlist` agus `graphql_allowlist` a cheangal ar sheiceáil-i `specification_path` faoin ról féin `files/`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`update/` reuses the already-initialized inventory."
msgstr "`update/` reuses an fardal cheana féin-initialized."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`update` (optional) controls live upstream monitoring. `update.monitored` defaults to `false`; `update.catalog` MUST name a supported external-test catalog adapter; `update.upstream_id` defaults to `<addon_id>`."
msgstr "`update` (roghnach) rialuithe beo monatóireacht sruth. `update.monitored` riachtanais uisce: measartha `false`; `update.catalog` MUST ainm tacaithe adapter chatalóg tástála seachtrach; `update.upstream_id` riachtanais uisce: measartha `<addon_id>`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`update` reuses the existing inventory; `disable` reaches ansible as an extra-var that renders services disabled, but does not touch the include."
msgstr "`update` athbhuail an fardal atá ann cheana; `disable` sroicheann ansiúd mar var breise a fhágann seirbhísí faoi mhíchumas, ach ní i dteagmháil leis an áireamh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`user_username` is resolved from `lookup('users', user_key).username` (fallback: `user_key`)"
msgstr "`user_username` Tá réiteach ó `lookup('users', user_key).username` (fallback: `user_key`)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`username` reads `from`."
msgstr "`username` léamha `from`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`users.<WORKSTATION_USER>.authorized_keys` (list; may be empty)"
msgstr "`users.<WORKSTATION_USER>.authorized_keys` (liosta; d'fhéadfadh a bheith folamh)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`users.<WORKSTATION_USER>.groups` (list)"
msgstr "`users.<WORKSTATION_USER>.groups` (liosta de na liosta)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`users.<WORKSTATION_USER>.username` (defaults to WORKSTATION_USER if missing)"
msgstr "`users.<WORKSTATION_USER>.username` (riachtanais uisce: measartha WORKSTATION_USER má tá tú in easnamh)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`users` lookup 👥"
msgstr "`users` taiseachas aeir: fliuch 👥"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`utils.cache.base._render_with_templar` and the two templar helpers behind it swallow every exception on purpose: a meta payload renders in rounds, and an expression that cannot resolve yet has to come back unchanged rather than abort the round."
msgstr "`utils.cache.base._render_with_templar` agus an dá Cúntóirí templar taobh thiar shlogtar sé gach eisceacht ar na críche sin: a payload meta rindreáil i babhtaí, agus abairt nach féidir a réiteach go fóill nach bhfuil le teacht ar ais gan athrú seachas abort an bhabhta."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`utils.inventory.bundle_apps` reads each named bundle, walks `all.children`, deduplicates the role groups across all bundles, and prints the resulting application list as CSV. The CSV is exported as `apps` before the delegated script runs."
msgstr "`utils.inventory.bundle_apps` léann gach bundle ainmnithe, siúlóidí `all.children`, deduplicates na grúpaí ról thar gach bundles, agus priontaí an liosta iarratais mar thoradh air mar CSV. Déantar CSV a onnmhairiú mar `apps` sula ritheann an script tarmligthe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`utils.roles.entity.name.get_entity_name` maps a role / application_id to its compose entity name (the longest matching category prefix stripped). The purge orchestrators need the inverse: given an entity name, which application_ids belong to it? This helper walks the roles directory and returns that mapping."
